data/adventures/gosses-company/bench.kyr:
Module pentrice "Gosse's Company" {
  // ── The Bench ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Four critics, named by the Guildhall, the Gullet, the Close and the Owl. Three votes give the Patent. Each has a
  // regard for Gosse's Company that what the company does, and what it plays, moves; each holds a different idea of
  // what a play is for, which can be learned by asking them, or by watching them watch.
  // What pleases a critic, and what does not: a vote is won by the one outweighing the other.
  Measure regard(group). Measure slight(group). Relation critic(group).
  Initially Assert critic(clay). Initially Assert critic(gammage). Initially Assert critic(mallory). Initially Assert critic(callow).
  Initially Set regard(gammage) to 1. Initially Set regard(callow) to 1.
  Discovery taste_clay "Ormsby Clay, the Guildhall's critic, wants order of a play: verse spoken as verse, decorum, every person brought to their proper end; he cannot abide clowns, bears or words that are not in the book." { Known by clay. }
  Discovery taste_gammage "Dame Thalia Gammage, the Gullet's critic, wants joy of a play: laughter, spectacle, a good cry and home; she hates pomp and long speeches, and has hated Ambrose Swale in print for fifteen years." { Known by gammage. }
  Discovery taste_mallory "Canon Mallory, the Close's critic, wants a play to leave its house better than it found it: a moral, and nobody the worse; he will not have indecency, nor the dead mocked." { Known by mallory. }
  Discovery taste_callow "Nym Carrow, the Owl's critic, wants a play to tell the truth to power, and despises anything the Office would license." { Known by callow. }
  // On a Trial night the Bench sits in the lords' room over the stage; otherwise each is where their trade is.
  Rule bench_to_wheel when critic(?c) and trialNight() and hour(clock) >= 18 and hour(clock) < 22 and at(?c, ?p) and not at(?c, wheel) {
    Retract at(?c, ?p). Assert at(?c, wheel). }
  Rule clay_back when (hour(clock) >= 23 or hour(clock) < 8) and at(clay, wheel) { Retract at(clay, wheel). Assert at(clay, owl_room). }
  Rule gammage_back when (hour(clock) >= 23 or hour(clock) < 8) and at(gammage, wheel) { Retract at(gammage, wheel). Assert at(gammage, gullet). }
  Rule mallory_back when (hour(clock) >= 23 or hour(clock) < 8) and at(mallory, wheel) { Retract at(mallory, wheel). Assert at(mallory, canon_study). }
  Rule callow_back when (hour(clock) >= 23 or hour(clock) < 8) and at(callow, wheel) { Retract at(callow, wheel). Assert at(callow, owl_room). }
  Observe bench_at_wheel at wheel when at(clay, wheel) and at(gammage, wheel) "Over the stage, in the lords' room, the Bench sits in a row like a jury: a thin man in black with a book open on his knee, a big woman in a bonnet with a bag of nuts, a plump clergyman, and a young man in a coat too good for him, already yawning.".

  // ── Ormsby Clay, the Guildhall's critic ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person clay "Ormsby Clay" at owl_room {
    Role "the Guildhall's critic". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner proud.
    Greets "Ormsby Clay is a thin man in black with a face like a closed book and a closed book in front of him, which he opens, so as to have something to look at while you speak.".
    Wants dido_kind.
  }
  Topic clay_taste with clay "Ask Ormsby Clay what a play is for" when true once {
    Says "'For order,' says Clay. 'A play is a small world made right: every person in it given their proper end, every line its proper measure. A tragedy shows us the fall of what was high, a comedy the righting of what was crooked, and both in verse, if they are worth anything.' He turns a page. 'I do not attend for the bear.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, taste_clay). }
  }
  Topic clay_gosse with clay "Ask Ormsby Clay about Gosse's Company" when true once {
    Says "Clay closes his book. 'Twenty years ago,' he says, 'a tragedy of mine was played at the Wheel. Dido. In five acts and in verse. It was played before Gosse's Company's jig, and when it was done, and the house was, I may say, attentive, their clown came on and did the whole of my fourth act in eight minutes in rhyme, with a ham for the funeral pyre.' He opens the book again. 'The pit preferred the ham. I have not written for the stage since, and I have not forgiven Absalom Gosse, who stood in the wings and laughed.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, clay_grudge). }
  }
  Discovery clay_grudge "Twenty years ago Ormsby Clay's tragedy, Dido, was played at the Wheel before Gosse's Company's jig, and Gosse's clown burlesqued its fourth act with a ham; Clay has not written for the stage since, nor forgiven Gosse." { Known by clay, gosse. }
  Kind dido_kind "a manuscript tragedy" is gear worth 0 weighing 1
    described "A manuscript in a careful hand, gone yellow, tied with black ribbon: DIDO, A TRAGEDY, BY O. CLAY. In the margins, here and there, in a big sprawling hand in pencil: Beautiful. Too long. Here, beautiful. And on the last page: Cut nothing. A.G.".
  Item dido "the manuscript of Dido" is dido_kind at tiring_house hidden until dido_found.
  Discovery dido_found "In the rack of old costumes in the Wheel's tiring-house, inside a moth-eaten queen's robe, is the prompt copy of Ormsby Clay's Dido, from twenty years ago, with notes in Absalom Gosse's hand in the margins: Beautiful. Too long. Cut nothing.".
  // Found by searching, and seen there while it is there.
  Observe dido_seen at tiring_house when searched(party, tiring_house) and at(dido, tiring_house) "In the rack of old costumes, inside the sleeve of a moth-eaten queen's robe, someone has rolled up a manuscript and tied it with black ribbon: DIDO, A TRAGEDY, BY O. CLAY. Its margins are full of pencil in a big sprawling hand." teaches dido_found.
  Initially Assert lends(gosse, dido, party).
  Event clay_reads near clay when keeps(clay, dido) "Clay unties the black ribbon as if it might bite. He turns the pages, and stops at the first pencil note, and reads it, and turns more slowly, and reads the next. Beautiful. Too long. Here, beautiful. At the last page he sits for a while with his hand flat on it, over CUT NOTHING. A.G. 'He wrote this,' he says, 'the night they burlesqued it.' He does not look up. 'He stood in the wings and laughed, and then he went home and wrote this.' He ties the ribbon again, carefully, and puts the manuscript inside his coat. 'Thank you,' he says, to the table." then {
    Increase regard(clay) by 2. Assert clayMoved(clay). }
  Relation clayMoved(group). Relation curtainRaiser(group).
  Topic gosse_dido with gosse "Ask Gosse to play the lament from Clay's Dido before the play, as a curtain-raiser" when knows(actor, clay_grudge) and knows(actor, dido_found) and inCompany(actor) and not swaleGone(swale) and not curtainRaiser(gosse) once {
    Says "Gosse is quiet. Then: 'Dido,' he says. 'The lament. Thirty lines, in the old measure, before the house is warm.' He makes a face. 'It is very long, and very beautiful, and the Gullet will throw nuts.' He looks at you. 'And Ormsby Clay will sit in the lords' room and hear his verses spoken by Ambrose Swale at the Wheel, properly, after twenty years.' He nods slowly. 'Swale will do it. Swale will do it like a bishop.'".
    On discuss { Assert curtainRaiser(gosse). }
  }

  // ── Dame Thalia Gammage, the Gullet's critic ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person gammage "Dame Thalia Gammage" at gullet {
    Role "the Gullet's critic, who keeps the ballad stall". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner jovial.
    Wants gull_note.
    Greets "Dame Thalia Gammage is a big woman in a bonnet with ribbons, behind a stall papered with ballad-sheets, eating hazelnuts out of a bag and cracking the shells in her teeth. 'Buy a ballad,' she says, 'or buy me a drink, or go away.'".
  }
  Topic gammage_taste with gammage "Ask Dame Gammage what a play is for" when true once {
    Says "'Joy,' says Dame Gammage, through a nut. 'A play is for a fishwife who has stood in the Gullet since four in the morning, to stand in the yard of the Wheel at seven and forget she has feet. Laugh, cry, see a bear, go home.' She spits a shell. 'Not to be talked at. Not to be preached at. Not to stand three hours watching Ambrose Swale die by inches in iambics.' She cracks another. 'Fifteen years I've been telling him so in print.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, taste_gammage). }
  }
  Topic gammage_swale with gammage "Ask Dame Gammage about Ambrose Swale" when true once {
    Says "'The Wooden Lear,' says Dame Gammage, with relish. 'I called him that in the year thirty and it stuck. The Wooden Lear, the Walking Cathedral, the Man Who Played Hamlet as a Bell-Tower.' She is smiling. 'Fifteen years, every time he's played the Wheel, I've gone and stood in the yard and written him down.' She stops smiling, though not on purpose. 'He has a voice, mind. Under all that marble. If he ever let it out, you'd hear it in the Close.'".
  }
  Discovery gammage_loves "Dame Gammage's scrapbook holds every notice she ever wrote of Ambrose Swale in fifteen years, each one cruel, and against each one, pressed, a flower." {
    Found by searching gullet "Under the ballad stall, in a dry box with Dame Gammage's spare bonnet, is a scrapbook. Every page is a cutting of one of her own notices, and every notice is of Ambrose Swale: the Wooden Lear, the Walking Cathedral. Against each one, pressed flat and brown, is a flower: a daisy, a pansy, a rose, a sprig of rosemary, fifteen years of them.".
  }
  Item gammage_notice "the old notice of Dorcas Quaile's Widow" is old_notice at gullet hidden until notice_given.
  Discovery notice_given "Dame Gammage has given you her old notice of Dorcas Quaile's Widow, from twelve years ago.".
  Topic gammage_dorcas with gammage "Ask Dame Gammage what she thinks of Dorcas Quaile" when true once {
    Says "'Dorcas Quaile!' Dame Gammage slaps the stall. 'Twelve years ago she played the Miller's Widow at the Wheel and I laughed so hard they carried me out. I wrote it up. I said, let her play nothing but widows.' She sighs. 'And she went on playing girls. They all do. They'd sooner be pretty than great.' She rummages under the stall. 'I've the cutting somewhere. I keep everything.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, notice_given). }
  }
  Initially Assert lends(gammage, gammage_notice, party).

  // ── The gulling of Swale and Gammage ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Pudding and Dorcas mean to make the tragedian and the critic who has savaged him for fifteen years each believe
  // the other is in love. They need someone to carry the notes.
  Relation gullOffered(group). Relation gammageGulled(group). Relation swaleGulled(group). Relation gullExposed(group).
  Relation truthTold(group). Relation understanding(group). Relation humiliated(group).
  Topic pudding_gull with pudding "Ask Pudding what he and Dorcas are whispering about" when inCompany(actor) and tday(pentrice) >= 1 and not dorcasGone(dorcas) and not gullOffered(pudding) once {
    Says "Pudding looks round the loft, and then at Dorcas, who looks at the ceiling. 'A comedy,' he says. 'An old one. Two people who've hated each other in public for fifteen years, and the company lets each one find a letter from the other.' He takes two folded notes out of his sleeve. 'Ambrose Swale and Thalia Gammage. Dorcas wrote his, I wrote hers, and we can neither of us go near them, because we'd laugh.' He holds them out. 'You carry them. Give hers to her at her stall, his to him in the loft. Then, tomorrow at four, they'll both be at the Owl, and so shall we, under a table.'".
    On discuss { Assert gullOffered(pudding). }
  }
  Kind gull_note "a folded note" is gear worth 0 weighing 0
    described "A folded note, sealed with candle-grease and a thumb.".
  Item note_gammage "a note 'from Ambrose Swale'" is gull_note at moon_loft hidden until notes_taken.
  Item note_swale "a note 'from Thalia Gammage'" is gull_note at moon_loft hidden until notes_taken.
  Discovery notes_taken "Pudding has given you the two forged notes, one for Swale and one for Dame Gammage.".
  Action take_notes(actor: group, recipient: member, site: place) "Take Pudding's two notes, to carry them" {
    Speaker pudding. Time 1 minute.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(pudding, site) and gullOffered(pudding)
      and memberOf(recipient, actor) and awake(recipient) and not knows(actor, notes_taken).
    Resolve acquire(note_gammage, gull_note, recipient).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, notes_taken). Retract at(note_gammage, moon_loft). }
    Result "Pudding presses the notes into your hand like a pickpocket in reverse. 'Hers is the one with the thumb,' he says. 'His is the other. Mind you don't mix them.'".
  }
  Action take_note_two(actor: group, recipient: member, site: place) "Take the second of Pudding's notes" {
    Speaker pudding. Time 1 minute.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and knows(actor, notes_taken) and at(note_swale, moon_loft)
      and memberOf(recipient, actor) and awake(recipient).
    Resolve acquire(note_swale, gull_note, recipient).
    On success { Retract at(note_swale, moon_loft). }
    Result "The second note is sealed with a thumb too, a bigger one.".
  }
  Initially Assert lends(pudding, note_gammage, party). Initially Assert lends(pudding, note_swale, party).
  Relation noteFair(group).
  Action forge_note(actor: group, site: place) "Copy Pudding's note for Dame Gammage out fair, in a hand like Swale's" {
    Time 3.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and carries(actor, note_gammage) and not noteFair(gammage) and not triedForge(actor).
    Resolve check(actor, deception, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert noteFair(gammage). }
    On failure { Assert triedForge(actor). }
    Result "You copy it out in a tall formal hand with long descenders, the hand of a man who signs his name across a whole playbill, and sign it with a flourish like a cloak. It looks like Ambrose Swale. It looks, if anything, more like Ambrose Swale than Swale does.".
    Otherwise "Your copy looks like what it is: somebody trying to write like somebody else.".
  }
  Relation triedForge(group).
  Action spell_note(actor: group, site: place) "Mend the spelling of Pudding's note for Dame Gammage, and put the metre right" {
    Time 3.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and carries(actor, note_gammage) and not noteFair(gammage) and not triedSpell(actor).
    Resolve check(actor, lore, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert noteFair(gammage). }
    On failure { Assert triedSpell(actor). }
    Result "Pudding spells sincerely with one R and admiration with a Q. You put them right, and the metre too, so that every line of it scans as Ambrose Swale's lines scan, like a man walking slowly up a staircase. It is quite a good poem now.".
    Otherwise "You correct the spelling, and in correcting it make it worse, and the metre goes on limping.".
  }
  Relation triedSpell(group).
  Event gammage_reads near gammage when keeps(gammage, note_gammage) and noteFair(gammage) "Dame Gammage reads it with a nut halfway to her mouth, and the nut stays there. She reads it again. Then she folds it very small and puts it down the front of her dress, and looks at you, and for a moment the big ribboned face is entirely unguarded. 'The Owl,' she says. 'Four o'clock.' Then: 'Go away.' You go. Behind you she has started, very quietly, to cry, or to laugh; you cannot tell which." then {
    Assert gammageGulled(gammage). }
  Event gammage_scorns near gammage when keeps(gammage, note_gammage) and not noteFair(gammage) "Dame Gammage reads it, and looks at the seal, and at you, and laughs out loud, not kindly. 'Ambrose Swale never wrote a word in his life that didn't scan,' she says. 'This is Jem Pudding's spelling. Tell him he's a cruel little man, and tell him I'll be in the yard on his night with a bag of something harder than nuts.'" then {
    Assert gullExposed(gammage). Increase slight(gammage) by 1. }
  Event swale_mixed near swale when keeps(swale, note_gammage) "Swale reads it, and frowns, and reads it again, and turns it over. 'This is signed with my name,' he says slowly. 'It is a love letter, in very bad metre, from me.' He looks at you, and across the loft at Pudding, who has gone under a hamper. 'I see,' says Ambrose Swale, with tremendous dignity, and folds it, and puts it in the fire." then {
    Assert gullExposed(gammage). }
  Event gammage_mixed near gammage when keeps(gammage, note_swale) "Dame Gammage reads it and begins to laugh, and cannot stop. 'It's from me,' she says at last, wiping her eyes. 'To him. Signed. Oh, Jem Pudding, you poor fool, you've sent the wrong one.' She tears it up very small and lets it go over the Gullet like snow." then {
    Assert gullExposed(gammage). }
  Event swale_reads_note near swale when keeps(swale, note_swale) "Swale reads it standing, at the window, as if it were a part. You watch him read it twice, and his ears go red, and the beautiful ruined face does something you have not seen it do on any stage. 'Fifteen years,' he says, to the window. 'Every notice. Every single one.' He folds it. 'Tomorrow, at four,' he says. 'I shall want my good coat.'" then {
    Assert swaleGulled(swale). }
  Action tell_swale_truth(actor: group, site: place) "Tell Swale the note was Pudding's, and tell him about Dame Gammage's scrapbook and its flowers" {
    Speaker swale. Time 5 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(swale, site) and swaleGulled(swale) and knows(actor, gammage_loves)
      and not truthTold(swale) and not understanding(swale) and not humiliated(swale).
    On success { Assert truthTold(swale). }
    Result "Swale hears it all, the forged note, Pudding's thumb, the scrapbook under the ballad stall, the flowers. He does not interrupt. When you have finished he sits down on a hamper. 'A pansy,' he says. 'Against the Walking Cathedral.' He puts his face in his hands, and his shoulders shake, and you see he is laughing. 'Very well,' he says at last, wiping his eyes. 'I shall go to the Owl at four, as the comedy requires, and I shall take her a flower.'".
  }
  // At four on the day after both notes are given, Swale and Gammage are at the Owl. Told the truth and holding a flower,
  // Swale makes it real; otherwise the forgery comes out in front of the whole long room.
  Measure tryst(group). Relation swaleWaited(group).
  Rule tryst_set when swaleGulled(swale) and tryst(swale) == 0 { Set tryst(swale) to tday(pentrice) + 1. }
  Query trystNow() means tryst(swale) > 0 and tday(pentrice) == tryst(swale) and hour(clock) >= 16 and not swaleGone(swale)
    and not understanding(swale) and not humiliated(swale) and not swaleWaited(swale).
  Rule tryst_true at owl_room when trystNow() and truthTold(swale) and gammageGulled(gammage)
    says "At four Ambrose Swale comes into the Owl in his good coat with a single pansy in his hand, and walks the length of the long room to where Dame Gammage is sitting very upright in a new bonnet, and gives it to her, and says, in a voice that carries to the kitchens: 'It was a forgery, madam. Pudding's. But the flowers were not.' Dame Gammage looks at the pansy for a long time. Then she moves her bag of nuts off the bench beside her, and he sits down, and the Owl, which has stopped talking, does not start again for some while." {
    Assert understanding(swale). Increase regard(gammage) by 2. }
  Rule tryst_stall at gullet when trystNow() and truthTold(swale) and not gammageGulled(gammage)
    says "At four Ambrose Swale comes down Fish Lane in his good coat, through the fishwives, who stop crying pike to watch, with a single pansy in his hand; and stops at the ballad stall, where Dame Gammage, who knows Jem Pudding's spelling when she sees it, is waiting with her arms folded. 'It was a forgery, madam,' he says. 'Pudding's. But I have seen your scrapbook, and the flowers were not.' Dame Gammage unfolds her arms. After a long time she takes the pansy." {
    Assert understanding(swale). Increase regard(gammage) by 2. }
  Rule tryst_false at owl_room when trystNow() and not truthTold(swale) and gammageGulled(gammage)
    says "At four Ambrose Swale comes into the Owl in his good coat and bows over Dame Gammage's hand and says, beautifully, that he has kept her letter next to his heart. 'My letter?' says Dame Gammage. 'I've kept yours.' They take them out. They read them. In the silence the whole long room hears Jem Pudding, under a table by the door, begin to laugh. Dame Gammage gets up, and puts on her bonnet, and walks out without a word, and Swale stands in the middle of the Owl with a note in Jem Pudding's spelling in his hand, and everybody looking." {
    Assert humiliated(swale). Assert gullExposed(gammage). Increase slight(gammage) by 3. Retract reconciled(swale). }
  Rule tryst_alone at owl_room when trystNow() and not truthTold(swale) and not gammageGulled(gammage)
    says "Ambrose Swale sits at the end table in the Owl from four o'clock in his good coat, with his back very straight, and Dame Gammage does not come, and does not come. At last, when the lamps are lit, he gets up and goes out, leaving his gloves on the table. Pudding, who has been watching from the door, does not laugh at all." {
    Assert humiliated(swale). Assert swaleWaited(swale). Retract reconciled(swale). }

  // ── Canon Mallory, the Close's critic, and the Children of the Close ────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person mallory "Canon Mallory" at canon_study {
    Role "the minster's precentor, and the Close's critic". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner compassionate.
    Greets "Canon Mallory is a plump pink clergyman with a pipe, a harpsichord and a kind, worried face. He rises when you come in, which nobody else in Pentrice does.".
    Profession priest.
    Offers healing "a dressing, and a psalm said over it" for 2 coin.
  }
  Topic mallory_taste with mallory "Ask Canon Mallory what a play is for" when true once {
    Says "'To send them home better,' says the Canon, and knocks out his pipe. 'Not preached at. I have the pulpit for that, and they do not come. But a play that shows them a kindness done, or a pride brought low, or a quarrel made up, and nobody the worse, why, they go home and are kinder for a week.' He hesitates. 'I will not have filth. And I will not have the dead mocked, who cannot answer. That is all.' He smiles. 'That is a great deal, in the theatre.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, taste_mallory). }
  }
  Topic mallory_voice with mallory "Ask Canon Mallory how the choir keeps a breaking voice through a season" when knows(actor, kit_fear) or knows(actor, ned_wants) once {
    Says "'Ah,' says the Canon, and sits down at the harpsichord and plays a note, and then a lower one. 'Honey and horehound, the horehound bruised and the honey stirred in off the boil. But that is not the trick.' He plays the first note again. 'The trick is to sing under the voice, not over it. A breaking voice breaks reaching up. Let every line come down to you, as if you were tired; never go up after the top of it.' He closes the lid. 'It will hold a night, done so. A season, perhaps. Not two.' He sighs. 'Ned Cherry's will go before the year is out, and then I shall lose him.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, mallory_trick). }
  }
  Discovery mallory_trick "Canon Mallory's way with a breaking voice: honey and horehound, the horehound bruised and the honey stirred in off the boil; and sing under the voice, letting every line come down, never reaching up after the top of it." { Known by mallory. }

  Person ned "Ned Cherry" at school_yard {
    Role "a treble of the Children of the Close". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner cheerful.
    Greets "A small boy in a surplice with a cardboard wing hanging off one shoulder detaches himself from the procession round the pump and comes over to the gate, fast, before the man with the stick can see.".
  }
  Topic ned_talk with ned "Ask the boy what he wants" when not nedRuns(ned) and not nedLent(ned) once {
    Says "'To be a player,' says Ned Cherry, in a rush. 'A real one, not an angel. I saw Gosse's Company at the Wheel when I was eight, and the clown, and the bear, and I've been an angel every Trial since and I'm sick of it.' He looks over his shoulder. 'The Children play The Patient Daughter on the third night and I'm the Fourth Angel and I have one line and it's Behold. I'd play anything for Gosse. I'd play the bear.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, ned_wants). }
  }
  Discovery ned_wants "Ned Cherry, a treble of the Children of the Close, wants to be a player with Gosse's Company instead of an angel." { Known by ned. }
  Relation nedRuns(group). Relation nedLent(group). Relation nedStays(group).
  Action help_ned(actor: group, site: place) "Help Ned Cherry over the choir school wall at dusk, and take him to the Moon" {
    Time 3.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, close) and knows(actor, ned_wants) and not nedRuns(ned) and not nedLent(ned)
      and not nedStays(ned) and hour(clock) >= 19 and week() and not triedNed(actor).
    Resolve check(actor, stealth, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert nedRuns(ned). Retract at(ned, school_yard). Assert at(ned, moon_loft). Increase slight(mallory) by 2. }
    On failure { Assert triedNed(actor). }
    Result "Ned comes over the wall at the corner by the lime tree, where the glass has been knocked off by generations of boys, and drops into your arms with his surplice over his head. You walk him to the Moon by the back lanes. He talks all the way, about the bear.".
    Otherwise "A window goes up in the school as Ned's hand comes over the wall, and a man's voice says, 'Cherry,' and the hand goes down again.".
  }
  Relation triedNed(group).
  Action ask_ned_lent(actor: group, site: place) "Ask Canon Mallory to lend Ned Cherry to Gosse's Company for the Trial" {
    Speaker mallory. Time 5 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(mallory, site) and knows(actor, ned_wants) and not nedRuns(ned) and not nedLent(ned)
      and not triedLend(actor) and week().
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert nedLent(ned). Retract at(ned, school_yard). Assert at(ned, moon_loft). Increase regard(mallory) by 1. }
    On failure { Assert triedLend(actor). }
    Result "The Canon hears you out with his pipe going out in his hand. 'He'll go before the year is out whatever I do,' he says at last. 'His voice, and then him.' He sighs. 'Better he goes to the players with my blessing than over the wall without it. He may have them for the Trial. He sings Behold for us on the third night, and then he is Gosse's.' He relights the pipe. 'Tell Absalom Gosse that if the boy learns one word in that loft he could not say before his mother, I shall preach about it.'".
    Otherwise "'He is an angel,' says the Canon gently, 'and he is twelve. Ask me again when he is a man.'".
  }
  Relation triedLend(group).
  Topic mallory_faith with mallory "Tell Canon Mallory, as one who keeps the faith, that the boy will be safe among the players" when craft(actor, craft_faith) and knows(actor, ned_wants) and not nedRuns(ned) and not nedLent(ned) once {
    Says "The Canon looks at you for a long moment, as one who has knelt to another. 'You'll see to it,' he says. 'Yourself.' You say you will. 'Then he may go to them for the Trial, with my blessing.' He rubs his eyes. 'He sings Behold for us on the third night, mind.'".
    On discuss { Assert nedLent(ned). Retract at(ned, school_yard). Assert at(ned, moon_loft). Increase regard(mallory) by 1. }
  }
  Action keep_ned(actor: group, site: place) "Tell Ned to stay with the Children and sing, this season" {
    Speaker ned. Time 2 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(ned, site) and knows(actor, ned_wants) and not nedRuns(ned) and not nedLent(ned) and not nedStays(ned).
    On success { Assert nedStays(ned). Increase regard(mallory) by 1. }
    Result "Ned looks at you as if you had hit him. Then he looks at his cardboard wing. 'One more season,' he says. 'Then I'll be too old to be an angel and they'll have to let me be something.' He goes back to the procession round the pump, and somebody tells the Canon, and the Canon, you hear afterward, is very grateful.".
  }

  // ── Nym Carrow, the Owl's critic ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person callow "Nym Carrow" at owl_room {
    Role "the Owl's critic". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner acerbic.
    Greets "Nym Carrow is a young man in a coat too good for him and boots too bad, with ink on his cuffs and a cup of the Owl's coffee he has been making last for an hour. 'If you want a notice,' he says, 'I charge. If you want the truth, it is free, and nobody ever wants it.'".
  }
  Topic callow_taste with callow "Ask Nym Carrow what a play is for" when true once {
    Says "'To tell the truth to the people who pay to be lied to,' says Carrow. 'The Siege of Arle has been played every Trial for eleven years, and in all that time nobody has said on that stage that the Fountain is dry, that the Book of Precedence is four hundred pages of who may kick whom, or that the Office of Plain Speech is a muzzle with a motto.' He drinks his cold coffee. 'Anything the Office licenses is a lie by definition. I give it nothing.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, taste_callow). }
  }
  Relation callowClaims(group). Relation callowCaught(group). Relation callowShamed(group).
  Topic callow_claim with callow "Ask Nym Carrow whether he has heard of Gosse's new play" when bookCome(pentrice) and tday(pentrice) >= 1 once {
    Says "Carrow puts down his cup. 'Heard of it?' he says. 'I wrote it.' He leans back. 'Anonymously, naturally. A satire on the late Lord Mayor and his Office, sent to the one company in Imbar with nothing to lose. Who else in this city could have written it?' He looks round the long room to see who is listening, and three people are. 'You may tell Gosse,' he says, 'that the author expects his share of the house.'".
    On discuss { Assert callowClaims(callow). }
  }
  Discovery callow_lies "Nym Carrow says he wrote The Alderman's Ghost, but he cannot say what happens in it after the second act: he has heard of the play, and not read it.".
  Action test_callow(actor: group, site: place) "Ask Carrow, as its author, what the bear does in the third act" {
    Speaker callow. Time 2 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(callow, site) and callowClaims(callow) and not knows(actor, callow_lies)
      and (rehearsedIII(pentrice) or knows(actor, parcel_open)).
    Resolve check(actor, insight, dc_easy).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, callow_lies). }
    Result "'The bear,' says Carrow, without a pause, 'is an allegory.' He drinks his coffee. 'Of the City.' You wait. He looks at you over the cup, and something goes out of him. 'There is a bear,' he says. 'Isn't there. There's always a bear, with Gosse.' A long pause. 'I heard of it in the Chepe. I have nine crowns of debt and no name, and a satire on the Office is a name.' He puts the cup down. 'Who did write it?'".
  }
  Action expose_callow(actor: group, site: place) "Tell the Owl, loud enough for the long room, that Carrow never read the play he says he wrote" {
    Speaker callow. Time 2 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(callow, site) and knows(actor, callow_lies) and not callowShamed(callow) and not callowCaught(callow).
    On success { Assert callowShamed(callow). Increase slight(callow) by 2. }
    Result "The long room hears it, and laughs, and Nym Carrow sits in the middle of the laughter going red, and then white, and then gets up and leaves his cold coffee and goes out into Paternoster Row without his hat.".
  }
  Action keep_callow(actor: group, site: place) "Tell Carrow, quietly, that you know, and that you will not tell" {
    Speaker callow. Time 2 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(callow, site) and knows(actor, callow_lies) and not callowShamed(callow) and not callowCaught(callow).
    On success { Assert callowCaught(callow). Increase regard(callow) by 1. }
    Result "Carrow looks at you for a long moment. 'You might have done me in front of the whole Owl,' he says. 'Everyone else would.' He turns his cup round in its saucer. 'I'll stop saying it. And on Gosse's night,' he says, 'I'll watch it as if I'd never heard of it, which God knows is true.'".
  }
}

data/adventures/gosses-company/clock.kyr:
Module pentrice "Gosse's Company" {
  // ── The week of the Trial ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The country counts its days from the first midnight after it is reached: what is left of the day the company comes
  // is the day of arrival (tday 0), and then four days, and the morning of the verdict.
  //   tday 1: Fallow at the Moon; Patience loose in the Gullet in the afternoon.
  //   tday 2: the bailiff at the Moon in the morning; the Siege of Arle at the Wheel at seven.
  //   tday 3: Fallow pays the heckler, and the watermen at dusk; the Children of the Close at seven.
  //   tday 4: the watermen strike from four; Gosse's Company at seven.
  //   tday 5: the Bench reads its verdict at ten in the morning.
  Measure tday(place).
  Rule day_one when watch(clock) >= 0 and tday(pentrice) < 1 { Set tday(pentrice) to 1. }
  Rule day_two when watch(clock) >= 144 and tday(pentrice) < 2 { Set tday(pentrice) to 2. }
  Rule day_three when watch(clock) >= 288 and tday(pentrice) < 3 { Set tday(pentrice) to 3. }
  Rule day_four when watch(clock) >= 432 and tday(pentrice) < 4 { Set tday(pentrice) to 4. }
  Rule day_five when watch(clock) >= 576 and tday(pentrice) < 5 { Set tday(pentrice) to 5. }
  Rule day_after when watch(clock) >= 720 and tday(pentrice) < 6 { Set tday(pentrice) to 6. }

  // Before the night itself: the week in which a play is made.
  Query week() means tday(pentrice) < 4 or (tday(pentrice) == 4 and hour(clock) < 18).
  Query daytime() means hour(clock) >= 8 and hour(clock) < 18.
  Query evening() means hour(clock) >= 17 and hour(clock) < 23.
  // A Trial night at the Wheel: the second, third and fourth days, from seven until a little after nine.
  Query showtime() means hour(clock) >= 19 and hour(clock) < 22.

  // ── Where the city's news reaches ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // What the city says to itself is heard in the city, on either bank, and not on the West Road.
  Relation cityRoom(place).
  Query inCity() means at(party, ?p) and cityRoom(?p).
  Relation spread(fact).

  // ── Who the company is, here ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // One of Gosse's Company (signed on, on the road or in the yard), and one of the Office's tallymen for the week.
  Relation inCompany(group). Relation tallyman(group).
  Relation arrived(group).
  Rule come_in when at(party, ?p) and cityRoom(?p) and not arrived(party) { Assert arrived(party). }
  // Whoever came while there was still a Trial to come to: the week's ending is theirs. A company that comes down the
  // West Road after the verdict hears it as the city's news.
  Relation cameForTrial(group).
  Rule come_for_trial when arrived(party) and tday(pentrice) < 5 and not cameForTrial(party) { Assert cameForTrial(party). }
  // Whoever signed on with the players on the green is one of the company from the first step into the city.
  Rule come_in_joined when arrived(party) and knows(party, joined) and not inCompany(party) { Assert inCompany(party). }
}

data/adventures/gosses-company/combat.ky:
Module pentrice_danger "Gosse's Company: the dogs and the weir" {
  // Two places in the week where the company can be hurt, and the ways round each.
  // Bowle's mastiffs keep the bear-garden (they stand and wait for the word before they come): in the kennels by day, unless Bowle looses them on someone who opens
  // Patience's pen under his nose; loose in the ring by night, when Bowle sleeps over the kennels. Paid, pleaded with,
  // a torch held up, or hushed by someone who knows dogs, they are no danger; beaten, Bowle whistles them off.
  // The weir-rats keep the weir stones by night: Long Nan Scullard's people, Gullet folk gone wrong, who live under
  // the drowned Bishop's Mill and charge two crowns for the stones. Pay, talk, face them down, name the Gullet, or
  // cross before dark; beaten, you are thrown in the Arle. The night the Gullet walks the weir, they are not seen again.

  // ── The bear-garden by night ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Place kennels "the kennels behind the bear-garden" is room within bear_garden at 1, 0.
  Person mastiffs "Bowle's mastiffs" at kennels {
    Role "three bear-dogs, brindled and scarred, with jaws like man-traps". Species cave_hound. Level 1. Numbers 3. Pronouns they.
    Called "Grip", "Tearwell", "Old Madam".
    Temperament territorial. Lair bear_pen. Refuge kennels. Fears flame.
    Warns "Three mastiffs come out across the sand and stop, side by side, between you and the pens. They do not bark. The one in the middle, a brindled bitch with half an ear, lowers her head and shows you all of her teeth, and waits for the word.".
    Comes "The mastiffs come at you across the sand without a sound, low and fast, the way they were taught to go at a bear.".
    Flinches "The mastiffs see the fire and break, and go back into the dark behind the pens with their tails down, snarling.".
    Pleads "The last of the mastiffs lies down on the sand with its ears flat and lets you by, and somewhere behind the pens Bowle whistles, and they go.".
  }
  Initially Assert takesPrisoners(mastiffs).
  Relation bowleLet(group). Relation dogsLoosed(group). Relation dogsHushed(group).
  // Bowle sleeps over the kennels; the dogs run the ring at night.
  Query bearNight() means hour(clock) >= 23 or hour(clock) < 6.
  Rule bowle_abed when bearNight() and at(bowle, bear_pen) { Retract at(bowle, bear_pen). Assert at(bowle, kennels). }
  Rule bowle_up when not bearNight() and at(bowle, kennels) { Retract at(bowle, kennels). Assert at(bowle, bear_pen). }
  Rule dogs_run when bearNight() and at(mastiffs, kennels) and not routed(mastiffs) and not dogsHushed(mastiffs) {
    Retract at(mastiffs, kennels). Assert at(mastiffs, bear_pen). }
  Rule dogs_kennelled when not bearNight() and at(mastiffs, bear_pen) and not dogsLoosed(mastiffs) and not assails(mastiffs, party) {
    Retract at(mastiffs, bear_pen). Assert at(mastiffs, kennels). }
  Observe bear_pen_night at bear_pen when bearNight() and at(mastiffs, bear_pen) and able(mastiffs) "The ring is dark but for a lantern on the stake, and in the dark something is moving round the edge of the sand, and then three things, close together.".
  // Opening the pen under Bowle's nose.
  Rule dogs_loosed at bear_pen when state(bear_pen_gate, open) and at(bowle, bear_pen) and not bowleLet(bowle) and not dogsLoosed(mastiffs)
    says "Bowle sees the pen open, and doesn't shout. He walks to the kennels, very quickly for a short man, and draws the bolt." {
    Assert dogsLoosed(mastiffs). Retract at(mastiffs, kennels). Assert at(mastiffs, bear_pen). }
  Rule dogs_done when dogsLoosed(mastiffs) and (routed(mastiffs) or tolerates(mastiffs, party) or not at(party, bear_pen)) and at(mastiffs, bear_pen) {
    Retract dogsLoosed(mastiffs). Retract at(mastiffs, bear_pen). Assert at(mastiffs, kennels). }
  // Ways round them.
  Relation triedHush(group).
  Action hush_dogs(actor: group, site: place) "Go down on your heels and talk to the mastiffs as a drover talks to dogs" {
    Time 1 minute.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(mastiffs, site) and able(mastiffs) and not routed(mastiffs)
      and not tolerates(mastiffs, actor) and not triedHush(actor).
    Resolve check(actor, woodcraft, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert triedHush(actor). Assert tolerates(mastiffs, actor). Retract assails(mastiffs, actor). Assert dogsHushed(mastiffs). }
    On failure { Assert triedHush(actor). Assert assails(mastiffs, actor). }
    Result "You go down on your heels with your hands open and talk to them, low and steady, nonsense, the way the drovers did on the west road. The first dog stops. The second sniffs your hand. The third lies down, puzzled, with its head on its paws, and looks at Bowle as if to ask what the fuss was.".
    Otherwise "You go down on your heels, and the first dog takes it for what it is, and comes.".
  }
  Topic bowle_dogs with bowle "Ask Bowle about the dogs" when true once {
    Says "'Bear-dogs,' says Bowle. 'Bred for it. They'd take a bear's ear off and think it was their birthday.' He looks at them with something like love. 'They run the ring at night, so nobody comes over the palings for my bears. Fire they don't like. Talk they don't understand, unless you talk dog.'".
  }
  // What a captor's rule says as the fight ends is not told (see friction); it is told where the company comes round.
  Relation bitten(place). Relation ducked(place). Measure cameRound(place).
  Rule mastiffs_captured when captured(mastiffs, party) {
    Retract captured(mastiffs, party). Assert bitten(pentrice). Set cameRound(pentrice) to watch(clock). Retract at(party, bear_pen). Assert at(party, soke_lane).
    Retract assails(mastiffs, party). Retract dogsLoosed(mastiffs).
    Retract following(the_bear, party). Retract acceptsEscort(the_bear, party).
    Assert at(the_bear, bear_pen). Assert state(bear_pen_gate, penned). Retract state(bear_pen_gate, open). Assert bearTaken(the_bear). }
  Rule bitten_told at soke_lane when bitten(pentrice) and watch(clock) > cameRound(pentrice)
    says "Bowle whistled, once, and the dogs let go. You come round on the cobbles of Soke Lane with Bowle standing over you, wiping his hands. 'Stray,' he says, 'found loose in the Liberty,' and goes back in. You are bitten in three places. Patience is in her pen again, and the padlock is a new one." { Retract bitten(pentrice). }

  // ── The weir stones ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Place weir_mill "under the drowned Bishop's Mill" is room within pentrice at 2, 4.
  Person weir_rats "the weir-rats" at weir_mill {
    Role "Long Nan Scullard's people, four of them, mudlarks grown up wrong, with boat-hooks and cudgels and a dark-lantern". Ancestry human. Calling thief. Level 1. Numbers 4. Pronouns they.
    Called "Long Nan Scullard", "Eel Joe", "the Hollander's boy", "Sal Cotter".
    Temperament proud. Refuge weir_mill.
    Warns "A dark-lantern opens on the ledge in front of you, and behind it there are four people with boat-hooks, and the tallest of them is a woman with a face like a hatchet and a waterman's red cap she did not get honestly. 'Toll,' says Long Nan Scullard. 'Two crowns for the stones. Or you can swim for nothing; the Arle's free.'".
    Comes "'Over she goes, then,' says Nan Scullard, and the weir-rats come at you along the slime with their hooks out, sure-footed as cats.".
    Pleads "Nan Scullard throws her boat-hook down on the stones. 'All right,' she says. 'All right. Go on over, and be damned to you, and mind the moss.'".
  }
  Initially Set tribute(weir_rats) to 2. Initially Assert takesPrisoners(weir_rats).
  Relation ratsGone(group). Relation gulletSent(group).
  Query ratNight() means hour(clock) >= 20 or hour(clock) < 2.
  Rule rats_out when ratNight() and at(weir_rats, weir_mill) and not routed(weir_rats) and not ratsGone(weir_rats) {
    Retract at(weir_rats, weir_mill). Assert at(weir_rats, weir_stones). }
  Rule rats_in when not ratNight() and at(weir_rats, weir_stones) { Retract at(weir_rats, weir_stones). Assert at(weir_rats, weir_mill). }
  Rule rats_scattered when crowdLed(pentrice) and not ratsGone(weir_rats) { Assert ratsGone(weir_rats). Retract at(weir_rats, weir_stones). Assert at(weir_rats, weir_mill). }
  Observe weir_rats_fire at weir_stones when not ratNight() and not ratsGone(weir_rats) "The fire on the ledge is cold, but it was lit last night, and the night before.".
  Observe weir_rats_gone at weir_stones when ratsGone(weir_rats) "The fire on the ledge is scattered, trodden by three thousand pairs of feet, and nobody has lit it again.".
  Action name_gullet(actor: group, site: place) "Tell Nan Scullard the Gullet showed you the stones" {
    Time 1 minute.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(weir_rats, site) and warned(weir_rats, actor) and gulletSent(actor).
    On success { Assert tolerates(weir_rats, actor). Retract warned(weir_rats, actor). }
    Result "'Garlick,' you say, 'or Ma Tolly; one of them,' and Nan Scullard lowers her lantern. 'Tolly's father walked these stones when I was a girl,' she says, 'with eels round his neck like a mayor's chain.' She stands aside on the slime. 'Keep to the moss. And tell the Gullet Nan said she's not forgotten.'".
  }
  Topic tolly_nan with tolly "Ask Ma Tolly who keeps the weir at night" when knows(actor, weir_known) once {
    Says "'Nan Scullard,' says Ma Tolly, and her face shuts. 'Gutted fish here for nine years and went to the bad, or the bad came to her: her man was a waterman and drowned under the Stairs, and the Wardens wouldn't bury him without the second penny. She lives under the old mill with three others like her.' She sniffs. 'Cross in daylight, or say my name. She'll have it, if she's sober.'".
    On discuss { Assert gulletSent(actor). }
  }
  Rule rats_captured when captured(weir_rats, party) {
    Retract captured(weir_rats, party). Assert ducked(pentrice). Set cameRound(pentrice) to watch(clock). Retract at(party, weir_stones). Assert at(party, soke_landing).
    Retract assails(weir_rats, party). Decrease quantity(party, gold) by 6. }
  Rule ducked_told at soke_landing when ducked(pentrice) and watch(clock) > cameRound(pentrice)
    says "The Arle took you at the lip of the weir and rolled you over twice and put you down, a long way off, among the piles of the Soke landing, where a waterman fished you out with a boat-hook for a penny and charges you two. Somebody has been through your purse." { Retract ducked(pentrice). }
}

data/adventures/gosses-company/company.k:
Module pentrice "Gosse's Company" {
  // The city played alone, from the road in: one traveller come down the West Road with a little coin, who never met
  // the players on the green (placed.kyr is the world's own company, and what the green told of it).
  Company party "You" of 1 at road_end.
  Initially Set quantity(party, gold) to 14. Initially Set quantity(party, rations) to 2.
  Entity word: fact "What is said of Pentrice in the country below.".
  Entity joined: fact "You have taken service with Gosse's Company for the season.".
  Entity freed: fact "You got the players' wagon off the chain, in a town on the west road.".
  Entity seen_show: fact "You have seen Gosse's Company play, in a town on the west road.".
  Entity lem_kept: fact "Lem Coyle, the players' chain-man, was paid what he was owed, and has gone to see the Trial.".
}

data/adventures/gosses-company/history.k:
Module pentrice "Gosse's Company" {
  // ── What the city remembers, and what it has forgotten ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The riot is told everywhere as a joke, by Gosse as a triumph and by the Master as a wound. What it cost is cut on
  // a brass plate by the minster's west door, and in the Office's own Ordinances, and nobody reads either: on the
  // second night of the singing a lamplighter fell from his ladder in the Chepe with the fool's song in his mouth, and
  // Ezra Orde made the Office the week after, for the widow's sake, not his own. The Office's chief clerk is the
  // lamplighter's son. Found, this turns the comedy over: the play is a daughter's love letter, and the Office a
  // grieving man's epitaph, and the joke was funny, and a man died of it.

  // The plate.
  Observe minster_plate at nave when true "Low on the wall by the west door, where nobody important is buried, there is a small brass plate, gone brown, which somebody still polishes: ABEL TUNSTALL, LAMPLIGHTER OF THE CHEPE, WHO FELL FROM HIS LADDER ON THE SECOND NIGHT OF THE SINGING. HE LIT THE LAMPS. Under it, cut smaller and later, by a different hand, are two lines of what is plainly a comic song: A MAN WHO WEIGHS HIS GOLD AND WIFE THE SAME / WILL FIND THEM BOTH TOO LIGHT, AND HIMSELF TO BLAME." teaches plate_read.
  Discovery plate_read "In the minster, a brass plate remembers Abel Tunstall, lamplighter of the Chepe, who fell from his ladder on the second night of the singing, forty years ago; under it is cut a couplet of the fool's song from the riot.".
  // In the evening, someone lights the Chepe's lamps as if he were being watched.
  Observe chepe_lamps at chepe when hour(clock) >= 18 and hour(clock) < 20 "A boy with a pole and a little ladder goes along the Chepe lighting the lamps, one by one, very carefully, as if somebody were watching to see that he did it right. The Chepe's lamps are lit before any others in the City: it is in the Ordinances.".

  // The son.
  Relation gosseKnowsFall(group).
  Topic tunstall_father with tunstall "Ask Tunstall about the lamplighter's plate in the minster" when knows(actor, plate_read) and not knows(actor, lamplighter_known) once {
    Says "Tunstall does not answer at once. He squares the ledger on the desk, and squares it again. 'My father,' he says. 'I was nine. They came up the Chepe singing it, a thousand of them, and somebody shook his ladder for the joke, and he came down on the cobbles with the pole in his hand and the lamp still lit.' He opens the ledger and does not look at it. 'Lord Mayor Orde came to our house the next morning and sat on our stool, which was too small for him, and asked my mother what she needed. She said she needed it not to happen again. So he made an Office.' A pause. 'He wrote the Eighth Ordinance himself, so that the stonecutter might put on the plate what my father was singing when he fell. It is the only line in Pentrice the Office may not strike. I took the Office's shilling at twelve. It has been very good to me.' He picks up his ruler. 'Next,' he says, though there is nobody there.".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, lamplighter_known). }
  }
  Discovery lamplighter_known "On the second night of the riot a lamplighter, Abel Tunstall's father, fell from his ladder when the crowd came up the Chepe singing Gosse's joke. Ezra Orde founded the Office of Plain Speech for the widow's sake, wrote the Eighth Ordinance so that the dead man's song could be cut on his plate, and took the boy into the Office.".
  Topic gosse_fall with gosse "Tell Gosse about the lamplighter who fell on the second night of the singing" when knows(actor, lamplighter_known) and not gosseKnowsFall(gosse) and not pensionTaken(gosse) once {
    Says "Gosse hears all of it standing up, and then sits down on the nearest thing, which is a hamper, and is quiet for longer than you have ever known him quiet. 'I went out of the Westgate on the first night,' he says at last, 'with a bag and the Fool's cap, laughing, and walked to Arle Bridge, and did not come back. I heard they had made an Office. I was proud of it.' He turns his hands over and looks at them, as if they were somebody else's. 'Forty years I have told that story in taprooms. I made an Office. How many players can say that.' He gets up. 'The clerk with the ruler. Tunstall.' He nods, slowly. 'He will be on the bench.'".
    On discuss { Assert gosseKnowsFall(gosse). }
  }
  // The morning after: two old men at a brass plate.
  Rule fate_plate when verdictRead(pentrice) and gosseKnowsFall(gosse) and not fateTold(fate_plate_known) and inCity()
    says "On the morning after the verdict Absalom Gosse goes to the minster, and stands a long time in front of the small brass plate by the west door, with his hat in his hands; and Abel Tunstall, who comes every week to polish it, finds him there. They do not say anything. After a while they polish it together." { Assert fateTold(fate_plate_known). }
  Discovery fate_plate_known "Gosse and Tunstall at the lamplighter's plate.".

  // ── Urania Orde, the widow ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Ezra Orde's widow keeps his chair, his custom of the Bench's supper, and his jokes. She is the Widow Gudgeon of the
  // play, and knows it, and knows who wrote it.
  Person urania "Urania Orde" at orde_parlour {
    Role "the late Lord Mayor's widow, the Master's mother". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner cheerful.
    Greets "A small upright old woman in lavender, with very bright eyes, is sitting in a chair that is plainly not hers: a big chair with the arms worn pale by somebody else's hands. 'You're not the coal,' she says. 'Sit down anyway.'".
  }
  Relation guest(group). Relation servant(group).
  Topic urania_ezra with urania "Ask Mistress Orde about her husband" when true once {
    Says "'Ezra?' She laughs, a laugh like a tray of cups going over. 'He was ridiculous. Everybody said so, except to his face. He paved the Chepe badly and was proud of it; he made speeches about drains. He proposed to me on that hearth-rug, there, on his knees, with crumbs on them, and I said no the first time, because of the crumbs.' She looks at the rug. 'He went to the Wheel every Trial and sat in the gallery and laughed louder than anybody. The night the fool said it, he laughed too. He sang it all the way home with Clemency asleep on his shoulder.' She stops laughing. 'Then on the second night a lamplighter fell off his ladder in the Chepe, singing it. Ezra never laughed in a theatre again. He made the Office the week after, and took the man's boy into it. People think it was his pride. It wasn't his pride. It was his conscience, which is much worse to live with, and much worse to be married to.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, ezra_known). Assert knows(actor, lamplighter_known). }
  }
  Discovery ezra_known "Ezra Orde, the Lord Mayor of the riot, was ridiculous and loved, laughed at the fool's joke himself, and proposed to his wife on the hearth-rug of the Orde parlour with crumbs on his knees.".
  Topic urania_daughter with urania "Ask Mistress Orde about her daughter" when true once {
    Says "'Clemency.' She looks at the mantel, where a child's crayon drawing hangs in a good frame: a man in a fool's cap with his mouth very wide. 'She keeps her father's Office, harder than he did. She was the funniest child in Pentrice, and she drew; she drew that the night of the riot, and I framed it to annoy her. She hasn't laughed since she was nine, that I have heard.' She smiles. 'She writes at night. She thinks I think it's letters.'".
  }
  Topic urania_supper with urania "Ask Mistress Orde about the Bench's supper" when not guest(actor) and not verdictRead(pentrice) once {
    Says "'After the last night of the Trial the Bench sups here,' she says. 'It always has. It was Ezra's custom, and I keep it to annoy them: nobody votes till they've eaten, and nobody eats till they've said one true thing about the play.' She looks at you with her bright eyes. 'Come. You look as if you could say a true thing, if you were frightened enough. It will do them good.'".
    On discuss { Assert guest(actor). }
  }
  // Sukey, who keeps the doors.
  Topic sukey_house with sukey "Ask Sukey about the house she serves" when true once {
    Says "'The old mistress and the young one,' says Sukey. 'The old mistress laughs at everything and the young one at nothing, and I keep the doors between them.' She considers. 'The old mistress makes a pie. On the last night of the Trial she makes it for the Bench, and they argue over it till one in the morning, and then they go and vote however they were going to anyway.'".
  }

  // ── Under the Wheel: the oldest stage in Pentrice ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The Wheel stands on the ring of an Aenean theatre whose stone seats run on under the yard. At the back of the
  // cellarage the top step of it shows, with letters on it: the rule of the old stage, from which the Liberty of the
  // Soke descends, though the Liberty has forgotten.
  Observe stage_stone at under_stage when true "At the back of the cellarage, set into the earth floor and older than every timber over it, a curved block of white stone shows, with letters cut along its edge, worn shallow: the top step of a much older theatre, whose seats go on down into the dark under the yard.".
  Discovery stone_read "Cut on the Aenean step under the Wheel's stage: WHO SPEAKS HERE IN THE MASK IS NOT ANSWERED FOR. The liberty of the Soke is a rule of the old stage, older than the City and its Book.".
  Relation triedStone(group).
  Action read_stone(actor: group, site: place) "Puzzle out the letters on the old stone step" {
    Time 3.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, under_stage) and not knows(actor, stone_read) and not triedStone(actor).
    Resolve check(actor, lore, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, stone_read). }
    On failure { Assert triedStone(actor). }
    Result "On your knees in the dirt with a candle, letter by letter. The Aenean is plain once you have the first word: WHO SPEAKS HERE IN THE MASK IS NOT ANSWERED FOR. You sit back on your heels. Over your head the boards creak where somebody crosses the stage, and you think of every company that ever stood up there, back and back, and of the Liberty of the Soke, which says much the same thing in worse Common, and has forgotten where it learned it.".
    Otherwise "Old letters, a word that might be MASK or might be MOUTH, and the candle guttering; the sense of it will not come.".
  }
  Topic wilmot_stone with wilmot "Ask Old Wilmot about the stone under the stage" when true once {
    Says "'Older than the Wheel,' says Wilmot. 'Older than the Soke. There's seats under the yard, rows of them, white, going down. They found them when they dug the drain in my grandfather's time and filled them in again quick, because of the faces cut in them.' He sucks his teeth. 'My grandfather said the writing was a curse. My father said it was a price list. Nobody's read it in my time.'".
  }

  // ── The third night: Gosse alone in the empty Wheel ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // After the Children have gone, the night before his own, Gosse goes over the river by himself to say his Prologue to
  // the empty house, and dries, alone, where nobody can see.
  Rule gosse_rehearses_alone when tday(pentrice) == 3 and hour(clock) >= 22 and hour(clock) < 23 and at(gosse, moon_taproom) and not pensionTaken(gosse) and not wentAlone(gosse) {
    Assert wentAlone(gosse). Retract at(gosse, moon_taproom). Assert at(gosse, wheel). }
  Rule gosse_back_alone when at(gosse, wheel) and wentAlone(gosse) and not crossed(pentrice) and (hour(clock) >= 23 or hour(clock) < 22) {
    Retract at(gosse, wheel). Assert at(gosse, moon_loft). }
  Relation wentAlone(group).
  Observe gosse_alone at wheel when at(gosse, wheel) and wentAlone(gosse) and not crossed(pentrice) "In the empty Wheel one lantern is burning on the edge of the stage, and Absalom Gosse is standing beside it in his shirtsleeves, saying the Prologue to the empty yard and the empty galleries. He gets as far as the last couplet, and stops, and goes back to the beginning, and stops again in the same place.".
  Topic gosse_alone_talk with gosse "Ask Gosse what he is doing here" when wentAlone(gosse) and at(gosse, wheel) and not crossed(pentrice) once {
    Says "Gosse does not hear you come, and does not jump when he sees you; he laughs, a little too loud. 'Learning my lines,' he says. 'Forty-one years, and learning my lines.' He sits down on the edge of the stage with his legs over the yard. 'A player dies twice, you know. Once when he forgets the words, and once later, which matters less.' He looks at the lantern. 'I cannot hear the left side. Did Hepzibah tell you? Of course she did. She thinks I don't know she knows.' He gets up. 'Don't tell her I was here. Tomorrow I shall be magnificent.' And he blows out the lantern, and you both stand in the dark of the Wheel until your eyes come round.".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, gosse_afraid). }
  }
  Discovery gosse_afraid "The night before his own, Gosse went alone to the empty Wheel to say his Prologue, and dried on the last couplet, and asked that nobody be told.".

  // ── The company, a little more of each ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Topic hepz_acted with hepzibah "Ask Hepzibah whether she ever acted" when true once {
    Says "'Once.' She keeps her eyes on the book. 'In a barn at Galt, in the winter of the hard frost, as the Second Witch, because the Second Witch had the measles. I dried on my first line, and Absalom gave it me from the wings, and I said it, and the barn laughed, because it was a line about a cat.' She turns a page. 'That was the night he decided I should hold the book. He was always better at the giving than the taking.'".
  }
  Topic pudding_clown with pudding "Ask Pudding what a clown is for" when true once {
    Says "'A clown,' says Pudding, 'is a man who falls down so you don't have to.' He juggles two onions, badly, on purpose. 'Every time I fall down on a stage, somebody in the yard who was going to fall down that week doesn't.' He catches the onions. 'It isn't true. It's what I tell myself, on the stairs, before.'".
  }
  Topic swale_mother with swale "Ask Swale about his mother" when reconciled(swale) once {
    Says "'She played the Nurse,' says Swale. 'Forty years, in companies that never once let her play anything else, and she laughed at all of them, and at me, and at the Nurse.' He is quiet. 'I thought it was a weakness in her. I thought a great deal of things in her were weaknesses that I find, now, I should like to have.'".
  }
  Topic kit_after with kit "Ask Kit what he will do when his voice goes" when true once {
    Says "Kit thinks about it, honestly. 'Fall down, probably,' he says, with a glance at Pudding. 'Or carry hampers. Or Tapwell, if there's a Tapwell going.' His voice goes up and comes down on the last word, and he does not even go red this time. 'Gosse says a voice is just the part of you the yard can hear. He says the rest of you goes on.'".
  }

  // ── Small things seen early, that the week will explain ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe office_laugh at office_hall when tday(pentrice) <= 2 and not knows(party, riot_clemency) "At the end desk two clerks are disputing in whispers whether anybody has ever heard the Master laugh. The elder says once, at the Wheel, when she was four, and that it was the last time anybody in Pentrice laughed without paying for it; the younger says that is a story, and gets on with his ruling.".
  Observe stairs_wardens at water_stairs when tday(pentrice) <= 3 and not watermenStrike(pentrice) "An old waterman at the top of the steps tells nobody in particular that the bridge wardens have been at Mr Fallow's house twice this week, and that a man who owns a bridge has no business being kind to a man who owns a boat.".
  Observe wall_names at tiring_house when true "The names nearest the door are the newest. Further in they go back by companies: THE CHILDREN OF THE CLOSE, a whole choir of them in round child's capitals; DOLL LACY, with a little wave cut under it, for the year the Arle came into the yard; the Lord Warden's Men, the Prince of Sarre's Men, Tobias Wake who wrote The Wolf King and played the wolf; and below them, older than the plaster, names in a letter nobody reads any more, scratched into the timber the plaster was put on. A little below A. GOSSE someone has cut, very small and very neatly, a lamp on a pole.".

  Milestone ms_fall "learned what the singing cost, and told Gosse" worth 200 when gosseKnowsFall(gosse).
  Milestone ms_stone "read the oldest rule in Pentrice" worth 100 when knows(party, stone_read).
}

data/adventures/gosses-company/night.kyr:
Module pentrice "Gosse's Company" {
  // ── The last night of the Trial: The Alderman's Ghost, or, Who Walks First ──────────────────────────────────────
  // At six on the fourth day the company goes over to the Wheel; at half past six the half is called and the company
  // takes its posts; at seven the play begins, and runs in nine scenes of twenty minutes (with Dido's lament before
  // them, if the company agreed to it). Each scene reads what the week made of the play, and offers the company, at
  // its post, what that made possible. Every telling is anchored at the Wheel: the play goes on whether or not anyone
  // is there to see it.
  Measure scene(place). Measure sceneAt(place). Measure temper(place). Measure fines(place). Measure crowd(place).
  Relation ghostOn(place). Relation ghostPlay(place). Relation galtPlay(place). Relation playEnded(place). Relation fromMemory(place).
  Kind post. Entity post_wing: post "the right-hand wing". Entity post_under: post "under the stage". Entity post_bench: post "the grey bench".
  Entity post_yard: post "the yard".
  Relation stand(group, post) exclusive.
  Query liberty() means ghostPlay(pentrice) and not state(book, copy_licensed) and not state(book, copy_warranted).
  Query bookCut() means ghostPlay(pentrice) and state(book, copy_licensed) and not ghostRestored(pentrice).
  Query linesClean() means linesCut(swale) or bookCut().
  Query sceneDone() means watch(clock) >= sceneAt(pentrice) + 2.
  // Halfway through a scene: what happens in it, seen once it has begun.
  Query midScene() means watch(clock) >= sceneAt(pentrice) + 1.
  Query inWing(a: group) means at(a, wheel) and stand(a, post_wing).
  Query underStage(a: group) means at(a, wheel) and stand(a, post_under).
  Query onBench(a: group) means at(a, wheel) and stand(a, post_bench).
  Query inYard(a: group) means at(a, wheel) and stand(a, post_yard).

  // ── Before: the company crosses at six; the half at half past ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Relation crossed(place). Relation halfCalled(place).
  Measure crossedAt(place).
  Rule company_crosses when tday(pentrice) == 4 and hour(clock) >= 18 and not crossed(pentrice) and not pensionTaken(gosse) {
    Assert crossed(pentrice). Assert playingTonight(pentrice). Set crossedAt(pentrice) to watch(clock). }
  Rule troupe_crosses when crossed(pentrice) and troupe(?p) and at(?p, ?q) and not at(?p, tiring_house) and not playEnded(pentrice) {
    Retract at(?p, ?q). Assert at(?p, tiring_house). }
  Rule bear_crosses when crossed(pentrice) and at(the_bear, moon_yard) and not playEnded(pentrice) { Retract at(the_bear, moon_yard). Assert at(the_bear, tiring_house). }
  Rule ned_crosses when crossed(pentrice) and atMoon(ned) and at(ned, ?q) and not at(ned, tiring_house) and not playEnded(pentrice) { Retract at(ned, ?q). Assert at(ned, tiring_house). }
  Rule meg_crosses when crossed(pentrice) and megCast(meg) and at(meg, gullet) { Retract at(meg, gullet). Assert at(meg, tiring_house). }
  // How full the yard is: the watermen, the weir, the bills, the bells.
  Rule house_counted when crossed(pentrice) and watch(clock) >= crossedAt(pentrice) + 3 and not halfCalled(pentrice) {
    Assert halfCalled(pentrice). Set crowd(pentrice) to 3. Set temper(pentrice) to 2. }
  Rule house_thin when halfCalled(pentrice) and watermenStrike(pentrice) and not crowdLed(pentrice) and crowd(pentrice) == 3 and not houseSet(pentrice) {
    Set crowd(pentrice) to 1. Decrease temper(pentrice) by 2. }
  Rule house_weir when halfCalled(pentrice) and watermenStrike(pentrice) and crowdLed(pentrice) and crowd(pentrice) == 3 and not houseSet(pentrice) {
    Set crowd(pentrice) to 2. Increase temper(pentrice) by 1. }
  Rule house_bills when halfCalled(pentrice) and (playbills(inchbald) or quartoPrinted(pentrice)) and not houseSet(pentrice) { Increase crowd(pentrice) by 1. Increase temper(pentrice) by 1. }
  Rule house_bells when halfCalled(pentrice) and pealRung(bunces) and not houseSet(pentrice) { Increase temper(pentrice) by 1. }
  Rule house_set when halfCalled(pentrice) and not houseSet(pentrice) { Assert houseSet(pentrice). }
  Relation houseSet(place).

  Observe wheel_full at wheel when halfCalled(pentrice) and not playEnded(pentrice) and crowd(pentrice) >= 3 "The Wheel is full. The yard is packed to the stage's edge, fishwives and prentices and clerks and watermen with their red caps, and the three galleries above are packed to the rails, and still people are coming in at the gate and being pushed back. Somebody is selling oranges. Somebody is selling beer. On the grey bench in front of the stage the Office sits in a row with its sticks across its knees, and in the middle of them, very upright, the Master of Plain Speech.".
  Observe wheel_thin at wheel when halfCalled(pentrice) and not playEnded(pentrice) and crowd(pentrice) <= 1 "The Wheel is a third full: the Soke's own people, a few who came over early, a row of watermen in red caps who have come to see what they struck against. The galleries are mostly empty. On the grey bench in front of the stage the Office sits in a row with its sticks across its knees, and in the middle of them, very upright, the Master of Plain Speech.".
  Observe wheel_wet at wheel when halfCalled(pentrice) and not playEnded(pentrice) and crowd(pentrice) == 2 "The yard of the Wheel is full of people wet to the knee, laughing, wringing out their skirts, who came over the weir in a chain; the galleries are half full. On the grey bench in front of the stage the Office sits with its sticks across its knees, and in the middle of them, very upright, the Master of Plain Speech.".
  Observe wheel_lem at wheel when halfCalled(pentrice) and not playEnded(pentrice) and knows(party, lem_kept) "Against the edge of the stage, in the front of the yard, in a clean shirt, is Lem Coyle, who led the bear on the green: he has walked all the way to see the Trial, as he said, and he has an orange for Patience.".
  Rule half_called at wheel when halfCalled(pentrice) and not spread(half_known)
    says "Hepzibah's voice, from the tiring-house door, not loud, carrying everywhere: 'The half, ladies and gentlemen. The half.' Behind the stage everybody stops what they are doing for one breath, and then goes on doing it faster." { Assert spread(half_known). }
  Discovery half_known "The half has been called at the Wheel: the play begins at seven.".
  Rule half_shirts at wheel when halfCalled(pentrice) and costumesTaken(pentrice) and at(party, wheel) and not spread(shirts_known)
    says "With the costumes in the bailiff's cart, Gosse's Company plays in its shirts, as Gosse promised: the Widow in a tablecloth, the Ghost in a bedsheet with a chain made of curtain-rings, Pomfret in his own coat turned inside out. The yard thinks it is part of the joke, and by the second scene it is." { Assert spread(shirts_known). }
  Discovery shirts_known "Gosse's Company played its night at the Wheel in its shirts.".

  Action post_wing(actor: group, site: place) "Take your place in the right-hand wing, by the prompt-copy of the scenes" {
    Time 1 minute.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, wheel) and inCompany(actor) and crossed(pentrice) and not playEnded(pentrice)
      and not stand(actor, post_wing).
    On success { Assert stand(actor, post_wing). }
    Result "You go up the two steps behind the right-hand door and stand in the wing, where you can see the whole stage edge-on and a slice of the yard beyond it, and Gosse's good side.".
  }
  Action post_under(actor: group, site: place) "Go down under the stage, to the trap, the pump and the lever" {
    Time 1 minute.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, wheel) and inCompany(actor) and crossed(pentrice) and not playEnded(pentrice)
      and not stand(actor, post_under).
    On success { Assert stand(actor, post_under). }
    Result "Down the ladder into the dark under the stage, where the light comes through the boards in stripes and you can hear every footstep overhead as if it were on your own head. The trap is above you, and the pump, and the tank, and the lever.".
  }
  Action post_bench(actor: group, site: place) "Take your place on the grey bench with the tallymen" {
    Time 1 minute.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, wheel) and tallyman(actor) and crossed(pentrice) and not playEnded(pentrice)
      and not stand(actor, post_bench).
    On success { Assert stand(actor, post_bench). }
    Result "You sit down on the grey bench in front of the stage with your stick across your knees, four places from the Master, who does not look at you. The stage is at the level of your eyes. You can see the players' feet.".
  }
  Action post_yard(actor: group, site: place) "Find a place in the yard among the groundlings" {
    Time 1 minute.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, wheel) and crossed(pentrice) and not playEnded(pentrice) and not stand(actor, post_yard).
    On success { Assert stand(actor, post_yard). }
    Result "You push into the yard among the fishwives and the prentices, right up against the stage's edge, where an orange-seller treads on your foot and apologises and treads on it again.".
  }
  // What was ready under the stage before the half: the trap freed, the pump and tank mended.
  Relation trapFree(place). Relation pumpMended(place). Relation lanternRigged(place).
  Thing stage_trap "the stage trap" at under_stage {
    State stuck "The trap's counterweighted platform is jammed: the lever will not move, and something grinds when you lean on it.".
    State free "The trap's platform rides up and down sweetly on its counterweight when the lever is pulled.".
    Change free_trap "Clear the grit out of the trap's runners and free the lever" from stuck to free needing mending.
  }
  Initially Assert state(stage_trap, stuck).
  Rule trap_freed when state(stage_trap, free) and not trapFree(pentrice) { Assert trapFree(pentrice). }
  Action force_trap(actor: group, site: place) "Hang your weight on the trap's lever until it gives" {
    Time 2.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, under_stage) and state(stage_trap, stuck) and not triedTrap(actor).
    Resolve check(actor, brawn, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert state(stage_trap, free). }
    On failure { Assert triedTrap(actor). }
    Result "You hang on it, and bounce, and it gives all at once with a crack, and the platform shoots up and bangs into the stage above and down again, and somewhere overhead a pigeon goes up out of the heavens in alarm. It runs sweetly after that.".
    Otherwise "It does not give.".
  }
  Relation triedTrap(group).
  Thing pump "the fountain pump" at under_stage {
    State leaking "The lead tank is split along one seam, and the pump's leather is perished: the Fountain in the third act will not run.".
    State sound "The tank is patched and the pump newly leathered, and when you try it a jet goes up through the pipe in the boards.".
    Change mend_pump "Patch the tank's seam and put a new leather in the pump" from leaking to sound needing mending.
  }
  Initially Assert state(pump, leaking).
  Rule pump_mended when state(pump, sound) and not pumpMended(pentrice) { Assert pumpMended(pentrice). }
  Topic tam_fountain with tam "Ask Tam about the fountain in the third act" when bookCome(pentrice) once {
    Says "'There's a pump under the Wheel's stage,' says Tam, 'and a lead tank, and a pipe up through the boards, for fountains and such. Put in for a masque two hundred years back.' He planes. 'The tank's split and the leather's gone. And the trap's jammed with two hundred years of grit. Somebody who can mend could have both going in an afternoon.' He looks at you. 'Not me. I'm all thumbs below stairs. I'm afraid of the dark.'".
  }
  Action rig_lantern(actor: group, site: place) "Climb into the heavens over the Wheel's stage and rig a lantern and a mirror to light the Ghost's rising" {
    Time 3.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, wheel) and not playingTonight(pentrice) and not lanternRigged(pentrice) and not triedRig(actor)
      and bookCome(pentrice).
    Resolve check(actor, climbing, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert lanternRigged(pentrice). }
    On failure { Assert triedRig(actor). }
    Result "Up the post at the back of the stage to the painted heavens, and along a beam with the yard thirty feet below, and you hang a dark-lantern and a shaving-mirror on a nail so that, opened, it will throw a white light straight down onto the trap. From up here the Wheel is a great wooden bowl, empty, waiting.".
    Otherwise "The post is greasy, and you get as far as the balcony and no further.".
  }
  Relation triedRig(group).

  // ── The curtain ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // What is played: The Alderman's Ghost, if there is a book, or if the company has rehearsed every act and can play it
  // without; otherwise The Wolf King, the old repertory, to whoever came.
  Rule curtain_ghost when halfCalled(pentrice) and houseSet(pentrice) and tday(pentrice) == 4 and hour(clock) >= 19 and not ghostOn(pentrice) and not galtPlay(pentrice)
    and not playEnded(pentrice) and (state(book, copy_fair) or state(book, copy_struck) or state(book, copy_licensed) or state(book, copy_warranted)) {
    Assert ghostOn(pentrice). Assert ghostPlay(pentrice). Set sceneAt(pentrice) to watch(clock). }
  Rule curtain_memory when halfCalled(pentrice) and houseSet(pentrice) and tday(pentrice) == 4 and hour(clock) >= 19 and not ghostOn(pentrice) and not galtPlay(pentrice)
    and not playEnded(pentrice) and (state(book, copy_seized) or state(book, copy_burned)) and rehearsedI(pentrice) and rehearsedII(pentrice) and rehearsedIII(pentrice) {
    Assert ghostOn(pentrice). Assert ghostPlay(pentrice). Assert fromMemory(pentrice). Set sceneAt(pentrice) to watch(clock). }
  Rule curtain_galt when halfCalled(pentrice) and houseSet(pentrice) and tday(pentrice) == 4 and hour(clock) >= 19 and not ghostOn(pentrice) and not galtPlay(pentrice)
    and not playEnded(pentrice) {
    Assert galtPlay(pentrice). Set sceneAt(pentrice) to watch(clock). }
  Rule curtain_scene when ghostOn(pentrice) and scene(pentrice) == 0 and not raiserDone(pentrice) and not curtainRaiser(gosse) { Set scene(pentrice) to 1. }
  Relation raiserDone(place).
  // Who plays the Ghost, if Swale has left: whoever said they would, or Gosse, doubling.
  Rule ghost_to_gosse when ghostOn(pentrice) and swaleGone(swale) and not plays(party, part_ghost) and not plays(gosse, part_ghost) { Assert plays(gosse, part_ghost). }

  // The Wolf King: the old repertory, a play the Bench has seen and the yard has not asked for.
  Rule galt_played at wheel when galtPlay(pentrice) and watch(clock) >= sceneAt(pentrice) + 1 and not playEnded(pentrice)
    says "With no book, Gosse's Company plays The Wolf King, which it has played four hundred times on greens and in barns: Gosse as the old king, Pudding as his gravedigger, and whoever is left of the company as everyone else, doubling furiously. It is very well done. The yard is polite. In the lords' room Ormsby Clay nods at the verse; Dame Gammage eats nuts; the Canon is satisfied; Nym Carrow writes nothing at all. When it is over the house claps as a house claps for a thing it has seen before, and goes home over the river talking of something else." {
    Assert playEnded(pentrice). Set endedAt(pentrice) to watch(clock). Retract playingTonight(pentrice). Increase regard(clay) by 2. Increase regard(mallory) by 2. Increase temper(pentrice) by 1. }

  // ── Before the play: Dido ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Rule dido_lament at wheel when ghostOn(pentrice) and curtainRaiser(gosse) and not raiserDone(pentrice) and sceneDone() and not swaleGone(swale)
    says "Before the play, Ambrose Swale comes out alone onto the bare stage in a black cloak, and the yard, which was expecting a ghost, quiets uncertainly, and he gives them the lament from Ormsby Clay's Dido, the old Aenean queen who was left on her shore, thirty lines in the old measure, as if every one were carved: 'Let no one sing of me; let no one say / she burned because a ship went out of the bay...' It is very beautiful and very long. Halfway through, a fishwife throws a nut. In the lords' room Ormsby Clay sits absolutely still with his hand over his eyes." {
    Assert raiserDone(pentrice). Increase regard(clay) by 2. Increase slight(gammage) by 1. Decrease temper(pentrice) by 1. Set scene(pentrice) to 1.
    Set sceneAt(pentrice) to watch(clock). }
  // Without Swale there is nobody to give it, and the play begins without it.
  Rule dido_dropped when ghostOn(pentrice) and curtainRaiser(gosse) and not raiserDone(pentrice) and swaleGone(swale) {
