    says "Patience will not go on. She sits in the wing in her bonnet with her back to the stage and declines, with great dignity, to be anybody's bear tonight; and the Keeper goes on without her, on all fours, in a hearthrug, being the bear himself, and is very funny, and is not a bear." {
    Increase temper(pentrice) by 1. Increase regard(gammage) by 1. }
  Rule s8_no_bear at wheel when ghostOn(pentrice) and scene(pentrice) == 8 and sceneDone() and not at(the_bear, tiring_house) and not sceneOver(scene_eight)
    says "There is no bear. The Keeper comes on as the bear in a hearthrug, and is very funny; but the playbills promised a bear, and in the yard somebody says so, loudly, and somebody else says Bowle has her, over the way, and the laugh goes thin." {
    Increase slight(gammage) by 1. }
  Rule s8_no_bear_bills when ghostOn(pentrice) and scene(pentrice) == 8 and sceneDone() and not at(the_bear, tiring_house) and playbills(inchbald) and not sceneOver(scene_eight) { Decrease temper(pentrice) by 1. }
  // Played from memory there is no book to send for, and the Office has no business in the wing.
  Rule s8_memory when ghostOn(pentrice) and scene(pentrice) == 8 and fromMemory(pentrice) and not hepzibahKept(pentrice) { Assert hepzibahKept(pentrice). }
  Rule s8_taken at wheel when ghostOn(pentrice) and scene(pentrice) == 8 and sceneDone() and not hepzibahKept(pentrice) and not state(book, copy_warranted) and not sceneOver(scene_eight)
    says "Behind it all, in the left-hand wing, the Office has its way: Hepzibah Dimmock goes round to the grey bench with the book in her arms and the Office's men on either side of her, and sits down on the end of the bench, and the left-hand wing is empty." {
    Assert hepzibahTaken(pentrice). }
  Rule s8_warranted when ghostOn(pentrice) and scene(pentrice) == 8 and sceneDone() and state(book, copy_warranted) and not sceneOver(scene_eight) { Assert hepzibahKept(pentrice). }
  Rule s8_fined when ghostOn(pentrice) and scene(pentrice) == 8 and sceneDone() and liberty() and not sceneOver(scene_eight) { Increase fines(pentrice) by 3. }
  Rule s8_close when ghostOn(pentrice) and scene(pentrice) == 8 and sceneDone() and not sceneOver(scene_eight) {
    Assert sceneOver(scene_eight). Set scene(pentrice) to 9. Set sceneAt(pentrice) to watch(clock). }

  // ── III.9 Who walks first; the epilogue ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Relation proposed(group). Relation emptyWing(group). Relation clemBowed(group).
  Rule s9_open at wheel when ghostOn(pentrice) and scene(pentrice) == 9 and not sceneBegun(scene_nine)
    says "The grave at last: the trap, with a painted headstone behind it, and the whole town come to see the Alderman buried a second time, in procession, by the Book. CHAMBERLAIN: By the Book. MASTER OF THE WEIGHTS: Page forty. They line up, and argue, and the Ghost stands at the edge of his grave and will not go down. GHOST: Not till it's said. MAYOR: What is he waiting for? WIDOW: The truth, I expect. He always was. Nobody says it. The Council looks at its feet. Then Lob, carrying the chain, trips over the Book of Precedence where it lies open on the stage, and goes down full length, and says from the floor, without meaning to: LOB: Oh, we all laughed at him! All of us! All his life! We loved him! A long silence. The Ghost turns round. GHOST: ...Did you. LOB: Yes, master. GHOST (taking off his chain, and putting it round Lob's neck): Then I'll go first." { Assert sceneBegun(scene_nine). }
  Observe s9_text at wheel when midScene() and ghostOn(pentrice) and scene(pentrice) == 9 "And the Ghost walks first, and the whole town after him in no order at all, the Mayor behind the Cousin and the Weights behind the bear; and at the graveside the Widow turns to Sir Rowley Pomfret and says, 'You may kneel,' and he kneels, on a clean rug, at last; and the Mayor marries Bell and Tapwell in one line, because the scene is nearly over.".
  Observe s9_master at wheel when midScene() and ghostOn(pentrice) and scene(pentrice) == 9 and knows(party, author_known) and clemTrust(clemency) >= 2 and not clemCold(clemency) and not clemBowed(clemency) "On the grey bench, in front of the stage, the Master of Plain Speech is sitting very straight with her hands in her lap, the inky finger and the clean, watching the Ghost of her father walk first to his grave. She is looking, now, at you.".
  Action nod_master(actor: group, site: place) "Look at the Master on the grey bench, and nod" {
    Time 0.
    Requires midScene() and able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, wheel) and ghostOn(pentrice) and scene(pentrice) == 9 and knows(actor, author_known)
      and clemTrust(clemency) >= 2 and not clemCold(clemency) and not clemBowed(clemency).
    On success { Assert clemBowed(clemency). }
    Result "You nod. For a long moment nothing happens. Then Clemency Orde, Master of Plain Speech, gets up off the grey bench, and climbs the two steps at the side of the stage of the Wheel, in front of the City, and walks out into the procession behind the Ghost of Alderman Gudgeon, and takes her place at the end of it, last, in her grey, with ink on her finger.".
  }
  Rule s9_walk at wheel when ghostOn(pentrice) and scene(pentrice) == 9 and sceneDone() and rehearsedIII(pentrice) and not sceneOver(scene_nine)
    says "The procession goes round the stage of the Wheel to a slow drum, every one of them in their place, the Ghost at the head of it and Lob at his heel, and it is ridiculous, and it is beautiful, and the Canon in the lords' room is mouthing the moral." {
    Increase temper(pentrice) by 1. Increase regard(mallory) by 1. Increase regard(clay) by 1. }
  Rule s9_shuffle at wheel when ghostOn(pentrice) and scene(pentrice) == 9 and sceneDone() and not rehearsedIII(pentrice) and not sceneOver(scene_nine)
    says "The procession is not rehearsed and goes round the stage the wrong way twice, and the Ghost walks first because he is the only one who knows where to go." {
    Increase regard(mallory) by 1. }
  Rule s9_bow at wheel when ghostOn(pentrice) and scene(pentrice) == 9 and sceneDone() and clemBowed(clemency) and not sceneOver(scene_nine)
    says "At the end of it, when the Ghost has gone down into his grave on the trap and the procession has turned to the house, Gosse looks along the line and sees who is standing at the end of it. He goes and takes her hand, and brings her down to the front of the stage, and says to the Wheel, not loud, so that the whole house leans in to hear it: 'Gentles: the author.' Clemency Orde says, quite clearly, so that the top gallery hears it: 'I wrote it. It is my father. He would have laughed.' And then she laughs, out loud, in front of the City, for the first time anyone in Pentrice can remember. On the grey bench the tallymen look at each other, and then one by one, starting with Abel Tunstall, they break their sticks across their knees." {
    Increase temper(pentrice) by 3. Increase regard(callow) by 2. Increase regard(mallory) by 1. Increase regard(clay) by 1. Set fines(pentrice) to 0. }
  Rule s9_propose at wheel when ghostOn(pentrice) and scene(pentrice) == 9 and sceneDone() and gosseMeans(gosse) and not hepzibahTaken(pentrice) and not sceneOver(scene_nine)
    says "Then the epilogue. Gosse, as Pomfret, comes down to the edge of the stage: 'So ends our town, sirs, which was never yours; / so ends our Alderman, who went through doors / the Book had shut, and first, as dead men may. / A comedy should end in marriage: so—' and then he stops, and turns away from the house, all the way round, to the left-hand wing, where a small grey woman is standing with a book in her hands and a pencil in her hair. 'Hepzibah,' he says, 'thirty-four years. Will you?' The whole Wheel turns to look at the wing. Hepzibah Dimmock looks at him over her spectacles for a long moment. Then she says, in her dry voice, the voice that has given him every line he ever had: 'Yes. And your line is: And so, good night.' And he says it." {
    Assert proposed(gosse). Increase temper(pentrice) by 2. Increase regard(gammage) by 1. Increase regard(mallory) by 1. }
  Rule s9_empty at wheel when ghostOn(pentrice) and scene(pentrice) == 9 and sceneDone() and gosseMeans(gosse) and hepzibahTaken(pentrice) and not sceneOver(scene_nine)
    says "Then the epilogue. Gosse, as Pomfret, comes down to the edge of the stage: 'So ends our town, sirs, which was never yours; / so ends our Alderman, who went through doors / the Book had shut, and first, as dead men may. / A comedy should end in marriage: so—' and then he stops, and turns away from the house, to the left-hand wing, and opens his mouth to say something that is not in the book. The left-hand wing is empty. Hepzibah is on the grey bench with the Office. Gosse stands looking at the empty wing for a long moment, with the whole house watching him. Then he turns back to the house and says, quite gently, 'And so, good night,' and the play is over." {
    Assert emptyWing(gosse). }
  Rule s9_plain at wheel when ghostOn(pentrice) and scene(pentrice) == 9 and sceneDone() and not gosseMeans(gosse) and not sceneOver(scene_nine)
    says "Then the epilogue. Gosse, as Pomfret, comes down to the edge of the stage: 'So ends our town, sirs, which was never yours; / so ends our Alderman, who went through doors / the Book had shut, and first, as dead men may. / A comedy should end in marriage: so / I ask your hands instead, and so I go. / And so, good night.' And he bows, beautifully, and the play is over." { Increase temper(pentrice) by 1. }
  Rule s9_fined when ghostOn(pentrice) and scene(pentrice) == 9 and sceneDone() and liberty() and not clemBowed(clemency) and not sceneOver(scene_nine) { Increase fines(pentrice) by 2. }
  Rule s9_close when ghostOn(pentrice) and scene(pentrice) == 9 and sceneDone() and not sceneOver(scene_nine) {
    Assert sceneOver(scene_nine). Assert playEnded(pentrice). Set endedAt(pentrice) to watch(clock). Retract ghostOn(pentrice). Retract playingTonight(pentrice). }

  // After the play the company goes home over the river, once the company that played it has gone too.
  Rule troupe_home when playEnded(pentrice) and troupe(?p) and at(?p, tiring_house) and not at(party, wheel) and not at(party, tiring_house) {
    Retract at(?p, tiring_house). Assert at(?p, moon_loft). }
  Rule bear_home_after when playEnded(pentrice) and at(the_bear, tiring_house) and not at(party, wheel) and not at(party, tiring_house) {
    Retract at(the_bear, tiring_house). Assert at(the_bear, moon_yard). }
  Rule ned_home_after when playEnded(pentrice) and at(ned, tiring_house) and not at(party, wheel) and not at(party, tiring_house) {
    Retract at(ned, tiring_house). Assert at(ned, moon_loft). }
  Rule meg_home_after when playEnded(pentrice) and at(meg, tiring_house) and not at(party, wheel) and not at(party, tiring_house) {
    Retract at(meg, tiring_house). Assert at(meg, gullet). }

  // ── After: the house, and the fines read ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Rule applause_great at wheel when playEnded(pentrice) and ghostPlay(pentrice) and temper(pentrice) >= 12 and not hepzibahTaken(pentrice) and not spread(applause_known)
    says "For a moment after the last line nobody in the Wheel does anything at all. Then the yard begins, and the galleries take it up, and it goes on so long that the players run out of bows and simply stand there in a row holding hands, Gosse in the middle with his wreath crooked and his face wet, until Hepzibah comes out of the wing and leads them off like children." { Assert spread(applause_known). }
  Rule applause_great_bench at wheel when playEnded(pentrice) and ghostPlay(pentrice) and temper(pentrice) >= 12 and hepzibahTaken(pentrice) and not spread(applause_known)
    says "For a moment after the last line nobody in the Wheel does anything at all. Then the yard begins, and the galleries take it up, and it goes on so long that the players run out of bows and simply stand there in a row holding hands, Gosse in the middle with his wreath crooked and his face wet, until Hepzibah, let go at last by the Office, comes round from the grey bench with the book under her arm and leads them off like children." { Assert spread(applause_known). }
  Rule applause_good at wheel when playEnded(pentrice) and ghostPlay(pentrice) and temper(pentrice) >= 7 and temper(pentrice) < 12 and not spread(applause_known)
    says "The house claps them, long and warm, and calls Gosse back twice, and Pudding once." { Assert spread(applause_known). }
  Rule applause_thin at wheel when playEnded(pentrice) and ghostPlay(pentrice) and temper(pentrice) < 7 and not spread(applause_known)
    says "The house claps them, as a house does, and goes out over the river talking." { Assert spread(applause_known). }
  Discovery applause_known "Gosse's Company has played its night at the Wheel.".
  Rule fines_read_one at wheel when playEnded(pentrice) and ghostPlay(pentrice) and fines(pentrice) == 1 and not spread(fines_known)
    says "When the house has gone, Abel Tunstall stands on the grey bench with the tallymen's sticks in a bundle under his arm, and finds one notch among them all, and reads it by lantern-light with every sign of satisfaction: one crown, to be paid at the Office before the Bench sits at ten tomorrow, or Absalom Gosse to answer for it in the Clink of the Soke." { Assert spread(fines_known). }
  Rule fines_read at wheel when playEnded(pentrice) and ghostPlay(pentrice) and fines(pentrice) > 1 and not spread(fines_known)
    says "When the house has gone, Abel Tunstall stands on the grey bench with the tallymen's sticks in a bundle under his arm, and reads the notches by lantern-light, at a crown a notch: {fines(pentrice)} crowns, to be paid at the Office before the Bench sits at ten tomorrow, or Absalom Gosse to answer for it in the Clink of the Soke." { Assert spread(fines_known). }
  Discovery fines_known "The Office has fined Gosse's Company for the unlicensed lines spoken at the Wheel, a crown a line, to be paid before the Bench sits at ten the next morning.".
}

data/adventures/gosses-company/nights.ky:
Module pentrice "Gosse's Company" {
  // ── The other companies' nights ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The Siege of Arle, by the Lord Mayor's Servants, on the second night; The Patient Daughter, by the Children of the
  // Close, on the third. Each from seven until a little after nine. Watching them, a company learns what the Bench
  // likes; behind them, in the tiring-house, it can help or hinder.
  Rule show_on when trialNight() and showtime() and not playingTonight(pentrice) { Assert playingTonight(pentrice). }
  Rule show_off when playingTonight(pentrice) and not (trialNight() and hour(clock) >= 18) and not ghostOn(pentrice) { Retract playingTonight(pentrice). }
  Relation siegeFell(group). Relation siegeHeld(group). Relation siegeSeen(group). Relation daughterSeen(group).
  Relation tallyCounted(group). Relation tallyLet(group).

  // The Siege of Arle.
  Observe siege_scene at wheel when tday(pentrice) == 2 and showtime() and not siegeFell(fallow) "On the Wheel's stage the Lord Mayor's Servants are playing The Siege of Arle, as they have every Trial for eleven years: a painted city wall, a siege-tower on wheels with a gilded knight in it, boys in long gowns as the City's weeping daughters, and verse, a great deal of it, every syllable as licensed. The yard is full and patient. The grey bench below the stage sits with its sticks still: nobody in the Servants has said an unlicensed word since the Siege was new.".
  Observe siege_fallen at wheel when tday(pentrice) == 2 and showtime() and siegeFell(fallow) "The siege-tower lies on its side across the Wheel's stage with its gilded knight still in it, waving his legs. The yard is in hysterics. The Lord Mayor's Servants are trying to go on with the verse round it.".
  Observe siege_clay at wheel when tday(pentrice) == 2 and showtime() and hour(clock) >= 20 "In the lords' room over the stage, Ormsby Clay is following the Siege in a printed copy with his finger, nodding at each line ending as at an old friend. Dame Gammage has fallen asleep with her mouth open. Canon Mallory is moved, quietly, by the weeping daughters. Nym Carrow is drawing a gallows in the margin of his programme." teaches siege_tastes.
  Discovery siege_tastes "At the Siege of Arle the Bench showed itself: Clay followed the verse line by line with pleasure; Gammage slept; Mallory was moved by the weeping daughters; Carrow drew a gallows.".
  Observe siege_tower at tiring_house when tday(pentrice) == 2 and hour(clock) >= 18 and hour(clock) < 21 and not siegeFell(fallow) and not siegeHeld(fallow) "Behind the stage the Lord Mayor's Servants' siege-tower stands waiting for its entrance, eighteen feet of painted canvas on a frame on four wheels; and you see that one of the back wheels is cracked through, and held on its axle by a wooden wedge that is working loose.".
  Action wedge_tower(actor: group, site: place) "Drive the loose wedge home on the siege-tower's cracked wheel, and lash it" {
    Time 3.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, tiring_house) and tday(pentrice) == 2 and hour(clock) >= 18 and hour(clock) < 21
      and not siegeFell(fallow) and not siegeHeld(fallow) and not triedWedge(actor).
    Resolve check(actor, mending, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert siegeHeld(fallow). Assert fallowGrateful(fallow). }
    On failure { Assert triedWedge(actor). }
    Result "You knock the wedge home with the heel of a property sword and lash the cracked felloe with a coil of rope off a hook. A minute later the stage-keeper comes running for the tower, and the siege rolls on. Afterward, while the yard is still clapping, Corin Fallow finds you in the tiring-house. He looks at the lashed wheel for a long moment. 'That would have gone in the second act,' he says. 'In front of the Bench.' He holds out his hand. 'I am in your debt, which I dislike very much. I shall try to deserve it.'".
    Otherwise "You hit the wedge, and it splits, and the stage-keeper shouts for the tower before you can find another.".
  }
  Relation triedWedge(group).
  Action pull_wedge(actor: group, site: place) "Knock the loose wedge out of the siege-tower's cracked wheel" {
    Time 1 minute.
    Grave "The tower will go over in the middle of the Siege, in front of the Bench, and somebody may be under it.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, tiring_house) and tday(pentrice) == 2 and hour(clock) >= 18 and hour(clock) < 21
      and not siegeFell(fallow) and not siegeHeld(fallow).
    On success { Assert siegeFell(fallow). }
    Result "One tap with the heel of a property sword and the wedge drops out into the sawdust. Nobody sees, you think. Twenty minutes later, in the second act, the siege-tower rolls on with the gilded knight in it, and the cracked wheel folds up under it like a man fainting, and the whole tower goes over sideways across the stage of the Wheel with a noise like a barn falling down.".
  }
  Rule siege_fall_counts when siegeFell(fallow) and not spread(siege_fall_known) { Assert spread(siege_fall_known). }
  Discovery siege_fall_known "The Lord Mayor's Servants' siege-tower fell over in the middle of the Siege of Arle.".
  // Jem Pudding sees everything that happens behind a stage, and tells Gosse the next morning.
  Rule pudding_saw when siegeFell(fallow) and tday(pentrice) >= 3 and not gosseAshamed(gosse) { Assert gosseAshamed(gosse). }
  Relation gosseAshamed(group).
  Rule pudding_saw_told at moon_loft when at(party, moon_loft) and gosseAshamed(gosse) and not spread(gosse_shamed_known)
    says "Gosse is waiting at the top of the loft stair. Pudding is behind him, not looking at you. 'Jem saw you,' says Gosse, very quietly, which is worse than shouting. 'In the tiring-house. With the wedge.' He looks at you a long time. 'We do not win by other people's falls. Not in this company. Not ever.' He turns away. 'You can stay. I have not decided whether I can bear it.'" { Assert spread(gosse_shamed_known). }
  Discovery gosse_shamed_known "Gosse knows who knocked out the wedge from under Fallow's siege-tower.".

  // The Patient Daughter.
  Observe daughter_scene at wheel when tday(pentrice) == 3 and showtime() "The Children of the Close are playing The Patient Daughter: a long, sweet, improving piece in which a girl of twelve bears everything and is taken up to Heaven by angels on a rope. The angels are small boys in surplices with cardboard wings, and they are very good, and very slow. The yard is affectionate and restless. Canon Mallory, in the lords' room, is mouthing every line with them.".
  Observe daughter_ned at wheel when tday(pentrice) == 3 and showtime() and hour(clock) >= 20 and not nedRuns(ned) "The Fourth Angel, Ned Cherry, comes to the edge of the stage, and lifts his face, and sings his one word, Behold, so that the whole Wheel goes quiet to the top gallery.".
  Observe daughter_no_ned at wheel when tday(pentrice) == 3 and showtime() and hour(clock) >= 20 and nedRuns(ned) "The Fourth Angel's place in the procession is empty, and when the moment comes the Third Angel, a very small boy, sings Behold twice, once for himself and once for Ned Cherry, in a voice like a wren's, looking anxiously at the lords' room.".
  Observe daughter_tastes at wheel when tday(pentrice) == 3 and showtime() and hour(clock) >= 20 "In the lords' room Canon Mallory is weeping freely at the ascension. Ormsby Clay is looking at his watch. Dame Gammage is eating nuts very loudly. Nym Carrow has gone out." teaches daughter_tastes_known.
  Discovery daughter_tastes_known "At the Patient Daughter Mallory wept, Clay looked at his watch, Gammage ate nuts, and Carrow went out.".

  // A tallyman on the grey bench on the third night: the Fifth Angel, aged nine, says a word that is not in the book.
  Observe angel_slip at wheel when tday(pentrice) == 3 and showtime() and hour(clock) >= 20 and tallyman(party) and not tallyCounted(party) and not tallyLet(party) "On the stage the Fifth Angel, aged about nine, catches his wing on the rope, and says, quite clearly, to the whole Wheel: 'Bum.' Beside you on the grey bench Abel Tunstall's knife is already moving on his stick. He looks sideways at yours.".
  Action count_angel(actor: group, site: place) "Cut a notch for the Fifth Angel's word" {
    Time 0.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, wheel) and tallyman(actor) and tday(pentrice) == 3 and showtime() and hour(clock) >= 20
      and not tallyCounted(actor) and not tallyLet(actor).
    On success { Assert tallyCounted(actor). }
    Result "You cut one notch. Tunstall nods once, as at a sum correctly done. The Children of the Close will be fined a crown, which the Canon will pay out of his own pocket, and the Fifth Angel will be told about it all the way home.".
  }
  Action let_angel(actor: group, site: place) "Let your knife lie still" {
    Time 0.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, wheel) and tallyman(actor) and tday(pentrice) == 3 and showtime() and hour(clock) >= 20
      and not tallyCounted(actor) and not tallyLet(actor).
    On success { Assert tallyLet(actor). Increase regard(mallory) by 1. }
    Result "You leave your stick on your knee. Tunstall looks at it, and at you, and writes something very small in his ledger. Up in the lords' room the Canon, who has seen the whole thing, catches your eye and looks away, pink.".
  }
  // A tallyman is paid each morning for the night before.
  Rule tally_pay_two when tallyman(party) and tday(pentrice) >= 3 and not tallyPaid(siege_tastes) { Assert tallyPaid(siege_tastes). Increase quantity(party, gold) by 1. }
  Rule tally_pay_three when tallyman(party) and tday(pentrice) >= 4 and not tallyPaid(daughter_tastes_known) { Assert tallyPaid(daughter_tastes_known). Increase quantity(party, gold) by 1. }
  Relation tallyPaid(fact).
}

data/adventures/gosses-company/office.ky:
Module pentrice "Gosse's Company" {
  // ── The parcel at the Painted Moon ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Left with the ostler on the night before the company came, by a woman in a hood, with twenty crowns: for "the one
  // who played the Fool at the Wheel the night of the riot". Gosse says that was him. Merriman has heard that before.
  Relation bookCome(place).
  Person merriman "Dick Merriman" at moon_yard {
    Role "the Painted Moon's ostler". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner cheerful.
    Greets "Dick Merriman is a broad young man with straw in his hair and a currycomb in his hand, and he grins at you as he grins at horses: to show there is nothing to be afraid of.".
  }
  Kind parcel_kind "a parcel in oilcloth" is gear worth 0 weighing 1
    described "A flat heavy parcel done up in oilcloth and good paper and tied with tape, addressed in a small upright hand: FOR THE FOOL OF THE WHEEL, THE NIGHT OF THE RIOT. TO BE CALLED FOR.".
  Item parcel "a parcel in oilcloth" is parcel_kind at moon_yard hidden until parcel_freed.
  Discovery parcel_freed "Dick Merriman has let the parcel go.".
  Initially Assert lends(merriman, parcel, party).
  Topic merriman_parcel with merriman "Ask Merriman whether anything has been left for Gosse's Company" when not bookCome(pentrice) and not knows(actor, parcel_freed) once {
    Says "'A parcel,' says Merriman, 'but not for them. For,' he shuts his eyes to get it right, 'the one who played the Fool at the Wheel the night of the riot. That's what she said, the lady. Twenty crowns in it, she said, and give it to nobody else, and I'll know him.' He opens his eyes. 'Old Gosse says that's him. Four men have told me that's them since Tuesday, and one of them was a goat-herd.' He shrugs. 'Riot was forty years ago. How would I know him?'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, parcel_waiting). }
  }
  Discovery parcel_waiting "A woman in a hood left a parcel with the Moon's ostler, Dick Merriman, with twenty crowns, for the one who played the Fool at the Wheel the night of the riot forty years ago; Merriman will not give it to anyone who cannot show him so." { Known by merriman. }
  Topic merriman_lady with merriman "Ask Merriman about the lady who left the parcel" when knows(actor, parcel_waiting) once {
    Says "'In a hood,' says Merriman. 'An old brown hood, a servant's, but she wasn't a servant. A servant doesn't look at a yard like that, like she's seeing it with somebody else's eyes. And she gave me a whole crown for it.' He thinks. 'Hands like a clerk. Ink on the second finger.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, hooded_lady). }
  }
  Discovery hooded_lady "The woman who left the parcel at the Painted Moon wore a servant's old brown hood, but was no servant, and had ink on her second finger." { Known by merriman. }
  Action show_bill(actor: group, recipient: member, site: place) "Show Merriman Gosse's old playbill from the riot night, with his name on it as the Fool" {
    Speaker merriman. Time 2 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(merriman, site) and carries(actor, gosse_bill)
      and knows(actor, parcel_waiting) and not knows(actor, parcel_freed) and not bookCome(pentrice)
      and memberOf(recipient, actor) and awake(recipient).
    Resolve acquire(parcel, parcel_kind, recipient).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, parcel_freed). Retract at(parcel, moon_yard). }
    Result "Merriman takes the playbill to the light of the stable door and reads it with his lips moving. 'The Fool: Mister A. Gosse,' he says. 'Well, I'm damned. It was him.' He goes into the tack-room and comes out with a flat parcel done up in oilcloth, and gives it to you with both hands. 'Tell him I'm sorry I put him in with the goat-herd. I didn't say it to his face.'".
  }
  Action lie_merriman(actor: group, recipient: member, site: place) "Tell Merriman you were the Fool at the Wheel the night of the riot yourself" {
    Speaker merriman. Time 2 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(merriman, site) and knows(actor, parcel_waiting)
      and not knows(actor, parcel_freed) and not bookCome(pentrice) and not triedLie(actor)
      and memberOf(recipient, actor) and awake(recipient).
    Resolve check(actor, deception, dc_formidable).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, parcel_freed). Assert lieWorked(actor). }
    On failure { Assert triedLie(actor). }
    Result "You tell it so well, the night of the riot, the line, the gallery, the Lord Mayor's face, that Merriman's mouth falls open. 'You must have been a baby,' he says. 'You must have been a prodigy.' He goes and fetches the parcel. You have the strong impression he is giving it to you for the story.".
    Otherwise "Merriman looks at you for a long moment. 'The riot,' he says, 'was forty years ago.' He goes back to his horse.".
  }
  Relation triedLie(group). Relation lieWorked(group).
  Action take_parcel(actor: group, recipient: member, site: place) "Take the parcel in oilcloth" {
    Time 1 minute.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, moon_yard) and lieWorked(actor) and at(parcel, moon_yard)
