    Says "'A wooing speech!' Gosse is delighted. 'The Duke of Morrow, act two. Never fails.' He gives it to Merriman in the yard at the top of his voice, and Merriman learns it on the spot, all twenty lines of it. It is magnificent. It is, you realise about halfway through, the speech of a villain luring a novice out of a convent.".
