  Rule nan_comes_down when hour(clock) == 3 and at(nan, crescent) and not carthReunited(carth) and not nanFled(nan) { Assert at(nan, laundry_yard). }
  Rule knock_resets when hour(clock) == 4 and knockTonight(nan) { Retract knockTonight(nan). }
  Discovery knocker_seen "Somebody in a laundress's cloak knocks at Carth House every night at two.".
  Observe knock_from_crescent at crescent when at(nan, crescent) and not carthReunited(carth) "At two in the morning a woman in a grey cloak comes along the Crescent from the top of the Parade, not hurrying, and goes up the steps of Carth House, and knocks, once. Then she stands there with her hand flat on the door, the way you would stand by a horse to feel it breathe. After a while she goes away down the hill." teaches knocker_seen.
  Observe knock_from_hall at carth_hall when at(nan, crescent) and not carthReunited(carth) "A knock. Once. The whole hall seems to hear it: the fires, the clocks, the furs. Sir Gervase is on his feet in front of his chair, facing the door, with his hands at his sides. He does not move toward it.".
  // Following her down.
  Action follow_knocker(actor: group, site: place) "Follow the woman in the grey cloak down the hill, at a distance" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, crescent) and at(nan, crescent) and not knows(actor, nan_knocks) and not triedFollow(actor).
    Time 3.
    Resolve check(actor, stealth, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, nan_knocks). Retract at(actor, crescent). Assert at(actor, laundry_yard). }
    On failure { Assert triedFollow(actor). }
    Result "Down the Parade, past the dark Pump Room, down Stall Street, through the laundries' steam, keeping to the walls: she does not look back once. In the laundry yard she lets herself in at a door under the stair, and a candle comes on in the window over the yard. In the morning, when you ask, the laundresses tell you the window is Nan Bellamy's.".
    Otherwise "At the top of the Parade she turns and looks straight back at you. Then she gathers her cloak and goes down the hill much faster than you can follow without running, and you lose her in the steam at the foot of Stall Street.".
  }
  Relation triedFollow(group).
  Discovery nan_knocks "The woman who knocks at Carth House at two in the morning is Nan Bellamy, a laundress in the Old Town.".
  Topic nan_why with nan "Ask Nan Bellamy why she knocks at Carth House" when knows(actor, nan_knocks) and not carthReunited(carth) once {
    Says "Nan Bellamy stops with her arms in the copper to the elbows, and stands there, and the steam goes up round her. 'So he'll know,' she says at last. 'That I'm not dead. That's all.' She takes her arms out and wrings a sheet as if it had done something. 'I was his wife. He put me out in the snow in my nightgown for a letter from my own brother. I walked down here. They took me in. Nine years.' She hangs the sheet. 'Brannagh tells me how Celia does. Thursdays. She's tall, Brannagh says. She reads.' Her voice does not change at all. 'I'd like to see her. Once. Awake.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, nan_is_lady). Assert nanSpoke(nan). }
  }
  Relation nanSpoke(group).
  Topic nan_door with nan "Ask Nan whether she would go in, if the door were opened" when nanSpoke(nan) and not carthReunited(carth) once {
    Says "'If he opened it.' Nan looks up the hill, though you cannot see Carth House from here, only steam. 'Himself. With his own hand, that shut it.' She turns back to the copper. 'Not Brannagh. Not you. If you opened it I'd turn round and come back down, and I'd not go up again.' She is quiet. 'He won't. He sits there. I can hear him breathing through the door.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, nan_terms). }
  }
  // The door opened by someone else: she will not come in, and does not come again.
  Action open_door_for_him(actor: group, site: place) "Draw the bolts and open the front door to the knock yourself" {
    Grave "She said she would turn round if anyone but him opened it, and not come up again.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, carth_hall) and at(nan, crescent) and not carthReunited(carth) and not nanFled(nan).
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Assert nanFled(nan). Assert at(nan, limbo). Assert state(front_door, open). Assert doorOpenedByOther(carth). }
    Result "You draw the bolts. The door swings in on the night and the cool air and the smell of the limes, and on the step a woman in a grey cloak, with her hand still up. She looks past you, at Sir Gervase on his feet by the chair. He does not move. Then she turns round and goes down the steps, and along the Crescent, and does not look back; and behind you, in the hall, all the candles lean in the draught, and two of them go out.".
  }
  Relation doorOpenedByOther(group).
  // The door opened by him: the reunion. He opens it himself only if he knows it is her, and has told the night to
  // someone, and, if he has been told Celia's lungs are sound, the house has had enough of winter.
  // Whether he does it is not a matter of how well it is said, but of what he has been through by then.
  Action ask_him_open(actor: group, site: place) "Tell Sir Gervase to open the door himself" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, carth_hall) and at(gervase, carth_hall) and at(nan, crescent)
      and not carthReunited(carth) and not nanFled(nan) and tolerates(gervase, actor) and not askedToOpen(gervase).
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Assert askedToOpen(gervase). }
    Result "'Open it,' you say. 'Yourself.' Sir Gervase looks at you as if you had spoken in another language.".
  }
  Relation askedToOpen(group).
  Rule he_opens at carth_hall when askedToOpen(gervase) and gervasePrepared() and at(nan, crescent) and not carthReunited(carth) and not nanFled(nan)
    says "He goes to the door. It takes him a long time to cross the hall, and you hear every clock not ticking. He draws the top bolt, and the bottom bolt, and takes down the bar, and opens the door of Carth House with his own hand, and the night comes in. On the step a woman in a grey laundress's cloak is standing with her hand up, as if to knock again. Neither of them says anything. Then she takes his hand, the one that opened the door, and turns it over, and looks at it, the way you would look at a thing you had lost and found in the street. 'It's warm out,' she says. 'You can let the fires go.'" {
    Assert carthReunited(carth). Assert state(front_door, open). Assert at(nan, carth_hall). Assert at(gervase, carth_hall). }
  Rule he_cannot at carth_hall when askedToOpen(gervase) and not gervasePrepared() and at(nan, crescent) and not carthReunited(carth) and not nanFled(nan) and not spread(he_cannot_told)
    says "Sir Gervase takes one step toward the door, and stops, and stands there with his hand out toward the bolt and not touching it, until the knocking-time is over and the footsteps go away down the hill. 'I can't,' he says. 'I don't know who it is. I don't know what I did.' He sits down." {
    Retract askedToOpen(gervase). Assert spread(he_cannot_told). }
  Entity he_cannot_told: fact "he could not open it".
  Rule asked_resets when askedToOpen(gervase) and not at(nan, crescent) and not carthReunited(carth) { Retract askedToOpen(gervase). Retract spread(he_cannot_told). }
  Relation carthReunited(group).
  // In the morning after, the shutters come down the whole length of the house.
  Rule shutters_down when carthReunited(carth) and not carthOpened(carth) and hour(clock) >= 7 and hour(clock) < 12 { Assert carthOpened(carth). }
  Relation carthOpened(group).
  Observe shutters_open at crescent when carthOpened(carth) and not dark() "At the end of the Crescent the shutters of Carth House are open, every one, for the first time in nine years, and men are carrying coal out of it in sacks, and in the drawing-room window a girl without a fur cap is leaning out on her elbows, looking at the lawn.".
  Rule celia_free_after when carthOpened(carth) and not celiaOut(celia) { Assert celiaOut(celia). }

  // ── Taking Celia out ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // By the window at night with Rob, or by the kitchen with Brannagh's help; to the Cherretts, who take her in.
  Action celia_by_window(actor: group, site: place) "Help Celia down from the drawing-room window to the area, and away" {
    Description "By night, when the Crescent is asleep. She wants to see the Season.".
    Grave "Sir Gervase will find his daughter gone in the morning, and know how she went.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and (at(actor, crescent) and state(drawing_window, ajar) or at(actor, carth_drawing))
      and at(celia, carth_drawing) and celiaWants(celia) and not celiaOut(celia) and not carthReunited(carth) and (hour(clock) >= 21 or hour(clock) < 5).
    Time 2.
    On success { Assert celiaOut(celia). Assert celiaTaken(celia). Assert at(celia, cherrett_parlour). Retract at(actor, site). Assert at(actor, cherrett_parlour). }
    Result "She comes over the sill in her fur cap and a cloak over her nightgown and a pair of Brannagh's boots, with Ovid under her arm, and down the railings after you, with your hands to guide her feet, and stands on the pavement of the Crescent in the warm dark and breathes, and breathes. 'It smells of grass,' she says. 'It smells of grass and horses.' You take her up the hill to the Circus, where Mrs Cherrett, roused out of her first sleep in her nightcap, looks at the girl in the fur cap for a long moment and says, 'Well, you'll want feeding,' and does not ask a single question.".
  }
  Action celia_by_kitchen(actor: group, site: place) "Take Celia down the back stair and out through the kitchen, with Mrs Brannagh's leave" {
    Grave "Sir Gervase will find his daughter gone, and know who let her go.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, carth_drawing) and at(celia, carth_drawing) and celiaWants(celia)
      and brannaghTrust(brannagh) >= 2 and not celiaOut(celia) and not carthReunited(carth).
    Time 2.
    On success { Assert celiaOut(celia). Assert celiaTaken(celia). Assert at(celia, cherrett_parlour). Retract at(actor, site). Assert at(actor, cherrett_parlour). }
    Result "Mrs Brannagh is waiting at the foot of the back stair with Celia's boots and a cloak and a basket with bread in it. She does not say anything. She does up the cloak's hooks herself, all the way to the chin, and kisses the girl on the forehead, and opens the kitchen door. 'Go on,' she says. 'Go on. He'll have it from me, not you.' Up the area steps, into the open air, and Celia stops on the pavement and breathes, and breathes, and puts her hand up against the sky as if it were a ceiling. 'It smells of grass,' she says. You take her up to the Circus, where Mrs Cherrett looks at the girl in the fur cap and says, 'Well, you'll want feeding,' and does not ask a single question.".
  }
  Relation celiaTaken(group).
  Rule gervase_bereft when celiaTaken(celia) and not carthReunited(carth) and not gervaseBereft(gervase) and hour(clock) >= 7 { Assert gervaseBereft(gervase). }
  Relation gervaseBereft(group).
  Rule celia_lodges when celiaOut(celia) and not carthReunited(carth) and not at(celia, cherrett_parlour) and not atBall(celia) and not celiaAway(celia) and not following(celia, party) and not travelsWith(celia, party) { Assert at(celia, cherrett_parlour). }
  Rule celia_home when carthReunited(carth) and carthOpened(carth) and not at(celia, carth_drawing) and not atBall(celia) and not celiaAway(celia) and not following(celia, party) and not travelsWith(celia, party) { Assert at(celia, carth_drawing). }
  // Taken to her mother, by day.
  Relation celiaMetMother(group).
  Topic celia_to_mother with celia "Tell Celia that her mother is alive, and washing linen in the Old Town" when knows(actor, nan_is_lady) and celiaOut(celia) and not nanFled(nan) and not celiaMetMother(celia) and not carthReunited(carth) once {
    Says "Celia Carth stands quite still with the bread Mrs Cherrett gave her in her hand. 'Alive,' she says. She puts the bread down. 'Take me. Now. Please.'".
    On discuss { Assert acceptsEscort(celia, actor). Assert following(celia, actor). Assert celiaAway(celia). }
  }
  Event celia_meets_mother at laundry_yard when at(party, laundry_yard) and following(celia, party) and at(nan, laundry_yard) and not dark() and not celiaMetMother(celia) "In the laundry yard Nan Bellamy is wringing a sheet. She looks up. The sheet falls into the copper. Neither of them moves, and then the girl in the fur cap walks across the wet flagstones and stops a yard away, and says, 'You're taller than I remembered,' which is absurd, as she was nine; and her mother laughs, and has her by both arms, wet to the elbows, and the laundresses stand round with their sleeves up and do not pretend to be doing anything else." then {
    Assert celiaMetMother(celia). Retract following(celia, party). Retract celiaAway(celia). }
  Event celia_meets_mother_night at laundry_yard when at(party, laundry_yard) and following(celia, party) and at(nan, laundry_yard) and dark() and not celiaMetMother(celia) "On the step under the stair, in the light of her one candle, Nan Bellamy looks up. She gets to her feet slowly, the way you get up for a stranger. Neither of them moves; and then the girl in the fur cap crosses the wet flagstones and stops a yard away, and says, 'You're taller than I remembered,' which is absurd, as she was nine; and her mother laughs out loud in the dark yard, and has her by both arms, and all round the yard, one after another, the laundresses' windows light up, and nobody pretends to be asleep." then {
    Assert celiaMetMother(celia). Retract following(celia, party). Retract celiaAway(celia). }
}

data/adventures/hessel/cherretts.kyr:
Module hessel "The Banns at Hessel" {
  // ── Mrs Cherrett ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Seventy-four. Her husband cut half the canals in three countries and she cooked for his gangs; now she has forty
  // thousand pounds, a heart that is giving out, and three young people to settle before it does. She takes Dr
  // Hartopp's drops at night for the pain, and knows what is in them. She does not know he has doubled them.
  Person cherrett "Mrs Abigail Cherrett" at cherrett_parlour {
    Role "a vast old woman in purple, with a laugh like a dropped coal-scuttle" when not gone(cherrett).
    Role "Mrs Cherrett, who did not wake" when gone(cherrett).
    Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner jovial.
    Greets "The old woman looks you up and down as if you were a horse she might buy. 'Well,' she says. 'Sit down where I can see you.'".
    Greets again "Mrs Cherrett waves you to a chair with her stick.".
  }
  Relation gone(group). Relation bedbound(group). Relation legs(group).
  // She keeps her room until she is up; the Pump Room at eight if she is well; her parlour by day; bed at ten.
  Query cherrettUp() means not gone(cherrett) and not bedbound(cherrett) and chairRan(cherrett).
  Rule cherrett_pump when cherrettUp() and not lingering(cherrett) and pumpHour() and not secondDayOnRoad() and not at(cherrett, pump_room) and failing(cherrett) < 4 { Assert at(cherrett, pump_room). }
  Rule cherrett_parlour when not gone(cherrett) and not lingering(cherrett) and hour(clock) >= 10 and hour(clock) < 22 and not at(cherrett, cherrett_parlour) and not atBall(cherrett) and not bedbound(cherrett) and chairRan(cherrett) { Assert at(cherrett, cherrett_parlour). }
  Rule cherrett_bed when (hour(clock) >= 22 or hour(clock) < 8 or bedbound(cherrett) and not lingering(cherrett) or gone(cherrett)) and not at(cherrett, cherrett_bedroom) and not atBall(cherrett) and chairRan(cherrett) { Assert at(cherrett, cherrett_bedroom). }
  Rule cherrett_mends when bedbound(cherrett) and dayN(hessel_town) >= 2 and hour(clock) >= 8 { Retract bedbound(cherrett). }
  Query secondDayOnRoad() means false.
  Observe cherrett_parlour_scene at cherrett_parlour when not visitedBefore(cherrett_parlour) "Mrs Cherrett's parlour: rented furniture, too good for anyone to sit on, and on top of it everything Mrs Cherrett has brought from home, which is a great deal, including a stuffed pike, a canal map of three counties framed in oak, and a footstool made of an elephant's foot. The window looks down over the Circus lawn.".
  Observe cherrett_parlour_again at cherrett_parlour when visitedBefore(cherrett_parlour) "Mrs Cherrett's parlour: the pike, the canal map, the elephant's foot.".
  Observe cherrett_bed_scene at cherrett_bedroom when true "Mrs Cherrett's bedroom: a great curtained bed, a fire kept in in all weathers, and a dressing-table crowded with pins and powders and bottles.".
  Observe cherrett_awake at cherrett_parlour when at(cherrett, cherrett_parlour) and failing(cherrett) < 3 and not gone(cherrett) "Mrs Cherrett sits in the middle of it all like the stuffed pike's mother, with her stick across her knees, and misses nothing.".
  Observe cherrett_drowsy at cherrett_parlour when at(cherrett, cherrett_parlour) and failing(cherrett) == 3 and not gone(cherrett) "Mrs Cherrett is asleep in her chair with her mouth open, at eleven in the morning; she wakes when you come in, says 'I wasn't,' and is asleep again before you are sat down.".
  Observe cherrett_grey at cherrett_parlour when at(cherrett, cherrett_parlour) and failing(cherrett) >= 4 and not gone(cherrett) "Mrs Cherrett is in her chair, grey in the face, with her eyes half open and her hands slack on her stick. Mopsa is beside her, holding one of them, and does not look up.".
  Observe cherrett_sharp at cherrett_parlour when at(cherrett, cherrett_parlour) and sharpened(cherrett) and dayN(hessel_town) == sharpDay(cherrett) and hour(clock) < 14 and not gone(cherrett) "Mrs Cherrett is wide awake, in a temper, and enjoying it. 'Slept like a cat on a griddle,' she says, to nobody. 'Best night's sleep I've had in a month.'".

  // ── The runaway chair ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The first time the company is in the Abbey Yard by day, Mrs Cherrett's bath-chair comes down the Parade without its
  // chairman. Kit Danby let go of the strap at the top because he looked up and saw Ismay on the Circus steps.
  Relation chairRan(group). Relation chairLoose(group). Relation chairCaught(group). Relation chairSteered(group).
  Relation chairThrown(group). Measure chairWatch(group).
  Hazard chair_blow "The bath-chair's wheel, and the railings" means "Deal (1d6) physical damage to ally unless dexterity save against (12).".
  Event chair_runs at abbey_yard when at(party, abbey_yard) and daytime() and cameToHessel(party) and not chairRan(cherrett) and not gone(cherrett) and not bedbound(cherrett) and failing(cherrett) < 4 "Somebody at the top of the Parade screams, and then everybody does. Down the hill toward you, gathering speed on the ridged paving, comes a bath-chair, a great wicker thing on three iron wheels, and in it, upright and furious and holding on to her bonnet, a very large old woman in purple. Behind it, much too far behind it, a chairman in a blue coat is running and shouting. The chair is aimed at the Pump Room colonnade, and the colonnade is stone." then {
    Assert chairRan(cherrett). Assert chairLoose(cherrett). Set chairWatch(cherrett) to watch(clock).
    Assert at(cherrett, abbey_yard). Assert at(kit, abbey_yard). Assert lingering(cherrett). Assert kitAway(kit). }
  // For half an hour after, the old woman and the chairman are in the Abbey Yard, being stared at.
  Relation lingering(group).
  Rule linger_over when lingering(cherrett) and watch(clock) > chairWatch(cherrett) + 3 { Retract lingering(cherrett). Retract kitAway(kit). }
  Action catch_chair(actor: group, site: place) "Get in front of the bath-chair and catch it by the handle" {
    Description "It is very heavy and moving very fast.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, abbey_yard) and chairLoose(cherrett).
    Time 1 minute.
    Resolve check(actor, brawn, dc_fair).
    On success { Retract chairLoose(cherrett). Assert chairCaught(cherrett). Increase goodwill(chairmen) by 1. }
    On failure { Retract chairLoose(cherrett). Assert chairThrown(cherrett). Assert chairTried(party). Assert bedbound(cherrett). Assert strikes(chair_blow, party). }
    Result "You plant your feet on the ridges and take the chair's handle full in the chest, and for a moment it is a question which of you is going to go on down the hill. Then it stops. The old woman in it lets go of her bonnet. 'Well,' she says, looking at you. 'Well, well.' The whole Abbey Yard is staring. A man in the Pump Room colonnade begins, for some reason, to clap.".
    Otherwise "You get a hand to the handle and the chair takes you off your feet and goes on with you under it, and hits the bottom step of the colonnade, and turns over. The old woman comes out of it like a sack off a cart. People run. When they have her up she is sitting on the step with her bonnet over one eye and her ankle swelling, saying words a canal gang would know. They are going to carry her up the hill to her lodgings in the Circus, in her own chair.".
  }
  Action steer_chair(actor: group, site: place) "Seize the side of the chair and drag it round into the church railings" {
    Description "It will stop. It will not stop gently.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, abbey_yard) and chairLoose(cherrett).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Retract chairLoose(cherrett). Assert chairSteered(cherrett). Assert strikes(chair_blow, party). }
    Result "You catch the side of the chair as it comes level and haul it round, and it leaves the colonnade and goes instead into the railings of Saint Ebba's with a noise like a dropped dresser, and stops, half in and half out of them, with a wheel going round in the air. Your arm is wrenched half out of its socket. The old woman in it straightens her bonnet. 'That,' she says, 'is the second time in my life a stranger has thrown me at a church.'".
  }
  // Whatever else the company does, the chair goes on: the next watch it hits the colonnade.
  Rule chair_crashes at abbey_yard when chairLoose(cherrett) and watch(clock) > chairWatch(cherrett) says "The chair goes past you and hits the bottom step of the colonnade and turns over, and the old woman comes out of it like a sack off a cart. When the crowd has her up she is sitting on the step with her ankle swelling, swearing like a canal gang. They are going to carry her up to her lodgings in the Circus, in her own chair." {
    Retract chairLoose(cherrett). Assert chairThrown(cherrett). Assert bedbound(cherrett). }
  Rule chair_crashes_away when chairLoose(cherrett) and watch(clock) > chairWatch(cherrett) and not at(party, abbey_yard) {
    Retract chairLoose(cherrett). Assert chairThrown(cherrett). Assert bedbound(cherrett). }
  // Kit is blamed for a thrown chair, and turned off by the evening, unless somebody speaks for him.
  Relation kitDismissed(group). Relation kitDefended(group).
  Rule kit_turned_off when chairThrown(cherrett) and not kitDefended(kit) and not kitDismissed(kit) and (hour(clock) >= 18 or dayN(hessel_town) >= 2) {
    Assert kitDismissed(kit). }
  Topic defend_kit with cherrett "Tell Mrs Cherrett it was not the chairman's fault" when chairThrown(cherrett) and not kitDismissed(kit) and not kitDefended(kit) once {
    Says "'Not his fault!' says Mrs Cherrett, from where they have propped her. 'He let go of me on the Parade! He let go of me like a hot potato!' She glares at you. Then, because she is fair, she thinks. 'What did he let go for, then?' You do not know. 'Well,' she says. 'Well. I'll not turn a man off for a thing nobody can explain to me. Tell him he can carry me tomorrow. Tell him if he drops me again I'll have him stuffed and put beside the pike.'".
    On discuss { Assert kitDefended(kit). Increase goodwill(chairmen) by 1. Increase kitTrust(kit) by 1. }
  }

  Action bind_ankle(actor: group, site: place) "Strap Mrs Cherrett's ankle properly, and get her up" {
    Description "A nurse's or a bonesetter's work.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(cherrett, site) and bedbound(cherrett) and not gone(cherrett)
      and capable(actor, mending) and not ankleBound(cherrett).
    Time 2.
    On success { Assert ankleBound(cherrett). Retract bedbound(cherrett). Increase softened(cherrett) by 1. }
    Result "You strap it firm, the way a bonesetter does, with a wet bandage that will shrink, and a stick under her other arm, and she gets up and stamps on it, and swears, and stamps again. 'Well,' she says. 'Somebody in this town knows something.'".
  }
  Relation ankleBound(group).
  // ── Taken up ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // After the chair, she wants the company. If it caught or steered her, at once and at the foot of the Parade; if it
  // let her go, from her bed, when somebody brings her word that it was the stranger who tried.
  Topic cherrett_takes_you with cherrett "Ask the old woman if she is hurt" when chairCaught(cherrett) or chairSteered(cherrett) once {
    Says "'Hurt? I cooked for four hundred navvies on the Delve cut through the wettest winter God ever sent,' says the old woman. 'I am Abigail Cherrett, and I am not hurt. I am dying, but that's another thing, and not your fault.' She looks at you again, longer. 'You've got legs,' she says. 'Mine are done, and that one's are' (the chairman, scarlet, holding his hat) 'evidently not to be trusted. I've a granddaughter to marry, and a great-nephew, and a companion, by the Closing Ball on Monday, and I'm in a town where I can't get up a hill. I'll pay you to be my legs for the Season. Fetch and carry. Go where I can't. Tell me what's what.' She sticks out a hand the size of a spade. 'Mrs Cherrett's lodgings, the Circus. Come up when you've a mind to say yes.'".
    On discuss { Assert cherrettAsked(party). }
  }
  Relation cherrettAsked(group).
  Topic cherrett_from_bed with cherrett "Tell Mrs Cherrett you were the one who tried to stop her chair" when chairThrown(cherrett) and chairTried(party) and not cherrettAsked(party) once {
    Says "Mrs Cherrett looks at you from where they have propped her, with her bad ankle up on somebody's hat-box. 'You were the one,' she says. 'I saw you go under. That was brave and it was no use, which is most of what brave is.' She pats the coverlet. 'I'm in a town where I can't get up a hill, and now I can't get up at all. I've a granddaughter to marry, and a great-nephew, and a companion, by the Closing Ball. I'll pay you to be my legs. Fetch and carry; go where I can't; tell me what's what.'".
    On discuss { Assert cherrettAsked(party). }
  }
  Relation chairTried(group).
  Topic cherrett_watched with cherrett "Tell Mrs Cherrett you are new in Hessel, and want work" when chairThrown(cherrett) and not chairTried(party) and not cherrettAsked(party) once {
    Says "Mrs Cherrett looks at you from where they have propped her, with her bad ankle up on somebody's hat-box. 'You were in the Abbey Yard,' she says. 'I saw you. You stood and watched, like the rest of them.' You admit it. 'Well, you're honest, which is more than the rest of them, and you've come up the hill to say so, which is more again.' She pats the coverlet. 'I'm in a town where I couldn't get up a hill, and now I can't get up at all. I've a granddaughter to marry, and a great-nephew, and a companion, by the Closing Ball. I'll pay you to be my legs. Fetch and carry; go where I can't; tell me what's what. And next time a chair comes down a hill at you, do something.'".
    On discuss { Assert cherrettAsked(party). }
  }
  Topic say_yes with cherrett "Tell Mrs Cherrett you will be her legs for the Season" when cherrettAsked(party) and not legs(party) and at(cherrett, ?p) and (at(party, cherrett_parlour) or at(party, cherrett_bedroom)) once {
    Says "'Good,' she says, and counts five coins into your hand out of a purse like a pudding-cloth. 'That's for now. There's more for results.' She settles back. 'Now. Here's what I want. Ismay, my granddaughter, is to marry the Honourable Rupert Wenlock on Monday; the banns are read the third time on Sunday, at Saint Ebba's; you'll see it isn't spoiled. Rob, my great-nephew, has my money after me and nothing in his head but poetry, and he's to be engaged by the Ball on Monday to a sensible girl, I've three in mind. And Mopsa, my companion, is twenty-eight and has no money and a tongue on her, and she must be married off before she's a poor relation, which is the worst thing a woman can be, I've seen it.' She folds her hands on her stick. 'And Mr Twiss has barred me from his Rooms, for laughing at a minuet, so none of it can be done at the Ball unless that's mended. Well? Go on.'".
    On discuss { Assert legs(party). Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 5. }
  }
  // The question she puts, once the company has been her legs a day: what would you do?
