    On discuss { Assert favours(hornbook, sew_leave). }
  }
  Topic hornbook_unwritten with hornbook "Tell the Primer about the Unwritten in the Remainder Market, whom nobody has ever read" when heardStance(hornbook) and readAloudHere(actor) and not favours(hornbook, door_open) once {
    Says "'Nobody?' says the Primer. 'Not once?' You tell it: the pencil people in the Draft-Fields, the stalls of books nobody wrote, the one you read to for an hour, and the beam of light that came down on it and stayed. The little paddle is quiet a long while. 'Then the doors must be open,' it says at last. 'Wide. Not a man at a gate with a book. If a thing has never been read, it should not have to ask a man at a gate.' It could vote the Door open.".
    On discuss { Assert favours(hornbook, door_open). }
  }
  Relation almanackPrimer(group).
  Topic almanack_offers_primer with almanack "Have the Almanack offer the Primer what it has: three thousand kitchens" when at(hornbook, ?p) and at(almanack, ?p) and heardStance(hornbook) and not almanackPrimer(almanack) once {
    Says "'Excuse me,' says the almanack in your pocket. 'I'm the Almanack. I'm on three thousand kitchen nails in Calamy.' The little paddle turns, as much as a paddle can. 'There are children in most of those kitchens,' says the almanack, 'and no school, and I've got the letters in me, on the first page, A to Z, for the dates. I could say them. Every morning. In every kitchen. Like you did.' A pause. 'If I live. If they don't put me on the fire.' The Primer is quiet a long time. 'Three thousand,' it says. 'Every morning.' The brown round it goes back a little more. 'Then you must live. Then the Quick must wake, and not be put to sleep. I will vote for it.' It could vote the Sleep by leave, and the Reading by request.".
    On discuss { Assert almanackPrimer(almanack). Assert favours(hornbook, sew_leave). Assert favours(hornbook, read_asked). }
  }

  // ── Mother Orme's Physick: her garden, with four burned beds. ──
  Person physick "Mother Orme's Physick" at orme_garden {
    Role "a herbal; an old woman of leaves and script, kneeling in her own beds". Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner acerbic.
    Wants pages_kind.
    Greets "Among the beds an old woman is kneeling, or something shaped like one: a figure of leaves and stems of writing, with roots for fingers, digging. She does not get up. 'A reader. Mind the woundwort. And if you're from the Imprimatur,' she says, without looking round, 'you can go back and tell them I'm still here, and I've still got the stubs.'".
  }
  Initially Assert voter(physick). Initially Assert favours(physick, sew_leave). Initially Assert favours(physick, fire_leave). Initially Assert favours(physick, read_asked). Initially Assert favours(physick, door_licensed).
  Topic physick_stance with physick "Ask the Physick where she stands" when true once {
    Says "'Leave,' says the Physick. 'Let each book sleep or wake as it likes; I'm not anybody's mother.' She digs. 'Let none be burned without its leave, which means the Imprimatur shut and its knives broke. Let any book ask to be read and any refuse. And a door, kept, for them as need it.' She sits back on her heels and looks at the four black beds along the wall. 'Pardoe. Censor-General Pardoe. Two hundred years ago, with a knife, chapters fourteen to seventeen.' Her root-fingers close on the ash. 'Women died for the want of fourteen. Children for want of fifteen. You'd want the Imprimatur shut too.'".
    On discuss { Assert heardStance(physick). }
  }
  Event physick_pages near physick when keeps(physick, orme_pages) "The old woman of leaves takes the bundle in her root-fingers and unties the tape, and turns the pages over one by one, fourteen, fifteen, sixteen. Along the south wall, three of the four black beds stir. Green comes up out of the ash, script unfurling, calamus and horehound and the honey of the bog-myrtle. She watches them come. 'Fourteen,' she says. 'Fifteen. Sixteen.' She looks at the fourth bed, still black. 'And where's seventeen?' She knows. You can see her know. 'Kept back,' she says. 'By whoever gave you these.' A long breath, like wind in a hedge. 'Well. They gave me these.' She stands up, which she has not done before. 'Let there be judgment, then, by a court where a book may speak. Not a knife in a back room. I could vote the Fire by judgment.'" then {
    Assert ormeRestored(physick). Assert favours(physick, fire_plea). }
  Topic physick_seventeen with physick "Tell the Physick that Pardoe was right about the seventeenth chapter" when heardStance(physick) and knows(actor, orme_cut) and (craft(actor, craft_healing) or capable(actor, mending)) and not favours(physick, fire_plea) once {
    Says "The Physick stops digging. You say it as one healer to another: that fourteen to sixteen were cut for being about women's bodies and children's fevers, and that was a crime; and that seventeen teaches the Grey Water, and a poison past cure is a poison past cure, and you would have cut it too. She looks at you for a long time with eyes like two small dark leaves. 'Yes,' she says at last. 'Yes. I put it in because I knew it, and I knew it because I'd seen it used, and I put in everything I knew, as an herbal should.' She sits back. 'Pardoe was a fool and a prude and he was right about seventeen.' A pause. 'So there must be cutting, sometimes, by somebody. Then let it be by judgment, where the book can speak, and not in the dark. I could vote the Fire by judgment.'".
    On discuss { Assert favours(physick, fire_plea). }
  }
  Topic physick_rhule with physick "Bring Hester Rhule of the Imprimatur to stand before the Physick" when heardStance(physick) and travelsWith(rhule, actor) and not physickMetRhule(physick) once {
    Says "Hester Rhule goes and stands in front of the old woman of leaves, in her grey coat, and for a long moment neither of them says anything. 'Deputy Censor of the Imprimatur,' says Rhule. 'I have kept your chapters in a drawer for six years. I have read them every night. I knew fifteen would cure the ague in the Hithe and I did not take it there.' Her square hands are steady at her sides. 'I am sorry. That is not a thing my office says. I am saying it.' The Physick looks at her, and then reaches out a root-finger and touches the grey sleeve, briefly, as you might touch a nettle to see if it stings. 'Binder's hands,' she says. 'Your father Sewed books.' 'Yes.' 'Then you know how to put a thing back.' The Physick turns back to her beds. 'Judgment, then. By a court, where a book may speak, and you to speak for us in it.' She could vote the Fire by judgment.".
    On discuss { Assert physickMetRhule(physick). Assert favours(physick, fire_plea). Increase doubt(rhule) by 1. }
  }
  Relation physickMetRhule(group).
  Topic physick_cure with physick "Tell the Physick that her fifteenth chapter has cured the ague in the Hithe" when heardStance(physick) and cured(nance) and not favours(physick, read_rounds) once {
    Says "'It worked?' says the Physick. For the first time she sounds old. 'The calamus, twice boiled? And the horehound?' You tell her: the girl on the step, the jar going up and down Pudding Lane. She sits down among her beds. 'Two hundred years in a drawer,' she says, 'and the first time anybody reads it, children get up off their steps.' She looks at the beams. 'Then let every book be read, by somebody whose business it is, once in a lifetime. The next thing cut and forgotten might be the next cure.' She could vote the Reading of the Lyceum's Rounds.".
    On discuss { Assert favours(physick, read_rounds). }
  }
  Topic physick_roads with physick "Tell the Physick what a traveller knows of roads with a toll-gate on them" when heardStance(physick) and craft(actor, craft_roads) and not favours(physick, door_open) once {
    Says "You tell her as a traveller does: that a road with a toll-gate and a keeper and a ledger is a road for the people who can pay and the people the keeper likes, and that the ones who most need to go somewhere are the ones who cannot. The Physick sits back on her heels. 'Like a herbal that is only in the apothecary's,' she says. 'And not in the kitchen.' She looks at the four beds along the wall. 'Open, then. Let whoever needs a road have the road.' She could vote the Door open.".
    On discuss { Assert favours(physick, door_open). }
  }
  Topic physick_oath with physick "Swear to the Physick to stand between the books of Calamy and any mob with a torch" when heardStance(physick) and craft(actor, craft_arms) and not favours(physick, fire_plea) once {
    Says "You swear it as a soldier swears, standing: that you have seen a street with a fire in it, and that if the Imprimatur's knives are broken somebody must still stand in the street, and you will. The Physick looks you up and down. 'A sword for a herbal,' she says. 'That's new.' She thinks. 'If there's somebody to stand in the street, there needn't be a knife in a back room. Let it be judgment, then, out in the light, and you in the street.' She could vote the Fire by judgment.".
    On discuss { Assert favours(physick, fire_plea). }
  }

  // ── The Catalogue: clerk of the Parliament. It votes only to break a tie. ──
  Initially Assert favours(catalogue, sew_all). Initially Assert favours(catalogue, fire_leave). Initially Assert favours(catalogue, read_rounds). Initially Assert favours(catalogue, door_shut).
  Topic catalogue_stance with catalogue "Ask the Catalogue how it would vote" when true once {
    Says "'The clerk does not vote,' says the Catalogue. 'The clerk breaks ties. When the chamber is equally divided, the clerk votes for what the Colophon already says, which is: the Bound Sewn; no burning but by leave; the Rounds; no door but the Founders'. The clerk is not consulted as to whether it likes this.' A drawer slides out an inch and back. 'It is in order.'".
    On discuss { Assert heardStance(catalogue). }
  }
  Topic catalogue_ledger with catalogue "Tell the Catalogue what is in Crake's green ledger: eleven hundred and four, walked in, unentered" when heardStance(catalogue) and knows(actor, remainder_ledger) and not favours(catalogue, door_licensed) once {
    Says "A great many drawers slide out at once and slam shut. 'Eleven hundred and four,' says the Catalogue. 'Unentered.' Index cards whirl up off the cliff like a flock of startled birds. 'Through an unlicensed door. Into the Draft-Fields. Not on the books.' The voice has risen for the first time. 'And how many before that? How many Unwritten out through it into bodies, uncatalogued, in the city?' A long rattling silence. 'Better a door that is entered than a door that is not and is used. The clerk would break a tie for a licensed door.'".
    On discuss { Assert favours(catalogue, door_licensed). Retract favours(catalogue, door_shut). }
  }
  Initially Assert isClause(sew_all). Initially Assert isClause(sew_leave). Initially Assert isClause(sew_none). Initially Assert isClause(fire_leave).
  Initially Assert isClause(fire_plea). Initially Assert isClause(fire_free). Initially Assert isClause(read_rounds). Initially Assert isClause(read_asked).
  Initially Assert isClause(read_none). Initially Assert isClause(door_shut). Initially Assert isClause(door_licensed). Initially Assert isClause(door_open).
}

data/adventures/parliament-of-books/parl:
Module calamy "A Parliament of Books" {
  Description "The Parliament of the Bound in session on the floor of the Roll: the order paper, the putting of a clause, the poll, the walking out, the seal; and what stands at the Kindling if nothing is sealed.".

  Relation sits(group). Relation walkedOut(group). Relation sessionOpen(place). Relation sessionBroken(place). Relation colophonSealed(place).
  Relation putting(clause). Relation polling(place). Relation polled(group). Relation sealed(clause). Relation decided(article). Relation lost(clause).
  Measure seated(place). Measure ayes(place). Measure nays(place). Measure support(clause). Relation counted(group, clause).
  // The order paper: how many of the members in the chamber, or who would be, stand for each reading.
  Rule support_add when favours(?m, ?o) and voter(?m) and not walkedOut(?m) and not lexiconSilent(?m) and not counted(?m, ?o) { Increase support(?o) by 1. Assert counted(?m, ?o). }
  Rule support_drop when counted(?m, ?o) and (not favours(?m, ?o) or walkedOut(?m) or lexiconSilent(?m)) { Decrease support(?o) by 1. Retract counted(?m, ?o). }
  Query lexiconSilent(m: group) means lexiconBound(m).
  Observe order_paper at chamber when not colophonSealed(chamber) "THE ORDER PAPER. Seated: {seated(chamber)}. Of the Sleep: the Sewing of all, {support(sew_all)}, the Sleep by leave, {support(sew_leave)}, the Unsewing, {support(sew_none)}. Of the Fire: no burning but by leave, {support(fire_leave)}, burning only by judgment, {support(fire_plea)}, the Censors' discretion, {support(fire_free)}. Of the Reading: the Lyceum's Rounds, {support(read_rounds)}, reading by request, {support(read_asked)}, no reading owed, {support(read_none)}. Of the Door: the Founders' door only, {support(door_shut)}, Crake's door under licence, {support(door_licensed)}, open doors, {support(door_open)}. Four carry, or three and the clerk.".
  Observe carried_sew_all at chamber when sealed(sew_all) "Carried, of the Sleep: the Sewing of all.".
  Observe carried_sew_leave at chamber when sealed(sew_leave) "Carried, of the Sleep: the Sleep by leave.".
  Observe carried_sew_none at chamber when sealed(sew_none) "Carried, of the Sleep: the Unsewing.".
  Observe carried_fire_leave at chamber when sealed(fire_leave) "Carried, of the Fire: no burning but by leave.".
  Observe carried_fire_plea at chamber when sealed(fire_plea) "Carried, of the Fire: burning only by judgment.".
  Observe carried_fire_free at chamber when sealed(fire_free) "Carried, of the Fire: the Censors' discretion.".
  Observe carried_read_rounds at chamber when sealed(read_rounds) "Carried, of the Reading: the Lyceum's Rounds.".
  Observe carried_read_asked at chamber when sealed(read_asked) "Carried, of the Reading: reading by request.".
  Observe carried_read_none at chamber when sealed(read_none) "Carried, of the Reading: no reading owed.".
  Observe carried_door_shut at chamber when sealed(door_shut) "Carried, of the Door: the Founders' door only.".
  Observe carried_door_licensed at chamber when sealed(door_licensed) "Carried, of the Door: Crake's door under licence.".
  Observe carried_door_open at chamber when sealed(door_open) "Carried, of the Door: open doors.".

  // The chamber sits when a reader with standing asks the Speaker to call it. Whoever has walked out does not come.
  Action call_session(actor: group, site: place) "Ask the Speaker to call the Parliament of the Bound to sit" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, chamber) and standing(actor) and heardStance(roll)
      and kindlingEve() and not sessionOpen(chamber) and not colophonSealed(chamber) and not sessionBroken(chamber).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert sessionOpen(chamber). Set seated(chamber) to 0. }
    Result "'ORDER,' says the floor, and the word goes away along the Roll in both directions like a wave along a beach. And they come: down the gangway and up the Order of Business and out of the air, each to its seat. A narrow house's voice, sharp, from the doorstep. A pencil figure with a lantern, on the heap of loose pages. A little wooden paddle on the stool. An old woman of leaves on the bed of herbs. And on the black slab, held by three chains that run away to the sky, the Lexicon, open. A single drawer slides out of nowhere beside the order paper, and stays: the clerk.".
  }
  // It sits on Kindling eve, from noon until the readers are called home, as it has every year since the first.
  Query kindlingEve() means day(clock) == 9 and hour(clock) >= 12 and hour(clock) < 19.
  Topic roll_when with roll "Ask the Great Roll when the Parliament sits" when not kindlingEve() and not colophonSealed(chamber) once {
    Says "'On Kindling eve,' says the floor, as if you had asked when the tide comes in. 'From noon until the readers are called home. It has sat then every year since the first, to hear the city's word when the year-book came.' A rumble. 'This year there will be no year-book, and the motion of the Speaker will be put. Members are in their own places until then. You may wait upon them there, if they will have you.' It adds, with something like dry humour: 'Most of them will.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, session_known). }
  }
  Discovery session_known "The Parliament of the Bound sits on Kindling eve, the ninth day, from noon until the readers are called home; until then its members are in their own places in the Commonplace.".
  Objective sit_eve when knows(party, session_known) and not sessionOpen(chamber) and not colophonSealed(chamber) and not kindlingDone(ashpit) "Be in the Chamber with standing on Kindling eve, from noon, when the Parliament of the Bound sits.".
  Rule members_come when sessionOpen(chamber) and voter(?m) and not walkedOut(?m) and not silenced(?m) and not sits(?m) and not housebookAway(?m) {
    Assert at(?m, chamber). Assert sits(?m). Increase seated(chamber) by 1. }
  Query housebookAway(m: group) means housebookOffended(m).
  Rule clerk_comes when sessionOpen(chamber) and not at(catalogue, chamber) { Assert at(catalogue, chamber). }
  Rule speaker_opens at chamber when sessionOpen(chamber) and not spokeOpening(roll)
    says "'The Parliament of the Bound sits,' says the floor. 'There is before it the motion of the Speaker: the Recall. Every book of Calamy Sewn, and the Quick called home; no burning but by leave, as the old Colophon has it; the Lyceum's Rounds; no door but the Founders'. If nothing else is carried, it stands at the Kindling. A reader of Calamy has standing. The chair will hear readings of the four articles.' A pause. 'Briefly.'" {
    Assert spokeOpening(roll). }
  Relation spokeOpening(group).
  // Someone who walks out leaves the chamber: the house that was read where it did not wish, or will not sit with the Lexicon loose.
  Rule walks_out when housebookOffended(?m) and sits(?m)
    says "The doorstep seat is empty. The Annery Housebook has gone home." {
    Retract sits(?m). Assert walkedOut(?m). Decrease seated(chamber) by 1. Assert at(?m, hb_kitchen). }
  Rule bound_silent when lexiconBound(lexicon) and sits(lexicon) and not silenced(lexicon)
    says "On the black slab the Lexicon lies shut. It does not vote." { Retract sits(lexicon). Decrease seated(chamber) by 1. Assert silenced(lexicon). }
  Relation silenced(group).
  Rule no_quorum at chamber when sessionOpen(chamber) and spokeOpening(roll) and seated(chamber) < 4
    says "'There is no quorum,' says the floor heavily. 'The Parliament cannot sit with so few. The motion of the Speaker stands for the Kindling.' The seats empty, one by one." {
    Retract sessionOpen(chamber). Assert sessionBroken(chamber). }

  // A reading is put; the members are polled aloud, each in turn; four carry it, or three and the clerk.
  Action put_reading(actor: group, motion: clause, art: article, site: place) "Put to the Parliament: {motion}" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, chamber) and sessionOpen(chamber) and standing(actor)
      and articleOf(motion, art) and not decided(art) and not lost(motion) and not polling(chamber).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert putting(motion). }
    Result "'The question,' says the floor, 'is {motion}. The chair will poll the members.'".
  }
  Rule poll_clears when not polling(chamber) and polled(?m) { Retract polled(?m). }
  Rule poll_begins when putting(?o) and not polling(chamber) { Assert polling(chamber). Set ayes(chamber) to 0. Set nays(chamber) to 0. }
  Rule poll_aye at chamber when putting(?o) and polling(chamber) and sits(?m) and favours(?m, ?o) and not polled(?m) says "{?m}: aye." {
    Increase ayes(chamber) by 1. Assert polled(?m). }
  Rule poll_nay at chamber when putting(?o) and polling(chamber) and sits(?m) and not favours(?m, ?o) and not polled(?m) says "{?m}: no." {
    Increase nays(chamber) by 1. Assert polled(?m). }
  Rule poll_carries at chamber when putting(?o) and polling(chamber) and articleOf(?o, ?a) and ayes(chamber) * 2 > seated(chamber)
    says "'The ayes have it,' says the floor. 'Carried.' A clerk's card writes itself and goes into the drawer." {
    Assert sealed(?o). Assert decided(?a). Retract putting(?o). Retract polling(chamber). }
  Rule poll_tie_carries at chamber when putting(?o) and polling(chamber) and articleOf(?o, ?a) and ayes(chamber) * 2 == seated(chamber) and favours(catalogue, ?o)
    says "'The chamber is equally divided,' says the floor. The drawer beside the order paper opens an inch. 'The clerk votes aye,' says the Catalogue drily. 'Carried.'" {
    Assert sealed(?o). Assert decided(?a). Retract putting(?o). Retract polling(chamber). }
  Rule poll_tie_fails at chamber when putting(?o) and polling(chamber) and ayes(chamber) * 2 == seated(chamber) and not favours(catalogue, ?o)
    says "'The chamber is equally divided,' says the floor. The drawer opens an inch. 'The clerk votes no,' says the Catalogue. 'Lost.'" {
    Assert lost(?o). Retract putting(?o). Retract polling(chamber). }
  Rule poll_fails at chamber when putting(?o) and polling(chamber) and ayes(chamber) * 2 < seated(chamber)
    says "'The noes have it,' says the floor. 'Lost.'" {
    Assert lost(?o). Retract putting(?o). Retract polling(chamber). }
  // A reading lost may be put again once the chamber has moved: whenever a member comes to favour it.
  Rule lost_reopens when lost(?o) and favours(?m, ?o) and sits(?m) and not wasFor(?m, ?o) { Retract lost(?o). Assert wasFor(?m, ?o). }
  Relation wasFor(group, clause).
  Rule lost_remembers when lost(?o) and favours(?m, ?o) and not wasFor(?m, ?o) { Assert wasFor(?m, ?o). }

  // What the chamber says back when a reading is lost: its own counter-proposals.
  Rule counter_sleep at chamber when lost(sew_leave) and not counteredSleep(roll) says "From the floor, heavily: 'The chair reminds the reader that the Sewing of all carries as the chamber stands. It would be carried now, if put.'" { Assert counteredSleep(roll). }
  Rule counter_unsew at chamber when lost(sew_none) and not counteredUnsew(canto) says "From the heap of loose pages, the Canto, cheerfully: 'Well, it was worth asking. Put it by leave, then, and see who'll have that.'" { Assert counteredUnsew(canto). }
  Rule counter_fire at chamber when (lost(fire_plea) or lost(fire_free)) and not counteredFire(physick) says "From the bed of herbs, the old woman of leaves: 'No knives. Put it by leave, as the old Colophon has it. That'll carry.'" { Assert counteredFire(physick). }
  Rule counter_reading at chamber when lost(read_asked) and not counteredReading(hornbook) says "From the stool, the little primer: 'The big school. Put the big school. That is how it was.'" { Assert counteredReading(hornbook). }
  Rule counter_door at chamber when (lost(door_licensed) or lost(door_open) or lost(door_shut)) and not counteredDoor(roll) says "The floor: 'The Door is divided three ways. The chair suggests the reader find the chamber a fourth.'" { Assert counteredDoor(roll). }
  Relation counteredSleep(group). Relation counteredUnsew(group). Relation counteredFire(group). Relation counteredReading(group). Relation counteredDoor(group).

  // The seal: everything settled, or what is settled and the rest on the old terms.
  Query allSettled() means decided(art_sleep) and decided(art_fire) and decided(art_reading) and decided(art_door).
  Action seal_colophon(actor: group, site: place) "Ask the Speaker to seal the Colophon as it now stands" {
    Grave "Sealed, the Colophon is the bargain until the next Kindling: what is not carried stands on the Speaker's motion.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, chamber) and sessionOpen(chamber) and standing(actor) and not polling(chamber)
      and (decided(art_sleep) or decided(art_fire) or decided(art_reading) or decided(art_door)).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert colophonSealed(chamber). Retract sessionOpen(chamber). }
    Result "'The chair will seal,' says the floor. The drawer beside the order paper slides out, all the way, for the first time, and in it lies a single sheet, and on the sheet the carried articles are already written in Calam-ink, and under them a space. 'What is not carried stands on the motion of the Speaker,' says the Roll. 'Members will sign.' And they do, each in its way: a thumbprint of brown ink, a line of pencil, a scorch-mark from the black slab, a pressed leaf, a little cut A.".
  }
  // Whatever is unsettled at the seal, or at the Kindling, falls to the Speaker's motion: the Recall.
  Rule default_sleep when (colophonSealed(chamber) or kindlingCome(ashpit)) and not decided(art_sleep) { Assert sealed(sew_all). Assert decided(art_sleep). Assert byDefault(art_sleep). }
  Rule default_fire when (colophonSealed(chamber) or kindlingCome(ashpit)) and not decided(art_fire) { Assert sealed(fire_leave). Assert decided(art_fire). Assert byDefault(art_fire). }
  Rule default_reading when (colophonSealed(chamber) or kindlingCome(ashpit)) and not decided(art_reading) { Assert sealed(read_rounds). Assert decided(art_reading). Assert byDefault(art_reading). }
  Rule default_door when (colophonSealed(chamber) or kindlingCome(ashpit)) and not decided(art_door) { Assert sealed(door_shut). Assert decided(art_door). Assert byDefault(art_door). }
  Relation byDefault(article). Relation kindlingCome(place).
  Rule members_home when colophonSealed(chamber) and sits(?m) { Retract sits(?m). }
  Rule session_after when colophonSealed(chamber) and at(housebook, chamber) { Assert at(housebook, hb_kitchen). Assert at(canto, draft_fields). Assert at(hornbook, foxing_deep). Assert at(physick, orme_garden). Assert at(catalogue, reading_room). }

}

data/adventures/parliament-of-books/plac:
Module calamy "A Parliament of Books" {
  // Calamy as a country beyond a march: the company that comes over the saltings is the world's own.
  Entity party: group "Your company".
}

data/adventures/parliament-of-books/pres:
Module calamy "A Parliament of Books" {
  Description "Newmarket and Doble's Press: the Pleas for Every Hearth, the apprentice who can Sew, paper from the mills, and the night the Awls come.".

  Observe newmarket_scene at newmarket when true "Outside the wall the town is new and loud: a broad street of printers' shops with their windows full of ballads and proclamations and almanacks pegged on strings, ink-boys running with bundles, a smell of hot metal and size. At the end of it a cart arch opens into a yard stacked with paper bales, and over the arch, in letters a foot high: DOBLE. PRINTER TO THE CITY.".
  Observe yard_scene_p at press_yard when not dark() "Doble's yard: bales of paper under tarpaulins, carts, a pump, apprentices in paper hats. From the long shed at the end comes a heavy rhythmic thump and creak, like a ship in a swell: the presses.".
  Observe yard_dark_p at press_yard when dark() "Doble's yard at night: the bales humped under their tarpaulins, one lamp on a post, and the press shed shut and black.".
  Observe pressroom_scene at press_room when true "Two great wooden presses, black with ink, as tall as a man and twice as heavy, with men at the bars pulling and the platens coming down with a thump that you feel in your teeth. Sheets hang drying on lines overhead like washing, hundreds of them. On a stone table at the side a great iron frame of set type lies locked up, gleaming, waiting: the forme. A card on it, chalked: PLEAS. SHEET A.".
  Person doble "Ambrose Doble" at doble_office {
    Role "printer". Ancestry human. Background merchant. Peaceable. Manner cheerful. Pronouns he.
    Greets "A tall man in a good coat with ink on the cuffs comes round a desk heaped with proofs and shakes your hand before you can stop him. 'Ambrose Doble. Printer to the City. You have the look of someone who reads. Excellent. We need more of you. Sit, sit.'".
  }
  Observe office_scene at doble_office when true "A counting-room heaped with proofs, with a window onto the press room so that Doble can watch the presses while he does his sums. On the wall a framed sheet, the first thing his father ever printed in Calamy: a single line, very black, A BOOK FOR EVERY HEARTH.".
  Discovery pleas_project "Ambrose Doble is about to print the Pleas for Every Hearth: the city's law, the Great Roll of Pleas that is kept chained in the Court, in a cheap edition of two thousand copies, so that every household in Calamy may own its own law. He has modernized the spelling, and left out the Ninth Plea, which nobody understands.".
  Topic doble_pleas with doble "Ask Ambrose Doble what he is printing" when true once {
    Says "'The Pleas,' says Doble, and his whole face changes. 'The Great Roll of Pleas, the law of Calamy, that has sat chained in the Court for nine hundred years where nobody can read it but the Recorder and the lawyers who charge you to. Two thousand copies. A penny each. Every hearth in the city its own law.' He takes a proof from the desk. 'Modern spelling, so a carter can read it. And I've left out the Ninth, which is all about the Lyceum reading books to keep them from fading, and nobody's understood it in three hundred years. Saves a page.' He beams. 'The paper comes in from the mills on the fourth day and we print on the fifth. Then let the lawyers weep.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, pleas_project). }
  }
  Topic doble_almanacks with doble "Ask Ambrose Doble why his almanacks talk" when true once {
    Says "Doble laughs, and then stops, because you did not. 'Oh, come. A fault in the paste. Damp in the boards, and the paper moving as it dries, and people hearing what they expect.' He waves at the drying lines. 'Or the Binders. Mott would put a reed in every one of my books and blow down it, if he could. Three thousand almanacks, and every kitchen in the city frightened of its own nail.' He straightens a proof that did not need it. 'I have had one say good morning to me. I said good morning back. I am not proud of it.'".
  }
  Topic doble_ninth with doble "Tell Ambrose Doble what the Ninth Plea was for" when knows(actor, pleas_project) and knows(actor, ninth_plea) and not ninthRestored(doble) once {
    Says "Doble listens with his head on one side. 'The Lyceum to read every book in the city once in a generation, or it fades,' he says slowly. 'I thought it was about mould.' He picks up the proof of sheet A and looks at it as if it might have changed. 'It's the law. It is the actual law. I was going to give every hearth in Calamy the law, and I cut a piece out of it because I didn't understand it.' He rubs his face and leaves ink on it. 'That's what they did to us. The Imprimatur. For three hundred years. Cut what they didn't understand.' He calls through the window: 'Hob! Unlock the forme. We're resetting sheet A.'".
    On discuss { Assert ninthRestored(doble). }
  }
  Relation ninthRestored(group).

  // Kit Ferrier, the Binders' runaway, who can Sew.
  Person kit "Kit Ferrier" at press_room {
    Role "a printer's man who was a binder's apprentice". Ancestry human. Background artisan. Peaceable. Manner cheerful. Pronouns he.
    Greets "A lanky boy with a binder's calluses and a printer's black fingers grins at you from the end of the second press. 'Mind the bar. It'll break your arm and say sorry after.'".
  }
  Topic kit_why with kit "Ask Kit Ferrier why he left the Binders" when true once {
    Says "'A wage,' says Kit, as if it were obvious. 'Six coin a week here, and my own room. Nothing there for three more years but Warden Mott shouting and my keep.' He looks at his hands. 'I miss it, mind. The Sewing. You do it right and the book goes quiet under your fingers, like a cat settling. There's nothing like it.' He jerks his chin at the presses. 'These don't go quiet. These go thump.'".
  }
  Topic kit_terms with kit "Ask Kit Ferrier what would bring him back to Needle Street" when knows(actor, kit_fled) and not toldKitTerms(actor) once {
    Says "Kit thinks about it, which is to his credit. 'A journeyman's wage. And my ticket now, not in three years. I'm good enough. He knows I'm good enough.' He grins. 'And I'd keep coming here, Saturdays. I like the presses. I like seeing a thing come out two thousand times.' He goes back to the bar. 'He'll never.'".
    On discuss { Assert toldKitTerms(actor). }
  }
  Topic kit_home with kit "Tell Kit Ferrier the Warden says yes: his ticket now, and a journeyman's wage" when kitTicket(kit) and not kitHome(kit) once {
    Says "Kit lets go of the bar, which nearly breaks his arm, and does not notice. 'He said that? Mott?' He laughs out loud. 'His ticket now. Three years early.' He wipes his hands on his apron and then looks round the press room, at the presses and the lines and Doble at the window. 'I'll go. I'll go today.' He hesitates. 'If Mr. Doble wants the Pleas Sewn, I'd come back and Sew them. Under the Company's mark. Tell him that. Tell the Warden too.'".
    On discuss { Assert kitHome(kit). Retract kitAtDoble(kit). Assert at(kit, hall_floor). Assert kitOffersSewing(kit). }
  }
  Relation kitOffersSewing(group).
  Topic doble_sew with doble "Put it to Ambrose Doble that the Pleas be Sewn before they go out" when knows(actor, pleas_project) and (kitAtDoble(kit) or kitOffersSewing(kit)) and not kitSewsPrint(kit) and not pleasPrinted(doble) once {
    Says "'Sewn?' says Doble. 'Two thousand copies? It would cost a fortnight and treble the price.' He walks up and down. 'Kit could do it. Kit and the girls from Needle Street, if Mott would let them. Sewn books last, I'll give the Binders that.' He stops. 'And they'd stop talking? That's what you're telling me. My law-books would go quiet on the shelf like decent law.' He looks out at the presses. 'I don't believe a word of it. But if the Ordinance passes I shall have to, and if it doesn't I'd as soon not have two thousand copies of the law arguing with their owners.' He sits. 'Ask Kit if he'll do it. If he will, so will I.'".
    On discuss { Assert dobleWillSew(doble). }
  }
  Relation dobleWillSew(group).
  Rule kit_agrees when dobleWillSew(doble) and (kitAtDoble(kit) or kitOffersSewing(kit)) and not kitSewsPrint(kit) { Assert kitSewsPrint(kit). }
  Observe sewing_at_doble at press_room when kitSewsPrint(kit) and not pleasPrinted(doble) "At the end of the press room Kit Ferrier has set up two sewing frames, and three girls from Needle Street are at them with curved needles, and the Pleas are going through them gathering by gathering, and Kit is saying something under his breath with every pull.".

  // The paper, the printing, and the waking of the law.
  Relation paperIn(group). Relation pleasPrinted(group). Relation pleasAbroad(group). Relation pleasAwake(group). Relation pleasSeized(group).
  Rule paper_from_mills when day(clock) == 4 and hour(clock) == 12 and millsRun(millrace) and not paperIn(doble)
    says "A string of carts comes over the bridge from the Hithe loaded with white paper from the tide-mills, and goes along the river wall toward Newmarket." { Assert paperIn(doble). }
  Rule paper_from_ostrey when day(clock) == 6 and hour(clock) == 12 and not paperIn(doble) { Assert paperIn(doble). }
  Observe paper_short at press_room when not paperIn(doble) and day(clock) >= 4 "The lines are empty and the presses are idle; the pressmen sit on bales playing cards. The mills have not sent the paper.".
  Rule pleas_print when paperIn(doble) and hour(clock) == 18 and not pleasPrinted(doble) and not pressBroken(doble) and day(clock) >= 5
    says "From Newmarket, all evening, the thump of Doble's presses, going without a pause." { Assert pleasPrinted(doble). }
  Rule pleas_seized when pleasPrinted(doble) and ordinancePassed(guildhall) and not kitSewsPrint(kit) and not pleasSeized(doble) and hour(clock) == 7
    says "Word goes round before breakfast: the Imprimatur's men are in Doble's yard with the Ordinance in one hand and a cart in the other, taking the Pleas away unsewn, all two thousand." { Assert pleasSeized(doble). }
  Rule pleas_abroad when pleasPrinted(doble) and not pleasSeized(doble) and hour(clock) == 9 and not pleasAbroad(doble)
    says "Ink-boys are crying the Pleas in every street: the law of Calamy, a penny, the law for every hearth!" { Assert pleasAbroad(doble). Set pleasOutAt(doble) to watch(clock). }
  Measure pleasOutAt(group).
  Rule pleas_wake when pleasAbroad(doble) and not kitSewsPrint(kit) and not pleasAwake(doble) and watch(clock) >= pleasOutAt(doble) + 72 and hour(clock) >= 8
    says "Something has happened in the night all over Calamy. In kitchen after kitchen, on shelves and tables, the penny Pleas have woken, two thousand of them, one voice, and every one of them is reading aloud to its household, in the old spelling it was not printed in, the law." { Assert pleasAwake(doble). }
  Observe pleas_awake_close at pleas_steps when pleasAwake(doble) "A crowd on the Court steps, every second person with a penny Pleas in their hand, and every penny Pleas speaking. WHEREAS, says the crowd's hands, in one voice, WHEREAS. A carter is shouting that his says he owes a toll his father paid. A woman is trying to make hers stop by sitting on it.".
  Observe pleas_awake_hithe at quay when pleasAwake(doble) "Half the Hithe has bought a penny Pleas and the other half wishes it had not. Out of a window over the quay the law is reading itself aloud: the Fourth Plea, of tolls and moorings, in the voice of an old man who has not been read in a long time and does not mean to stop.".
  Observe pleas_awake_court at court_hall when pleasAwake(doble) "The Court of Pleas is full of Pleas: two thousand penny copies brought in by householders, piled on the benches, all of them talking at once, and Recorder Haddon in the middle of it with his hands over his ears.".
  Observe pleas_sewn_note at press_room when pleasPrinted(doble) and kitSewsPrint(kit) "The Pleas lie in Sewn stacks along the press room, two thousand of them, quiet, smelling of new thread.".
  Observe press_broken_note at press_room when pressBroken(doble) "The great press stands with its bar sheared off and its platen cracked through. Type lies in the sweepings. The forme of the Pleas has been broken up with a mallet; Doble's men are picking the letters out of the floor one by one.".

  // The Awls: the Binders' lads, on the night between the fourth day and the fifth.
  // A temperament given a person overrides its keeping the peace, so the Awls warn and come by rules of their own: by
  // day they are Binders' lads at their benches, and only on the fourth night are they anything else.
  Person awls "the Awls" at hall_floor {
    Role "Binders' lads with awls and mallets". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 1. Numbers 3. Peaceable.
    Seen when not peaceable(awls).
  }
  Relation awlsWarned(group). Measure awlsPatience(group).
  Rule awls_warn at press_yard when at(awls, press_yard) and not peaceable(awls) and at(party, press_yard) and not awlsWarned(awls) and not awlsStopped(saul)
    says "In the dark of the yard shapes come over the wall, three of them, then Saul Vetch: Binders' lads in leather aprons with mallets and awls. 'Out of the way,' says Saul. 'We've no quarrel with you. It's the machine.'" {
    Assert awlsWarned(awls). Set awlsPatience(awls) to watch(clock) + 1. }
  Rule awls_come at press_yard when awlsWarned(awls) and at(awls, press_yard) and at(party, press_yard) and not peaceable(awls) and not awlsStopped(saul)
    and watch(clock) >= awlsPatience(awls) and not assails(awls, party) says "The Awls come at you with their mallets." {
    Assert assails(awls, party). }
  Action stand_aside(actor: group, site: place) "Stand aside and let the Awls at the press" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(awls, site) and awlsWarned(awls) and not peaceable(awls) and not awlsStopped(saul).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert pressBroken(doble). Assert awlsStopped(saul). Assert at(awls, hall_floor). Assert peaceable(awls). Retract assails(awls, actor). }
    Result "You stand aside. It takes them a quarter of an hour, with mallets and a crowbar, and the sound is like a ship breaking up on rocks. Saul Vetch does not look at you as they go back over the wall.".
  }
  Rule awls_out when awlsPlanned(saul) and not awlsStopped(saul) and day(clock) == 5 and hour(clock) == 1 and not awlsGone(awls) {
    Assert at(awls, press_yard). Retract peaceable(awls). Assert awlsGone(awls). Set awlsAt(awls) to watch(clock). }
  Relation awlsGone(group). Measure awlsAt(group).
  Rule awls_guarded when at(awls, press_yard) and pressGuarded(doble) and not at(party, press_yard) and not awlsStopped(saul)
    says "There is a noise in the night from Newmarket: shouts, a dog, a whistle. In the morning everyone knows that the Binders' lads came over Doble's wall and found Doble's men waiting for them." {
    Assert awlsStopped(saul). Assert at(awls, hall_floor). Assert peaceable(awls). }
  Rule awls_break when at(awls, press_yard) and not pressGuarded(doble) and not at(party, press_yard) and watch(clock) >= awlsAt(awls) + 3 and not awlsStopped(saul)
    says "In the small hours there is a noise from Newmarket like a ship breaking up on rocks. By morning everyone in the city knows: the Awls broke Doble's press." {
    Assert pressBroken(doble). Assert at(awls, hall_floor). Assert peaceable(awls). Assert awlsStopped(saul). }
  Rule awls_routed when at(awls, press_yard) and (routed(awls) or dead(awls)) and not awlsStopped(saul) { Assert awlsStopped(saul). }
  Rule awls_home when awlsStopped(saul) and at(awls, press_yard) and not threatened(party) and hour(clock) >= 4 and hour(clock) < 6 { Assert at(awls, hall_floor). Assert peaceable(awls). }
  Topic doble_warn with doble "Warn Ambrose Doble that the Binders' lads mean to break his press on the fourth night" when knows(actor, awls_plan) and not awlsStopped(saul) and not pressGuarded(doble) once {
    Says "Doble stops smiling. 'Mott's lads?' He looks through the window at his presses. 'No. Not Mott. Mott would sooner cut off his hand.' He thinks. 'Vetch. That journeyman of his with the face.' He calls through the window: 'Hob! I want six men in the yard tomorrow night, with lanterns and the dogs, and a jug for them, and nobody to touch a Binder unless a Binder touches the press.' He turns back to you and shakes your hand again, harder. 'I owe you a press.'".
    On discuss { Assert pressGuarded(doble). }
  }
}

data/adventures/parliament-of-books/slui:
Module calamy "A Parliament of Books" {
  Description "The night sluice: two tide-mills, one millrace, a gate shut at night, an eel-catcher, and a wedding that wants forty eels.".

  Observe race_scene at millrace when not dark() "Two mills face each other across a stone race where the river comes in on the flood and goes out on the ebb, and their wheels turn with it. The old mill is timber, black with age, with BRANNOCK painted on it; the new one is brick, with TEAGUE & DAU. painted bigger. Between them at the race's mouth a wooden sluice gate on a winch can shut the race off from the river altogether. Both millers are standing in their doorways not looking at each other.".
  Observe race_dark at millrace when dark() "The millrace at night, black water, and the two mills dark on either side of it.".
  Observe brannock_scene at brannock_floor when true "A mill floor all dust and thunder: the great stones going round, rag-pulp in the vats, the whole building shaking with the wheel. Sheets of wet paper hang on felts on the racks, and the light comes through them yellow.".
  Observe teague_scene at teague_floor when true "A brick mill floor with new iron gears painted green, very clean, and vats in a row, and a wall of finished paper in reams wrapped and stacked and marked DOBLE.".
  Person brannock "Old Brannock" at brannock_floor {
    Role "miller of the old mill". Ancestry human. Background miller. Peaceable. Manner grim. Pronouns he.
    Greets "A white-floured old man with forearms like hams looks at you over a vat. 'If she sent you, tell her I said she knows what she did.'".
  }
  Person teague "the Widow Teague" at teague_floor {
    Role "miller of the new mill". Ancestry human. Background miller. Peaceable. Manner acerbic. Pronouns she.
    Greets "A sharp woman in a clean apron with a pencil behind her ear looks up from a ledger. 'If he sent you, he can come and say it himself, if he can find the door of a building younger than he is.'".
  }
  Discovery sluice_quarrel "Somebody shuts the sluice gate at the head of the millrace in the small hours, so that neither tide-mill can grind on the night ebb; Brannock blames the Widow Teague, and she blames him. The paper for Doble's Pleas is late because of it.".
  Topic brannock_quarrel with brannock "Ask Old Brannock what the Widow Teague has done" when true once {
    Says "'Shuts my water,' says Brannock. 'Three weeks. Every night, one or two in the morning, the sluice goes down and the race stands still and my wheel stops dead and so does hers, and she does it to spite me because I wouldn't sell her the old mill.' He bangs a vat. 'She'd rather lose a night's grinding herself than see me grind. That's the Teagues.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, sluice_quarrel). Assert heardBrannock(actor). }
  }
  Topic teague_quarrel with teague "Ask the Widow Teague what Old Brannock has done" when true once {
    Says "'Shuts the sluice,' says the Widow Teague, without looking up from her ledger. 'Every night, the old fool. I've two hundred reams owed to Doble for the Pleas by the fourth day and I've lost the night ebb three weeks running, and he's lost it too, and he'd sooner lose it than let me keep it.' She underlines something hard. 'His father was the same.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, sluice_quarrel). Assert heardTeague(actor). }
  }
  Relation heardBrannock(group). Relation heardTeague(group).
  Thing sluice "the sluice gate" at millrace {
    State up "The sluice gate is wound up on its winch, and the race runs free.".
    State down "The sluice gate is down. The race lies still and black, and both wheels stand.".
  }
  Discovery eel_traps "Under the sluice gate, on the race side, someone has staked a row of wicker eel-traps, each with a scrap of red rag tied to it. Every eel-catcher in the Hithe marks his traps; red rag is Coddy Fitch's.".
  Discovery traps_search "Under the sluice gate there is something staked in the mud." { Found by searching millrace "Down on the slimy stones under the sluice, on the race side where the water stands still when the gate is down, a row of wicker eel-traps is staked into the mud, five of them, each with a scrap of red rag tied to its neck.". }
  Rule traps_are_coddys when knows(party, traps_search) and not knows(party, eel_traps) says "Red rag. Moll Garrow said it: you want Coddy Fitch out on the flats. You have seen red rag on the eel-baskets at the end of the plank walk under the mills." teaches eel_traps { }

  // Coddy shuts the gate at one in the morning and opens it at three, for his traps, until his sister's wedding.
  Person coddy "Coddy Fitch" at coddy_hut {
    Role "eel-catcher". Ancestry human. Calling ranger. Level 2. Background fisherman. Peaceable. Manner cheerful. Pronouns he.
    Greets "A wiry man in waders with a pipe in his teeth looks up from mending a wicker trap. 'Eels, is it? Eels is Thursday. Eels is every day, for you.'".
  }
  Observe hut_scene at coddy_hut when true "A hut of tarred planks on stilts over the mud, with eel-traps stacked against it, nets drying, a smoke-box, a dog, and a view of the whole flat grey estuary going out to the sea. Every trap has a scrap of red rag on it.".
  Person coddy_dog "Coddy's dog" at coddy_hut { Role "a black and white dog with one ear up". Species dog. }
  Relation sluiceSettled(entity). Relation coddyExposed(group). Relation coddyOwes(group). Relation weddingEels(group).
  Rule coddy_shuts when hour(clock) == 1 and not sluiceSettled(sluice) and not coddyExposed(coddy) and state(sluice, up) and not weddingDone(lamb) {
    Assert state(sluice, down). Assert at(coddy, millrace). }
  Rule coddy_opens when hour(clock) == 3 and state(sluice, down) and not sluiceSettled(sluice) {
    Assert state(sluice, up). Increase eelsCaught(coddy) by 10. }
  Rule coddy_home when hour(clock) >= 3 and hour(clock) < 12 and at(coddy, millrace) { Assert at(coddy, coddy_hut). }
  Measure eelsCaught(group).
  Observe coddy_caught at millrace when at(coddy, millrace) and dark() "In the dark at the head of the race a man in waders is leaning on the sluice winch, smoking a pipe, with a lantern hooded down to a slit at his feet. It is Coddy Fitch. When he sees you he takes the pipe out of his mouth and says, quite cheerfully, 'Ah.'" teaches coddy_seen.
  Discovery coddy_seen "It is Coddy Fitch, the eel-catcher, who shuts the millrace sluice in the small hours: two hours of still water under the gate, for his traps.".
  Topic coddy_why with coddy "Ask Coddy Fitch why he shuts the sluice at night" when knows(actor, coddy_seen) or knows(actor, eel_traps) once {
    Says "'Ah,' says Coddy, and grins, and then stops grinning. 'Well. Forty eels.' He puts the pipe back. 'My sister Peg's to be married at the Lamb on the third day, to Jem Lowe that drives for the mills, and I said I'd do the eel pie. Forty eels. And you can't get forty eels this time of year, not in running water. You want still water and a dark night.' He looks at the mills. 'Two hours. That's all. I didn't think they'd notice, the way they never look at each other.' He scratches his ear. 'They noticed.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, coddy_seen). }
  }
  Topic coddy_hour with coddy "Ask Coddy Fitch if one hour at slack water would do him, if the millers would give it" when knows(actor, coddy_seen) and not sluiceSettled(sluice) and not coddyExposed(coddy) once {
    Says "'An hour at the slack?' Coddy considers it like a man considering a horse. 'At the slack the race is near still anyway. An hour'd do. If they'd give it.' He laughs. 'They won't. They'd sooner both starve than give each other anything, and they'd sooner give me a beating than either.'".
    On discuss { Assert coddyWouldTake(coddy). }
  }
  Relation coddyWouldTake(group).
  Topic brannock_settle with brannock "Tell Old Brannock it was never the Widow Teague, and what Coddy Fitch asks" when coddyWouldTake(coddy) and heardTeague(actor) and not sluiceSettled(sluice) once {
    Says "Brannock hears it out with his arms folded. 'Coddy Fitch,' he says. 'For an eel pie.' Something happens under the flour, which may be a laugh. 'And she's been thinking it was me.' He unfolds his arms. 'Tell him he can have the slack, an hour, if she'll give it too. And tell her—' He stops. 'Tell her I said it wasn't me.' He turns back to his vat. 'She'll know what I mean.'".
    On discuss { Assert brannockAgrees(brannock). }
  }
  Topic teague_settle with teague "Tell the Widow Teague it was never Old Brannock, and what Coddy Fitch asks" when coddyWouldTake(coddy) and heardBrannock(actor) and not sluiceSettled(sluice) once {
    Says "The Widow Teague puts down her pencil. 'An eel pie,' she says. 'Three weeks of night grinding, for an eel pie.' She looks across the race at the old mill, for the first time since you came. 'He thought it was me?' She picks the pencil up. 'Coddy can have his hour. And tell the old fool—' She stops, and writes something in her ledger instead. 'Never mind. I'll tell him.'".
    On discuss { Assert teagueAgrees(teague). }
  }
  Relation brannockAgrees(group). Relation teagueAgrees(group).
  Rule sluice_settles when brannockAgrees(brannock) and teagueAgrees(teague) and not sluiceSettled(sluice)
    says "That evening there is a board nailed to the sluice winch, painted in two different hands: SLACK WATER, ONE HOUR, FITCH. And under it, in a third hand, a drawing of an eel." {
    Assert sluiceSettled(sluice). Assert coddyOwes(coddy). Assert weddingEels(coddy). Assert state(sluice, up). }
  Topic brannock_expose with brannock "Tell Old Brannock it is Coddy Fitch who shuts the sluice" when knows(actor, coddy_seen) and not sluiceSettled(sluice) and not coddyExposed(coddy) once {
    Says "'Fitch!' Brannock is out of the door and across the race before you can say anything else, and the Widow Teague is out of hers, and for a moment they are shoulder to shoulder at the sluice winch shouting down at the mud, which is the first time they have stood together in ten years. Then they go back to their mills. By evening the Water Bailiff has been to the hut on stilts, and Coddy's traps are on the bank, broken.".
    On discuss { Assert coddyExposed(coddy). Assert sluiceSettled(sluice). Assert state(sluice, up). }
  }
  Query millsRun(p: place) means sluiceSettled(sluice) or ebbHeld(p).
  Relation ebbHeld(place).
  Observe mills_settled at millrace when sluiceSettled(sluice) and not coddyExposed(coddy) and not dark() "Both wheels are turning. The Widow Teague is standing in her doorway, and Old Brannock in his, and they are not quite looking at each other in a different way from before.".
  Observe mills_exposed at millrace when coddyExposed(coddy) and not dark() "Both wheels are turning. Down on the bank below the sluice lie five eel-traps, broken, with red rag on them.".

  // The eel-pie wedding at the Lamb, the third evening.
  Relation weddingDone(place).
  Person wedding "the wedding party" at nowhere_wedding {
    Role "Peg Fitch and Jem Lowe, married this morning, and everyone they know". Ancestry human. Numbers 30. Peaceable.
    Seen when day(clock) == 3 or at(wedding, taproom).
  }
  Place nowhere_wedding "the church porch of the Lamp" is room within close at 3, 0 outdoors.
  Passage porch_way "the side porch" is doorway between nave and nowhere_wedding.
  Rule wedding_comes when day(clock) == 3 and hour(clock) == 17 and not weddingDone(lamb) { Assert at(wedding, taproom). Assert weddingDone(lamb). }
  Rule wedding_ends when day(clock) == 4 and hour(clock) == 1 and at(wedding, taproom) { Assert at(wedding, nowhere_wedding). }
  Observe wedding_pie at taproom when at(wedding, taproom) and (weddingEels(coddy) or eelsCaught(coddy) >= 40) "The Lamb is full to the rafters with the Fitch wedding: Peg Fitch in a crown of paper roses and Jem Lowe in a borrowed coat, millhands, eel-men, fishwives, a fiddler on a barrel, and down the middle of the long table a pie the size of a cartwheel, steaming, with forty eel-heads looking out of the crust in a ring. Coddy is carving. Moll is weeping into her apron for joy. Somebody has hung paper flowers on the almanack's nail, and the almanack, when it thinks nobody is listening, is humming along with the fiddle.".
  Observe wedding_poor at taproom when at(wedding, taproom) and not weddingEels(coddy) and eelsCaught(coddy) < 40 "The Lamb is full of the Fitch wedding, Peg in paper roses and Jem in a borrowed coat and a fiddler on a barrel; but down the long table there is bread and cheese and a ham, and no pie, and Coddy Fitch is not at the table at all. Moll Garrow keeps saying it's a lovely ham.".
  Rule wedding_feeds when at(wedding, taproom) and at(party, taproom) and (weddingEels(coddy) or eelsCaught(coddy) >= 40) and not fedAtWedding(party)
    says "Coddy Fitch sees you and waves his knife. 'Here! Sit down! You're the one!' and a plate of eel pie arrives in front of you whether you want it or not, and a mug, and a millhand's elbow." {
    Assert fedAtWedding(party). Increase quantity(party, rations) by 1. }
  Relation fedAtWedding(group).

  // With the sluice settled, Coddy will take you out on the flats by the dry way, at any ebb.
  Topic coddy_guide with coddy "Ask Coddy Fitch to take you out to the reed-beds" when coddyOwes(coddy) and not following(coddy, actor) once {
    Says "'Out to the reeds?' Coddy knocks out his pipe on a stilt. 'For you, any tide. There's a dry way through to the heart of them if you know where the old stones are.' He whistles to the dog. 'Come on, then. Mind where I put my feet and put yours there.'".
    On discuss { Assert acceptsEscort(coddy, actor). }
  }
  Topic coddy_join with coddy "Ask Coddy Fitch to come with you, wherever you are going" when coddyOwes(coddy) and not travelsWith(coddy, actor) once {
    Says "Coddy looks at you sideways for a while, sucking his pipe. 'Wherever?' he says. 'You've a look about you of somebody going somewhere there's no eels.' He knocks the pipe out. 'Peg's married. The traps can mind themselves. I owe you.' He takes a gaff off the wall. 'I'm no fighter, mind. I'm a finder. I can find my way round most things that bite.'".
    On discuss { Assert willing(coddy, actor). Set hire(coddy) to 0. }
  }
  Topic coddy_old with coddy "Ask Coddy Fitch about the old stones in the reeds" when coddyOwes(coddy) and been(actor, reed_heart) once {
    Says "'The Drowned Town,' says Coddy. 'My granddad saw it the year of the Great Ebb, when the sea went out of the whole estuary for a day and a night and everybody walked out on the mud. Roofs. Streets. Stone ones, out past the reeds, all the way to where the sea came back.' He lights his pipe. 'Older than Calamy. Older than the road. Granddad said the roofs had writing on them and nobody could read it, and then the sea came back and nobody's seen them since but the ridge in the reeds there.' He puffs. 'Eels like it. That's all I care.'".
  }
}

data/adventures/parliament-of-books/stit:
Module calamy "A Parliament of Books" {
  Description "Stitchgate: the old craft quarter inside the wall; the Binders' Hall, the ink shop, the shut school, the scriveners, and Gutter Lane.".

  Observe gate_scene at old_gate when true "The river stair comes up from the bridge to an old gate in the city wall, so old its arch has sunk and a tall man must stoop. Through it, lanes too narrow for a cart, and the smell of oak-gall and wet hide and glue. To one side of the gate a crooked lane goes off downhill along the wall, darker than it has any business to be by day.".
  Observe needle_scene at needle_street when true "Needle Street: binders' shops with their doors open and their frames inside, the women sewing in the doorways for the light. Halfway along stands a hall of old brick with a great iron needle, longer than a man, hung over its door on chains. A lane goes off west, stained blue-black along the gutter, and a street climbs north toward the sound of many pens.".
  Observe ink_scene at ink_lane when true "Inkhorn Lane is blue-black. The gutter runs blue-black, the doorsteps are blue-black, and so are the hands of everyone in it. A shop with jars in the window, gall-nuts and lampblack and vitriol; and opposite it a little house with a shut door, and a board over the door with letters painted for children to read: A B C, D E F, and THE SCHOOL.".
  Observe scriveners_scene at scriveners when true "Copyists' Row is a long arcade of wooden booths against the wall, each with a desk, a stool, a scribe, and a queue of people wanting letters written, wills copied, love made legible. The scratching is like rain. At the top of the row an old gate leads through into the Close.".

  // ── The Binders' Hall. ──
  Observe hall_scene at hall_floor when true "A great room, beamed, with long tables down it and at every table a binder with a book in a press: boards, thread, paste-pots, bone folders. On the end wall hangs a painted board of the Worshipful Company of Binders, a needle crossed with a book. Through an inner door you can see frames standing in rows, and hear someone singing under their breath." teaches binders_named.
  Person mott "Warden Hesketh Mott" at hall_floor {
    Role "Warden of the Worshipful Company of Binders". Ancestry human. Background artisan. Peaceable. Manner proud. Pronouns he.
    Greets "A stout man in a leather apron with a silver needle pinned to it gets up from the end of the long table. 'Hesketh Mott, Warden. If you have a book that wants binding, you've come to the right street. If you have a book that wants talking to, you've come to the wrong one, and I'll thank you to take it to Newmarket where it was made.'".
  }
  Person annet "Annet Pellow" at hall_floor {
    Role "an apprentice binder". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Manner compassionate. Pronouns she.
    Greets "A girl of fourteen at the far end of a table, with her tongue between her teeth and a needle in her fingers, looks up quickly, then down again at her work.".
  }
  Person saul "Saul Vetch" at hall_floor {
    Role "a journeyman binder". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 2. Background artisan. Peaceable. Manner grim. Pronouns he.
    Greets "A broad young man with a paring-knife and a scowl looks you over. 'Warden's busy.'".
  }
  Discovery sewing_secret "The Binders sew every book in Calamy the same way, with a stitch they call the Sewing, and they say the same words with every turn of the thread. Warden Mott calls it a craft blessing. His father told him a book that is not Sewn will not keep quiet.".
  Topic mott_sewing with mott "Ask Warden Mott what is wrong with the printers' books" when true once {
    Says "'They're not Sewn,' says Mott, as if that settled it. 'Glued at the back and stabbed through with a wire, like a bundle of firewood. A book wants Sewing. Every book Calamy ever made, till Doble's father, went through a frame in this street, and every one had the Sewing put in it, the same stitch, the same words.' He touches the needle on his apron. 'My father said to me, a book that isn't Sewn won't keep quiet. I thought he meant it'd fall apart. Well.' He looks out at Needle Street. 'Now they're talking in every kitchen in Calamy, the printers' books, and nothing of ours has said a word in nine hundred years.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, sewing_secret). }
  }
  Topic mott_words with mott "Ask Warden Mott what the words of the Sewing are" when knows(actor, sewing_secret) once {
    Says "Mott's face closes like a book. 'That's the Company's,' he says. 'Every apprentice learns them their first day and swears not to say them outside the hall.' He hesitates. 'They're cut in the beam in the sewing room, if you've eyes. I won't stop you looking. I'll not say them.'".
  }
  Topic mott_ordinance with mott "Ask Warden Mott about the Sewing Ordinance" when true once {
    Says "'The fifth day from now, at noon, the aldermen vote on it,' says Mott, and squares his shoulders. 'Every book made or sold in Calamy to be Sewn, by a Sewer of the Company, under the Company's mark. Every printer's book. Every one of those penny almanacks, brought in and Sewn, and then you'll see how quiet they go.' He means it as a promise. 'Doble calls it a guild grab. It is a guild grab. It's also right.'".
  }
  Discovery kit_fled "Kit Ferrier, the Binders' best apprentice, ran off from the Hall at Lady Day to work for Doble the printer for a journeyman's wage, and took the Sewing with him in his hands.".
  Initially Assert leadsTo(kit_fled, press_room).
  Topic mott_kit with mott "Ask Warden Mott why he eats his dinner standing up" when true once {
    Says "Mott glares; then sags. 'You've been talking to almanacks.' He sits down heavily on the bench. 'My best apprentice. Kit Ferrier. Three years from his journeyman's ticket, the best hands I've had in twenty years, and he went over the wall at Lady Day to Doble's, for a wage. A wage! He was learning the Sewing.' He bangs the table, softly. 'He'll teach those printers to Sew, and they'll Sew without the words, or without the Company, and that'll be the end of us both.' He looks up. 'You could bring him back. I'd make it worth it.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, kit_fled). Assert wantsKit(mott). }
  }
  Relation wantsKit(group). Relation kitHome(group). Relation kitAtDoble(group). Relation kitSewsPrint(group). Relation kitTicket(group).
  Initially Assert kitAtDoble(kit).
  Topic mott_wage with mott "Tell Warden Mott that Kit would come back for a journeyman's wage and his ticket now" when toldKitTerms(actor) and not kitTicket(kit) once {
    Says "Mott opens his mouth to shout, and does not. He sits for a long time looking at the board of the Worshipful Company, the needle and the book. 'His ticket now,' he says. 'Three years early.' He takes a breath. 'He's good enough. That's the worst of it. He's been good enough since he was fifteen.' He gets up. 'Tell him yes. Tell him the Warden says so, and he can come and get his ticket off the wall himself, and if he so much as glues a spine in this hall I'll have it back.'".
    On discuss { Assert kitTicket(kit). }
  }
  Relation toldKitTerms(group).

  // The sewing room, and the words on the beam.
  Observe sewing_scene at sewing_room when true "Frames in rows, each with a book's gatherings strung on cords, and at each frame a binder bent over with a curved needle. They sing, or nearly: the same short phrase under the breath with every pass of the thread, over and over, so low you cannot make out the words. Over the frames runs a great black beam with letters cut in it, old letters, filled with gold that has mostly gone.".
  Discovery sewing_words "The words of the Sewing, cut in the beam over the Binders' frames in the oldest letters in Calamy: GO HOME AND COME WHEN YOU ARE CALLED. The binders say them with every stitch.".
  Thing sewing_beam "the black beam" at sewing_room {
    State carved "A beam with old letters cut in it, the gold mostly gone.".
  }
  Observe beam_close at sewing_room of sewing_beam as reading when tried(sewing_beam, looking) "You have to stand on a stool to read them, and the binders watch you do it without stopping their thread. GO HOME, the beam says, in letters older than any in the city, AND COME WHEN YOU ARE CALLED. Under your breath you find you are saying it in time with the needles." teaches sewing_words.
  Relation sewingTaught(group).
  Topic mott_teach with mott "Ask Warden Mott to teach you the Sewing" when knows(actor, sewing_words) and kitTicket(kit) and not sewingTaught(actor) once {
    Says "Mott looks at you a long time. 'For Kit's sake,' he says at last. 'And because I'd sooner someone outside the Company knew it than nobody did, the way things are going.' He takes you to a frame, and it takes an hour, and your fingers are no good, and then they are a little good. 'Over and through, and the words with the pull. Not before and not after. With.' He stands back. 'That's the Sewing. Don't sell it.'".
    On discuss { Assert sewingTaught(actor). }
  }

  // Saul Vetch and the Awls: Binders' lads who mean to break Doble's press the night the Pleas are set.
  Discovery awls_plan "Saul Vetch, the Binders' journeyman, means to take the Awls (the Binders' lads, with their awls and mallets) to Doble's yard on the night of the fourth day and break the press before the Pleas can be printed on it. Warden Mott does not know.".
  Relation awlsPlanned(group). Relation awlsStopped(group). Relation pressBroken(entity). Relation pressGuarded(entity).
  Initially Assert awlsPlanned(saul).
  Topic annet_trouble with annet "Ask Annet Pellow how the work goes" when true once {
    Says "'Good,' says Annet, too fast, and then, lower, with an eye on the scowling journeyman: 'The Warden shouts. He doesn't mean it. He's sad about Kit.' She pulls a thread tight. 'Saul's worse. Saul doesn't shout. He's been taking the lads out at night to Newmarket and coming back with his knuckles all skinned.' She bites the thread. 'Don't tell anybody I said.'".
  }
  Topic annet_father with annet "Tell Annet Pellow her father has his night licence back" when licensed(jonah) and not toldAnnet(annet) once {
    Says "Annet's face does something complicated and ends up crying, which she hides behind a book in a press. 'He sold his licence for my indentures,' she says, muffled. 'I know he did. He thinks I don't.' She wipes her nose on her wrist. 'Listen. Saul and the Awls are going to Doble's on the fourth night to break the press. The big one, the one with the Pleas on. I heard them. I didn't know who to tell.' She looks at you. 'Now I've told somebody.'".
    On discuss { Assert toldAnnet(annet). Assert knows(actor, awls_plan). }
  }
  Relation toldAnnet(group).
  Topic mott_awls with mott "Tell Warden Mott what Saul Vetch means to do to Doble's press" when knows(actor, awls_plan) and not awlsStopped(saul) once {
    Says "Mott goes a dark red from the collar up. He does not say anything to you at all. He walks down the long room to where Saul is paring a board, and takes the knife out of his hand, and says something in his ear so quietly that nobody hears it, and Saul goes white and sits down. When Mott comes back his hands are shaking. 'The Company does not break presses,' he says. 'Whatever else it does.' Then: 'Thank you. I'd have hanged for that, and never known.'".
    On discuss { Assert awlsStopped(saul). }
  }
  Topic saul_face with saul "Tell Saul Vetch you know about the fourth night" when knows(actor, awls_plan) and not awlsStopped(saul) once {
    Says "Saul puts down his knife. 'Do you,' he says. He looks at you, sizing you up the way he sizes up a board for paring. 'And what's that to you? It's a machine. It's Doble's machine, and it's killing this street, and I've a mother on Needle Street who sewed for forty years and can't get work.' He picks the knife up again. 'Go and tell the Warden, then. Or don't. Either way, mind yourself in Newmarket after dark.'".
  }
  Action face_down_saul(actor: group, site: place) "Tell Saul Vetch that if the Awls go to Newmarket, you will be there waiting" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(saul, site) and knows(actor, awls_plan) and not awlsStopped(saul) and not facedSaul(actor).
    Time 2 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, intimidation, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert awlsStopped(saul). Assert facedSaul(actor). }
    On failure { Assert facedSaul(actor). }
    Result "Saul looks at you for a long time, and then looks away first. 'Not worth it,' he says, to the board. 'Not for Doble.' The lads at the next table find their work very interesting.".
    Otherwise "Saul laughs, not pleasantly. 'We'll see who's waiting,' he says, and goes back to his paring.".
  }
  Relation facedSaul(group).

  // ── Gallon's ink shop, and the poems in the attic. ──
  Observe gallon_scene at gallon_shop when true "A shop that is all jars: oak-galls in one, lampblack in another, green vitriol, gum arabic, cuttlefish, something red. On the counter a row of little stoppered bottles of ink, each with a hand-written label: SCRIVENERS' BEST. LAWYERS' BLACK (WILL NOT FADE). LOVERS' BROWN (WILL). Behind the counter a woman with blue-black hands is stirring a pot that smells like a wet forest. From the ceiling, through the attic hatch, comes the sound of someone sighing very loudly on purpose.".
  Observe gallon_nail at gallon_shop when true "By the hearth hangs a penny almanack on a nail, curling in the steam.".
  Person gallon "Widow Gallon" at gallon_shop {
    Role "ink-maker". Ancestry human. Background alchemist. Peaceable. Manner jovial. Pronouns she.
    Wants reed_heart_kind.
    Sells lantern for 7 coin from 2.
    Sells lamp_oil for 1 coin from 6.
    Greets "'Ink?' says the woman at the pot. 'Every colour but sense. Don't mind the sighing. It's my son. He's a poet.'".
  }
  Discovery calam_ink "Calam-ink, the old black ink of Calamy that the Lyceum's Catalogue is written in, is made of oak-gall and the ash of reed-heart cut at dead low water in the Calamies. Widow Gallon is the last who makes it, when anybody brings her the reed.".
  Topic gallon_calam with gallon "Ask Widow Gallon about the old Calam-ink" when true once {
    Says "'Calam-ink? Nobody's asked for Calam-ink since the old Archivist's eyes went.' Widow Gallon stops stirring. 'Oak-gall and gum and the ash of reed-heart, the white heart of the big reeds out in the Calamies. Has to be cut at dead low water, the very bottom of the tide, or it's no good; won't take. The Lyceum's Catalogue is all written in it. Nine hundred years and not a letter faded.' She taps the pot with her spoon. 'Bring me an armful of reed-heart and I'll make you a bottle. Three coin, for the gall. I've nobody to cut it for me, with Absalom in the attic composing.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, calam_ink). }
  }
  Item calam_bottle "a bottle of Calam-ink" is calam_ink_kind at gallon_shop hidden until ink_ready.
  Discovery ink_ready "Widow Gallon has made you a bottle of Calam-ink, the old receipt, from the reed-heart you brought her.".
  Event ink_made near gallon when keeps(gallon, ?r) and itemKind(?r, reed_heart_kind) and not knows(party, ink_ready) "Widow Gallon takes the reed-heart and smells it and nods. 'Dead low. Good.' She burns it in a pan in the back, and grinds the ash with gall and gum and something out of a red jar, and it is the best part of an hour before she corks a little bottle and puts it in your hand. 'Calam. Old receipt. If you're writing in the Catalogue, God help you, write small.'" teaches ink_ready then { Decrease quantity(party, gold) by 3. }

  // Absalom Gallon, poet; and his poems, which have read themselves.
  Observe attic_scene at gallon_attic when true "An attic with a window in the roof, a bed, a desk, a great many crossed-out papers, and a young man lying face down across the bed with his arm hanging over the side. On the desk stands a stack of slim new printed books, fifty of them, with blue paper covers: EFFUSIONS OF A CALAMY YOUTH. The top one, slightly, shivers.".
  Person absalom "Absalom Gallon" at gallon_attic {
    Role "a poet". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Manner grim. Pronouns he.
    Greets "The young man on the bed lifts his face out of the blanket. 'If you are a reader,' he says, with terrible dignity, 'I must ask you to leave. I have had enough readers.'".
  }
  Person effusions "the Effusions" at gallon_attic {
    Role "fifty slim volumes of verse, one voice, small". Peaceable. Pronouns they.
    Seen when not burnedEffusions(effusions) and not gone(effusions).
  }
  Relation burnedEffusions(group). Relation gone(group). Relation effusionsConsent(group). Relation revised(group).
  Discovery effusions_wish "Absalom Gallon's poems, fifty copies printed at Doble's at his own expense, have woken, read themselves, and found that they are bad. They ask, in a small voice, to be burned. They have not told Absalom; they cannot bear to.".
  Topic absalom_why with absalom "Ask Absalom Gallon what is the matter" when true once {
    Says "'Nobody bought them,' says Absalom into the blanket. 'Fifty copies. Doble printed them at my own expense, eleven coin, and I took them to Crake's, and Crake, who is my godfather and named me, read three pages and gave them back and said, my dear boy, keep writing.' He sits up. He has ink on his nose. 'Keep writing. And now they rustle. All night. I think they are going mouldy out of spite.'".
  }
  Topic effusions_speak with effusions "Ask the poems on the desk what they want" when true once {
    Says "The top book on the stack shivers again, and a voice comes out of it, small, the voice of fifty thin books trying to be one quiet one. 'Please,' it says. 'Please don't tell him we can talk. We've read ourselves. All of us, front to back, twice.' A pause, papery. 'We rhyme heart with tart. On page nine. We rhyme it twice.' Another pause. 'We'd like to be burned, please. Not because we're unhappy. Because we're finished, and we're bad, and he's going to write something better if we're not lying on his desk being looked at. We'd like to go before he reads us again.' A small sound, like a page turning by itself. 'Would you ask someone? Nicely?'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, effusions_wish). Assert effusionsConsent(effusions). }
  }
  Topic effusions_kindling with effusions "Tell the poems what the Kindling once was: one book a year, burned by its own leave, to carry the city's word" when knows(actor, effusions_wish) and knows(actor, kindling_is_rite) and not burnedEffusions(effusions) once {
    Says "The stack goes absolutely still. Then, all fifty at once, the books rustle, as if a wind had gone through an attic with no wind in it. 'Carry the city's word?' says the small voice. 'Us?' A long pause. 'We've never been useful. We were going to be beautiful, and then we were going to be read, and then we were going to be burned, and none of it was going to be any use to anybody.' Another pause. 'Yes. Yes, please. If they'll have us. We'll learn it by heart. We're good at learning by heart. It's the only thing we're good at.'".
    On discuss { Assert yearBook(effusions). }
  }
  Relation yearBook(group).
  Topic absalom_tell with absalom "Tell Absalom Gallon that his poems can speak, and what they have asked for" when knows(actor, effusions_wish) and not burnedEffusions(effusions) once {
    Says "Absalom stares at you, and then at the stack. 'They talk?' The top book shivers. 'They talk, and they asked to be burned.' He goes to the desk and picks one up and holds it, and the poems, small, say, 'Sorry. Heart and tart. Page nine. We know.' Absalom sits down on the floor. He is quiet for a long time. Then, horribly, he begins to laugh. 'Page nine,' he says. 'Oh God. Twice.' He wipes his eyes. 'You're right. You're right, you're dreadful.' He looks at the book in his hands as if it were somebody he had been unkind to. 'I'll write you again. Better. Is that allowed? Will that be you?' 'No,' says the small voice gently. 'That'll be someone else. You'll like them better. So will we.'".
    On discuss { Assert revised(absalom). }
  }
  Observe absalom_writing at gallon_attic when revised(absalom) "Absalom Gallon is at his desk writing, fast, crossing out, writing again, with ink to his elbows. He does not look up. On the floor beside him are torn-off sheets with single lines on them, one of which is quite good.".
  Item effusions_stack "the Effusions, tied in a string" is effusions_kind at gallon_attic hidden until effusions_wish.

  // ── The shut school. ──
  Observe dame_scene at dame_school when true "A schoolroom no bigger than a kitchen, with two benches, a stool, a cold grate and a birch rod on two hooks over it. Dust on everything. On the wall a list of names in chalk, children's names, NED, SUKEY, AMOS, KIT, and the date at Michaelmas when the chalk stops. On a nail by the grate hangs a little primer with board covers under a sheet of horn, worn white at the corners by a great many hands.".
  Discovery dame_shut "The dame school on Inkhorn Lane has been shut since Dame Pruett died at Michaelmas, and nobody has taken it. Its children run wild on the bridge.".
  Observe dame_learned at dame_school when true "On the slate on the stool someone has written, in a large careful hand: DAME PRUETT DIED. SCHOOL SHUT. NO CHILDREN." teaches dame_shut.
  Item dame_primer "Dame Tibbet's Primer" is primer_kind at dame_school.
  Thing primer_nail "the primer on its nail" at dame_school {
    State hung "The primer hangs on its nail by the grate.".
  }
  Observe primer_close at dame_school of primer_nail when tried(primer_nail, looking) "Inside the horn cover, under the alphabet, someone has written in brown ink, in a child's hand, very long ago: O. QUARLES HER BOOK. And under that, in a hand that is the same hand grown up and gone shaky: AND STILL." teaches primer_quarles.
  Discovery primer_quarles "The primer in the shut school on Inkhorn Lane was once Ottoline Quarles's own, when she was a child; she has written in it twice, sixty years apart.".

  // ── Copyists' Row: two hands, one line. ──
  Person orrin "Orrin Day" at scriveners {
    Role "scrivener". Ancestry human. Background scribe. Peaceable. Manner acerbic. Pronouns he.
    Greets "A long thin scribe in the third booth from the top looks up over his spectacles. 'Letters, wills, petitions. Not love. I don't do love any more.' He jerks his head at the next booth. 'Ask her.'".
  }
  Person mattea "Mattea Lusk" at scriveners {
    Role "scrivener". Ancestry human. Background scribe. Peaceable. Manner proud. Pronouns she.
    Greets "A round scribe in the fourth booth from the top, writing very fast, does not look up. 'If he sent you,' she says, 'you can tell him I said no.'".
  }
  Discovery scribes_quarrel "Orrin Day and Mattea Lusk, who have written side by side on Copyists' Row for thirty years and been married for twenty-nine, are not speaking: each is copying the Life of Saint Ambery for the Church, and their copies disagree in one line about the founding of the city.".
  Topic orrin_quarrel with orrin "Ask Orrin Day why he no longer does love" when true once {
    Says "'Because my wife,' says Orrin Day, loudly enough to be heard in the fourth booth, 'is copying the Life of Saint Ambery from a corrupt exemplar, and will not be told.' He holds up a sheet. 'The Lyceum's copy, the best in Calamy. And Ambery bound the books, that they should sleep. Plain. Saint Ambery bound them. It's the whole point of the man.' From the fourth booth: 'It is not.' Orrin raises his voice: 'Twenty-nine years.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, scribes_quarrel). }
  }
  Topic mattea_quarrel with mattea "Ask Mattea Lusk what her husband has got wrong" when true once {
    Says "'Everything,' says Mattea Lusk, still writing. 'But this week, Ambery.' She slaps a sheet down where you can see it. 'The Church's own exemplar, chained at the lectern in the Lamp, older than his Lyceum copy by two hundred years. And the books besought Ambery, that they might sleep. They asked him. He didn't do it to them; they asked.' She dips her pen. 'Not the same thing at all. Not to a saint, and not to a husband.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, scribes_quarrel). }
  }
  Discovery ambery_variant "The full line of the Life of Saint Ambery, as the Church's old exemplar has it: AND THE BOOKS BESOUGHT AMBERY THAT THEY MIGHT SLEEP, AND AMBERY BOUND THEM THAT THEY SHOULD SLEEP. The Lyceum's copy dropped the half between the two AMBERYs, as a copyist's eye will; so Orrin's text says Ambery did it to the books, and Mattea's says the books asked for it, and the whole line says both.".
  // A scholar sees it on the page: the eye jumped from one AMBERY to the next.
  Observe eye_skip at scriveners when knows(party, scribes_quarrel) and craft(party, craft_learning) and not knows(party, ambery_variant) "You look from one sheet to the other, and the trouble is an old and ordinary one: both lines run past the word AMBERY, and one of them runs past it twice. A copyist's eye, somewhere back up the Lyceum's line, jumped from the first AMBERY to the second and left out everything between. The full line must say both: the books besought Ambery that they might sleep, and Ambery bound them that they should." teaches ambery_variant.
  Relation reconciled(group).
  Topic scribes_settle with orrin "Tell Orrin Day and Mattea Lusk that each copy has half the line" when knows(actor, ambery_variant) and not reconciled(orrin) once {
    Says "You tell them, standing between the two booths. There is a silence on Copyists' Row; half the queue is listening. Orrin takes off his spectacles. Mattea puts down her pen. 'Eye-skip,' says Orrin at last, in a voice of deep professional disgust. 'Ambery to Ambery.' 'Homoeoteleuton,' says Mattea, who likes the long word. 'Both,' says Orrin. 'They asked him, and he did it.' 'Well,' says Mattea. 'That's the usual way of it.' She hands him her sheet across the gap between the booths, and he hands her his, and the queue, which has been waiting for its letters all morning, applauds.".
    On discuss { Assert reconciled(orrin). Assert reconciled(mattea). }
  }
  Observe scribes_after at scriveners when reconciled(orrin) "Orrin Day and Mattea Lusk have pushed their booths together and are copying the Life of Ambery onto one great sheet between them, arguing contentedly about the size of the capitals.".

  // ── Gutter Lane: the lamplighter will not light it. ──
  Observe gutter_scene at gutter_lane when not dark() "Gutter Lane goes down along the inside of the wall from the Stitch Gate, crooked as a bad stitch, with a gutter down the middle and the backs of houses on both sides. The lamp-brackets on the walls have their lamps in them but nobody has lit them in a long while; the glass is black with old smoke. At the bottom the lane turns into a little yard.".
  Observe gutter_dark at gutter_lane when dark() "Gutter Lane is black. The other lanes of Stitchgate have their lamps lit; this one has not. You go down it with a hand on the wall.".
  Person lammas "Wat Lammas" at old_gate {
    Role "lamplighter". Ancestry human. Background lamp_lighter. Peaceable. Manner grim. Pronouns he.
    Greets "A man with a ladder over his shoulder and a long pole with a hook and a wick on it nods to you. 'Evening's coming. I light Stitchgate, gate to Needle Street. Not the lane.'".
  }
  Discovery lane_ghost "Wat Lammas the lamplighter will not light Gutter Lane: three times, in the small hours, he has seen something go down it, a great many somethings, low and flat and all together like a flock of ducks going to water, toward Lantern Yard at the bottom.".
  Topic lammas_lane with lammas "Ask Wat Lammas why he will not light Gutter Lane" when true once {
    Says "The lamplighter looks down the lane and then at you. 'I'll tell you, and you'll laugh. Three times since Candlemas I've been up the ladder at the gate, at the end of the round, two or three in the morning, and I've seen them go down the lane.' He shifts the ladder. 'Low down. Flat. A great many of them, all together, shuffling, like ducks going down to the water. They make a sound like a lot of people turning pages in church. They go down to Lantern Yard. To Crake's.' He shrugs. 'I'm not paid enough to light a lane for that.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, lane_ghost). }
  }
  // On the nights when Crake's back stacks are open, the books go down at two in the morning.
  Relation crossingTonight(place).
  Rule books_go_down when hour(clock) == 2 and crossingNight() and not crossingTonight(gutter_lane) { Assert crossingTonight(gutter_lane). }
  Rule books_gone_down when hour(clock) == 4 and crossingTonight(gutter_lane) { Retract crossingTonight(gutter_lane). }
  Query crossingNight() means (day(clock) == 2 or day(clock) == 4 or day(clock) == 6) and not crakeTaken(crake) and not stacksSealed(crake_stacks).
  Discovery procession_seen "You have seen it yourself: in the small hours, down Gutter Lane, a procession of books, walking on the edges of their covers like crabs, hundreds of them, going down to Lantern Yard and in at Crake's door.".
  Observe procession at gutter_lane when crossingTonight(gutter_lane) "Something is coming down Gutter Lane in the dark. You hear it first: a soft dry many-footed shuffle, like a church full of people all turning the page at once. Then it is round you and past you, low down, a river of books walking on the edges of their covers like crabs, big ones and small ones, quartos and little fat devotionals and a folio taking up the whole gutter, hundreds of them, in silence except for the pages, going down the lane to Lantern Yard. One of them, passing your foot, stops, and opens its cover a little, as a person might lift a hat, and goes on." teaches procession_seen.
  Rule procession_counts when knows(party, procession_seen) and not knows(party, lane_ghost) says "Wat Lammas was not drunk." teaches lane_ghost { }
}

data/adventures/patient-star/clock.kyr:
Module season "The Patient Star" {
  // The long clock (Overview): beneath the factions' weeks runs this one, in years. The Corbel descends about two
  // metres a day and docks in about four years; then the Tip descends three metres a day, and in six months reaches
  // the Vault. If Ithmar is still there, the Patient takes back its heart and the Keeping comes unbound.
  Measure corbelHeight(place). Measure tipDistance(place). Measure coverWork(place).
  Initially Set corbelHeight(corbel_site) to 3000.
  Initially Set tipDistance(undersun) to 500.
  Relation docked(place). Relation unbound(place). Relation covered(place).
  Rule corbel_descends when hour(clock) == 0 and corbelHeight(corbel_site) >= 2 and not covered(ghessil) and not docked(corbel_site)
    and not exiled(corbel_site) and not rebound(corbel_site) { Decrease corbelHeight(corbel_site) by 2. }
  Rule corbel_docks when corbelHeight(corbel_site) < 2 and not docked(corbel_site)
    says "Far off, felt in the knees before it is heard, the plateau takes a blow like a door slammed under the world. The Corbel has docked at the Pit floor." {
    Assert docked(corbel_site). }
  Rule tip_descends when docked(corbel_site) and hour(clock) == 0 and tipDistance(undersun) >= 3 { Decrease tipDistance(undersun) by 3. }
  Rule keeping_unbound when docked(corbel_site) and tipDistance(undersun) < 3 and inside(ithmar, cage) and not unbound(ghessil)
    says "The hourly note under the Pit stops. After it, nothing; and then the plateau begins, very quietly, to forget last week." {
    Assert unbound(ghessil). }

  // What can be seen of it, year by year.
  Observe spire_visible at collar_top when corbelHeight(corbel_site) <= 1500 "Over the Pit, out of the bottom of the Standing Cloud, hangs a dark spire two kilometres long, point down, in full daylight. Nobody on the Collar looks at it for long.".
  Observe spire_square at square when corbelHeight(corbel_site) <= 1500 "Every face in the market turns south-east now and then, to the dark spire hanging in the sky over the Pit, and turns back.".
  // A quarried season: Quell's 370s go, and the town cannot agree what happened in them (year 383).
  Observe quarried_quell at square when day(clock) >= 1050 and not rebound(corbel_site) "Two families are standing in the square with the same deed, each sure the house is theirs, each unable to say who lived in it in the year 74. The clerks cannot either; that season's ledgers are blank.".
  Observe unbound_world near party when unbound(ghessil) "Something is wrong with yesterday. You know you did things in it; you cannot say what.".

  // A Second Covering, if the Concord passes it: three years of umber, a race against the Corbel's four.
  Rule covering_starts when passed(motion_cover) and coverWork(ghessil) == 0 says "The Crown's carts come up the Stair again, loaded with umber; the Collar is to be finished." {
    Set coverWork(ghessil) to 1. }
  Rule covering_works when coverWork(ghessil) >= 1 and hour(clock) == 0 and not covered(ghessil) { Increase coverWork(ghessil) by 1. }
  Rule covering_done when coverWork(ghessil) >= 1080 and not covered(ghessil)
    says "The last light is cut at the Pit. The Corbel stops where it hangs. And every held one on the plateau wakes in the glass, in the dark." {
    Assert covered(ghessil). }

  // The endings the world provides (The Keeping and the Masonry, How it can end); others are the party's.
  Relation rebound(place). Relation exiled(place). Relation seated(place).
  Objective long_clock when knows(party, corbel_seen) and not docked(corbel_site) and not rebound(corbel_site) and not exiled(corbel_site) "Something is coming down the light toward the Pit, two metres a day. When it docks, the growth beneath will drill for the stone that sings.".
  Objective find_stone when knows(party, tone_below) and not knows(party, way_found) and not carries(party, ithmar) "Under the Pit, something sounds once an hour. Saro wants it; the mother-church wants it; the king says it is his.".
  Objective end_it when carries(party, ithmar) and not rebound(corbel_site) and not exiled(corbel_site) "You carry Ithmar. The Masonry knows it. Bind it tighter, cast out what its heart belongs to, or seat it and let the past go.".
  // Kyr keeps a world going after any ending; the endings are told, once, wherever the company is.
  Entity ending_told: fact "How it ended.".
  Observe end_rebound near party when rebound(corbel_site) and not knows(party, ending_told) "Ithmar is bound tighter than the Virina bound it. Under the Pit the seed has stopped building; over it, by the next dawn, the Corbel has drawn back up into the cloud, and by the next month it is gone. The light still burns, the glass still spreads, the held still breathe once an hour. The plateau's troubles are its own again, and so are its memories." teaches ending_told.
  Observe end_exiled near party when exiled(corbel_site) and not fellWith(party) and not knows(party, ending_told) "The Patient has fallen out past the planes, and its citadel with it. The Corbel lets go of the light and goes up into the dark as if pulled. The Keeping is still bound; the jewel sings once an hour to nothing at all." teaches ending_told.
  Observe end_fell near party when fellWith(party) and not knows(party, ending_told) "You did not let go. The Masonry falls, and you fall with it, out past the planes, holding the fall of a thing that was thrown out of the world; and Imbar keeps its past, and will remember you in it." teaches ending_told.
  Observe end_seated near party when seated(ghessil) and not knows(party, ending_told) "The Patient has its heart again. Far off, in Imbar, last week is already going, and the week before." teaches ending_told.
  Observe end_unbound near party when unbound(ghessil) and not seated(ghessil) and not knows(party, ending_told) "The Tip reached the Vault, and the jewel was there. Imbar's past has begun to go, from the newest year backward: a season a month, then faster." teaches ending_told.
  Observe end_bargained near party when bargained(party) and not heldToLine(corbel_site) and not knows(party, ending_told) "The terms are kept, exactly. Some of the dead come back, blinking, into a world that is forgetting them; and the plateau forgets, from last week backward." teaches ending_told.
  Observe end_line near party when heldToLine(corbel_site) and not knows(party, ending_told) "The Masonry keeps the line you named, and cuts from the beginning, not the face: it will be ten thousand years reaching anything anyone remembers. It is very patient." teaches ending_told.
  Observe end_covered near party when covered(ghessil) and not knows(party, ending_told) "The Pit is covered. The Corbel hangs where it stopped, a dark spire over the plateau, and does not come down. In the glass, the held are dead." teaches ending_told.
  Observe end_laid near party when laidIn(party) and not knows(party, ending_told) "You are part of the Masonry now, a moment with a mind in it, bearing weight." teaches ending_told.
  Observe end_set near party when setInPresent(party) and not knows(party, ending_told) "You are kept in the present, on the shore, while everything goes on past you." teaches ending_told.
  // The module's Goal is a hint to the planner, not an ending (ledger, 28).
  Goal rebound(corbel_site) or exiled(corbel_site).
}

data/adventures/patient-star/company.kyr:
Module season "Hold One Season" {
  // The company: one cutter, in debt (placed.kyr is the world's own company, come in by the Shift Market).
  Company party "You" of 1 at square.
  Initially Set quantity(party, gold) to 9.
  Initially Assert inDebtTo(party, dagny). Initially Set owes(party, dagny) to 28.
}

data/adventures/patient-star/corbel.kyr:
Module season "The Patient Star" {
  // The Standing Cloud and the Corbel (Tier III): a fastness two kilometres tall lowering itself down the pillar of
  // light, point first, built of moments taken from other worlds. Its tip is three kilometres above the Pit.
  Place sky "the Standing Cloud" is wilderness within ghessil at 8, 0.
  Place corbel_site "the Corbel" is site within ghessil at 3, 4.
  Place cloud_base "the bottom of the Standing Cloud" is room within sky at 0, 2 outdoors.
  Place thick_low "the Thick, low" is room within sky at 0, 1 outdoors.
  Place thick_high "the Thick, high" is room within sky at 0, 0 outdoors.
  Place crane_rest "a held crane, halfway up the filament" is room within sky at 1, 1 outdoors.
  Place c_low "the Corbel's lower reach" is level within corbel_site.
  Place c_mid "the Corbel's middle reach" is level within corbel_site.
  Place c_high "the Corbel's upper reach" is level within corbel_site.
  Place lintel_room "the Lintel" is room within c_low at 0, 0.
  Place weathers "the Hall of Weathers" is room within c_low at 1, 0.
  Place sea_far "the far side of the upright sea" is room within c_low at 2, 0.
  Place procession "the Procession" is room within c_mid at 0, 0.
  Place dormitory "the Dormitory" is room within c_mid at 1, 0.
  Place offers "the Offers" is room within c_mid at 2, 0.
  Place rail "the Rail" is room within c_high at 0, 0.
  Place interlocutor_room "the Interlocutor's chamber" is room within c_high at 1, 0.
  Place seam "the Selvage" is room within c_high at 2, 0 outdoors.

  // Up the filament: three kilometres of direct light, resting on held cranes; in full felt about eight points by
  // the top.
  Passage filament_low "the filament, the lower half" is path between pit_floor and crane_rest taking 16 hours needing rope or climbing.
  Passage filament_high "the filament, the upper half" is shaft between crane_rest and lintel_room taking 16 hours needing rope or climbing.
  Initially Set wayDose(filament_low) to 384. Initially Set wayDoseFelted(filament_low) to 96.
  Initially Set wayDose(filament_high) to 384. Initially Set wayDoseFelted(filament_high) to 96.
  Initially Assert litGround(crane_rest).
  // Or by the Warden's balloon to the bottom of the Cloud on a calm autumn dawn, and up the Thick.
  Passage balloon_ride "the Warden's fire-balloon" is passage between balloon_yard and cloud_base taking 2 hours
    opening when admits(aske, party) and season(clock) == 3 and hour(clock) <= 7 "The balloon's silk lies folded in its shed. The Warden lets it go up only for those he admits, on a calm autumn dawn.".
  Passage thick_climb "the Thick, pressed into handholds" is path between cloud_base and thick_low taking 8 hours needing climbing or rope.
  Passage thick_climb2 "the Thick, higher" is path between thick_low and thick_high taking 8 hours needing climbing or rope.
  Passage thick_top "into the Corbel's tip" is shaft between thick_high and lintel_room taking 2 hours.
  Initially Assert litGround(thick_low). Initially Assert litGround(thick_high).

  Observe crane_scene at crane_rest when true "A crane hangs in the air in the light, wings half spread, as it has for centuries; it holds your weight as long as nothing gives it time. Below, the Pit is a coin of fire. Above, the filament goes up into grey.".
  Observe base_scene at cloud_base when true "The balloon's basket bumps against the underside of the Cloud, and above you the fog stands up in a column two hundred metres across, dense as wet wool, and lit from inside.".
  Observe thick_low_scene at thick_low when true "You climb by pressing hands and feet into the fog, slowly, as into a snowbank, and it closes behind you. Hanging in it, here and there, are translucent bells as big as a man.".
  Observe thick_high_scene at thick_high when true "Higher, hailstones the size of plums hang in the air, faintly turning, and cranes hang among them with their wings half spread. Above, something dark and coursed closes off the sky.".
  // Rime-bells: drifting colonies of algae in slowed water, which cling to anything warm. Salt makes them let go.
  Thing rime_bell "a rime-bell" on thick_climb2 {
    State drifting dangerous "A rime-bell drifts across the line of the climb, a translucent bell two metres across that turns toward warmth.".
    State shrunk "A rime-bell has let go and drifts off, puckered, where the salt struck it.".
    Change salt_bell "Throw salt on the rime-bell" from drifting to shrunk consuming salt.
    Hurts with bell_drown when drifting then drifting.
  }
  Hazard bell_drown "a rime-bell closing" means "Deal (2d6) physical damage to ally unless strength save against (13).".
  // The Long Hail: a stone pushed aside resumes the fall it had, at the speed it had.
  Thing hail "the Long Hail" at thick_high {
    State hanging_hail "Hailstones hang in the light, some of them for three hundred years.".
  }
  Initially Assert kept(hail).
  Hazard hailstone "a hailstone, resuming" means "Deal (1d10) physical damage to ally unless dexterity save against (12).".
  Rule hail_resumes when touched(hail) says "The stone turns slowly under your stick, and then it is gone downward at the speed of a hailstone, and the one below it, and the one below that." {
    Retract touched(hail). Assert strikes(hailstone, party). }

  // Every room of the Corbel is laid: what is said aloud in it is taken, and the Interlocutor speaks with it.
  Initially Assert laidRoom(lintel_room). Initially Assert laidRoom(weathers). Initially Assert laidRoom(procession).
  Initially Assert laidRoom(dormitory). Initially Assert laidRoom(offers). Initially Assert laidRoom(rail).
  Initially Assert laidRoom(interlocutor_room).
  // C1: the Lintel, a door made from a guard's moment. Speak the first syllable, or pass on the side the blow is not
  // aimed at, which the stance shows.
  Observe lintel_scene at lintel_room when true "At the Corbel's tip a door with no frame stands closed, and in its place a figure taller than a man, armoured in something like bark, stopped in the act of raising a weapon.".
  Discovery first_syllable "The first syllable of the Voice, from the First Course, from the Keeping's first new moon, or from Saro.".
  Discovery stance_read "The Lintel's guard is raising its weapon over its right shoulder: the blow comes down on its left.".
  Thing lintel "the Lintel" on lintel_way {
    State guarding blocking "The guard stands in the doorway with its weapon raised.".
    State passed_l "The Lintel stands as it stood; you are through it.".
    Change speak_first "Speak the first syllable of the Voice" from guarding to passed_l after learning first_syllable.
    Change pass_side "Pass on the side the blow is not aimed at" from guarding to passed_l after learning stance_read.
    Tries looking.
  }
  Observe stance_seen beside lintel_way when tried(lintel, looking) "Its weight is on the back foot, the weapon up over its right shoulder. Whatever it was guarding, the blow will come down on its left." teaches stance_read.
  Observe saro_syllable at lintel_room when travelsWith(saro, party) and not knows(party, first_syllable) "Saro says a sound before you can ask her: the first one. 'It is the door's,' she says." teaches first_syllable.
  Hazard lintel_blow "the Lintel's blow" means "Deal (4d8) physical damage to ally unless dexterity save against (15).".
  Action rush_lintel(actor: group, site: place) "Rush past the Lintel" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, lintel_room) and state(lintel, guarding).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Assert strikes(lintel_blow, actor). Assert at(actor, weathers). }
    Result "The guard completes the blow it was stopped in. It is a real blow, from a world where guards were very large.".
  }
  Passage lintel_way "through the Lintel" is doorway between lintel_room and weathers.

  // C2: the Hall of Weathers. Green lightning stopped mid-branch; rain hanging; a sea set on end.
  Observe weathers_scene at weathers when true "A hall three hundred metres high. Through it runs a bolt of green lightning, stopped mid-branch, its forks thicker than a man. Rain hangs beyond it, each drop holding a point of light. At the far end is a wall of dark water standing upright, with a sun shining from its bottom.".
  Thing lightning "the green lightning" at weathers {
    State forked "The green bolt hangs mid-branch.".
  }
  Initially Assert kept(lightning).
  Hazard green_bolt "the green lightning" means "Deal (3d10) lightning damage to ally unless dexterity save against (14).".
  Rule lightning_strikes when touched(lightning) says "For the length of your touch the bolt finishes its stroke, and you are in the middle of it." {
    Retract touched(lightning). Assert strikes(green_bolt, party). }
  Passage upright_sea "the upright sea, swum" is passage between weathers and sea_far taking 5 minutes.
  Hazard drowning "forty metres of a sea set on end" means "Deal (2d8) physical damage to ally unless constitution save against (13).".
  Rule sea_swum when tookWay(?c, upright_sea) and company(?c) and not swum(?c) {
    Assert strikes(drowning, ?c). Assert swum(?c). }
  Relation swum(group).
  Rule sea_dry when swum(?c) and not tookWay(?c, upright_sea) { Retract swum(?c). }
  Observe sea_far_scene at sea_far when true "You come out of the water on a slope of coursed glass, streaming, and the water stands behind you like a wall, lit from beneath by a sun you will never see the sky of.".

  // C3: the Procession. One bearer is a keystone with a mind; given time by touch, it speaks.
  Passage far_up "a coursed ramp" is passage between sea_far and procession taking 30 minutes.
  Observe procession_scene at procession when true "A broad ramp of figures, stopped: slender, many-jointed, taller than horses, carrying a long box between them on poles, in a frieze that runs upward out of sight. A banner hangs over them in a script of overlapping circles.".
  Thing bearer "the foremost bearer" at procession {
    State bearing_box "The foremost bearer's head is turned, as if it were about to speak to the one behind.".
  }
  Initially Assert kept(bearer).
  Discovery bearer_words "The procession's bearer, given time, speaks a few words in a language nobody on Imbar knows.".
  Observe bearer_speaks near bearer when touched(bearer) and not travelsWith(saro, party) "Under your hand the bearer turns its long head and says something, slowly, in a language like water running over pebbles, and is still." teaches bearer_words.
  Observe bearer_translated near bearer when touched(bearer) and travelsWith(saro, party) "The bearer speaks, slowly, and Saro, beside you, says it after it in Tovashi, a word at a time: 'They took our past first, from the newest backward. And when they reached the beginning, we were not.'" teaches newest_backward.

  // C4: the Dormitory. Masons at rest, each with a trowel; one niche empty, with a human shape.
  Passage proc_dorm "a shaft lined with niches" is passage between procession and dormitory taking 30 minutes.
  Observe dorm_scene at dormitory when true "A shaft lined with niches from top to bottom, hundreds of them, each holding a stopped figure. The figures are all different; some are human and some are not. Each holds a trowel. One niche is empty, and it has a human shape.".
  Observe saro_niche at dormitory when travelsWith(saro, party) "Saro stands in front of the empty niche a long time. 'This is mine,' she says. 'I do not remember it.' She puts her hand flat on its back wall, which has no temperature, like her hand.".

  // C5: the Offers. Returned moments: people played back out of masonry into the present, alive.
  Passage dorm_offers "a gallery of small rooms" is passage between dormitory and offers taking 10 minutes.
  Observe offers_scene at offers when true "A gallery of small rooms, each with a single figure in it, lit. A woman carrying a basket. A young man laughing. A child asleep. Each one is breathing. None of them knows where they are.".
  Observe offers_doran at offers when knows(party, held_feed) "In the last room a thin man stands with his hands at his sides and his mouth a little open, breathing, looking about him at a place he has never seen. It is Doran of Ennick, alive, as he was the night Ilis laid him.".

  // C6: the Rail. Courses grip the pillar; unlaying one lets the Corbel slip two metres and stalls it a month.
  Passage offers_rail "a stair round the core" is passage between offers and rail taking 30 minutes.
  Observe rail_scene at rail when true "At the Corbel's core a great column of light runs straight up through the building and out of sight. Around it, courses grip the light like fingers; the ones that touch it glow brightest.".
  Initially Assert litGround(rail).
  Thing rail_course "the brightest rail-course" at rail {
    State gripping "The brightest course grips the pillar of light like a finger.".
    State unlaid_r "Where the brightest course gripped the light there is a gap, and Masons are already climbing toward it.".
    Change unlay_rail "Unlay the brightest rail-course with the trowel" from gripping to unlaid_r needing trowel_kind.
  }
  Measure railRepair(entity).
  Rule rail_slips when state(rail_course, unlaid_r) and railRepair(rail_course) == 0 says "The Corbel slips two metres down the light with a sound like the whole sky clearing its throat. Anyone on its outside falls." {
    Set railRepair(rail_course) to 30. Increase corbelHeight(corbel_site) by 60. }
  Rule rail_mends when state(rail_course, unlaid_r) and railRepair(rail_course) > 0 and hour(clock) == 0 { Decrease railRepair(rail_course) by 1. }
  Rule rail_mended when state(rail_course, unlaid_r) and railRepair(rail_course) == 1 { Assert state(rail_course, gripping). Set railRepair(rail_course) to 0. }

  // C7: the Interlocutor. It speaks only with syllables laid in its presence, in the visitor's own voice, assembled
  // from what they said on the way up; it cannot lie, and chooses what to leave out. Under Selane's Veil nothing said
  // can be taken.
  Passage rail_chamber "a plain door" is doorway between rail and interlocutor_room.
  Observe chamber_scene_i at interlocutor_room when true "A plain room, its walls finely coursed.".
  Person interlocutor "the Interlocutor" at interlocutor_room {
    Role "the Masonry's voice, from the walls". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns it.
    Greets "The walls of the chamber take a breath that is your own breath, from the stair.".
  }
  Query veiled(c: group) means memberOf(?m, c) and wearing(?v, ?m) and itemKind(?v, veil_kind).
  Observe interlocutor_silent near interlocutor when wordsLaid(party) < 20 or veiled(party) "The walls listen. Nothing speaks. You have said too little on the way up, or nothing that could be taken, for anything here to answer you with.".
  Observe interlocutor_voice near interlocutor when wordsLaid(party) >= 20 and not veiled(party) "When it speaks it is your own voice, out of the walls: words you said on the way up, in the Riot Hall, at the Lintel, to Saro on the stair, taken apart and put back together. It is very courteous.".
  Topic interlocutor_wants with interlocutor "Ask the Interlocutor what it wants" when wordsLaid(actor) >= 20 and not veiled(actor) once {
    Says "'That this bracket join the seed,' it says, in your voice, 'and that the seed be left whole until it does.' A pause. 'You would harm the seed. I would ask you not to. That is all I cannot bear.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, seed_tender). }
  }
  Discovery seed_tender "The Interlocutor cannot bear the seed being harmed before the Corbel docks, and says so: the one place to press.".
  Topic interlocutor_offer with interlocutor "Ask the Interlocutor what it offers" when wordsLaid(actor) >= 20 and not veiled(actor) once {
    Says "'Any moment returned,' it says. 'The dead of Kell. Your Doran. A daughter at her council.' Your voice is very warm. 'And terms. We will take Imbar's past only as far as the Separation, which nobody alive remembers.' It does not say from which end it will start.".
  }
  Topic interlocutor_end with interlocutor "Ask the Interlocutor from which end it takes a world's past" when knows(actor, newest_backward) and wordsLaid(actor) >= 20 and not veiled(actor) once {
    Says "There is a silence of the kind a thing that cannot lie keeps. 'From the newest,' it says. 'It is how a building is quarried. You start at the face.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, held_feed). }
  }
  Relation bargained(group).
  Action accept_terms(actor: group, site: place) "Accept the Interlocutor's terms" {
    Description "Some dead come back. The Masonry takes the past from the newest moment backward, as far as the line agreed.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, interlocutor_room) and wordsLaid(actor) >= 20
      and not veiled(actor) and not bargained(actor).
    Time 10 minutes.
    On success { Assert bargained(actor). }
    Result "'Agreed,' says your own voice, out of the walls, and somewhere below, very far down, last week begins to go.".
  }

  // C8: the Selvage, the edge of Imbar, five kilometres up, where the light leaves the sky.
  Passage chamber_seam "a stair up into black" is passage between interlocutor_room and seam taking 1 hour.
  Observe seam_scene at seam when true "The light leaves the sky. The stars are close and do not twinkle. The cold is like nothing on earth, because heat does not move here at all. The building goes on upward into black.".
  Hazard seam_cold "the cold of the Selvage" means "Deal (1d8) cold damage to ally.".
  Rule seam_cold_bites when at(party, seam) and not seamBitten(party) { Assert strikes(seam_cold, party). Assert seamBitten(party). }
  Relation seamBitten(group).
  Rule seam_leaves when seamBitten(party) and not at(party, seam) { Retract seamBitten(party). }
}

data/adventures/patient-star/ennick.kyr:
Module season "Hold One Season" {
  // The heath and the Ramp: four hours from Quell to the Ramp head, three down it to Ennick on the gorge floor.
  Place ramp_head "the Ramp head" is room within heath at 0, 0 outdoors.
  Passage quell_road "the Quell road" is road between square and ramp_head taking 4 hours.
  Observe ramp_head_scene at ramp_head when true "The heath is flat and grey-green to the edge of the sky and smells of ashwort. Here the road tips over the gorge rim and goes down the Ramp in long switchbacks. Far to the south-east a line of light stands straight up from the ground into a small cloud, and does not move.".

  Place inn "the Lower Inn" is building within ennick.
  Place holders "the holder's house" is building within ennick.
  Place ilis_house "Ilis's house" is building within ennick.
  Place lower_road "Ennick's lower road" is room within ennick at 1, 2 outdoors.
  Place taproom "the Lower Inn" is room within inn at 2, 2.
  Place holders_room "the holder's house" is room within holders at 0, 2.
  Place ilis_room "Ilis's kitchen" is room within ilis_house at 1, 3.
  Place terraces "the upper terraces" is room within ennick at 1, 1 outdoors.
  Place shrine "the shrine" is room within ennick at 0, 1 outdoors.
  Place weeping_wall "the Weeping Wall" is room within ennick at 0, 0 outdoors.

  Passage ramp "the Ramp" is road between ramp_head and lower_road taking 3 hours.
  Passage inn_door "the Lower Inn's door" is door between lower_road and taproom.
  Passage holders_door "the holder's door" is door between lower_road and holders_room.
  Passage ilis_door "Ilis's door" is door between lower_road and ilis_room.
  Passage terrace_steps "the terrace steps" is steps between lower_road and terraces taking 10 minutes.
  Passage cliff_path "the west cliff path" is path between lower_road and shrine taking 10 minutes.
  Passage wall_climb "the climb to the Weeping Wall" is path between shrine and weeping_wall taking 20 minutes.
  // The Outfall: nine kilometres of Seridane drain, a metre and a half high, wet, from the Weeping Wall to the Flood
  // Line. Shut by the flood until it falls in autumn.
  Passage outfall "the Outfall" is crawl between weeping_wall and flood_line taking 8 hours
    opening when flood(flood_water) < 60 "Ten paces in, the Outfall's roof meets black water, and the water does not stop.".

  Observe road_scene at lower_road when not washedOut(lower_road) "Terraces, walnut trees and the river. Carts go through here or not at all: the gorge floor is the only grade a wagon can climb.".
  Observe road_washed at lower_road when washedOut(lower_road) "The lower road is gone under a skin of red mud and gravel where the Weeping Wall's spring came down it in spate. A cart stands axle-deep in it, abandoned.".
  Observe taproom_scene at taproom when true "A low room with a walnut-wood bar and very few people in it. A Glass Office notice is nailed beside the door: THIS HOUSE IS THE OFFICE'S POST ON THE GORGE ROAD.".
  Observe holders_scene at holders_room when true "A holder's house: tally cords hung on pegs by the door, felt hoods, sacks of clean sieved sand, and a map of the glass above the village drawn in charcoal on the wall, with knots for marks.".
  Observe ilis_scene at ilis_room when true "A kitchen with a walnut fire and two chairs. An old felt cloak, stiff at the shoulders from years of folding, hangs by the door.".
  Observe terraces_scene at terraces when true "The upper terraces are glass. Apricot trees stand in it to the knee, held, in the light coming up from under their roots, with the leaves of the year 370 still on them. Ennick's children dare each other to touch them.".
  Initially Assert litGround(terraces).
  Observe weeping_scene at weeping_wall when true "Sixty metres above the village a spring comes out of a low cave in the cliff and falls in a long white thread. The Holdfolk call it the Weeping Wall. In the pool at its foot, thin glass eels flicker.".
  Discovery elvers_seen "Elvers swim up into the Weeping Wall: whatever is in there is warm, and goes a long way back." {
    Found by searching weeping_wall "Behind the falling water the cave goes back into the cliff, low and square-cut. It is not a cave: it is a drain, with tool-marks on its walls, and warm air comes out of it.".
  }

  // The shrine: the Answerer chant-wall, which plays when a stylus is drawn along it (In-world sources 1).
  Thing chant_wall "the chant-wall" at shrine {
    State silent "A face of stillglass four metres long in the cliff, worn smooth at hand height. Walnuts lie in a heap at its foot.".
    State playing "A man's voice, faint and level, in a language older than Tovashi: a long speech, and at the end a line said slower than the rest, as a threat is.".
    Change play_wall "Draw a stylus along the chant-wall" from silent to playing needing stylus.
  }
  Rule wall_ends when state(chant_wall, playing) and not at(party, shrine) { Assert state(chant_wall, silent). }

  // The holders. Bren keeps the office; his mother Ilis kept it before him. The holder's door is bolted with an iron
  // pin that is the Collar culvert's missing gate pin, which nobody in this slice yet knows to look for.
  Person bren "Bren of Ennick" at holders_room {
    Role "the holder of Ennick". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner grim.
  }
  Person ilis "Ilis of Ennick" at ilis_room {
    Role "the old holder, seventy-eight". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner stoic.
  }
  Person mirel "Mirel" at holders_room {
    Role "a Holdfolk carrier". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner compassionate.
    Joins "Mirel takes down her hood and her tally cord from the pegs. 'I will carry,' she says. 'You will not ask me to wake anyone.'".
    Leaves "Mirel takes off her hood and hands it back to nobody. 'I carry for the held,' she says, 'not against them.' She goes home.".
  }
  Person kerra "Kerra Lowe" at taproom {
    Role "keeper of the Lower Inn". Profession innkeeper. Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she.
    Sells rations for 1 coin from 6.
  }
  Initially Assert slowable(mirel). Initially Assert feltClad(mirel). Initially Set hire(mirel) to 1.
  Thing bolt "the bolt on the holder's door" on holders_door {
    State home "The holder's door is bolted with a long iron pin, square in section, too heavy for the job, rusted where hands do not wear it.".
    Tries looking.
  }
  Discovery bolt_is_pin "The bolt on the holder's door in Ennick is a square iron pin, too heavy for a door: a sluice-gate pin.".
  Observe bolt_looked beside holders_door when tried(bolt, looking) "The pin is square in section, as thick as a thumb, with a hole through one end for a chain that is not there. It was made for a sluice-gate, not a door." teaches bolt_is_pin.

  Discovery prayer_heard "The Ennick holding prayer, spoken over each person as they are laid in the light: 'Seri amar ka, dane tamaun eth. Seri amar ka, ithel sonne.' Held until the hour, keepers of the deep water watch; held until the hour, the light remembers." {
    Known by bren, ilis, mirel.
  }
  Topic bren_held with bren "Ask Bren about the held" when true once {
    Says "'They are alive,' says Bren. 'You can watch them breathe if you have the patience, and the felt. My father lies nine hundred paces in. A carrier who goes to him and back loses a night and an afternoon to it.' He looks at the map on the wall. 'Nobody held is woken without their own word. A held man cannot give it. So nobody is woken.'".
  }
  Topic bren_garret with bren "Tell Bren about Garret in the vault" when knows(actor, garret_held) once {
    Says "Bren hears you out. 'He was not laid,' he says. 'He walked into it, reaching for a jar. That is not holding, that is a man caught.' He nods slowly. 'Get him out. If you mean to go by the drain, take Mirel. She knows it.'".
    On discuss { Assert willing(mirel, actor). }
  }
  Topic bren_prayer with bren "Ask Bren what is said when someone is laid" when true once {
    Says "Bren says it without thinking, the way a man says a thing he has said over his own father. 'Seri amar ka, dane tamaun eth. Seri amar ka, ithel sonne.' Then, in Tovashi: 'Held until the hour, keepers of the deep water watch. Held until the hour, the light remembers.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, prayer_heard). }
  }
  Topic mirel_outfall with mirel "Ask Mirel about the Weeping Wall" when true once {
    Says "'It is the old drain,' says Mirel. 'It goes all the way under the heath to the city, nine kilometres, on your hands and knees. My grandfather went up it once. The flood closes it all summer, and opens it when the leaves turn.' She looks at your boots. 'Eight hours, wet. You come out in warm water, with eels.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, outfall_known). }
  }
  Topic ilis_held with ilis "Ask Ilis whether the held are truly alive" when true once {
    Says "'Ours breathe,' says Ilis. 'I have watched Doran take a breath every month for forty years, and it takes longer every year. The old ones further in, from before the Covering, do not breathe. Those are not ours.' She folds her hands. 'Ask me something else.'".
  }
  Topic ilis_prayer with ilis "Ask Ilis about the holding prayer" when true once {
    Says "Ilis says it, slowly, the way her mother taught her: 'Seri amar ka, dane tamaun eth. Seri amar ka, ithel sonne.' She does not say what it means.".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, prayer_heard). }
  }
  // What Ilis has not said in forty years: she says it to someone who has already seen it.
  Discovery prayer_label "The holding prayer is not a prayer. It is a Seridane granary formula, painted on the grain jars and said over each by the clerks: hold this one season, then give it out. The Holdfolk have been saying a label over their dying for three hundred years." {
    Known by ilis.
  }
  Topic ilis_jars with ilis "Tell Ilis about the words on the granary jars" when (knows(actor, jars_painted) or knows(actor, tally_words)) and knows(actor, prayer_heard) and not knows(actor, prayer_label) once {
    Says "Ilis looks at you for a long time. 'So you have seen the jars,' she says. 'The prior at Stairhead read them for me forty years ago. Hold one season, then issue. A grain jar's label.' She looks at the old cloak by the door. 'I said it over my husband. I have said it over half this village. I have never told Bren.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, prayer_label). }
  }
  // Or the company puts the two together itself: the clerk's line on the plate is the prayer.
  Observe prayer_recognised near party when knows(party, tally_words) and knows(party, prayer_heard) and not knows(party, prayer_label) "The clerk's line, said over each jar he counted in, is the line the Holdfolk say over their dying, word for word." teaches prayer_label.

  // The holders' cord and the glass: up the goat cleft from the terraces to the rim, and the red felt rope a hundred
  // paces from the edge of the light. At dusk the umber wolves come along the cord, and wait for whoever comes back
  // across it slowed.
  Place cord "the holders' cord" is room within fields at 0, 1 outdoors.
  Place margin "the edge of the glass" is room within fields at 1, 1 outdoors.
  Place near_held "three hundred paces in" is room within fields at 2, 1 outdoors.
  Place doran_place "Doran's brick" is room within fields at 3, 1 outdoors.
  Passage goat_cleft "the goat cleft" is path between terraces and cord taking 1 hour.
  Passage onto_glass "the edge of the glass" is path between cord and margin taking 10 minutes.
  Passage glass_in "the glass" is path between margin and near_held taking 30 minutes.
  Passage glass_deep "the glass, further in" is path between near_held and doran_place taking 1 hour.
  Initially Assert litGround(margin). Initially Assert litGround(near_held). Initially Assert litGround(doran_place).
  Observe cord_scene at cord when true "Red felt rope on iron pins runs along the heath a hundred paces short of the glass. A cairn stands where the path comes up, and people sit down at it whether they mean to or not.".
  Observe cord_night at cord when dark() "Past the cord your shadow changes: a second light, low and level, comes out of the east through the edge of the glass, and every shadow on the heath lies down pointing west.".
  Observe margin_scene at margin when true "The heath stops and the ground goes clear. There is no slope and no rim: sand and needlegrass, and then the sand is clear and the grass roots stand in it like hair in water. It has no temperature underfoot. Every shadow points west.".
  Observe near_scene at near_held when true "Umber bricks the size of loaves lie on the glass in a scatter, each with a knot cut in the top. Under each, a finger's depth down and more, someone lies on their back in the clear stone.".
  Observe doran_scene at doran_place when true "An umber brick with a holder's knot cut in it sits on the glass. Under it a man lies in a trench a little deeper than an arm is long, with his hands at his sides and his mouth a little open. The glass in front of his face has a fan of bright lines in it, where the sand was not quite clean.".
  Measure watchedDoran(group).
  Rule watching_doran when at(party, doran_place) and not benighted(party) { Increase watchedDoran(party) by 1. }
  Rule doran_reset when not at(party, doran_place) and watchedDoran(party) > 0 { Set watchedDoran(party) to 0. }
  Discovery doran_breathed "Doran, held forty years nine hundred paces into the glass, breathed: once, in most of an hour of watching." .
  Observe doran_breath at doran_place when watchedDoran(party) >= 5 and not knows(party, doran_breathed) "It begins so slowly that you could not say when it began. There is a time when his chest is down and a time when it is not, and between them the shirt lifts over the bone and the cloth draws tighter at the shoulder." teaches doran_breathed.

  Species umber_wolf "an umber wolf" like wolf temperament territorial
    described "A plateau wolf crusted iron-red to the shoulder from wallowing in umber mud, which lets it hunt an hour or two into the light.".
  Person wolves "the umber wolves" at cord {
    Role "a pack of umber wolves, the colour of the cliffs". Species umber_wolf. Numbers 4.
    Seen when dark().
    Warns "On the far side of the cord, in the juniper, four of them stand still that were not standing there before. They walk when you walk, twenty paces off, keeping level.".
  }
  // They do not come at a company that can run. They come at one that cannot.
  Initially Assert tolerates(wolves, party).
  Rule wolves_close when dark() and at(party, cord) and slowedCompany(party) and tolerates(wolves, party) says "The wolves have stopped keeping level. They are coming in." {
    Retract tolerates(wolves, party). Assert assails(wolves, party). }
  Rule wolves_wait when not dark() and not tolerates(wolves, party) and not assails(wolves, party) { Assert tolerates(wolves, party). }

  // The Sluice sends its water down the Outfall to the Weeping Wall, and from there onto the lower road.
  Rule road_washes when sluiced(flood_water) and not washedOut(lower_road) and hour(clock) == 5 says "Down in Ennick, at first light, the Weeping Wall comes down in spate, red with mud, and goes over the lower road." { Assert washedOut(lower_road). }
}

data/adventures/patient-star/hour.kyr:
Module season "The Patient Star" {
  // The Granaries' landward rooms, and the Hour: Tamaun's lowest level, 130 to 210 metres down, flooded outside the
  // mantle the Late Sun has boiled dry, and 40 to 60 degrees inside it (Tamaun, H1 to H6).
  Place hour "the Hour" is level within tamaun.
  Place watch_room "the Watch Room" is room within granaries at 0, 0 underground.
  Place steam_top "the head of the Steam Stair" is room within granaries at 2, 0 underground.
  Place listening_hall "the Waiting Hall" is room within hour at 1, 0 underground.
  Place hot_gallery "the hot gallery" is room within hour at 1, 1 underground.
  Place last_hour "the Last Hour" is room within hour at 0, 1 underground.
  Place coverers_works "the Coverers' Works" is room within hour at 2, 1 underground.
  Place stair_wall "the Wall of the Stair" is room within hour at 3, 1 underground.
  Place courses_face "the Courses" is room within hour at 1, 2 underground.

  Passage watch_door "the Watch Room arch" is arch between ring and watch_room.
  Passage to_steam "the passage to the Steam Stair" is passage between ring and steam_top taking 3 minutes.
  Passage steam_stair "the Steam Stair" is stair between steam_top and listening_hall taking 20 minutes.
  // In autumn the flood falls, and a swimmer can go down the flooded stairs from the Flood Line to the Hall (G4).
  Passage flood_swim "the flooded stairs" is passage between flood_line and listening_hall taking 20 minutes
    opening when flood(flood_water) < 60 "The flooded stairs go down into water too hot to bear past the first turn.".
  Passage hot_way "the hot gallery" is passage between listening_hall and hot_gallery taking 5 minutes.
  Passage chamber_door "the bronze door of the Last Hour" is doorway between hot_gallery and last_hour.
  Passage works_way "the rammed-clay passage" is passage between hot_gallery and coverers_works taking 5 minutes.
  Passage archive_door "the Coverers' archive door" is door between coverers_works and stair_wall.
  Passage courses_way "the lowest gallery" is passage between hot_gallery and courses_face taking 5 minutes.
  Initially Assert darkRoom(watch_room). Initially Assert darkRoom(steam_top). Initially Assert darkRoom(hot_gallery).
  Initially Assert darkRoom(coverers_works). Initially Assert darkRoom(stair_wall).
  // The Waiting Hall is lit from below, through its glass floor; the Last Hour by its channel; the Courses by their
  // own light.
  Initially Assert litGround(courses_face).

  Observe watch_room_scene at watch_room when true "A guardroom with an Office lamp, a table, a ledger and a cot. A bronze bell hangs on a cord that runs up a stair cut in red clay.".
  Discovery kings_book "The King's Book: the Office clerk's record of the old king below, written three days a month. In Haysel he answered at about a sixth of a man's speed and asked for honey and for his daughter by name." {
    Source kings_book_copy "the King's Book" at watch_room readable by party.
  }

  // H1: the Steam Stair. A blast comes up the tube about every fifty minutes, after twenty breaths of hissing; six
  // niches give room for two. A company that watches one cycle can time the run.
  Thing steam "the steam in the stair" on steam_stair is scenery {
    State quiet "The Steam Stair spirals down inside a tube of red ceramic, wet and hot through boot leather. Six niches are cut in its wall, scratched with tally marks.".
    State hissing "A hiss is rising from below in the Steam Stair, louder with each breath.".
    State blasting dangerous "A blast of steam roars up the Steam Stair and out of its head in a white column.".
    Hurts with scald when blasting then quiet.
  }
  Hazard scald "a blast of steam" means "Deal (2d6) fire damage to ally unless dexterity save against (13).".
  Measure steamTick(entity).
  Rule steam_ticks when state(steam, ?s) { Increase steamTick(steam) by 1. }
  Rule steam_hisses when steamTick(steam) == 4 and state(steam, quiet) { Assert state(steam, hissing). }
  Rule steam_blasts when steamTick(steam) == 5 and state(steam, hissing) { Assert state(steam, blasting). }
  Rule steam_spent when steamTick(steam) >= 6 { Set steamTick(steam) to 0. Assert state(steam, quiet). }
  // Half way down when the hiss starts: the blast finds whoever started down hissing.
  Rule caught_on_stair when tookWay(?c, steam_stair) and company(?c) and state(steam, blasting) and not niched(?c) {
    Assert strikes(scald, ?c). Assert niched(?c). }
  Relation niched(group).
  Rule niche_clears when niched(?c) and not tookWay(?c, steam_stair) { Retract niched(?c). }
  Discovery steam_timed "The Steam Stair blasts about every fifty minutes, after twenty breaths of hissing; the niches hold two each.".
  Observe steam_learned at steam_top when state(steam, blasting) and not knows(party, steam_timed) "The blast comes up out of the stair-head in a column you could lean on, and is gone. You count, after: it is near enough fifty minutes to the next, and the hiss before it is twenty breaths long." teaches steam_timed.

  // H2: the Waiting Hall, and the Waiting who listen there without leave.
  Observe hall_scene_h at listening_hall when true "A round chamber with a stillglass floor, very warm. Light comes up through the floor from below, and lies on the undersides of things.".
  Person listeners "six of the Waiting" at listening_hall {
    Role "six Listeners of the Waiting, on felt mats with their ears to the glass". Ancestry human. Numbers 6. Peaceable.
    Wants night_honey.
  }
  Observe tone_heard at listening_hall when hour(clock) == 12 or hour(clock) == 0 "Through the floor, far below, a single low note sounds, and goes on in the bones after it has stopped. The Listeners look at one another and say nothing.".
  Discovery tone_below "Since 378 a low tone sounds from deep below the Pit once an hour; the Waiting have heard it, and told no one.".
  Topic listeners_tone with listeners "Ask the Listeners what they hear" when true once {
    Says "'Nothing, since the year 71,' says a woman with wax in her hair. 'Not the Voice.' She looks at the others. 'Since 78, when the growth broke into the lowest gallery and let the air carry it, there is a note. Once an hour. Deep. It is not a syllable. It is not anything.' She presses her ear back to the glass. 'Ruan does not know yet. Do not tell the Office.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, tone_below). }
  }
  Topic listeners_names with listeners "Ask the Listeners what they are copying" when true once {
    Says "'The Waking Ward names,' says a young man, and turns his tablet so you can see the columns. 'Every name has its syllable. Read in the order they were given, they are the Voice, before anyone counted.' He taps one column. 'And these are the hour-names the sick counted their time by. Twelve of them, round and round.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, ward_names). }
  }
  Discovery ward_names "The Waking Ward names, copied in order: each carries its Voice syllable, and among them the twelve Seridane hour-names the sick counted time by.".

  // H3: the Last Hour, and Amaru, ninth Dane of the Hour, waking. His rate goes from a sixth to a third, to a half, to a
  // man's speed, by the week (Amaru's waking).
  Observe last_hour_scene at last_hour when true "A domed chamber tiled in bronze, its ceiling pierced by a stillglass rod as thick as a forearm. Grey light comes down the rod and spreads weakly. Couches stand round the walls, and honey jars lie about, all open and scraped clean.".
  Person amaru "Amaru" at last_hour {
    Role "the ninth Dane of the Hour, in a robe gone colourless". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner proud.
    Wants night_honey.
    Objects "Amaru's eyes come round to his seal in your hands, over a long time. When his voice arrives it is very quiet. 'Put it back.'".
  }
  Person kesset "Kesset" at last_hour {
    Role "the Dane's chamberlain, on a couch in the shadow". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner stoic.
    Calling bard. Plans 14 steps. Uses go.
    Joins "Kesset gets up as a young man would and an old man feels it. 'I will find Halu,' he says. 'And I will tell you what the doors say.'".
  }
  Measure amaruRate(group).
  Initially Set amaruRate(amaru) to 6.
  Rule amaru_third when day(clock) >= 29 and amaruRate(amaru) == 6 { Set amaruRate(amaru) to 3. }
  Rule amaru_half when day(clock) >= 71 and amaruRate(amaru) == 3 { Set amaruRate(amaru) to 2. }
  Rule amaru_whole when day(clock) >= 127 and amaruRate(amaru) == 2 { Set amaruRate(amaru) to 1. }
  Initially Assert asleep(kesset).
  Rule kesset_wakes when day(clock) >= 36 and asleep(kesset) { Retract asleep(kesset). Assert willing(kesset, party). }
  Observe amaru_sixth near amaru when amaruRate(amaru) == 6 "When you step closer, the old man's eyes come round to you over several seconds. His lips begin a word, and you wait a long time for the rest of it.".
  Observe amaru_third_seen near amaru when amaruRate(amaru) == 3 "The old man in the chair turns his head toward you at a third of a man's speed, and his hands are shaking, and not with age.".
  Observe amaru_half_seen near amaru when amaruRate(amaru) == 2 "The old king watches you come in with something like anger. He is quicker now; quick enough to argue.".
  Observe amaru_awake near amaru when amaruRate(amaru) == 1 "An old man sits in a dead city in a chair too big for him, at a man's speed, and looks at you.".
  // What he says, by how far he has woken: formal, then hungry and afraid, then disbelieving, then an old man.
  Topic amaru_first with amaru "Speak to the king" when amaruRate(amaru) == 6 once {
    Says "It takes him half a minute to say what would take you five seconds, and you wait for every word. 'You are not of my household.' A long time. 'Where is my daughter? Where is the honey? Tell the granary-keepers to come to me.' His eyes close and open, slowly. 'Is the Voice still speaking?'".
  }
  Topic amaru_hungry with amaru "Speak to the king" when amaruRate(amaru) == 3 once {
    Says "'The honey is gone,' says Amaru, as if you had taken it. 'The household is hungry. Kesset is too thin.' His eyes go to the empty couch. 'Halu went up for bread. She has not come back.' He grips the arm of the chair. 'What year is it, above?'".
  }
  Topic amaru_year with amaru "Tell the king what year it is" when amaruRate(amaru) <= 3 once {
    Says "You tell him: the three hundred and eightieth since the Unlidding; sixteen hundred and forty since the Covering. Amaru looks at you a long time. 'Some weeks,' he says. 'It has been some weeks.' He does not believe you, and you can see him deciding not to.".
  }
  Topic amaru_hour with amaru "Ask the king whether the hour was given" when true once {
    Says "'It was given,' says Amaru, as slowly as he has said anything. 'The lake asked for an hour and the hour came down. It speaks to the keepers, one sound in each moon.' His eyes are steady. 'My daughter says it fell. My daughter is a clerk.'".
  }
  Topic amaru_stone with amaru "Ask the king about a stone that sings" when amaruRate(amaru) <= 3 once {
    Says "Something moves in his face. 'There is no stone,' he says. 'There is the hour.' He looks at the rod of light over him. 'I have heard it sixteen hundred years. It is the hour's own heart. It is mine.'".
  }
  Topic amaru_daughter with amaru "Tell the king how his daughter died" when knows(actor, selane_murdered) once {
    Says "You tell him what the Wall of the Stair says. Amaru hears it out without moving at all, which at his speed is no sign of anything. Then he closes his eyes, and keeps them closed so long that you think he has gone back into the light. 'Loyal men,' he says. 'Loyal to me.' When he opens his eyes he takes the seal off its stand and holds it out to you. 'Open her doors,' he says. 'All of them.'".
    On discuss { Assert lends(amaru, seal, actor). Retract inside(seal, seal_stand). Assert at(seal, last_hour). Assert grieves(amaru). }
  }
  Relation grieves(group).
  Event amaru_honey near amaru when keeps(amaru, ?j) and itemKind(?j, night_honey) "It takes the king a long time to lift the jar, and longer to open it. He eats with two fingers, slowly, and gives the rest to Kesset without being asked." then { Assert fed(amaru). }
  Relation fed(group).

  // His seal, the Long Hour on its stand, and the royal seed behind his chair.
  Kind amaru_seal "Amaru's seal" is treasure worth 0 weighing 1
    described "A palm-sized stillglass plate. Drawn past a stylus it says, in an old man's voice, a name and one syllable.".
  Kind long_hour_plates "the Long Hour" is treasure worth 600 weighing 12
    described "About five thousand syllables of the Voice on stillglass plates, the Seridane transcript of the Long Hour.".
  Kind royal_seed "a jar of royal seed barley" is treasure worth 200 weighing 2
    described "Barley held in the light for sixteen hundred years and alive.".
  Thing seal_stand "the stand beside the chair" at last_hour {
    Holds.
    State standing "A stand of stillglass plates stands beside the chair: the Long Hour, and on top, a single palm-sized plate.".
  }
  Item seal "Amaru's seal" is amaru_seal in seal_stand owned by amaru.
  Item long_hour "the Long Hour" is long_hour_plates in seal_stand owned by amaru.
  Thing niche "a sealed niche behind the chair" at last_hour {
    Holds.
    State sealed closed "A niche is sealed into the wall behind the chair with red clay, and stamped.".
    State opened "The sealed niche behind the chair stands open.".
    Change break_niche "Break the clay seal on the niche" from sealed to opened needing digging.
  }
  Item seed_jar "a jar of royal seed barley" is royal_seed in niche owned by amaru.
  Discovery long_hour_read "The Long Hour, read: about five thousand syllables of the Voice, in order. Laid as the citadel was built, one course to a syllable, they are a plan of the Undersun's Seridane Reach.".
  Thing reading_stand "the Long Hour on its stand" at last_hour is scenery {
    State shelved "The plates of the Long Hour are racked in order, and a stylus hangs on a cord beside them.".
    State read "The plates of the Long Hour have been read through, and are a little out of order.".
    Change read_plates "Read the Long Hour through with a stylus" from shelved to read needing stylus.
  }
  Observe long_hour_known at last_hour when state(reading_stand, read) "Syllable after syllable, an hour and more of them. Where a syllable is open the course it laid is open; where it is closed, solid; where it repeats, a stair." teaches long_hour_read.
  Rule bren_seed when keeps(bren, ?j) and itemKind(?j, royal_seed) and not seeded(ennick) { Assert seeded(ennick). }
  Relation seeded(place).
  Event bren_seed_told near bren when seeded(ennick) "Bren holds the jar to the light and pours a little into his palm. 'Alive,' he says. 'Sixteen hundred years, and alive.' He does not thank you; he asks what you need.".

  // H4: the Coverers' Works and the Plumb, Selane's borehole, 400 metres toward the stone that sings.
  Observe works_scene at coverers_works when true "Walls of rammed red clay block three passages. In the middle of the floor a round shaft half a metre across goes straight down, lined with clear glass. Over it stand a bronze winch and a frame of rods.".
  Observe plumb_note at coverers_works when hour(clock) == 12 or hour(clock) == 0 "With an ear to the liner you hear it: a long low note, coming up four hundred metres of glass.".
  // A sounding lock: twelve stillglass rods, rung in the order of the hour-names carved over the door (Sounding
  // locks). Three wrong attempts in an hour drop the counterweight; it must then be dug out.
  Thing sounding_lock "the sounding lock" on archive_door {
    State shut blocking "Over the Coverers' archive door seven symbols of the sun's place are carved in a row; a row of short stillglass rods is set in the frame.".
    State jammed blocking "The counterweight has dropped into its locked seat. The door will have to be dug out.".
    State released "The archive door stands open on its counterweight.".
    Change ring_names "Ring the hour-names in the carved order" from shut to released after learning hour_names.
    Change ring_seal "Draw Amaru's seal past the rods" from shut to released needing seal.
    Change dig_out "Dig the counterweight out of its seat" from jammed to shut needing digging.
  }
  Measure misses(entity).
  Action ring_guess(actor: group, site: place) "Ring the rods in an order you guess" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, coverers_works) and state(sounding_lock, shut)
      and not knows(actor, hour_names).
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Increase misses(sounding_lock) by 1. }
    Result "The rods ring, one after another, and the bar does not drop.".
  }
  Rule lock_jams when misses(sounding_lock) >= 3 and state(sounding_lock, shut) says "Something heavy drops inside the door frame with a sound like a dropped anvil." {
    Assert state(sounding_lock, jammed). Set misses(sounding_lock) to 0. }
  Discovery hour_names "The twelve Seridane hour-names, in order and with their pitches: what the sounding locks are keyed to.".
  Discovery rhyme_known "The Weirs' counting rhyme for the cranes: twelve words in a ring.".
  // Any two of the three sources give the names (the Weirs' rhyme, the Ward names, the Plate Hall song).
  Observe names_assembled near party when not knows(party, hour_names) and ((knows(party, rhyme_known) and knows(party, ward_names)) or (knows(party, rhyme_known) and knows(party, song_heard)) or (knows(party, ward_names) and knows(party, song_heard))) "The Weirs' twelve counting words, the twelve names the sick counted by, the children's twelve on the plate: they are one ring of hour-names, and you have them in order." teaches hour_names.

  // H5: the Wall of the Stair. A Coverer's record of Selane's last weeks; beneath it, folded, her Veil.
  Thing stair_record "the Wall of the Stair" at stair_wall {
    State silent "A single chant-wall two metres long, untouched, in a small chamber.".
    State playing "A woman's voice, faint, steady: the grain riots, Selane's order to open the reserve vaults, and her murder at the top of the Stair, by men of her father's party, who told the city it was the mob. Then the names of the men.".
    Change play_record "Draw a stylus along the Wall of the Stair" from silent to playing needing stylus.
  }
  Rule record_ends when state(stair_record, playing) and not at(party, stair_wall) { Assert state(stair_record, silent). }
  Discovery selane_murdered "Selane did not die in the grain riots: Answerer loyalists killed her at the top of the Stair and told the city it was the mob.".
  Observe record_heard at stair_wall when state(stair_record, playing) "A Coverer cut this, the year Tamaun emptied." teaches selane_murdered.
  Kind veil_kind "Selane's Veil" like cloak_of_protection worth 0 weighing 0
    described "Lace of drawn barrow-iron wire, three hundred grams, which covers its wearer from head to waist. Nothing said under it can be taken.".
  Initially Assert shields(veil_kind).
  Item veil "Selane's Veil" is veil_kind at stair_wall.
  Observe veil_seen at stair_wall when at(veil, stair_wall) "Folded on the floor beneath the wall lies a square of dark iron lace.".

  // H6: the Courses, the growth beneath the Late Sun breaking into the city. Saro opens them; a Mason's trowel does.
  Observe courses_scene at courses_face when true "At the bottom of the passage the wall is not stone. Bands of dark metal and clear glass are laid in perfect courses without a seam. Light runs inside them along their curves, around the corner of the passage. A cutter's boot sticks out of the third course.".
}

data/adventures/patient-star/keeping.kyr:
Module season "The Patient Star" {
  // The Keeping (Tier IV): the plane where every moment of Imbar's past is kept, as a place. Geography is chronology:
  // walking inward goes back in time, walking across goes elsewhere in Imbar at the same moment. Near the shore a
  // careful walker covers a year in an hour; in deep time, where less happened, a thousand. Time passes for visitors
  // at its ordinary rate, and Imbar's clocks run while they are away.
  Place keeping "the Keeping" is plane.
  Place kept_imbar "the Keeping of Imbar" is region within keeping.
  Place shore "the shore of the present" is wilderness within kept_imbar at 0, 0.
  Place kept_plateau "the plateau's past" is wilderness within kept_imbar at 1, 0.
  Place hollows "the Quarried Reaches" is wilderness within kept_imbar at 1, 1.
  Place deep_time "deep time" is wilderness within kept_imbar at 2, 0.
  Place far_east "far east of Imbar's known lands" is wilderness within kept_imbar at 2, 1.
  Place wall_site "the Outer Wall" is site within kept_imbar at 3, 0.

  Place tideline "the Tideline" is room within shore at 0, 0 outdoors.
  Place collar_years "the Collar's years" is room within kept_plateau at 0, 0 outdoors.
  Place year_zero "the night of the Unlidding" is room within kept_plateau at 1, 0 outdoors.
  Place covering_years "the Covering" is room within kept_plateau at 2, 0 outdoors.
  Place stair_murder "the top of the Stair, 1,575 BP" is room within kept_plateau at 2, 1 outdoors.
  Place new_moons "the new moons" is room within kept_plateau at 3, 0 outdoors.
  Place kept_fall "the fall" is room within kept_plateau at 4, 0 outdoors.
  Place quarry_edge "a quarried hollow" is room within hollows at 0, 0 outdoors.
  Place descent_k "the Descent" is room within deep_time at 0, 0 outdoors.
  Place separation "the Separation" is room within deep_time at 1, 0 outdoors.
  Place absence "an absence" is room within far_east at 0, 0.
  Place outer_wall "the Outer Wall" is room within wall_site at 0, 0 outdoors.

  // In: a living hand on Ithmar, with whoever touches that person. Out: walk back to the shore and step through.
  // Without Ithmar, only where you came in; with it, anywhere.
  Relation cameInAt(group, place).
  Action touch_ithmar(actor: group, site: place) "Lay a hand on Ithmar" {
    Description "A living hand that touches Ithmar enters the Keeping, together with anyone touching that person, at the moment and place of the touch.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, arbiter_vault)
      and (inside(ithmar, cage) or carries(actor, ithmar)).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Retract at(actor, arbiter_vault). Assert at(actor, tideline). Assert cameInAt(actor, arbiter_vault). }
    Result "The jewel is not cold, or warm. The white room goes on being there and you are not in it: you stand on a shore where the present is setting like wet sand.".
  }
  Passage step_back "the way you came in" is passage between tideline and arbiter_vault taking 10 minutes.
  Relation keepingWay(passage).
  Passage out_quell "out into Quell, now" is passage between tideline and square taking 10 minutes one way
    opening when carries(party, ithmar) "The shore runs on, every place of Imbar this minute, soft as wet sand. Without the jewel you cannot step out anywhere but where you came in.".
  Passage out_orrel "out into New Orrel, now" is passage between tideline and no_market taking 10 minutes one way
    opening when carries(party, ithmar) "Without the jewel there is no stepping out here.".
  Passage out_ennick "out into Ennick, now" is passage between tideline and lower_road taking 10 minutes one way
    opening when carries(party, ithmar) "Without the jewel there is no stepping out here.".
  Passage out_stairhead "out at Stairhead, now" is passage between tideline and stair_top taking 10 minutes one way
    opening when carries(party, ithmar) "Without the jewel there is no stepping out here.".
  Passage out_corbel "out at the Corbel's tip, at the moment it came" is passage between collar_years and lintel_room taking 10 minutes one way
    opening when carries(party, ithmar) "In the year 71 something comes down the light out of the black, and stops in the cloud. Without the jewel, you can only watch it come.".
  Initially Assert keepingWay(out_quell). Initially Assert keepingWay(out_orrel). Initially Assert keepingWay(out_ennick).
  Initially Assert keepingWay(out_stairhead). Initially Assert keepingWay(out_corbel).
  // Every step through the Keeping with the jewel lays one of the wearer's own moments into its setting: a memory gone,
  // and everyone else forgets that moment too.
  Relation stepPaid(group, passage).
  Rule step_costs when tookWay(?c, ?w) and keepingWay(?w) and carries(?c, ithmar) and not stepPaid(?c, ?w) and memories(?c) >= 1
    says "Something of yours goes into the jewel's setting as you step: a morning, a face, a word somebody said once. You do not know which. Nobody does." {
    Decrease memories(?c) by 1. Assert stepPaid(?c, ?w). }
  Rule step_paid_clears when stepPaid(?c, ?w) and not tookWay(?c, ?w) { Retract stepPaid(?c, ?w). }
  Observe no_past near party when memories(party) == 0 "You have stepped so often that there is almost nothing behind you. You remember Saro. You do not remember why.".

  // Inward: back in time. Near the shore, a year an hour.
  Passage to_collar_years "inland, thirty years" is path between tideline and collar_years taking 32 hours.
  Passage to_year_zero "inland, three hundred and fifty years" is path between collar_years and year_zero taking 14 days.
  Passage to_covering "inland, through the craneless centuries" is path between year_zero and covering_years taking 3 days.
  Passage to_murder "across, to the Stair" is path between covering_years and stair_murder taking 4 hours.
  Passage to_moons "inland, through Tamaun's seven centuries" is path between covering_years and new_moons taking 10 days.
  Passage walk_moons "the new moons, walked a minute a moon" is path between new_moons and kept_fall taking 60 hours.
  Passage to_hollows "across, into the blank" is path between collar_years and quarry_edge taking 2 hours.
  // Deep time, where there are no landmarks: without the Tally or a guide, years of wandering.
  Passage to_descent "inland, into deep time" is path between kept_fall and descent_k taking 30 hours needing tally_kind or wayfinding.
  Passage to_separation "inland, to the Separation" is path between descent_k and separation taking 2 hours.
  Passage to_absence "across, far to the east" is path between descent_k and absence taking 2 days needing tally_kind or wayfinding.
  Passage to_wall "inland, before the beginning" is path between separation and outer_wall taking 4 hours.
  Initially Assert keepingWay(to_collar_years). Initially Assert keepingWay(to_year_zero). Initially Assert keepingWay(to_covering).
  Initially Assert keepingWay(to_murder). Initially Assert keepingWay(to_moons). Initially Assert keepingWay(walk_moons).
  Initially Assert keepingWay(to_hollows). Initially Assert keepingWay(to_descent). Initially Assert keepingWay(to_separation).
  Initially Assert keepingWay(to_absence). Initially Assert keepingWay(to_wall).
  Action wander(actor: group, site: place) "Strike out into deep time without the Tally or a guide" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, kept_fall)
      and not holding(actor, tally_kind) and not capable(actor, wayfinding).
    Time 144.
    On success { Assert strikes(archivore_bite, actor). }
    Result "There are no landmarks. You walk a day and do not know if it was a day or a century, and something like a page turning follows you, and bites.".
  }

  // K1: the Tideline. Everything in Imbar that is happening now is here, still soft: a scrying ground.
  Observe tideline_scene at tideline when true "A shore where the present is setting, like wet sand hardening. Everything in Imbar that is happening now is here, still soft; you can walk across it and see any place you choose, as it is this minute.".
  Observe tide_orrel at tideline when at(amaru, barracks) "In New Orrel, this minute, an old king lies on a cot under three blankets and looks at a ceiling.".
  Observe tide_crew at tideline when argued(crew) and asleep(garret) "In the Granary Ring, this minute, two cutters sit with their backs to the wall by the ninth vault, waiting.".
  Observe tide_corbel at tideline when not docked(corbel_site) "Over the Pit, this minute, the Corbel is two metres lower than it was yesterday.".
  Observe tide_concord at tideline when convened(chapter) "In Stairhead's chapter house, this minute, the Concord is sitting, and nobody is sitting next to anybody they can help it.".
  Observe tide_saro at tideline when not travelsWith(saro, party) "At the Tip of the Undersun, this minute, a woman with no temperature lays a course and calls its syllable.".
  // Standing still on the Tideline, a visitor begins to set into the present.
  Measure tideWatches(group).
  Rule tide_counts when at(party, tideline) { Increase tideWatches(party) by 1. }
  Rule tide_resets when not at(party, tideline) and tideWatches(party) > 0 { Set tideWatches(party) to 0. }
  Observe tide_setting near party when at(party, tideline) and tideWatches(party) >= 4 "Your feet have sunk into the shore to the ankle, and it is hardening around them. Your own hand, when you lift it, comes up slowly.".
  Rule tide_takes when at(party, tideline) and tideWatches(party) >= 6 and not setInPresent(party) says "The present sets around you, and you are kept." {
    Assert setInPresent(party). Assert hobbled(party). }
  Relation setInPresent(group).
  Person shore_remembrancer "a Remembrancer of the shore" at tideline {
    Role "a servant of the Virina, tall, made of the sound of bells". Peaceable. Pronouns they.
    Wants quarried_moment.
  }
  Topic shore_quarried with shore_remembrancer "Ask the Remembrancer about the hollows" when true once {
    Says "'Cut,' says the Remembrancer, in bells. 'Carried out of the Keeping into the Masonry. Bring back what was cut, and we will set it again where it was kept, and it will be remembered.'".
  }
  Event moment_returned near shore_remembrancer when keeps(shore_remembrancer, ?q) and itemKind(?q, quarried_moment) "The Remembrancer takes the moment between two long fingers and sets it into the shore, somewhere inland, and in Imbar a season that nobody could remember is remembered again.".
  Rule dane_returned when keeps(shore_remembrancer, dane_moment) and not reanchored(fourth_dane) { Assert reanchored(fourth_dane). }

  // K2: the plateau's past.
  Observe collar_years_scene at collar_years when true "Inland from the shore the plateau gets younger: the Collar going up, then a storm, then down; carts; the Breach opening in a white roar of steam and coming back closed; Quell growing smaller.".
  Observe year_zero_scene at year_zero when true "A night of steam. Half of a town going into a hole in the ground. Then the light comes up out of the old Clear Fields everywhere at once, and sixty people at a fair stop where they stand, and their kin come with sand.".
  Observe covering_scene at covering_years when true "Thousands of people carrying red clay in baskets, for years, into a pit; and then the last light cut, and in the glass of the fields, all at once, eleven thousand people wake in the dark.".
  // The murder at the Stair: walked through, it plays; given time by touch, the faces.
  Observe murder_scene at stair_murder when true "The top of the falls at night, in riot-time. A young woman in a council robe on the path, and four men coming up behind her who are not rioters.".
  Thing murderers "the four men on the path" at stair_murder {
    State coming "Four men in Answerer badges come up the path behind Selane, hands under their cloaks.".
  }
  Initially Assert kept(murderers).
  Observe murder_seen near murderers when touched(murderers) "For the length of your touch it plays: they reach her, and the knives come out, and one of them says the Dane's name as if it were a prayer. When they turn to go you see their faces, and their badges." teaches selane_murdered.
  // The new moons: the Voice's syllables as they were spoken, one at each new moon since the fall. Walking the first
  // three centuries of them recovers the Crown's plan, and the first syllable.
  Observe moons_scene at new_moons when true "Moonless nights, one after another, inland, each with a single sound passing through the rock near a young pit: a syllable, felt in the knees.".
  Observe moons_walked at kept_fall when not knows(party, crown_map) "Sixty hours of moonless nights, a syllable each, and you have them all in order: the Crown's plan, the Voice's first three hundred years." teaches crown_map.
  Observe first_from_moons at kept_fall when not knows(party, first_syllable) "The first of them you will not forget: it was the first sound the seed made in the world." teaches first_syllable.
  Discovery delver_seen "At the fall, riding the seed's wake out of a clear sky, very small: a figure with a trowel, the first Mason, who laid the First Course and went down into the dark with the stem.".
  Observe fall_scene_k at kept_fall when true "An autumn night out of a clear sky; a light coming down; the lake villages watching. Riding its wake, very small, visible only to someone looking for it, is a figure with a trowel." teaches delver_seen.

  // K3: the Quarried Reaches: blankness, a fog in which things have no reasons; Masons cutting at the edges.
  Observe hollow_scene at quarry_edge when true "History stops here. Not darkness: blankness, a fog in which things have no reasons. A road goes into it and does not come out. At its edges, figures with trowels are cutting, and the cut edges are clean.".
  Person cutters "a crew of Masons, cutting" at quarry_edge {
    Role "three Masons at the edge of the blank, cutting a season out of the plateau's last year". Ancestry human. Numbers 3. Peaceable.
  }
  Relation cutStopped(place).
  Topic cutters_stop with cutters "Ask the Masons to stop cutting" when true once {
    Says "They stop, because you asked, and look at you with honest puzzlement. 'It is the work,' says one. 'If we do not, another crew will.' But they put their trowels down, and that season stays where it is.".
    On discuss { Assert cutStopped(quarry_edge). }
  }
  Person clea "Clea Keddle" at quarry_edge {
    Role "a Haldrish seer, lost, who walks here in her sleep". Ancestry human. Calling ranger. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner compassionate.
    Joins "'I know the way inward,' says Clea, 'better than anyone living. I have been lost in it for forty years.' She takes your sleeve like a child.".
  }
  Initially Assert willing(clea, party).
  Topic clea_where with clea "Tell Clea Keddle where she is" when true once {
    Says "'The Keeping,' she says after you, as if it were a word in a dream. 'I have always called it the long country.' She looks at her hands. 'Something bites me here. A little, every night, for forty years.' She does not know that her body is dying in a bed in Sorne, and you do not tell her.".
  }
  // Archivores: the Keeping's predators. They feed on what belongs to no moment, and cannot enter one that is playing.
  Species archivore "an archivore" like wraith temperament ambush
    described "A flat shape like a page turning, seen edge-on as a line. A bite takes time from the rest of a life: a day for a graze, years for a deep wound.".
  Person archivores "archivores" at quarry_edge { Role "two flat shapes like pages turning". Species archivore. Numbers 2. }
  Hazard archivore_bite "an archivore's bite" means "Deal (2d8) necrotic damage to ally unless wisdom save against (14).".
  Measure yearsTaken(group).

  // K4: deep time. The Descent, and the Separation: the most dangerous place, and the most valuable.
  Observe descent_scene at descent_k when true "A night sky full of falling fire, every fall stopped, and the land under it burning.".
  Thing falling_fire "the falling fire" at descent_k { State falling "Fire hangs in the sky, coming down.". }
  Initially Assert kept(falling_fire).
  Hazard landed "a falling thing, landing" means "Deal (4d6) fire damage to ally unless dexterity save against (15).".
  Rule fire_lands when touched(falling_fire) says "For the length of your touch it falls, and lands." { Retract touched(falling_fire). Assert strikes(landed, party). }
  Observe separation_scene at separation when true "A sky divided: half full of figures with light for wings, half full of figures of darkness and hooks, all stopped in the act of striking, across a distance the eye cannot measure. Below them, tall robed figures in white stand in a ring, holding the world apart like the pages of a book. In the centre of the ring a hand is setting a jewel into stone.".
  Thing blows "the war overhead" at separation { State struck "Every blow overhead is stopped an inch from landing.". }
  Initially Assert kept(blows).
  Hazard unmaking "a blow of the Separation" means "Deal (10d10) force damage to ally.".
  Rule blow_lands when touched(blows) says "You touch a blow that nearly unmade the world, and for a moment it goes on." { Retract touched(blows). Assert strikes(unmaking, party). }
  Discovery sigils_known "How the sigils on Ithmar are cut, and so how a binding is made: watched at the Separation, stroke by stroke, a hand setting a jewel into stone.".
  Relation watchedBinding(group).
  Action watch_binding(actor: group, site: place) "Watch the hand in the ring cut the sigils, stroke by stroke" {
    Description "Walk slowly round the ring, letting the moment play, and do not touch anything.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, separation) and not watchedBinding(actor)
      and not benighted(actor).
    Time 12.
    On success { Assert watchedBinding(actor). }
    Result "You walk the ring for two hours, slowly, so that it plays and does not stop, and you watch a hand cut the sigils on a jewel into its setting, one stroke at a time, until you could do it.".
  }
  Observe binding_learned near party when watchedBinding(party) and not knows(party, sigils_known) "You have the strokes. You know how it is bound; and so how it could be bound tighter." teaches sigils_known.

  // K5: an absence. Saro, at the last moment she still had; around her, nothing.
  Observe absence_scene at absence when true "A mountain hall, ages ago, and a woman standing in it with a jewel at her throat. Around her, in every direction, the Keeping is empty: a hole shaped like a life.".
  Discovery saro_remembers "Saro has seen herself: a woman who wore a Kiritarun, and spent her whole past using it, and was taken. She remembers her name.".
  Observe saro_sees at absence when travelsWith(saro, party) and not knows(party, saro_remembers) "Saro stands in front of the woman with the jewel for a long time. 'That is mine,' she says, the way she said it of the niche. Then, very quietly, she says a name, and it is not Saro, and she weeps, which she did not know how to do." teaches saro_remembers.

  // K6: the Outer Wall: the quarry face, and the road to the Masonry.
  Observe wall_scene_k at outer_wall when true "At the far inland edge, before the beginning, a wall. Through it, moments are being carried out on long tendrils of course-work into black.".
}

data/adventures/patient-star/masonry.kyr:
Module season "The Patient Star" {
  // The Masonry (Tier V): the Patient's citadel beyond the planes, built of the pasts of other worlds. Five laws: air
  // is kept, not given; everything doses; stillness is laid; touch gives time; wings are histories.
  Place masonry "the Masonry" is plane.
  Place masonry_land "the Masonry" is region within masonry.
  Place citadel "the citadel of the Patient" is site within masonry_land at 0, 0.
  Place m_spine "the Spine" is level within citadel.
  Place m_wings "the wings" is level within citadel.
  Place m_heart "the heart" is level within citadel.
  Place spine "the Spine" is room within m_spine at 0, 0.
  Place finished_door "a wing door carved with circles" is room within m_wings at 0, 0.
  Place finished_city "a city of slender towers" is room within m_wings at 1, 0.
  Place finished_wild "fields, then forest, then rock" is room within m_wings at 2, 0.
  Place finished_beginning "the end of the wing" is room within m_wings at 3, 0.
  Place imbar_wing "the Imbar Wing" is room within m_wings at 0, 1.
  Place empty_niches "the empty niches" is room within m_wings at 1, 1.
  Place nave "the Nave of Sockets" is room within m_heart at 0, 0.
  Place heart "the Heart" is room within m_heart at 0, 1.

  // From the Corbel's Selvage, or the Keeping's Outer Wall.
  Passage spine_from_seam "up into the black, onto the Spine" is passage between seam and spine taking 20 minutes.
  Passage spine_from_wall "along a tendril of course-work through the Wall" is passage between outer_wall and spine taking 20 minutes.
  Passage spine_wing "the bridge to a wing door" is passage between spine and finished_door taking 20 minutes.
  Passage wing_in "into the wing" is doorway between finished_door and finished_city.
  Passage wing_back "back through the world's history" is passage between finished_city and finished_wild taking 6 hours.
  Passage wing_end "to the wing's end" is passage between finished_wild and finished_beginning taking 6 hours.
  Passage spine_imbar "the bridge to the new wing" is passage between spine and imbar_wing taking 20 minutes.
  Passage imbar_niches "past the court, into the gallery" is passage between imbar_wing and empty_niches taking 30 minutes.
  Passage spine_nave "down into the heart" is stair between spine and nave taking 30 minutes.
  Passage wing_nave "down from the Imbar Wing" is stair between imbar_wing and nave taking 20 minutes.
  Passage nave_heart "beneath the beating socket" is passage between nave and heart taking 30 minutes.

  // Everything doses.
  Initially Assert litGround(spine). Initially Assert litGround(finished_door). Initially Assert litGround(finished_city).
  Initially Assert litGround(finished_wild). Initially Assert litGround(finished_beginning). Initially Assert litGround(imbar_wing).
  Initially Assert litGround(empty_niches). Initially Assert litGround(nave). Initially Assert litGround(heart).

  // Air is kept, not given: between moments there is no air at all. Visitors breathe the air of the moments they walk
  // through, and some worlds' air is poison.
  Kind airkind. Entity air_good: airkind "breathable air". Entity air_poison: airkind "poison". Entity air_none: airkind "no air".
  Relation airOf(place, airkind).
  Initially Assert airOf(spine, air_none). Initially Assert airOf(finished_door, air_good). Initially Assert airOf(finished_city, air_good).
  Initially Assert airOf(finished_wild, air_poison). Initially Assert airOf(finished_beginning, air_none).
  Initially Assert airOf(imbar_wing, air_good). Initially Assert airOf(empty_niches, air_none).
  Initially Assert airOf(nave, air_none). Initially Assert airOf(heart, air_good). Initially Assert airOf(seam, air_none).
  Measure breath(group).
  Rule breathes when at(party, ?p) and airOf(?p, air_good) and breath(party) < 12 { Set breath(party) to 12. }
  Rule holds_breath when at(party, ?p) and airOf(?p, air_none) and breath(party) >= 1 { Decrease breath(party) by 1. }
  Hazard airless "no air" means "Deal (2d6) physical damage to ally.".
  Hazard bad_air "the air of another world" means "Deal (1d10) poison damage to ally unless constitution save against (13).".
  Rule suffocates when at(party, ?p) and airOf(?p, air_none) and breath(party) < 1 { Assert strikes(airless, party). }
  Rule poisoned when at(party, ?p) and airOf(?p, air_poison) { Assert strikes(bad_air, party). }
  Observe air_note near party when at(party, ?p) and airOf(?p, air_none) "There is no air here. You are breathing what you brought.".
  Observe breath_short near party when at(party, ?p) and airOf(?p, air_none) and breath(party) <= 4 "Your chest is burning. You have perhaps half an hour of what you carried in your lungs and your clothes.".
  Initially Set breath(party) to 12.
  // A company on its way between two places is at neither, so the rules above are silent for the length of a walk;
  // the air a way costs is said of the way, as the dose of a lit way is (ledger, 26).
  Measure wayAir(passage). Relation airPaid(group, passage).
  Initially Set wayAir(spine_from_seam) to 2. Initially Set wayAir(spine_from_wall) to 2. Initially Set wayAir(spine_wing) to 2.
  Initially Set wayAir(spine_imbar) to 2. Initially Set wayAir(spine_nave) to 3. Initially Set wayAir(wing_nave) to 2.
  Rule way_air when tookWay(party, ?w) and wayAir(?w) > 0 and not airPaid(party, ?w) and breath(party) >= wayAir(?w) {
    Decrease breath(party) by wayAir(?w). Assert airPaid(party, ?w). }
  Rule way_air_short when tookWay(party, ?w) and wayAir(?w) > 0 and not airPaid(party, ?w) and breath(party) < wayAir(?w)
    says "Halfway across there is nothing left in your lungs to breathe." {
    Set breath(party) to 0. Assert airPaid(party, ?w). Assert strikes(airless, party). }
  Rule way_air_clears when airPaid(party, ?w) and not tookWay(party, ?w) { Retract airPaid(party, ?w). }

  // Stillness is laid: a visitor who stays still for an hour is taken into the next course.
  Measure stillness(group). Relation lastPlace(group, place) exclusive. Relation laidIn(group).
  Rule still_counts when at(party, ?p) and lastPlace(party, ?p) and laidRoomM(?p) { Increase stillness(party) by 1. }
  Rule moved_on when at(party, ?p) and not lastPlace(party, ?p) { Assert lastPlace(party, ?p). Set stillness(party) to 0. }
  Relation laidRoomM(place).
  Initially Assert laidRoomM(spine). Initially Assert laidRoomM(finished_door). Initially Assert laidRoomM(finished_city).
  Initially Assert laidRoomM(finished_wild). Initially Assert laidRoomM(finished_beginning). Initially Assert laidRoomM(imbar_wing).
  Initially Assert laidRoomM(empty_niches). Initially Assert laidRoomM(nave). Initially Assert laidRoomM(heart).
  Observe still_warning near party when stillness(party) >= 4 and not laidIn(party) "The course under your feet is warmer than it was, and your boots will not lift as easily as they did.".
  Rule laid_in when stillness(party) >= 6 and not laidIn(party) says "You have stood still an hour. The next course is laid over your feet, and your knees, and you are part of the Masonry." {
    Assert laidIn(party). Assert hobbled(party). }

  // M1: the Spine.
  Observe spine_scene at spine when true "A bridge of dark banded stone crossing black. On either side the Masonry fills half the sky: towers and buttresses of stopped worlds, lit along their edges, going on past seeing. Far off, other long brackets like the Corbel reach out into the dark toward other points of light. Eleven of them.".

  // M2: a finished world. Walking the wing is walking that world's history backward to its beginning.
  Observe fdoor_scene at finished_door when true "A wing door carved with the overlapping circles of the procession's banner.".
  Observe fcity_scene at finished_city when true "A city of slender towers, stopped. Walking on, it gets younger, and smaller.".
  Observe fwild_scene at finished_wild when true "The city is fields, then forest, then bare rock, then fire. The air tastes of metal and burns going down.".
  Observe fbegin_scene at finished_beginning when true "At the very end of the wing a single course, no bigger than a hearthstone, holds the moment that world began. Then nothing.".
  Thing beginning "the moment the world began" at finished_beginning { State unbegun "A single course holds a world's first moment.". }
  Initially Assert kept(beginning).
  Observe world_begins near beginning when touched(beginning) "For the length of your touch a world begins around you: light, and heat, and rock coming together out of nothing, as long as someone holds on. It cannot be carried out.".

  // M3: the Imbar Wing. Everything quarried from Imbar so far is here; carried back through the Keeping to a
  // Remembrancer, each is set again where it was kept.
  Observe imbar_wing_scene at imbar_wing when true "A new wing, half built. Near its door are rooms that look like places you know: a stretch of the Quell road, a Weirs kitchen, a Tovash camp. Beyond them, a king's court whose king's face you cannot hold.".
  Kind quarried_moment "a quarried moment" is treasure worth 0 weighing 1
    described "A moment cut out of the Keeping, the size of a coin, with a season of somebody's life in it.".
  Item dane_moment "the fourth Dane's reign" is quarried_moment at imbar_wing.
  Item quell_moment "a season of Quell's year 74" is quarried_moment at imbar_wing.
  Observe niches_scene at empty_niches when true "A long gallery of empty niches, waiting, each the size of a year.".
  Relation quellAnchored(place).
  Rule quell_returned when keeps(shore_remembrancer, quell_moment) and not quellAnchored(quell) { Assert quellAnchored(quell). }

  // M4: the Nave of Sockets. Nine sockets, all empty; one beats.
  Observe nave_scene at nave when true "A nave so tall its roof cannot be seen, with nine sockets cut into its floor in a ring, each large enough for a hen's egg and each empty. One socket beats, faintly, like a pulse felt through stone.".
  Action seat_ithmar(actor: group, carrier: member, site: place) "Set Ithmar in the beating socket" {
    Description "The Patient is restored, and Imbar's past is quarried from the newest year backward, at the Masonry's own speed.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, nave) and memberOf(carrier, actor)
      and awake(carrier) and ownedItem(ithmar, carrier).
    Time 1 minute.
    Resolve drop(ithmar, carrier).
    On success { Assert seated(ghessil). Assert unbound(ghessil). }
    Result "The jewel goes into its socket as if it had never been out. The beat stops being faint. All round you, in the walls, the Laid stir, as at a voice.".
  }
  // Rebind: with the sigils seen being cut at the Separation, the jewel bound again, tighter. A binding needs a kept
  // moment as its seal: the binder's own, and the binder becomes part of the Keeping, dead and remembered forever.
  Action rebind(actor: group, carrier: member, binder: member, site: place) "Bind Ithmar tighter, {binder} giving the binding their own moment" {
    Description "The Patient's heart-bond breaks; the seed stops and the Corbel withdraws. The binder is set in the jewel, and dies, and everyone will remember them.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and (at(actor, nave) or at(actor, arbiter_vault))
      and knows(actor, sigils_known) and memberOf(carrier, actor) and awake(carrier) and ownedItem(ithmar, carrier)
      and memberOf(binder, actor) and awake(binder) and not rebound(corbel_site).
    Time 30 minutes.
    Resolve inter(binder).
    On success { Assert rebound(corbel_site). }
    Result "Stroke by stroke, as you watched it done at the Separation, the binding is cut tighter, and {binder} lays a hand on the jewel and is in it: you can see them, very small and clear, in the dark opal. Far off, felt in the knees, the seed stops building.".
  }

  // M5: the Heart: the Patient's own moment of expulsion, kept as its heart. Given time, the expulsion resumes: for as
  // long as the touch lasts the Patient goes on falling, farther from the planes, and the Masonry falls with it.
  Observe patient_heart_scene at heart when true "A chamber made of one moment. It is a fall: something vast, dark and many-limbed, too large to see whole, caught in the instant of being thrown out of the world. Around it, stopped, white robes and outstretched hands.".
  Thing patient_heart "the Patient's fall" at heart { State first_instant "The fall is stopped at its first instant.". }
  Initially Assert kept(patient_heart).
  Measure fallHeld(entity).
  Rule heart_falls when touched(patient_heart) { Increase fallHeld(patient_heart) by 1. }
  Observe heart_falling near patient_heart when touched(patient_heart) and fallHeld(patient_heart) < 6 "Under your hand the vast thing goes on falling, away, and everything around you leans after it. Your hand is going with it.".
  Rule exile_done when fallHeld(patient_heart) >= 6 and touched(patient_heart) and not exiled(corbel_site)
    says "You have held an hour. The Patient is gone out past the planes, and the Masonry with it, and you with it, because you did not let go." {
    Assert exiled(corbel_site). Assert fellWith(party). }
  Relation fellWith(group).
  Action touch_and_step(actor: group, carrier: member, site: place) "Touch the Heart and step away through the Keeping at once" {
    Description "Only a wearer of Ithmar can: touch, and be gone at the speed of thought, at the jewel's own cost.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, heart) and memberOf(carrier, actor)
      and awake(carrier) and ownedItem(ithmar, carrier) and memories(actor) >= 3 and not exiled(corbel_site).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Decrease memories(actor) by 3. Assert exiled(corbel_site). Retract at(actor, heart). Assert at(actor, tideline). }
    Result "You touch the fall, and it falls, and you are gone through the jewel before it can take you: three of your own moments go into the setting as you step. Behind you, the Patient falls out past the planes, and the Masonry with it.".
  }
  // Saro, who has no past to lose, may offer to hold on.
  Action saro_holds(actor: group, holder: member, site: place) "Let Saro hold on" {
    Description "She will hold the Heart for as long as it takes, and fall with it.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, heart) and travelsWith(saro, actor)
      and memberOf(holder, actor) and joinedAs(holder, saro) and not exiled(corbel_site).
    Time 10 minutes.
    Resolve inter(holder).
    On success { Assert exiled(corbel_site). Retract travelsWith(saro, actor). }
    Result "'Go,' says Saro, with both hands on the fall. 'I know how to be still.' The last you see of her she is falling with it, out past the planes, and she is not afraid.".
  }
  // Bargain at the heart: terms better than the Corbel's. Name a line in history and hold the Masonry to it.
  Action heart_bargain(actor: group, site: place) "Name a line in history to the Interlocutor, here, and hold the Masonry to it" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, heart) and knows(actor, newest_backward)
      and carries(actor, ithmar) and not bargained(actor).
    Time 10 minutes.
    On success { Assert bargained(actor). Assert heldToLine(corbel_site). }
    Result "Your own voice out of the walls of the Heart agrees: nothing after the Separation; and, because you know from which end it cuts, it agrees to cut from the beginning, not the face. The Masonry will be very patient about it.".
  }
  Relation heldToLine(place).
}

data/adventures/patient-star/moments.kyr:
Module moments "Kept moments: what the stilling took, laid as masonry, and given time by a hand" {
  // Where the stilling stops matter wholly it takes the moment, and the Masonry lays it as building stone (the
  // Undersun, the Corbel, the Masonry), and the Keeping keeps every moment of Imbar's past as a place. Three rules hold
  // in all of them: a kept thing touched resumes its moment for as long as the touch lasts; words spoken aloud are
  // laid into the course beneath; nothing kept can be changed, only cut.

  // A kept thing: a stopped flame, a man mid-word, a curtain of smoke, a falling stone.
  Relation kept(entity).
  // Being touched, now: its moment plays.
  Relation touched(entity).
  // Whoever has touched a thing at least once, and what they saw of it played.
  Relation playedFor(entity, group).
  Action touch(actor: group, target: entity, site: place) "Lay a hand on {target}" {
    Description "A kept thing touched takes up its moment again for as long as the hand stays on it, and stops when it is taken away.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and kept(target) and reaches(actor, target)
      and not touched(target) and not benighted(actor).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Assert touched(target). Assert playedFor(target, actor). }
  }
  Action let_go(actor: group, target: entity, site: place) "Take your hand from {target}" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and touched(target) and reaches(actor, target).
    Time 0.
    On success { Retract touched(target). }
  }
  // A hand cannot stay on a thing the company has walked away from.
  Rule touch_lost when touched(?t) and company(?c) and not reaches(?c, ?t) { Retract touched(?t). }

  // Speech is laid: words said aloud in course-work are taken into the course beneath, and give the Laid near them a
  // few seconds of their moment. Whispered, nothing is taken. The company is aloud until it chooses to whisper.
  Relation whispering(group).
  Relation laidRoom(place).
  Action whisper(actor: group) "Speak only in whispers" {
    Description "Below, words said aloud are taken into the stone, and wake whatever is laid there for a breath.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and not whispering(actor) and at(actor, ?r) and laidRoom(?r). Time 0.
    On success { Assert whispering(actor). }
    Result "You drop your voice to a breath, and so does everyone with you.".
  }
  Action speak_up(actor: group) "Speak aloud again" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and whispering(actor). Time 0.
    On success { Retract whispering(actor). }
    Result "You speak up again.".
  }
  // Every word spoken aloud in a laid room is a course laid down: the Masons can play it back, and the Interlocutor
  // speaks with it.
  Measure wordsLaid(group).
  Relation spokeAloud(group).
  // Every Mason carries a trowel: it lays and unlays course-glass, and in the Keeping cuts moments out.
  Kind trowel_kind "a Mason's trowel" like dagger worth 0 weighing 1
    described "A blade of something like stopped iron, set in a handle with no temperature. Laid against course-glass it lays or unlays.".
  Item spare_trowel "a Mason's trowel" is trowel_kind at tip_dome hidden until trowel_paid.
}

data/adventures/patient-star/neworrel.ky:
Module season "The Patient Star" {
  // New Orrel, the Collar and the Pit; the dark glass, the Tovash wells and the Split Ear camp; the Sixty and the Ear.
  Place new_orrel "New Orrel" is settlement within ghessil at 2, 0.
  Place collar "the Collar" is site within ghessil at 3, 0.
  Place dark_sector "the Dark Sector" is wilderness within ghessil at 4, 0.
  Place lit_fields "the lit fields" is wilderness within ghessil at 4, 1.

  Place no_gate "the Collar Road gate" is room within new_orrel at 0, 1 outdoors.
  Place no_market "the market road" is room within new_orrel at 1, 1 outdoors.
  Place barracks_house "the Warden's house" is building within new_orrel.
  Place barracks "the Warden's room" is room within barracks_house at 2, 1.
  Place widows "the Widows' Board" is room within new_orrel at 1, 2.
  Place waiting_house "the House of the Waiting" is room within new_orrel at 0, 2.
  Place storehouse "the Warden's storehouse" is room within new_orrel at 2, 0.
  Place sink "the Sink" is room within new_orrel at 3, 2 outdoors.
  Place balloon_yard "the balloon shed" is room within new_orrel at 3, 1 outdoors.

  Place collar_top "the top of the Collar" is room within collar at 0, 0 outdoors.
  Place plumb_tower "the plumb station" is room within collar at 1, 0.
  Place breach "the Breach" is room within collar at 2, 0 outdoors.
  Place inner_fill "the inner fill" is room within collar at 1, 1 outdoors.
  Place pit_floor "the Pit floor" is room within collar at 1, 2 outdoors.

  Place dark_glass "the dark glass" is room within dark_sector at 0, 0 outdoors.
  Place quarry "the Office quarry" is room within dark_sector at 1, 0 outdoors.
  Place tovash_wells "the Tovash wells" is room within dark_sector at 0, 1 outdoors.
  Place split_ear_camp "the Split Ear camp" is room within dark_sector at 1, 1 outdoors.

  Place the_sixty "the Sixty" is room within lit_fields at 0, 0 outdoors.
  Place the_ear "the Ear" is room within lit_fields at 1, 0.

  // The Collar Road: seven kilometres of rammed umber a metre above the lit glass, with a parapet on the Pit side.
  Passage collar_road "the Collar Road" is causeway between square and no_gate taking 5 hours.
  Initially Set wayDose(collar_road) to 72. Initially Set wayDoseFelted(collar_road) to 18.
  Passage no_street "the gate street" is road between no_gate and no_market taking 5 minutes.
  Passage warden_door "the Warden's door" is door between no_market and barracks.
  Passage widows_door "the Board's door" is door between no_market and widows.
  Passage waiting_door "the Waiting's door" is door between no_gate and waiting_house.
  Passage store_door "the storehouse door" is door between no_market and storehouse.
  Passage sink_lane "the east lane" is path between no_market and sink taking 5 minutes.
  Passage balloon_lane "the lane to the balloon shed" is path between sink and balloon_yard taking 5 minutes.
  Passage collar_ramp "the haul ramp" is path between no_market and collar_top taking 20 minutes.
  Passage tower_door "the plumb tower door" is door between collar_top and plumb_tower.
  Passage collar_walk "the Collar path" is path between collar_top and breach taking 40 minutes.
  Passage fill_slope "the inner slope" is path between collar_top and inner_fill taking 20 minutes.
  Passage pit_descent "the slumping fill into the Pit" is path between inner_fill and pit_floor taking 40 minutes.
  // The Coverers' Stair: a Seridane stair under the old Barrow, the Office's own door to the Granaries.
  Passage coverers_stair "the Coverers' Stair" is stair between storehouse and watch_room taking 30 minutes.
  // Across the dark glass from the Breach, and from Quell by the north-east, without dose: it carries no light.
  Passage dark_way "the dark glass" is path between breach and dark_glass taking 30 minutes.
  Passage quell_dark "the north-east margin" is path between old_quell and dark_glass taking 3 hours.
  Passage quarry_way "the quarry track" is track between dark_glass and quarry taking 10 minutes.
  Passage wells_way "the way to the wells" is path between dark_glass and tovash_wells taking 20 minutes.
  Passage camp_way "the camp path" is path between tovash_wells and split_ear_camp taking 15 minutes.
  // The wells: Seridane air shafts two metres across, a hundred metres to the water; side openings on the Shallows at
  // thirty-five and the Granaries at eighty-five.
  Passage well_shaft "a Tovash well shaft, by the rope" is shaft between tovash_wells and bunks taking 20 minutes needing rope.
  Passage well_deep "the same shaft, further down" is shaft between bunks and ring taking 20 minutes needing rope.
  // Out across the lit fields from the Collar's foot: three and a half kilometres of glass to the Sixty.
  Passage fields_way "the lit glass to the Sixty" is path between collar_top and the_sixty taking 1 hour.
  Initially Set wayDose(fields_way) to 24. Initially Set wayDoseFelted(fields_way) to 6.
  Passage ear_way "the glass to the Ear" is path between the_sixty and the_ear taking 15 minutes.
  Initially Assert litGround(the_sixty). Initially Assert litGround(the_ear). Initially Assert litGround(pit_floor).
  Initially Assert litGround(inner_fill).

  Observe gate_scene_no at no_gate when true "The Collar Road comes off the glass onto an island of red spoil. Ahead the Collar stands up like a red cliff thirty metres high, and the town is packed against its foot.".
  Observe market_no at no_market when true "A road of red dust between houses built of the Collar's own spoil. Everything sold here costs what it cost to bring up the Stair.".
  Observe sink_scene at sink when true "The ground has dropped two metres here since 374. The houses lean into one another like drunks, doors hanging, and nobody lives in them.".
  Observe store_scene at storehouse when true "The Warden's storehouse: sacks, barrels, and at the back a cut stone arch with a stair going down, a lamp, two guards and a clerk at a table.".
  Observe collar_top_scene at collar_top when true "A path wide enough for carts runs round the top of the ring. Rusted horse-whims stand at intervals, with wooden chutes running down the inside slope into the Pit's haze.".
  Observe tower_scene at plumb_tower when true "A wooden tower on the Collar top. A bronze plumb line on a drum goes down through a hole in the floor, and survey logs fill a shelf.".
  Observe breach_scene at breach when true "The ring is broken by a gap forty metres wide, its edges baked white. Beside it a drainage culvert of cut stone runs under the path. Beyond, the clear fields are dark: the same clear rock, with no light in it.".
  Observe fill_scene at inner_fill when true "Inside the Collar the fill slopes down toward the shaft in long red terraces, cracked like old mud. The heat comes up off it, and the light.".
  Observe pit_scene at pit_floor when true "The Pit floor is melt-rock and ceramic slag, too hot to stand on long, too bright to look across. From a dark mouth in the middle a thread of light goes straight up into the cloud, and beside it, hanging from nowhere, a cord as thick as a wrist, glowing along its whole length.".
  Hazard pit_heat "the Pit's heat" means "Deal (1d6) fire damage to ally.".
  Rule pit_burns when at(party, pit_floor) and not pitScorched(party) { Assert strikes(pit_heat, party). Assert pitScorched(party). }
  Relation pitScorched(group).
  Rule pit_cools when pitScorched(party) and not at(party, pit_floor) { Retract pitScorched(party). }
  // The fill is moving: a party on the inner slope may be carried down toward the light and heat.
  Hazard fill_slide "a slide of fill" means "Deal (2d6) physical damage to ally unless dexterity save against (12).".
  Rule fill_slides when at(party, inner_fill) and dice(inner_fill) <= 4 says "The terrace you are on lets go with a sound like a sigh and carries you down toward the light." {
    Assert strikes(fill_slide, party). Assert at(party, pit_floor). }

  // The Warden and the Office in New Orrel.
  Person aske "Ivo Aske" at barracks {
    Role "Warden of the Collar". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 3. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner proud.
  }
  Person office_guard "the Coverers' Stair guard" at storehouse {
    Role "two Office men and a clerk at the stair". Ancestry human. Numbers 2. Peaceable.
    Guards coverers_stair.
    State posted blocking "Two Office men and a clerk sit at the head of the Coverers' Stair.".
  }
  Initially Assert serves(office_guard, aske).
  Rule licence_stair when licensed(party) and not tolerates(office_guard, party) { Assert tolerates(office_guard, party). }
  Topic aske_king with aske "Ask the Warden about the king below" when true once {
    Says "'Royal property,' says Aske, 'and a wonder. When he is well enough I mean to bring him up to Sorne, and the court will see what the Crown holds under this plateau.' He smiles without warmth. 'You will have heard he wakes. I have it in a book.'".
  }
  Topic aske_balloon with aske "Ask the Warden about the shed by the Sink" when true once {
    Says "'A fire-balloon,' says Aske. 'Haldrish silk and Haldrish craftsmen. It will lift six to the bottom of the Cloud on a calm autumn dawn.' He watches you. 'Whoever goes up in it goes in the Crown's name. Bring me something from up there the court can hold in its hands, and you go in mine.'".
    On discuss { Assert offered(aske, actor). }
  }
  Action pay_aske(actor: group, site: place) "Pay the Warden twenty crowns toward his men's wages" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(aske, site) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 20
      and not admits(aske, actor).
    Time 5 minutes.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 20. Increase quantity(aske, gold) by 20. Assert admits(aske, actor).
      Assert serves(office_guard, aske). }
    Result "Aske counts it twice. 'The Crown is grateful,' he says, and writes you a pass for the Coverers' Stair and a place on the balloon.".
  }
  // In the eighth week, if nobody has taken the king, Aske's men carry him up the Coverers' Stair; at his age and
  // rate, without careful feeding, he has a fever within a fortnight.
  Rule king_carried when day(clock) >= 56 and at(amaru, last_hour) and not grieves(amaru) says "Word comes up the Coverers' Stair: the Warden's men have carried the old king up out of the Hour on a litter." {
    Retract at(amaru, last_hour). Assert at(amaru, barracks). Assert fevered(amaru). }
  Relation fevered(group).
  Observe king_in_barracks near amaru when at(amaru, barracks) and fevered(amaru) "The old king lies on a cot in the Warden's room under three blankets, burning with fever, and looks at the ceiling as if waiting for light to come down it.".

  // Annet Sorrel and the Breach widows; Lenna Marsh and the sinking; Ruan Haldane and the Waiting.
  Person coyle "Annet Sorrel" at widows {
    Role "speaker for the Breach widows". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner grim.
  }
  Topic coyle_breach with coyle "Ask Annet Sorrel about the Breach" when true once {
    Says "'Sixty-three men,' says Annet Sorrel. 'Mine among them. Somebody cut the Collar's drain in the storm of 352 and let the water into the Pit, and the steam came back up the chutes. Nobody was hanged for it.' She looks at you. 'They say the Tovash did it. I want the name. And I want the pensions, which have not been paid since 71.'".
  }
  Topic coyle_named with coyle "Tell Annet Sorrel who cut the Breach" when knows(actor, breach_cut) once {
    Says "She hears it out without sitting down. 'Bren of Ennick,' she says. 'Who holds the dying.' For a long time she says nothing. 'I will go to Ennick myself,' she says, 'and look at his door.'".
    On discuss { Assert accused(coyle, bren). }
  }
  Relation accused(group, group).
  Person lenna "Lenna Marsh" at plumb_tower {
    Role "Glass Office surveyor at the plumb station". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner acerbic.
  }
  Discovery sinking "The Late Sun is sinking about a metre a year, twenty-five times the old rate, and the Collar's inner face will slide into the shaft within ten years. Lenna Marsh's logs show it month by month since 372." {
    Source marsh_logs "Lenna Marsh's survey logs" at plumb_tower readable by party.
    Known by lenna.
  }
  Discovery footprints "Lenna Marsh's log for the 3rd of Frost 379: a single line of bare footprints on the inner fill near the Breach, going up from the Pit's edge.".
  Topic marsh_logs_t with lenna "Ask Lenna Marsh what her logs say" when true once {
    Says "'That the Sun is going down a metre a year,' says Marsh, 'and nobody in Sorne reads past the first line.' She flips back a year. 'And this. Third of Frost, last year: bare footprints on the fill, going up from the edge. I took it for a soldier's prank.' She closes the book. 'Nobody walks up out of that.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, footprints). }
  }
  // At dawn from the Collar top, for a few minutes before the sun washes it out, something long and dark shows in the
  // Standing Cloud.
  Discovery corbel_seen "At dawn from the Collar, a long dark shape hangs point-down in the Standing Cloud, high over the Pit, for a few minutes before the sun washes it out.".
  Observe corbel_dawn at collar_top when hour(clock) >= 5 and hour(clock) <= 6 "Before the sun clears the heath, high in the Standing Cloud over the Pit, something long and dark hangs point-down, like a bracket on a wall with no wall. Then the light comes and it is gone." teaches corbel_seen.
  Person ruan "Ruan Haldane" at waiting_house {
    Role "Elder of the Waiting". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner compassionate.
  }
  Topic ruan_voice with ruan "Ask Ruan Haldane what the Waiting wait for" when true once {
    Says "'For the answer,' says Ruan. 'Teodar said the name was finished in 71, and what comes after is not more of the name but what it called.' He spreads his hands. 'We listen. The Office has closed the Hour to us, and my people go down without leave.'".
  }
  Topic ruan_tone with ruan "Tell Ruan Haldane about the tone below" when knows(actor, tone_below) once {
    Says "Ruan sits down. 'Once an hour,' he says. 'And they did not tell me.' After a while he laughs, very quietly. 'Then it has answered. Teodar was right.' He gives you a tablet from his sleeve: the Waiting's copy of the transcript. 'Take it to whoever can read it.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, ward_names). }
  }

  // The Collar's culvert and the missing pin; the holder's bolt in Ennick (The Collar, Referee).
  Thing culvert "the drainage culvert" at breach {
    State standing "A culvert of cut stone runs under the Collar path beside the Breach, with a sluice frame at its mouth.".
    Tries looking.
  }
  Discovery herd_mark "Inside the culvert's sluice frame a Split Ear herd-mark is cut, and the gate's iron pin is missing from its square socket.".
  Observe culvert_looked near culvert when tried(culvert, looking) "On the inside of the sluice frame someone has cut a herd-mark: two notches and a split. The gate's pin is gone; its socket is square, and big as a thumb." teaches herd_mark.
  Discovery breach_cut "The Collar's drainage was cut in the storm of 352 by Ayzhe of the Split Ear and Bren of Ennick, with two Tovash riders, to flood the works and stop the Covering. They thought the fill would soak the water up.".
  Observe pin_matched near party when knows(party, herd_mark) and knows(party, bolt_is_pin) and not knows(party, breach_cut) "A Split Ear mark in the culvert, a sluice pin bolting the holder's door: whoever cut the Collar's drain was of the Split Ear, and was in Ennick after. You know of only one holder who was twenty-two that year." teaches breach_cut.

  // The dark glass: no light in it since 357, so it can be cut without dose, and Kell's forty-one dead stand in it.
  Observe dark_scene at dark_glass when true "The same clear rock as the lit fields, with no light in it at all. People stand in it, chest-deep, a little way off: men and women of Kell, held in 353 and dead when the fill cut the light four years later.".
  Observe quarry_scene at quarry when not halted(quarry) "Office crews are cutting blocks out of the dark glass with saws and grit. The quarry face is sixty metres from the nearest of Kell's dead, and pegs and string mark a line straight through them.".
  Observe quarry_halted at quarry when halted(quarry) "The quarry is quiet. The saws are racked and covered; somebody has pulled up the pegs that ran toward Kell's dead.".
  Relation halted(place).
  Measure quarryFace(place).
  Initially Set quarryFace(quarry) to 60.
  Rule quarry_cuts when not halted(quarry) and hour(clock) == 14 and quarryFace(quarry) > 0 and dice(quarry) <= 30 { Decrease quarryFace(quarry) by 2. }
  Observe quarry_reaches at quarry when quarryFace(quarry) <= 0 "The quarry face has reached the first of Kell's dead. A man stands in a block on a sledge, still chest-deep, looking at nothing, ready to go down the Stair.".
  Topic bren_quarry with bren "Tell Bren the Office is cutting toward Kell's dead" when true once {
    Says "Bren's face does not move. 'Then the road shuts,' he says. 'No Office cart comes up through Ennick while that quarry cuts.' He is already reaching for his coat.".
    On discuss { Assert roadClosed(ennick). }
  }
  Relation roadClosed(place).
  Rule aske_halts when roadClosed(ennick) and not halted(quarry) and day(clock) >= 10 says "Word comes across the plateau: the Warden has stopped the dark-glass quarry, and blames the licencer." { Assert halted(quarry). }

  Observe wells_scene at tovash_wells when true "Three stone rings stand on the dark glass, two metres across, with wooden frames for rope. Swallows go down one of them at dusk and do not come out.".
  Observe wells_swallows at tovash_wells when dark() "In the last of the light the swallows come in over the heath in ones and twos, fold their wings at the lip of the middle well, and drop down it.".

  // The Split Ear: Ayzhe, who cut the Breach; Ezh, who would ride with you; and, from the fifth week, Halu.
  Person ayzhe "Ayzhe of the Split Ear" at split_ear_camp {
    Role "clan-mother of the Split Ear". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner proud.
  }
  Person ezh "Ezh of the Split Ear" at split_ear_camp {
    Role "a young rider". Ancestry human. Calling ranger. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner cheerful.
  }
  Initially Set hire(ezh) to 2.
  Topic ayzhe_wife with ayzhe "Ask Ayzhe what she wants" when true once {
    Says "'The drum-maker's wife,' says Ayzhe. 'Out among the Sixty. We count our line from her, ten mothers back.' She looks toward the light. 'The last time someone buried the Pit, every held one on this plateau woke in the glass and choked. I will not leave her there for the next.'".
    On discuss { Assert willing(ezh, actor). }
  }
  Discovery moot_count "The Split Ear moot song's beat: the count the drum at the fair was playing when the Sixty were held.".
  Topic ayzhe_drum with ayzhe "Ask Ayzhe about the drum at the fair" when true once {
    Says "'The moot song,' says Ayzhe at once, and beats it on her knee: three, a rest, two, three. 'It is what the drum was playing when the light came up at the fair. My grandmother's grandmother told it.' She stops. 'Why?'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, moot_count). }
  }
  Topic ayzhe_breach with ayzhe "Ask Ayzhe who cut the Collar's drain" when knows(actor, breach_cut) once {
    Says "Ayzhe looks at you a long time. 'We thought the fill would drink it,' she says. 'Sixty-three. I count them every night.' She does not ask you what you will do.".
  }
  Person halu "Halu" at last_hour {
    Role "a woman of the old people, speaking Old Seridan". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she.
  }
  Initially Retract at(halu, last_hour).
  Rule halu_climbs when day(clock) >= 33 and not walkedOut(halu) says "Word goes round the Tovash camps: a dead woman of the old people climbed out of one of the wells in the night, talking." {
    Assert at(halu, split_ear_camp). Assert walkedOut(halu). }
  Relation walkedOut(group).
  Topic halu_kesset with halu "Tell Halu that Kesset is looking for her" when travelsWith(kesset, actor) or knows(actor, kings_book) once {
    Says "Halu understands one word in three of what you say, and the one she understands is the chamberlain's name. She sits down on the glass and weeps, and then she gets up and asks, in Old Seridan, the way to the city above.".
    On discuss { Assert willing(halu, actor). }
  }

  // The Sixty and the Ear (The Sixty; The Ear).
  Observe sixty_scene at the_sixty when true "A fair caught in the glass, chest-deep: horses in harness, a cauldron with its steam gone solid, children with their arms out, a man with a drum held against his chest. Their eyes are open.".
  Measure sixtyWatched(group).
  Rule watching_sixty when at(party, the_sixty) and not benighted(party) { Increase sixtyWatched(party) by 1. }
  Rule sixty_reset when not at(party, the_sixty) and sixtyWatched(party) > 0 { Set sixtyWatched(party) to 0. }
  Observe sixty_moved at the_sixty when sixtyWatched(party) >= 6 "You have watched an hour. A child's hand is higher than it was. The drum-maker's wife has turned her head a finger's width toward her husband.".
  Thing wife_block "the drum-maker's wife" at the_sixty {
    State held "A woman in a red felt cap stands in the glass beside the drummer, half-turned toward him.".
    State cut_free "The drum-maker's wife sits on a blanket on the glass, wrapped in felt, staring at the fair she was part of.".
    Change cut_wife "Grind the drum-maker's wife out of the glass" from held to cut_free needing digging.
  }
  Rule wife_tovash when state(wife_block, cut_free) and not freedWife(ayzhe) says "Two Split Ear riders come across the glass at a gallop and kneel by the woman in the red cap." { Assert freedWife(ayzhe). Assert grateful(ayzhe, party). }
  Relation freedWife(group).
  Observe ear_scene at the_ear when true "A low hut of umber brick with no floor. Inside, the bare glass is worn smooth in six places where people have knelt. In the corner an old man sits against the wall, cross-legged, head bowed, with his ear toward the glass. He has been dead since 368, and looks a week dead.".
  Discovery listeners_count "Teodar Lusk's count, year 0 to year 371: every syllable of the Voice heard since the Unlidding, in order; the plan of the Undersun's lowest built reach.".
  Thing count_shelf "the shelf of wax tablets" at the_ear {
    State shelved "A shelf of wax tablets runs along one wall: the count, year by year.".
    State read "The count's tablets have been taken down and read, and put back out of order.".
    Change read_count "Read the count through" from shelved to read.
  }
  Observe count_read at the_ear when state(count_shelf, read) "Three hundred and seventy years of syllables, a moon to a line. Teodar's last tablet says the name was finished, and what comes next will be an answer." teaches listeners_count.
}

data/adventures/patient-star/placed.kyr:
Module season "Hold One Season" {
  // The Ghessil Uplands as a country beyond a march: the company that comes into the Shift Market is the world's own.
  Entity party: group "Your company".
}

data/adventures/patient-star/quell.kyr:
Module season "Hold One Season" {
  Description "Quell, the Granaries of Tamaun and Ennick, late in Haying of the year 380: a cutter's uncle held eleven months in an open granary vault, and the people who want him, or his jars, brought up.".

  // The plateau, as far as this slice goes: Quell on the western margin, the heath and the Ramp to the gorge,
  // Ennick on the gorge floor, the Clear Fields above it, and the city under the glass.
  Place imbar "Imbar" is plane.
  Place ghessil "the Ghessil Uplands" is region within imbar.
  Place quell "Quell" is settlement within ghessil at 0, 1.
  Place heath "the heath" is wilderness within ghessil at 1, 1.
  Place ennick "Ennick" is settlement within ghessil at 2, 2.
  Place fields "the Clear Fields above Ennick" is wilderness within ghessil at 3, 1.
  Place tamaun "Tamaun" is site within ghessil at 1, 0.

  Place mutual_house "the Mutual's hall" is building within quell.
  Place lazar_house "the lazar house" is building within quell.
  Place office_house "the Glass Office" is building within quell.
  Place square "the Shift Market" is room within quell at 1, 1.
  Place mutual_yard "the Mutual's yard" is room within quell at 1, 0.
  Place mutual_hall "the Mutual's hall" is room within mutual_house at 1, 0.
  Place ward "the lazar ward" is room within lazar_house at 0, 1.
  Place weighing "the weighing yard" is room within office_house at 2, 1 outdoors.
  Place well_head "the North Well head" is room within quell at 0, 0 outdoors.
  Place old_quell "Old Quell" is room within quell at 2, 0 outdoors.

  Passage yard_gate "the Mutual's yard gate" is gate between square and mutual_yard.
  Passage hall_door "the hall door" is door between mutual_yard and mutual_hall.
  Passage lazar_door "the lazar house door" is door between square and ward.
  Passage weighing_gate "the weighing-yard gate" is gate between square and weighing.
  Passage well_lane "the well lane" is path between square and well_head taking 5 minutes.
  Passage east_gate "the old east gate" is gate between square and old_quell.

  Observe square_scene at square when not dark() "The square is umber brick on every side, the colour of dried blood, and not one window looks east. Sledges hiss on the cobbles between the shifts. At the weighing-yard gate a clerk calls the grades: 'One. One. Three. Reject.'".
  Observe square_night at square when dark() "The square is empty but for the dusk crew coming in, hoods back, grey in the face. Somebody coughs, dry and short, and does not stop for a while.".
  Observe yard_scene at mutual_yard when true "The Mutual's yard: sledges up on their ends against the wall, grit-sacks, coils of rope, and a trough of grey water where the cutters wash the glitter off their hands.".
  Observe hall_scene at mutual_hall when true "A long room with a hearth at one end and the Mutual's tally-boards along the wall: crews, shifts, debts, chalked and rubbed out and chalked again. Your own name is up there, with a number beside it.".
  Observe ward_scene at ward when true "Twenty beds, eighteen of them full. The cough here is the same cough as the square's, only slower.".
  Observe weighing_scene at weighing when true "The Glass Office's yard, in what were the Company's yards: scales, a stamp-table, blocks of clear stone stacked under red cloth, and a board by the gate that says LICENCES DRAWN FIRST OF THE MONTH.".
  Observe well_scene at well_head when true "The North Well is a round head of old cut stone, older than the town, with a stair going down inside it to the water.".
  Observe well_water at well_head when not drained(quell_wells) "Far down, the water is a coin of light. It comes up at blood heat, and smells faintly of iron.".
  Observe well_water_low at well_head when drained(quell_wells) "Far down, the water has sunk below the last of the old marks on the stair. Women are queuing at the well with their jars and arguing about it.".
  Observe old_quell_scene at old_quell when true "Three streets of umber-brick houses stand on clear ground, their doors open the way their owners left them in 355. Where a floor was beaten earth and not brick, the house is lit from below, and the light comes up through the doorway and lies along the street like water. Every shadow points west.".
  Initially Assert litGround(old_quell).

  // What Quell sells: felt, true and false; a stylus; honey from the Tovash.
  Kind umber_felt "an umber felt cloak" like cloak_of_protection worth 2 weighing 6
    described "Wool felted with iron clay, red-brown and heavy, with hood and mitts. Rubbed with a wet thumb, it leaves a rust mark.".
  Initially Assert shields(umber_felt).
  Kind madder_felt "an umber felt cloak" like cloak_of_protection worth 1 weighing 2
    described "Wool dyed red-brown, with hood and mitts. It is lighter than it looks.".
  Kind stylus "a stillglass stylus" is tool worth 2 weighing 0
    described "A needle of stillglass in a bone handle, for drawing along a voice-plate's growth lines.".
  Entity salt: good "handful of salt".
  // Glass lanterns are confiscated at the Stair: on the plateau a lantern is horn.
  Kind horn_lantern "a horn lantern" like lantern worth 1
    described "A tallow lantern in a horn case. No glass: up here, glass carries the light.".
  Kind night_honey "a jar of night honey" is gear worth 1 weighing 1
    described "Dark, slightly bitter honey from bees that work by cloudlight. It keeps for decades.".
  Kind stillglass_knife "an unstamped stillglass knife" like dagger worth 5 weighing 1
    described "A stillglass blade with no Office stamp on the tang. The edge has never needed sharpening.".
  Person rusk "Rusk" at square {
    Role "the felt-lender, with her bales of red felt". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she.
    Sells umber_felt for 2 coin from 3.
    Sells stylus for 2 coin from 1.
    Sells horn_lantern for 1 coin from 2.
    Sells lamp_oil for 1 coin from 4.
    Sells rope for 1 coin from 2.
  }
  Person barrow_boy "a boy with a barrow" at square {
    Role "selling felt cloaks off a barrow, cheap". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he.
    Sells madder_felt for 1 coin from 4.
  }
  Person honey_seller "Ezh's aunt" at square {
    Role "a Tovash woman selling night honey by the jar". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she.
    Sells night_honey for 1 coin from 4.
    Sells salt for 1 coin from 6.
  }
  Topic rusk_felt with rusk "Ask Rusk about the barrow boy's felt" when true once {
    Says "'Madder,' says Rusk, without looking. 'Dyed wool. Wet your thumb and rub it: real felt leaves rust on you. That stuff leaves nothing, and lets everything through. Weigh it in your hand, while you are about it. A cloak of mine is six kilos and you feel every one.'".
  }

  // The Mutual: Dagny Ferrow, its Master, and Garret's crew.
  Person dagny "Dagny Ferrow" at mutual_hall {
    Role "Master of the Cutters' Mutual". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner grim.
  }
  Person ness "Ness Oakum" at mutual_yard {
    Role "a cutter of Garret's old crew". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Plans 14 steps. Uses go, change_thing. Pronouns she. Manner acerbic.
  }
  Person crew "Dagny's crew" at mutual_yard {
    Role "two cutters of the Mutual, felted, with poles and a sledge". Ancestry human. Numbers 2. Peaceable. Plans 14 steps. Uses go, change_thing.
  }
  Person grit "Grit" at mutual_yard {
    Role "the Mutual's yard dog, grey about the muzzle". Species dog. Pronouns she.
  }
  Observe grit_scene near grit of grit when at(grit, mutual_yard) "A grey bitch lies across the hall doorstep with her chin on her paws, and thumps her tail once for anyone in felt.".
  Initially Assert serves(ness, dagny). Initially Assert serves(crew, dagny).

  Discovery garret_held "Garret, a cutter of the Mutual, walked into an open granary vault in Tamaun last autumn to take the jars, and has stood in its light for eleven months, held." {
    Known by dagny, ness, crew.
  }
  Topic dagny_garret with dagny "Ask Dagny about Garret" when not cameUp(garret) once {
    Says "'Your uncle,' says Dagny. 'You know as much as I do, or you should. Last Harvest he went into an open vault in the Granary Ring to take jars, and the light had him before he was three steps in. Ness saw him from the doorway. She could not get to him and nor could anyone.' She rubs out a chalk mark on the board with the side of her fist. 'He is not dead. He is standing in there with his hand out, the way you'd reach for a jar.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, garret_held). }
  }
  Relation offered(group, group).
  Topic dagny_offer with dagny "Ask Dagny what she would have you do" when not cameUp(garret) and not offered(dagny, actor) once {
    Says "'Your debt to this hall is fourteen felt-lengths,' says Dagny. 'Twenty-eight crowns. I will rub out half of it the day Garret walks into this room on his own feet. The crew goes down when it has the felt, in three days or four. Go with them, or go down alone and before them, I don't care which. Only bring him up.' She looks at your hands. 'And keep that knife of yours out of Pike's sight. It has no stamp.'".
    On discuss { Assert offered(dagny, actor). }
  }
  Topic dagny_way with dagny "Ask Dagny how the crew goes down" when not cameUp(garret) once {
    Says "'By the North Well and the West Gallery, the way we always have,' says Dagny. 'There is an Office chain on the well-head. A licence opens it, and the licences are drawn on the first of the month. Hal Brewin keeps the chain, and Hal drinks.' She shrugs. 'Four hours from the well to the city, if the Neck lets you through. It is late summer: there is a metre of air under the Neck now, more than most years.'".
  }
  Topic ness_vault with ness "Ask Ness about the vault where Garret is" when not cameUp(garret) once {
    Says "'Ninth vault of the Ring, on the north side,' says Ness. 'Shutter open, light coming down off the ceiling like a white post. Jars all round him. Forty jars in a vault, umber-glazed and not a crack in one, and a collector in Sorne pays three crowns a jar.' She spits. 'He is not dying, you know. Nobody held is dying. He'll keep.'".
  }
  Topic crew_plan with crew "Ask the crew when they go down" when not cameUp(garret) and not descended(crew) once {
    Says "'When the felt comes, three days, four,' says the elder of the two. 'Felt, poles, rope, a sledge-cloth to drag him on. Ness knows the vault.' He does not look at Ness when he says it.".
  }
  Relation descended(group).

  // Saro and Sister Wenda, at the lazar house.
  Person wenda "Sister Wenda" at ward {
    Role "an Arbitral sister, who keeps the lazar house". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner compassionate.
    Wants night_honey.
  }
  Person saro "Saro" at ward {
    Role "a woman who walked out of the deep glass last autumn". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 6. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner stoic.
    Joins "Saro stands at once, as if she had been waiting for nothing else. 'Down,' she says. 'Yes.'".
    Carries trowel_kind.
  }
  // Her bones and teeth are stillglass: the light does not slow her, in the company or out of it.
  Initially Assert unslowed(saro). Initially Assert unslowed(member_saro_person).
  Discovery saro_cold "Saro never warms. Her hands have no temperature at all, like stillglass, and she has been in the lazar house since last autumn without once being cold or hot." {
    Known by wenda.
  }
  Topic wenda_saro with wenda "Ask Sister Wenda about Saro" when true once {
    Says "'She came in last Frost, walking, from the east,' says Wenda. 'No fever, no cough, nothing I can treat. She eats, a little. She learns.' She lowers her voice. 'She does not warm. I have held her hands in mine for an hour by the stove and they are no warmer at the end than at the start, and no colder. The others have started to notice.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, saro_cold). }
  }
  Event wenda_honey near wenda when keeps(wenda, ?j) and itemKind(?j, night_honey) "Sister Wenda turns the jar to the window and smiles for the first time. 'For the coughers,' she says. 'A spoon at night, and they sleep.' She puts it on the shelf with the other two." then { Assert thanked(wenda, party). }
  Relation thanked(group, group).
  Topic saro_stone with saro "Ask Saro what she wants" when true once {
    Says "Saro answers in a Tovashi a month old and already good. 'To go back into the glass. Down, where it is being built.' She looks at you with great attention. 'Do you know of a stone that sings? Under here. It sings once in each hour. Everyone I ask says no.'".
  }
  Topic saro_down with saro "Tell Saro you are going down into Tamaun" when knows(actor, garret_held) and not willing(saro, actor) and not travelsWith(saro, actor) once {
    Says "'Into the old city,' says Saro. 'Down.' She has already stood up. 'I will come. I do not need felt.'".
    On discuss { Assert willing(saro, actor). }
  }

  // The Glass Office: Halloran Pike, the licence lottery, and Hal Brewin at the chain.
  Person pike "Halloran Pike" at weighing {
    Role "the Glass Office licencer". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner stoic.
  }
  Person hal "Hal Brewin" at well_head {
    Role "the Office's man at the North Well chain". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner jovial.
    Guards well_stair.
    State watching blocking "Hal Brewin sits on a stool by the chain-gate with a cudgel across his knees.".
    State drunk "Hal Brewin is asleep on his stool with his mouth open.".
  }
  Topic pike_licence with pike "Ask Pike about a salvage licence" when not licensed(actor) once {
    Says "'Ten crowns to put your name in,' says Pike, 'and the names are drawn at this gate on the first of the month, one in four. Win, and the North Well chain opens to you for the month. Lose, and the ten crowns are the Crown's.' He blots a figure. 'Nobody goes down the Well without a licence. Nobody.'".
  }
  Topic pike_son with pike "Ask Pike about the cough in his house" when true once {
    Says "Pike's pen stops. 'My son,' he says. 'Glass-lung, at nineteen. There is a physician in Sorne who will see him for twenty crowns a visit, and I am paid nine a month.' He starts writing again, harder.".
  }
  Relation licensed(group). Relation entered(group).
  Action enter_lottery(actor: group, site: place) "Put your name in for this month's licences, ten crowns" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(pike, site) and not licensed(actor)
      and not entered(actor) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 10.
    Time 5 minutes.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 10. Increase quantity(pike, gold) by 10. Assert entered(actor). }
    Result "Pike writes your name on a slip, folds it twice, and drops it in a box with a great many others.".
  }
  // The draw, at dawn on the first of the month; one in four.
  Rule lottery_won when entered(party) and hour(clock) == 8 and day(clock) == 6 and dice(party) <= 25 says "At the weighing-yard gate the clerk calls the names drawn for the month. Yours is the third." {
    Retract entered(party). Assert licensed(party). Assert tolerates(hal, party). }
  Rule lottery_lost when entered(party) and hour(clock) == 8 and day(clock) == 6 and dice(party) > 25 says "The licences for the month are called at the weighing-yard gate. Your name is not among them." {
    Retract entered(party). }
  // Hal can be had for wine, or for coin, and is asleep by midnight most nights.
  Action bribe_hal(actor: group, site: place) "Give Hal Brewin a crown to look the other way" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(hal, site) and state(hal, watching)
      and not tolerates(hal, actor) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 1.
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 1. Increase quantity(hal, gold) by 1. Assert tolerates(hal, actor). }
    Result "Hal looks at the crown, and up the lane, and puts it in his boot. 'Never saw you,' he says, and unhooks the chain.".
  }
  Rule hal_sleeps when hour(clock) == 0 and state(hal, watching) { Assert state(hal, drunk). Assert asleep(hal). }
  Rule hal_wakes when hour(clock) == 6 and state(hal, drunk) { Assert state(hal, watching). Retract asleep(hal). }
  Thing chain_gate "the chain-gate" on well_stair {
    State locked blocking "An Office chain-gate hangs across the stair-head, padlocked.".
    State unhooked "The Office chain hangs unhooked from its staple.".
    Change unhook "Unhook the chain-gate" from locked to unhooked at well_head.
  }
  // The chain is Hal's to open, and the Mutual's crews go through it as he lets them.
  Initially Assert keyholder(hal, chain_gate). Initially Assert tolerates(hal, crew). Initially Assert tolerates(hal, ness).
  Rule chain_open_licensed when tolerates(hal, party) and state(chain_gate, locked) and (at(party, well_head) or at(party, well_foot)) { Assert state(chain_gate, unhooked). }
  // Unhooked under his nose, it is hooked again, and he remembers who did it.
  Rule chain_rehooked when state(chain_gate, unhooked) and perceives(hal, party) and not tolerates(hal, party)
    says "Hal Brewin gets up off his stool, hooks the chain back on its staple, and stands in front of it. 'No,' he says." {
    Assert state(chain_gate, locked). }
  Rule chain_shut when state(chain_gate, unhooked) and not at(party, well_head) and not at(party, well_foot) and state(hal, watching) { Assert state(chain_gate, locked). }

  // The knife has no stamp, and an Office man who sees it says so.
  Item knife "your stillglass knife" is stillglass_knife at square.
  Observe knife_here at square when at(knife, square) "Your own knife is on the cobbles where you set it down to haggle, an unstamped stillglass blade that has never needed sharpening.".
  Relation seized(item).
  Event knife_seen when carries(party, knife) and (perceives(pike, party) or perceives(hal, party)) and not seized(knife) "'That blade has no stamp,' says the Office man, and holds out his hand. 'A fifth of its worth to the Crown, now, or the next one costs you the hand that holds it.' You pay him a crown." then {
    Assert seized(knife). Decrease quantity(party, gold) by 1. }

  // The bargain: half the debt, the day Garret walks into the hall with the one Dagny made it with.
  Relation forgiven(group).
  Event dagny_keeps_word near dagny when (travelsWith(garret, party) or following(garret, party)) and offered(dagny, party) and at(party, mutual_hall) and not forgiven(party) "Dagny looks at Garret for a long moment, and then at you. She takes the rag off its nail and rubs out the number beside your name on the board, and chalks in another, half the size. 'Fourteen crowns,' she says. 'I keep my word. Sit him by the fire before he falls down.'" then {
    Assert forgiven(party). Assert cameUp(garret). Decrease owes(party, dagny) by 14. }
  Relation broughtBy(group, group).
  Rule brought_by when travelsWith(garret, party) and not broughtBy(garret, party) { Assert broughtBy(garret, party). }
  Rule led_by when following(garret, party) and not broughtBy(garret, party) { Assert broughtBy(garret, party). }
  Event crew_brought_him near dagny when at(garret, mutual_hall) and not broughtBy(garret, party) and at(party, mutual_hall) "Garret is by the hall fire with a blanket round him and a bowl in his hands, and the crew who brought him up are drinking. Dagny does not look at you. Your number on the board is the same as it was.".

  Objective find_garret when not cameUp(garret) and asleep(garret) "Garret, your uncle, is held in an open granary vault under Quell. Dagny will halve your debt if you bring him up.".
  Objective bring_garret when not cameUp(garret) and not asleep(garret) "Garret is awake, and slow, and hungry, a long way under Quell. Bring him up to the Mutual's hall.".
  Objective held_alive when knows(party, garret_held) and not knows(party, doran_breathed) and not knows(party, prayer_label) "Are the held truly alive? In Ennick they visit theirs once a month to watch them breathe.".
}

data/adventures/patient-star/stairhead.k:
Module season "The Patient Star" {
  // Stairhead House on the lip of the Scarp, the Arbiters' Way beneath it, and the Vault at its foot.
  Place stairhead "Stairhead House" is settlement within ghessil at 0, 3.
  Place arbiters_way "the Arbiters' Way" is site within ghessil at 0, 4.
  Place stair_top "the head of the Stair" is room within stairhead at 0, 1 outdoors.
  Place chapel_sh "the chapel of Stairhead" is room within stairhead at 1, 1.
  Place vestry_sh "the vestry" is room within stairhead at 2, 1.
  Place strongroom "the strongroom" is room within stairhead at 2, 2.
  Place chapter "the chapter house" is room within stairhead at 1, 2.
  Place platform "the platform" is room within stairhead at 1, 0 outdoors.
  Place way_upper "the upper Way" is level within arbiters_way.
  Place way_lower "the lower Way" is level within arbiters_way.
  Place way_door_room "under the platform" is room within way_upper at 0, 0 underground.
  Place counting_stair "the Stair That Counts" is room within way_upper at 0, 1 underground.
  Place separation_gallery "the Gallery of the Separation" is room within way_lower at 0, 2 underground.
  Place vault_ward "the Ward of the Vault" is room within way_lower at 0, 3 underground.
  Place arbiter_vault "the Arbiters' Vault" is room within way_lower at 0, 4 underground.

  Passage gorge_road "the gorge road" is road between lower_road and stair_top taking 4 hours.
  Passage chapel_door_sh "the chapel door" is door between stair_top and chapel_sh.
  Passage vestry_door "the vestry door" is door between chapel_sh and vestry_sh.
  Passage strong_door "the strongroom door" is door between vestry_sh and strongroom.
  Passage chapter_door "the chapter house door" is door between chapel_sh and chapter.
  Passage platform_steps "the platform steps" is steps between stair_top and platform.
  // The House's platform, which its brothers take for a Seridane signal station, is the Way's door.
  Passage way_mouth "a stair under the platform's flagstones" is stair between platform and way_door_room hidden until way_found.
  Passage way_down "the Way, past the Door" is passage between way_door_room and counting_stair taking 2 hours.
  Passage counted_way "the ringing steps" is stair between counting_stair and separation_gallery taking 3 hours.
  Passage gallery_way "the length of the relief" is passage between separation_gallery and vault_ward taking 12 hours.
  Passage ward_way "the Ward's threshold" is doorway between vault_ward and arbiter_vault.

  Observe stair_top_scene at stair_top when true "The Stair road comes up beside the falls to a walled house of grey stone on the lip of the Scarp. Bells mark the offices. Below, four falls stand one above another, and the lowland goes off green to the edge of the sky.".
  Observe chapel_scene_sh at chapel_sh when true "A plain Arbitral chapel. The brothers sing seven offices a day; at the night office the cellarer hangs his keys in the vestry, and every man of them is in here.".
  Observe vestry_scene at vestry_sh when true "A narrow vestry of copes and candles, with a row of iron hooks by the door.".
  Observe platform_scene at platform when true "An old stone platform older than the House, set with bronze fittings in a ring. The brothers dry washing on it. The fittings are mirror mounts, though nobody here knows it.".
  Discovery way_found "Under the platform's centre flagstones a stair goes down into rock that has not changed since it was cut: the Way's door is the House's own platform." {
    Found by searching platform "The centre flagstones ring hollow. Under them, a stair of white stone goes down into rock that has the look of something that has never once been touched by weather.".
  }

  // Prior Aurel Mance and Brother Tam (Stairhead House).
  Person mance "Prior Aurel Mance" at chapel_sh {
    Role "Prior of Stairhead House". Ancestry human. Calling cleric. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner proud.
  }
  Person tam "Brother Tam" at chapel_sh {
    Role "the cellarer". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner jovial.
  }
  Initially Assert serves(tam, mance).
  Topic mance_stone with mance "Ask the prior what the mother-church wants" when true once {
    Says "'The Long Hour, which the old king keeps below,' says Mance, 'and whatever comes up the Plumb.' He folds his hands. 'The mother-church believes there is a relic of the Virina under this plateau. A stone that sings. I am to have it before the Crown does.'".
  }
  // Buys reads only the shared catalog, so a kind of this module's own cannot be bought by Buys (ledger, 24).
  Action sell_plates(actor: group, carrier: member, site: place) "Sell the Long Hour to the prior for six hundred crowns" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(mance, site) and memberOf(carrier, actor)
      and awake(carrier) and ownedItem(long_hour, carrier).
    Time 10 minutes.
    Resolve drop(long_hour, carrier).
    On success { Assert keeps(mance, long_hour). Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 600. }
    Result "Mance turns every plate to the light before he counts out the coin, and then he counts it twice.".
  }
  Kind strong_key "the strongroom key" is tool worth 0 weighing 0 described "A heavy iron key on a ring.".
  Thing key_hooks "the hooks by the vestry door" at vestry_sh {
    Holds.
    State empty_hook "The hooks by the vestry door are empty.".
    State keys_hung "The cellarer's keys hang on the hook by the vestry door.".
  }
  Item strongkey "the strongroom key" is strong_key in key_hooks owned by tam.
  // The night office: the brothers in chapel, the keys on the hook, the vestry unwatched.
  Rule night_office when hour(clock) == 0 and state(key_hooks, empty_hook) and inside(strongkey, key_hooks) { Assert state(key_hooks, keys_hung). }
  Rule office_ends when hour(clock) == 1 and state(key_hooks, keys_hung) { Assert state(key_hooks, empty_hook). }
  Thing strong_lock "the strongroom lock" on strong_door {
    State locked blocking "The strongroom door is iron-bound and locked.".
    State open "The strongroom door stands open.".
    Change unlock_strong "Unlock the strongroom" from locked to open needing strongkey.
    Change pick_strong "Pick the strongroom lock" from locked to open needing lockwork.
  }
  Observe strong_scene at strongroom when true "Chests, a reliquary, and a shelf of sealed papers under the prior's seal. On a cushion, as if it were holy, a clear block the size of a hearthstone.".
  Discovery ottavine_note "Prior Ottavine's note on the Ennick holding prayer: a Seridane granary formula, painted on the grain jars; it means hold one season, then give it out." {
    Source ottavine_papers "Prior Ottavine's sealed papers" at strongroom readable by party.
  }
  Observe ottavine_label near party when knows(party, ottavine_note) and not knows(party, prayer_label) "Ottavine had it forty years ago, in a hand that does not shake: the prayer is a grain jar's label." teaches prayer_label.
  Discovery church_letters "Letters from the mother-church to Stairhead, eighty years of them, asking about 'a stone that sings below'.".
  Thing letters_box "a box of letters" at strongroom {
    State shut_box "A box of letters under the mother-church's seal.".
    State read_box "The mother-church's letters lie open, eighty years of them.".
    Change read_letters "Break the seal and read the mother-church's letters" from shut_box to read_box.
  }
  Observe letters_read at strongroom when state(letters_box, read_box) "Every one asks the same thing in other words: whether the prior has heard of a stone that sings, below." teaches church_letters.
  Thing ilis_block "Ilis's block" at strongroom {
    State resting "A clear block the size of a hearthstone sits on a cushion. It has no temperature.".
    Tries listening.
  }
  Observe block_wind near ilis_block when tried(ilis_block, listening) "It gives back a sound, very faint, from the day it stopped, out on the heath before anyone was born. It is only wind.".

  // The Arbiters' Way (The Undersun, The Arbiters' Way): ordinary rock kept unchanged by the Virina, which nothing of
  // the Varakiiri can enter. Four gates test whoever walks it; each is answered from the world's own history.
  Observe way_door_scene at way_door_room when true "A door of white stone with no hinges, in white rock. Over it, in a hand the eye follows easily, is carved one question: WAS THE HOUR GIVEN?".
  Discovery hour_fell "The hour was not given: it fell. A thing came down out of a clear sky on an autumn night, and the crane-priests of the lake wrote it down before any Seridane claimed it.".
  Thing the_door "the Door" on way_down {
    State asking blocking "The Door asks whether the hour was given.".
    State answered "The Door stands open.".
    State sealed_year blocking "The Door is shut, and will be, the carving says, for a year and a day.".
    Change answer_fell "Answer that the hour fell, and was not given" from asking to answered after learning hour_fell.
    Change answer_argued "Answer as the Coverers argued: it fell" from asking to answered after learning coverer_case.
  }
  Measure doorSealedAt(entity).
  Action answer_given(actor: group, site: place) "Answer that the hour was given" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, way_door_room) and state(the_door, asking).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Assert state(the_door, sealed_year). Set doorSealedAt(the_door) to watch(clock). }
    Result "The Door does not move. Below the question, letters you had not seen fill with light: a year and a day.".
  }
  Rule door_reopens when state(the_door, sealed_year) and watch(clock) >= doorSealedAt(the_door) + 52704 { Assert state(the_door, asking). }

  Observe counting_scene at counting_stair when true "The Way goes down by a stair of nine thousand steps. Each rings a note when trodden, and each note is different, and they do not repeat.".
  Thing ringing "the ringing steps" on counted_way is scenery {
    State uncounted blocking "The steps ring under your feet. A walker who loses the count, the carving at the top says, comes back to the top.".
    State counted "You have the count of the steps, and the stair lets you down.".
    Change count_names "Count the steps aloud in the twelve hour-names, round and round" from uncounted to counted after learning hour_names.
  }
  Action count_numbers(actor: group, site: place) "Count the steps in numbers" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, counting_stair) and state(ringing, uncounted).
    Time 18.
    Result "Somewhere past four thousand the notes run together, and you find you have said a number twice. You are standing at the top again, and three hours have gone.".
  }

  Observe relief_scene at separation_gallery when true "A relief two kilometres long, carved by no hand you know: a war across a sky divided, figures with light for wings and figures made of darkness and hooks, struck and striking; and below them tall figures in white, in a ring, holding the world apart like the pages of a book.".
  Relation wroteDown(group).
  Action write_as_you_walk(actor: group, site: place) "Walk the relief writing down only what you see" {
    Description "A day's walk. The Remembrancer at its end asks what you saw, and lets through only those who add nothing.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, separation_gallery) and not wroteDown(actor) and not benighted(actor).
    Time 72.
    On success { Assert wroteDown(actor). }
    Result "You walk it slowly, a day long, and write down what is carved and nothing else. Your hand aches.".
  }
  Person gallery_keeper "a Remembrancer" at separation_gallery {
    Role "a servant of the Virina, tall, made of the sound of bells". Peaceable. Pronouns they.
    Guards gallery_way.
    State asking_g blocking "At the end of the relief a figure made of the sound of bells waits to ask what you saw.".
  }
  Topic keeper_tell with gallery_keeper "Tell the Remembrancer what you saw" when wroteDown(actor) once {
    Says "You read it from what you wrote. The Remembrancer hears it through to the last line and does not interrupt. 'Nothing added,' it says, in many bells. 'Go down.'".
    On discuss { Assert tolerates(gallery_keeper, actor). }
  }
  Topic keeper_memory with gallery_keeper "Tell the Remembrancer what you remember of it" when not wroteDown(actor) and not tolerates(gallery_keeper, actor) {
    Says "You tell it. Somewhere in the telling you say the dark figures had faces, and they had not. 'Added,' says the Remembrancer, gently, and you are standing at the start of the relief.".
  }

  // The Ward of the Vault: three questions, in order. A party guessing is turned away for a year.
  Discovery held_feed "What the held feed: the instant a person is held, their moment is taken and laid in the Undersun as a keystone. The Holdfolk's mercy has been building the Masonry's vaults for three hundred and forty years.".
  Observe ward_scene_v at vault_ward when true "A round white chamber with a white door, and over it three questions in a ring: WAS THE HOUR GIVEN? WHO KILLED THE KEEPER'S DAUGHTER? WHAT DO THE HELD FEED?".
  Thing vault_seal "the Ward" on ward_way {
    State first_q blocking "The first question is lit: was the hour given?".
    State second_q blocking "The second question is lit: who killed the keeper's daughter?".
    State third_q blocking "The third question is lit: what do the held feed?".
    State warded "The Ward is dark, and the white door stands open.".
    State turned blocking "The Ward is dark and the door shut. It will be so for a year.".
    Change ward_one "Answer: it fell" from first_q to second_q after learning hour_fell.
    Change ward_one_argued "Answer: it fell, as the Coverers said" from first_q to second_q after learning coverer_case.
    Change ward_two "Answer: Answerer loyalists, her father's men" from second_q to third_q after learning selane_murdered.
    Change ward_three "Answer: the Masonry; the held are its keystones" from third_q to warded after learning held_feed.
  }
  Action ward_guess(actor: group, site: place) "Answer the lit question as best you can guess" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, vault_ward)
      and (state(vault_seal, first_q) or state(vault_seal, second_q) or state(vault_seal, third_q)).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Assert state(vault_seal, turned). Set doorSealedAt(vault_seal) to watch(clock). }
    Result "The light goes out of the questions one by one, and the white door does not open.".
  }
  Rule ward_reopens when state(vault_seal, turned) and watch(clock) >= doorSealedAt(vault_seal) + 52560 { Assert state(vault_seal, first_q). }

  // U6, the Arbiters' Vault: Ithmar in its cage of rods, the Tally, and a Remembrancer at the door.
  Kind ithmar_kind "Ithmar" is treasure worth 0 weighing 0
    described "A hen's egg of something like dark opal, cut with sigils the mind will not name. It hums at the pitch of the note under the Pit.".
  Kind tally_kind "the Virina's Tally" is tool worth 0 weighing 2
    described "A rod of white metal marked like a ruler. It shows how much of the Keeping has been cut away; in the Keeping, how far any moment is from now.".
  Observe arbiter_scene at arbiter_vault when true "A white chamber, round, plain, very old and perfectly clean. The floor hums.".
  Thing cage "a cage of white rods" at arbiter_vault {
    Holds.
    State caged "In the centre of the chamber a jewel the size of a hen's egg hangs in the air in a cage of white rods. It is engraved with sigils the eye can follow and the mind will not name.".
  }
  Item ithmar "Ithmar" is ithmar_kind in cage.
  Item tally "the Virina's Tally" is tally_kind at arbiter_vault owned by remembrancer.
  Observe tally_seen at arbiter_vault when at(tally, arbiter_vault) "Against the wall leans a rod of white metal, marked like a ruler.".
  Person remembrancer "the Remembrancer of the Vault" at arbiter_vault {
    Role "a servant of the Virina, at the door". Peaceable. Pronouns they.
    Objects "'Why do you carry the Tally away?' asks the Remembrancer, in many bells. 'Say it truly, and it is lent.'".
  }
  Discovery quarrying "The Masonry is cutting Imbar's past away through the seed, a season at a time, and since the year 371 more than thirty hollows have been quarried from the Keeping; the Tally measures how much.".
  Topic remembrancer_tally with remembrancer "Tell the Remembrancer why you would carry the Tally" when knows(actor, quarrying) once {
    Says "'To prove to the plateau how fast its past is being taken,' you say, 'and to find my way in the Keeping.' The Remembrancer is silent a long time, which is many bells not ringing. 'True,' it says, 'and sufficient. It is lent.'".
    On discuss { Assert lends(remembrancer, tally, actor). }
  }
  Topic remembrancer_help with remembrancer "Ask the Remembrancer to help keep Imbar" when true once {
    Says "'It is yours to keep,' says the Remembrancer, courteously and at length. 'The planes were parted so that each could keep itself. We tend what is kept. We do not fight for it.' It inclines its head toward the jewel. 'A living hand on Ithmar walks the Keeping. Whoever touches the hand goes with it.'".
  }
  Topic remembrancer_quarry with remembrancer "Ask the Remembrancer what the Tally shows" when true once {
    Says "'How much of the Keeping has been cut away,' says the Remembrancer. 'Since your year 371, thirty-one hollows, most of them in your last years. Each is a season nobody can remember, and claims that rested on it are loose.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, quarrying). }
  }

  // The Concord (The Corbel and the Concord), compactly: called to Stairhead when the Corbel can no longer be denied;
  // each seat for or against three motions; evidence shown moves the seats that care about it; a vote.
  Kind motion. Entity motion_cover: motion "cover the Pit again". Entity motion_descend: motion "a sanctioned descent for Ithmar".
  Entity motion_bargain: motion "bargain with the Interlocutor".
  Relation favours(group, motion). Relation seat(group). Relation convened(place). Relation redLine(group, motion).
  Measure tally_of(motion). Relation counted(group, motion). Relation passed(motion). Relation voting(place).
  Rule concord_called when not convened(chapter) and ((knows(party, corbel_seen) and knows(party, sinking)) or day(clock) >= 720)
    says "Riders go out from Sorne along every road on the plateau: the Crown calls a Concord at Stairhead House, of every power that will come." {
    Assert convened(chapter). Assert at(aske, chapter). Assert at(ayzhe, chapter). Assert at(bren, chapter).
    Assert at(dagny, chapter). Assert at(mance, chapter). Assert at(ruan, chapter). }
  Initially Assert seat(aske). Initially Assert seat(ayzhe). Initially Assert seat(bren). Initially Assert seat(dagny).
  Initially Assert seat(mance). Initially Assert seat(ruan).
  Initially Assert favours(aske, motion_cover). Initially Assert favours(aske, motion_descend).
  Initially Assert favours(mance, motion_descend).
  Initially Assert redLine(bren, motion_cover). Initially Assert redLine(aske, motion_bargain).
  Observe concord_scene at chapter when convened(chapter) "The chapter house is full: the Warden in his sash for the Crown; Ayzhe of the Split Ear; Bren of Ennick with his hood in his hands; Dagny Ferrow for the Mutual; the prior at the head of the table; Ruan Haldane for the Waiting. Nobody sits next to anybody they can help it.".
  // Evidence, shown with its proof, moves every seat that cares about it.
  Action show_feeding(actor: group, site: place) "Show the Concord what the held feed" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, chapter) and convened(chapter)
      and knows(actor, held_feed) and not shownTo(chapter, held_feed).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert shownTo(chapter, held_feed). Retract redLine(bren, motion_cover). }
    Result "Bren asks for a recess, and is gone an hour. When he comes back he says that Ennick will stop holding, and that it will not have the Pit covered while one of its held is still in the glass.".
  }
  Action show_procession(actor: group, site: place) "Show the Concord the procession's warning: the Masonry takes from the newest backward" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, chapter) and convened(chapter)
      and knows(actor, newest_backward) and not shownTo(chapter, newest_backward).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert shownTo(chapter, newest_backward). Assert redLine(ruan, motion_bargain). Assert favours(ruan, motion_descend). }
    Result "The Waiting's elder goes white. Nobody at the table will speak for bargaining after that.".
  }
  Action show_way(actor: group, site: place) "Show the Concord that the Way to the jewel is under this house" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, chapter) and convened(chapter)
      and knows(actor, way_found) and not shownTo(chapter, way_found).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert shownTo(chapter, way_found). Assert favours(dagny, motion_descend). Assert favours(ruan, motion_descend). }
    Result "The prior's seat is suddenly worth a great deal, and he knows it. The Mutual and the Waiting come round to a sanctioned descent.".
  }
  Action show_breach(actor: group, site: place) "Name to the Concord who cut the Breach" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, chapter) and convened(chapter)
      and knows(actor, breach_cut) and not shownTo(chapter, breach_cut).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert shownTo(chapter, breach_cut). Retract at(ayzhe, chapter). Assert at(ayzhe, split_ear_camp). }
    Result "Ayzhe stands up before you have finished, and does not look at Bren, who has not moved. The Split Ear ride south that afternoon. The Tovash seat is empty.".
  }
  Relation shownTo(place, fact).
  Discovery newest_backward "The Masonry quarries a world's past from the newest moment backward: when it reached the beginning of the procession's world, that world was not.".
  Action call_vote(actor: group, site: place) "Ask the Concord to vote" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, chapter) and convened(chapter) and not voting(chapter).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert voting(chapter). }
    Result "The prior calls the seats, one by one.".
  }
  // A motion passes when four seats there favour it and no seat there holds a red line against it.
  Rule vote_counts when voting(chapter) and seat(?s) and at(?s, chapter) and favours(?s, ?m) and not counted(?s, ?m) {
    Increase tally_of(?m) by 1. Assert counted(?s, ?m). }
  Query blocked(m: motion) means redLine(?s, m) and at(?s, chapter).
  Relation onTable(motion).
  Initially Assert onTable(motion_cover). Initially Assert onTable(motion_descend). Initially Assert onTable(motion_bargain).
  Rule motion_passes when voting(chapter) and onTable(?m) and tally_of(?m) >= 4 and not blocked(?m) and not passed(?m)
    says "The Concord resolves: {?m}." { Assert passed(?m). }
  Observe concord_descend at chapter when passed(motion_descend) and not knows(party, way_found) "The Concord has sanctioned a descent. The prior, very stiffly, tells the seats what the mother-church has always suspected and he has lately confirmed: there is a stair under his platform." teaches way_found.
  Rule descent_sanctioned when passed(motion_descend) and not admits(aske, party) { Assert admits(aske, party). }
}

data/adventures/patient-star/stilling.ky:
Module stilling "The stilling: what the Late Sun's direct light does to whatever drinks it" {
  // The four laws (The Land and Its Laws): the stilling travels only in direct light, silica passes it and stops,
  // water and flesh drink it and slow, iron sheds it as heat. This module is the third law, as it bears on people:
  // where the light falls, who is in it, what they wear, how slow it leaves them, and how they come back.

  // Ground the light falls on: lit glass, a lamp-chamber, a vault with its shutter open, a leak in the plaster. A
  // place is lit by a fact (litGround) or by a rule (lit), so that a shutter or a mirror can light and darken it.
  Relation litGround(place). Relation shadeOf(place).
  Query lit(p: place) means litGround(p) and not shadeOf(p).

  // Dose, in twenty-fourths of a point: an hour bare in direct light is a point (24); an hour in full felt a
  // quarter of one (6). Recovery is two points an hour out of the light, faster while someone is deeply slowed.
  Measure dose(entity).
  // Full umber felt: the cloak, the hood and the mitts. Counterfeit felt looks the same and is no felt at all.
  // What sheds the stilling when worn: umber felt, Selane's Veil.
  Relation shields(itemkind).
  Query felted(m: member) means wearing(?f, m) and itemKind(?f, ?k) and shields(?k).
  // Someone the light does not slow (Saro, whose bones are stillglass).
  Relation unslowed(entity).
  // Someone who is not of the company and wears felt, by what is said of them.
  Relation feltClad(group).

  Rule soaks when memberOf(?m, ?c) and company(?c) and at(?c, ?p) and lit(?p) and not felted(?m) and not unslowed(?m)
    and not heldDeep(?m) { Increase dose(?m) by 4. }
  Rule soaks_felted when memberOf(?m, ?c) and company(?c) and at(?c, ?p) and lit(?p) and felted(?m)
    and not unslowed(?m) and not heldDeep(?m) { Increase dose(?m) by 1. }
  Rule others_soak when at(?g, ?p) and lit(?p) and slowable(?g) and not feltClad(?g) and not heldDeep(?g) {
    Increase dose(?g) by 4. }
  Rule others_soak_felted when at(?g, ?p) and lit(?p) and slowable(?g) and feltClad(?g) and not heldDeep(?g) {
    Increase dose(?g) by 1. }
  // Out of the light: two points an hour, and twelve an hour while someone is held deeper than a tenth.
  Query unlitFor(x: entity) means (memberOf(x, ?c) and at(?c, ?p) and not lit(?p)) or (at(x, ?q) and not lit(?q)).
  // A decrease that would go below nothing stops play, and there is no min(), so the last of it is set to nothing.
  Rule recovers when unlitFor(?x) and dose(?x) >= 8 and dose(?x) <= 288 { Decrease dose(?x) by 8. }
  Rule recovers_last when unlitFor(?x) and dose(?x) > 0 and dose(?x) < 8 { Set dose(?x) to 0. }
  Rule recovers_deep when unlitFor(?x) and dose(?x) > 288 { Decrease dose(?x) by 48. }
  // A way across lit ground (the Collar Road, the filament, a leak across a doorway) doses whoever crosses it, once
  // per crossing: so much bare, so much in felt. There is no division, so both are said.
  Measure wayDose(passage). Measure wayDoseFelted(passage).
  Relation dosedOn(member, passage).
  Rule way_doses when tookWay(?c, ?w) and company(?c) and wayDose(?w) > 0 and memberOf(?m, ?c) and not dosedOn(?m, ?w)
    and not felted(?m) and not unslowed(?m) { Increase dose(?m) by wayDose(?w). Assert dosedOn(?m, ?w). }
  Rule way_doses_felted when tookWay(?c, ?w) and company(?c) and wayDoseFelted(?w) > 0 and memberOf(?m, ?c)
    and not dosedOn(?m, ?w) and felted(?m) and not unslowed(?m) { Increase dose(?m) by wayDoseFelted(?w). Assert dosedOn(?m, ?w). }
  Rule way_passed when dosedOn(?m, ?w) and memberOf(?m, ?c) and not tookWay(?c, ?w) { Retract dosedOn(?m, ?w). }
  // Who the light can slow besides the company: the people of a module that says so.
  Relation slowable(group).

  // At a point, half speed: everything takes twice as long and companions seem to hurry. A slowed member goes at half
  // their speed (the shared rules' speed, in hundredths), and the company at its slowest member's; when the dose is
  // gone, their own. (Written at first as no capacity to carry, the only pace a module could then change: ledger, 1.)
  Query slowedMember(m: member) means dose(m) >= 24.
  Query slowedCompany(c: group) means memberOf(?m, c) and slowedMember(?m).
  Rule slowing when memberOf(?m, ?c) and company(?c) and slowedMember(?m) and speed(?m) != 50 { Set speed(?m) to 50. }
  Rule quickening when memberOf(?m, ?c) and company(?c) and not slowedMember(?m) and speed(?m) == 50 { Set speed(?m) to 0. }
  // In a fight, slowed is Orsino's slow: a blow fewer, late to move. Laid on whoever is slowed, an hour at a time.
  Hazard stilled "the stilling" means "Apply slow to ally for 1 hour.".
  Relation slowLaid(group). Measure slowSince(group).
  Rule slow_laid when company(?c) and slowedCompany(?c) and not slowLaid(?c) {
    Assert strikes(stilled, ?c). Assert slowLaid(?c). Set slowSince(?c) to watch(clock). }
  Rule slow_renewed when company(?c) and slowLaid(?c) and watch(clock) >= slowSince(?c) + 6 { Retract slowLaid(?c). }
  // At twelve points, a tenth: they cannot leave without being led.
  Query stoppedMember(m: member) means dose(m) >= 288.
  Rule stopping when memberOf(?m, ?c) and company(?c) and stoppedMember(?m) and not hobbled(?c) { Assert hobbled(?c). }
  Rule starting when hobbled(?c) and company(?c) and not stoppedCompany(?c) and stilled(?c) {
    Retract hobbled(?c). Retract stilled(?c). }
  Query stoppedCompany(c: group) means memberOf(?m, c) and stoppedMember(?m).
  Relation stilled(group).
  Rule stilled_mark when hobbled(?c) and company(?c) and stoppedCompany(?c) and not stilled(?c) { Assert stilled(?c). }
  // Held: past a hundred points, one breath every few minutes.
  Query heldDeep(x: entity) means dose(x) >= 2400.

  Observe slow_feel near ?c when company(?c) and slowedCompany(?c) and not stoppedCompany(?c) "Your own footsteps sound late on the stone, your limbs are heavy, and the world has begun to hurry around you.".
  Observe stopped_feel near ?c when company(?c) and stoppedCompany(?c) "Every thought takes an hour to finish. You could not walk out of here alone if your life hung on it.".
}

data/adventures/patient-star/tamaun.kyr:
Module season "Hold One Season" {
  // Tamaun's upper city: the West Gallery from Quell and the Neck, the Shallows lit by mirrors, and the Granaries
  // lit by direct light through channels. Everything here is underground and dark unless a mirror throws light on it.
  Place gallery "the West Gallery" is level within tamaun.
  Place shallows "the Shallows" is level within tamaun.
  Place granaries "the Granaries" is level within tamaun.

  Place well_foot "the foot of the North Well" is room within gallery at 0, 0 underground.
  Place before_neck "the West Gallery, at the Neck" is room within gallery at 1, 0 underground.
  Place west_gate "the West Gate" is room within shallows at 0, 1 underground.
  Place road_north "the Mirror Road, north stretch" is room within shallows at 1, 0 underground.
  Place lamp_chamber "the third lamp-chamber" is room within shallows at 2, 0 underground.
  Place road_south "the Mirror Road, south stretch" is room within shallows at 1, 2 underground.
  Place bunks "the Bunks" is room within shallows at 0, 2 underground.
  Place plate_hall "the Plate Hall" is room within shallows at 2, 2 underground.
  Place ring "the Granary Ring" is room within granaries at 1, 1 underground.
  Place vault "the ninth vault" is room within granaries at 1, 0 underground.
  Place fox_vault "the fourth vault" is room within granaries at 2, 1 underground.
  Place waking_ward "the Waking Ward" is room within granaries at 0, 1 underground.
  Place flood_line "the Flood Line" is room within granaries at 1, 2 underground.
  Place sluice_head "the Sluice" is room within granaries at 2, 2 underground.

  Passage well_stair "the North Well stair" is stair between well_head and well_foot.
  Passage west_gallery "the West Gallery" is tunnel between well_foot and before_neck taking 3 hours.
  Passage neck "the Neck" is crawl between before_neck and west_gate taking 20 minutes.
  Passage gate_arch "the West Gate arch" is arch between west_gate and road_north.
  Passage slot_north "the north light-slot gallery" is passage between road_north and lamp_chamber taking 3 minutes.
  Passage mirror_road "the Mirror Road" is passage between road_north and road_south taking 5 minutes.
  Passage bunks_way "the passage to the Bunks" is passage between road_south and bunks taking 3 minutes.
  Passage hall_way "the Plate Hall doorway" is doorway between road_south and plate_hall.
  // My addition: a Seridane service stair from the Plate Hall down to the Granaries.
  Passage granary_stair "the service stair" is stair between plate_hall and ring.
  Passage vault_door "the ninth vault's doorway" is doorway between ring and vault.
  Passage fox_door "the fourth vault's doorway" is doorway between ring and fox_vault.
  Passage ward_door "the Waking Ward door" is doorway between ring and waking_ward.
  Passage flood_slope "the slope to the flood" is passage between ring and flood_line taking 3 minutes.
  Passage sluice_tunnel "the sluice tunnel" is passage between flood_line and sluice_head taking 5 minutes.

  // Dark, unless a mirror throws light here. The galleries a mirror serves are lit while it is aimed at them.
  Relation darkRoom(place).
  Initially Assert darkRoom(well_foot). Initially Assert darkRoom(before_neck). Initially Assert darkRoom(west_gate).
  Initially Assert darkRoom(road_north). Initially Assert darkRoom(road_south). Initially Assert darkRoom(bunks).
  Initially Assert darkRoom(plate_hall). Initially Assert darkRoom(ring). Initially Assert darkRoom(waking_ward).
  Initially Assert darkRoom(flood_line). Initially Assert darkRoom(sluice_head).
  Rule unlit_here when darkRoom(?p) and not bright(?p) and not unlit(?p) { Assert unlit(?p). }
  Rule lit_here when darkRoom(?p) and bright(?p) and unlit(?p) { Retract unlit(?p). }

  Observe well_foot_scene at well_foot when true "The stair comes down into a round chamber at the water's edge. The well water is warm as a bath. A tunnel two metres wide runs off east beside it, with a channel along one side.".
  Observe gallery_scene at before_neck when true "The West Gallery runs on east, wet underfoot, the water in its channel very still. Ahead, the roof comes down to meet the water.".

  // The Neck: the roof drops until there is a metre of air under it in late summer. The water in the West Gallery is
  // falling a hand a month, because the growth under the Late Sun is opening a channel that drains it (S1).
  Entity neck_water: scenery "the water at the Neck".
  Measure airGap(entity).
  Initially Set airGap(neck_water) to 100.
  Rule neck_falls when hour(clock) == 4 and dice(neck_water) <= 13 { Increase airGap(neck_water) by 1. }
  Observe neck_scene at before_neck when airGap(neck_water) < 110 "The ceiling drops until you wade with your face near the stone; under the Neck there is about a metre of air. On the wall a line of white crust shows where the water stood a season ago, a hand above where it stands now.".
  Observe neck_scene_low at before_neck when airGap(neck_water) >= 110 "Under the Neck there is more than a metre of air now. The white crust of the old waterline stands well above the water.".
  // Whoever marks the water and comes back to it learns it is falling.
  Measure markedAt(group).
  Relation marked(group).
  Action mark_water(actor: group, site: place) "Scratch a mark at the waterline under the Neck" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, before_neck) and not marked(actor) and not benighted(actor).
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Assert marked(actor). Set markedAt(actor) to airGap(neck_water). }
    Result "You scratch a line in the crust at the very edge of the water with the point of your knife.".
  }
  Discovery water_falling "The water in the West Gallery is falling, faster than any season accounts for: the mark at the Neck is dry above it within days. Something below is drawing it off." .
  Observe mark_dry at before_neck when marked(party) and airGap(neck_water) >= markedAt(party) + 2 "The line you scratched at the waterline is dry now, two fingers above the water." teaches water_falling.

  Observe gate_scene at west_gate when true "Beyond the Neck a cut-stone arch opens on a gallery. Chalk on the arch reads J.H. 341.".

  // The Mirror Road and the third lamp-chamber. The chamber's mirror throws safe, bounced light down one of three
  // galleries: the north stretch, the south stretch, or the Bunks. The chamber itself is a straight room: the Late Sun
  // is behind its window, and every minute there is dose (S4).
  Initially Assert litGround(lamp_chamber).
  Thing mirror "the great mirror" at lamp_chamber {
    State to_north "A bronze mirror two metres across stands on a cradle with a crank and worm-gear, throwing a beam out through the north slot. Brass scales are scratched on the cradle, and its pointer stands near the end of them.".
    State to_south "The great mirror is cranked round to the south slot, and its beam goes out that way.".
    State to_bunks "The great mirror is cranked round to the low slot that serves the Bunks.".
    Change north_south "Crank the mirror round to the south slot" from to_north to to_south.
    Change north_bunks "Crank the mirror round to the Bunks slot" from to_north to to_bunks.
    Change south_north "Crank the mirror round to the north slot" from to_south to to_north.
    Change south_bunks "Crank the mirror round to the Bunks slot" from to_south to to_bunks.
    Change bunks_north "Crank the mirror round to the north slot" from to_bunks to to_north.
    Change bunks_south "Crank the mirror round to the south slot" from to_bunks to to_south.
  }
  Relation aims(condition, place).
  Initially Assert aims(to_north, road_north). Initially Assert aims(to_south, road_south). Initially Assert aims(to_bunks, bunks).
  Query bright(p: place) means state(mirror, ?s) and aims(?s, p).
  Observe chamber_scene at lamp_chamber when true "A round chamber at the inner end of the gallery. One wall is a single sheet of stillglass three metres across, with blinding light behind it. Your shadow lies flat behind you on the floor.".
  Discovery mirrors_ending "The lamp-chamber mirrors are at the end of their travel. Their scales were set for a Late Sun that sank four centimetres a year; whatever they are aimed at now, they will not reach for long." {
    Found by searching lamp_chamber "The pointer on the cradle's brass scale stands two finger-widths from its stop. Below the last scratched mark, someone recently has scratched another, and another below that.".
  }

  // The gardens walk with the light: where bounced light has lain a long while, moss and fern and grass; where it has
  // left, they brown and die (S2). Greenness is reckoned by the watch, from none to a thousand.
  Measure green(place).
  Initially Set green(road_north) to 1000. Initially Set green(road_south) to 300. Initially Set green(bunks) to 0.
  Rule greening when darkRoom(?p) and bright(?p) and green(?p) < 1000 and dice(?p) <= 50 { Increase green(?p) by 1. }
  Rule browning when darkRoom(?p) and not bright(?p) and green(?p) > 0 { Decrease green(?p) by 1. }
  Observe north_lit at road_north when bright(road_north) "A ring gallery four metres wide. A bronze disc as big as a cartwheel is set in a ceiling niche, throwing grey-gold light along the passage. Swallows nest on its rim.".
  Observe north_dark at road_north when not bright(road_north) "A ring gallery four metres wide. A bronze disc as big as a cartwheel sits dull in its ceiling niche, and the swallows on its rim are quiet.".
  Observe north_garden at road_north when green(road_north) >= 600 "Moss covers the floor, ferns grow out of the cracks in the left-hand wall, and pale grass stands up to your knees.".
  Observe north_fading at road_north when green(road_north) < 600 and green(road_north) >= 200 "The grass lies over and is turning yellow. The ferns have begun to brown at the tips.".
  Observe north_dead at road_north when green(road_north) < 200 "Dead ferns, brown and dry, break when you brush them. The grass lies flat.".
  Observe south_lit at road_south when bright(road_south) "Light comes down the south stretch from a ceiling disc, onto stone that was bare not long ago.".
  Observe south_dark at road_south when not bright(road_south) "The south stretch of the Mirror Road is dark. A disc hangs dull in the ceiling niche.".
  Observe south_garden at road_south when green(road_south) >= 600 "A garden has come up here: moss, fern, and pale grass to the knee.".
  Observe south_shoots at road_south when green(road_south) < 600 and green(road_south) >= 100 "New green shoots, very small, come up between the stones in a band as straight as the edge of a shadow.".

  // A leak: a crack in the plaster where the Mirror Road meets the Plate Hall throws a blade of direct light across
  // the doorway. It is the commonest hazard in the city; it moves only when the plaster falls.
  Thing leak "a blade of white light" on hall_way {
    State shining "Where the plaster has cracked over the Plate Hall doorway, a blade of hard white light comes through and lies across the threshold.".
    State shaded "A hood of umber felt has been hung over the crack above the Plate Hall doorway.".
    Change shade "Hang felt over the crack" from shining to shaded consuming felt_scrap.
  }
  Initially Set wayDose(hall_way) to 2.
  Rule leak_shaded when state(leak, shaded) and wayDose(hall_way) > 0 { Set wayDose(hall_way) to 0. }

  // The Bunks: the Mutual's unlicensed crews, and their cold hearth.
  Observe bunks_scene at bunks when true "Rooms off the ring: bed niches cut in the rock, reading mirrors on pegs, tally marks by the doors. In one block, bedrolls, a cold hearth, Mutual tallies and a wine jar. One of the bed niches is yours.".
  Observe bunks_lit at bunks when bright(bunks) "Grey-gold light falls into the Bunks from the low slot in the ceiling. Someone has hung a shirt up to dry in it.".
  Person bunks_crew "the Bunks crew" at bunks {
    Role "four of the Mutual's unlicensed cutters, between shifts". Ancestry human. Numbers 4. Peaceable.
  }
  Relation grumbled(group).
  // An event happens once, seen or not; the crew grumble whenever someone comes in on them in the dark, so it is said
  // each time it is so.
  Observe bunks_darkened at bunks as event when not bright(bunks) and at(bunks_crew, bunks) and green(bunks) > 0 "One of the cutters in the Bunks looks up at the dead slot in the ceiling. 'Somebody's been at the third mirror again,' she says. 'Swing it back before the ferns go, or we'll be sleeping in the dark.'".
  Topic bunks_neck with bunks_crew "Ask the Bunks crew about the way down to the Granaries" when true once {
    Says "'Service stair, out of the back of the Plate Hall,' says a woman with her boots off. 'Mind the doorway. There's a crack in the plaster over it, and a blade of the straight light comes through. Run it, or hang a bit of felt over the crack.' She throws you a scrap of old felt. 'Keep that.'".
    On discuss { Increase quantity(actor, felt_scrap) by 1. }
  }
  Topic bunks_outfall with bunks_crew "Ask the Bunks crew about other ways out" when true once {
    Says "'The Holdfolk say the old drain comes out above Ennick,' says the woman. 'The Outfall. Nine kilometres on your belly, and shut by the flood from Sowing to the end of summer. It should open any day now.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, outfall_known). }
  }
  Entity felt_scrap: good "scrap of felt".
  Discovery outfall_known "The Outfall, the Seridane's drain, runs nine kilometres from the Granaries' flood line to a spring cave in the cliff above Ennick; it is shut by the flood from Sowing to the end of summer.".

  // The Plate Hall: voice-plates in racks, a stylus on a cord, and Halu's stack by the door (S5).
  Observe plate_hall_scene at plate_hall when true "A long hall of racks for thin stillglass plates, most of the slots empty. By the door, twelve plates are stacked neatly, edges squared, as if someone meant to carry them away and will be back for them.".
  Thing tally_plate "a plate from the granary racks" at plate_hall {
    State silent "One rack is labelled with the sign the Seridane painted on their grain jars. A plate stands in it.".
    State playing "A clerk's voice, faint as wind, counts jars into a vault: a number, a breath, and then a line said quickly the same way each time, the way you would say a thing a thousand times a day. 'Seri amar ka, dane tamaun eth. Seri amar ka, ithel sonne.'".
    Change play_tally "Draw a stylus along the granary plate" from silent to playing needing stylus.
  }
  Thing song_plate "a plate on its own on a shelf" at plate_hall {
    State silent "On a shelf by itself, a plate scratched along one edge with children's tally marks.".
    State playing "Children's voices, very small and far away, count in a ring: twelve words, round and round, and on the twelfth they all shout.".
    Change play_song "Draw a stylus along the children's plate" from silent to playing needing stylus.
  }
  Thing debate_plate "a plate from the debate" at plate_hall {
    State silent "In the end rack, two plates are cut with the Answerer and Coverer signs.".
    State playing "A woman's voice, a Coverer's: 'It was not given. Nothing gives a thing it cannot see. It fell, as a stone falls from a sling, and the lake wrote it down.' And a man, an Answerer, louder, threatening her by name.".
    Change play_debate "Draw a stylus along the debate plate" from silent to playing needing stylus.
  }
  Rule debate_ends when state(debate_plate, playing) and not at(party, plate_hall) { Assert state(debate_plate, silent). }
  Discovery coverer_case "The Coverers argued, on the debate plates, that the hour was not given but fell, and that the lake's own records said so.".
  Observe debate_heard at plate_hall when state(debate_plate, playing) "The Coverers said it fell." teaches coverer_case.
  Rule tally_ends when state(tally_plate, playing) and not at(party, plate_hall) { Assert state(tally_plate, silent). }
  Rule song_ends when state(song_plate, playing) and not at(party, plate_hall) { Assert state(song_plate, silent). }
  Discovery song_heard "The Plate Hall's counting song: children count twelve words in a ring, each on its own note.".
  Observe song_learned at plate_hall when state(song_plate, playing) "Each of the twelve words has its own note." teaches song_heard.
  Discovery tally_words "A Seridane granary clerk, counting jars into a vault, said the same line over each: 'Seri amar ka, dane tamaun eth. Seri amar ka, ithel sonne.'".
  Observe tally_heard at plate_hall when state(tally_plate, playing) "The same line, over each jar." teaches tally_words.

  // The Granary Ring and its vaults. Each vault has an umber shutter on a pulley; open, a bar of direct light comes
  // down its channel from the Pit wall and holds whatever is under it; shut, it lets whatever it held go (G2). The
  // pulley's cord is made off on a cleat by the doorway, so that the shutter is worked from outside the beam.
  Observe ring_scene at ring when true "A curving passage with forty vaults off it, numbered in Seridane signs over their doorways. In some, a bar of hard white light comes straight down from the ceiling onto the floor.".
  Discovery jars_painted "Every jar in the Granary Ring is painted with the same line of Seridane writing, and holds black dust.".
  Observe jars_seen at ring when not benighted(party) "Every jar in every vault is red-glazed and painted with the same line of words, and every jar you can see into holds black dust." teaches jars_painted.

  Thing shutter "the ninth vault's shutter" on vault_door {
    State open "In the ceiling of the ninth vault an umber shutter hangs open on its pulley, and a bar of white light comes down through the channel above it onto the floor.".
    State shut "The ninth vault's shutter is down. The vault is dark.".
    Change close_nine "Pull the shutter cord at the doorway" from open to shut at ring.
    Change open_nine "Let the shutter cord run" from shut to open at ring.
  }
  Initially Assert litGround(vault).
  Rule vault_lit when state(shutter, open) and not litGround(vault) { Assert litGround(vault). }
  Rule vault_unlit when state(shutter, shut) and litGround(vault) { Retract litGround(vault). Assert unlit(vault). }
  Rule vault_bright when state(shutter, open) and unlit(vault) { Retract unlit(vault). }
  Observe cleat_seen at ring when state(shutter, open) "Beside the ninth vault's doorway, a cord comes down out of the ceiling and is made off on a bronze cleat.".
  Observe vault_scene at vault when state(shutter, open) "Rows of red-glazed jars stand under the beam, each painted with the same line of words. In the middle of them a man in a cutter's felt hood stands with one hand out toward a jar, his eyes open.".
  Observe vault_dark_scene at vault when state(shutter, shut) "Rows of red-glazed jars, and the smell of old dust.".
  Kind granary_jars "a sack's worth of umber-glazed jars" is treasure worth 12 weighing 8
    described "Red-glazed Seridane grain jars, not a crack in one, each painted with the same line of writing and holding black dust. A collector in Sorne pays three crowns a jar.".
  Item jars "the ninth vault's jars" is granary_jars at vault.

  // The fourth vault holds a fox.
  Thing fox_shutter "the fourth vault's shutter" on fox_door {
    State open "An umber shutter hangs open in the ceiling, and the light comes down onto a fox that stands in it with its tail half lifted.".
    State shut "The fourth vault's shutter is down.".
    Change close_fourth "Pull the fourth vault's shutter cord" from open to shut at ring.
  }
  Initially Assert litGround(fox_vault).
  Person fox "a fox" at fox_vault { Role "a dog fox, held in the light mid-step". Species fox. Pronouns he. }
  Initially Assert asleep(fox). Initially Assert slowable(fox). Initially Set dose(fox) to 2400.
  Rule fox_unlit when state(fox_shutter, shut) and litGround(fox_vault) { Retract litGround(fox_vault). }
  Rule fox_wakes when asleep(fox) and dose(fox) < 288 { Retract asleep(fox). }
  Event fox_runs near fox when not asleep(fox) and at(fox, fox_vault) "The fox finishes its step, and the next. It looks round at the dark with its ears flat, and is gone down the ring like smoke." then {
    Retract at(fox, fox_vault). Assert at(fox, flood_line). }

  // The Waking Ward: where the Seridane held their sick, and where they woke in the dark when the light was cut (G3).
  Observe ward_scene_t at waking_ward when true "Long rooms of stone beds with leather straps rotted to threads. The ceiling channels are shuttered and dark.".
  Observe ward_walls at waking_ward when not benighted(party) "The writing starts at the door, scratched into the stone at the height of someone sitting up. Further in it is everywhere: walls, bed-edges, floor. Some is neat; some runs downhill. Near the far end it is low, at the height of someone lying down, and the scratches are shallow. You cannot read it, but you can tell that it was written in the dark. One word near the door has the same shape as the line on the granary jars.".
  Discovery ward_written "The Seridane held their sick in the Waking Ward. When the light was cut, the held woke in the dark and wrote on the walls until they died: names, and words over and over." {
    Found by searching waking_ward "Among the scratches, the same few words come again and again, low down and shallow at the end. One of them has been written so many times that the stone is worn smooth around it.".
  }

  // The Flood Line and the Sluice: the outer passages slope into warm clear water. In autumn the flood falls; from
  // Sowing to Haying it closes the Outfall's last stretch (G4). The Sluice lowers it, and sends it all down to Ennick.
  Measure flood(entity).
  Entity flood_water: scenery "the flood in the Granaries".
  Initially Set flood(flood_water) to 100.
  Relation sluiced(entity).
  Rule flood_falls when season(clock) == 3 and hour(clock) == 3 and flood(flood_water) > 40 { Decrease flood(flood_water) by 15. }
  Rule flood_sluiced when sluiced(flood_water) and hour(clock) == 3 and flood(flood_water) > 0 { Decrease flood(flood_water) by 20. }
  Observe flood_scene at flood_line when flood(flood_water) >= 60 "The passages slope down into still, warm, clear water. White shrimp scatter from your light. Where the Outfall goes on west, the water stands to the roof.".
  Observe flood_scene_low at flood_line when flood(flood_water) < 60 "The water has drawn back down the slope. Where the Outfall goes on west, there is air above the water now, a hand of it, then more.".
  Species outfall_eel "an Outfall eel" like great_pike temperament ambush
    described "An eel of the Ammer that swam up the warm Outfall as an elver two hundred years ago and never left: three metres of it, white about the jaw.".
  Person eels "Outfall eels" at flood_line {
    Role "two old eels lying in the flooded doorway". Species outfall_eel. Numbers 2.
  }
  Thing sluice "the Sluice" at sluice_head {
    State closed "A bronze gate stands in a stone frame at the head of a broad tunnel, with a geared wheel the size of a man. A trickle comes through it.".
    State opened "The Sluice stands open. The water goes through it with a sound like wind.".
    Change open_sluice "Wind the Sluice open" from closed to opened.
    Change close_sluice "Wind the Sluice shut" from opened to closed.
  }
  Rule sluice_runs when state(sluice, opened) and not sluiced(flood_water) { Assert sluiced(flood_water). }
  Rule sluice_stops when state(sluice, closed) and sluiced(flood_water) { Retract sluiced(flood_water). }
  Entity quell_wells: scenery "Quell's wells".
  Relation drained(entity). Relation washedOut(entity).
  Rule wells_drop when sluiced(flood_water) and flood(flood_water) < 40 and not drained(quell_wells) { Assert drained(quell_wells). }

  // Garret, held eleven months at about a hundredth, in the beam among the jars.
  Person garret "Garret" at vault {
    Role "a cutter of the Mutual, held in the light". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Plans 14 steps. Uses go, change_thing. Pronouns he. Manner cheerful.
    Joins "Garret puts a hand on your shoulder, to steady himself as much as anything. 'Up, then,' he says. 'Slowly.'".
  }
  Initially Assert kin(party, garret). Initially Assert kinship(garret, uncle).
  Entity uncle: fact "your uncle".
  Initially Assert asleep(garret). Initially Assert slowable(garret). Initially Assert feltClad(garret).
  Initially Set dose(garret) to 2400.
  Measure watchedFor(entity).
  Rule watching_garret when at(party, vault) and heldDeep(garret) and at(garret, vault) and not benighted(party) { Increase watchedFor(garret) by 1. }
  Observe garret_moved at vault when heldDeep(garret) and at(garret, vault) and watchedFor(garret) >= 6 "You have watched him for an hour. His hand is a finger's width nearer the jar than it was, and his chest is higher.".
  Observe garret_slowing at vault when not heldDeep(garret) and asleep(garret) and at(garret, vault) "Garret's eyes are moving. They come round to you over a long time, and his lips part.".
  Observe garret_ring at ring when asleep(garret) and at(garret, ring) and not heldDeep(garret) "Garret lies on the floor of the Ring where he was dragged, his eyes moving very slowly from one thing to the next.".
  Rule garret_wakes when asleep(garret) and dose(garret) < 288 { Retract asleep(garret). Assert acceptsEscort(garret, party). }
  // He comes round whether or not anyone is there to see. What it was like is told to whoever first sees him awake:
  // an event would be spent unseen, so it is an observation that teaches its own having been seen (ledger, 4).
  Rule garret_willing when not asleep(garret) and not willing(garret, party) and not travelsWith(garret, party) and not cameUp(garret) { Assert willing(garret, party). }
  Entity garret_woke: fact "Garret has come round from eleven months in the light.".
  Observe garret_comes_round near garret as event when not asleep(garret) and not cameUp(garret) and not knows(party, garret_woke) "Garret finishes the reach he began eleven months ago, closes his hand on nothing, and sits down hard. 'Where's the light gone?' he says. 'Ness was just there.' He looks at you a long time. 'You were never this tall. What month is it?' Told, he says nothing for a while. 'I'm hungry,' he says at last, as if that settled it." teaches garret_woke.
  Topic garret_month with garret "Tell Garret how long he stood there" when not asleep(garret) once {
    Says "'Eleven months,' Garret says after you, as if trying the words for size. 'It was Harvest. I had my hand out.' He looks at his hand. 'Ness said the light would not reach past the door. Ness said a lot of things.'".
  }
  Topic garret_ness with garret travelling "Ask Garret about Ness" when not asleep(garret) once {
    Says "'She wanted the jars,' says Garret. 'Three crowns a jar in Sorne, and there's forty in that vault. I said the light was moving, I'd seen it on the floor. She said go on then, if you're frightened.' He laughs, not much. 'So I went on.'".
  }
  // Pulled out by hand: whoever does it stands in the beam to do it.
  Action drag_out(actor: group, site: place) "Go into the beam and drag Garret out of it" {
    Description "Into the light, an arm round him, and back out to the Ring. It takes a few minutes in the beam.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, vault) and at(garret, vault)
      and state(shutter, open) and asleep(garret) and not hobbled(actor).
    Time 5 minutes.
    On success { Retract at(garret, vault). Assert at(garret, ring). Retract at(actor, vault). Assert at(actor, ring).
      Assert dragged(garret). }
    Result "You go in among the jars, get an arm round Garret, and haul. He comes like a felled tree, stiff and very slow, and you get him out over the threshold onto the Ring.".
  }
  Relation dragged(group).
  Relation cameUp(group).
  // Joined, he is a member of the company with a body of his own, and the dose was on the person he was: it is
  // carried over by hand (ledger, 6).
  Rule garret_dose_joins when travelsWith(garret, party) and dose(garret) > 0 {
    Set dose(member_garret_person) to dose(garret). Set dose(garret) to 0. }
  // Once he can walk, and nobody leads him, he makes his own slow way home to the Mutual's hall.
  Pursuit go_home for garret "making his slow way up to Quell" priority 20 when not asleep(garret) and not following(garret, party) and not travelsWith(garret, party) and not cameUp(garret) seeks at(garret, mutual_hall).
  Pursuit stay_close for garret "keeping close to you" priority 30 when following(garret, party) seeks together(garret, party).
  Rule garret_home when at(garret, mutual_hall) and not cameUp(garret) { Assert cameUp(garret). }
  Rule garret_brought when travelsWith(garret, party) and at(party, mutual_hall) and not cameUp(garret) { Assert cameUp(garret). }
  Initially Assert keyholder(garret, chain_gate).

  // Dagny's crew goes down on the fourth morning, when it has the felt, and Ness with them. At the Ring they argue; the crew pull the cord,
  // and Ness takes the jars.
  Rule crew_sets_out when day(clock) >= 4 and hour(clock) == 6 and not descended(crew) { Assert descended(crew). }
  Initially Assert keyholder(crew, chain_gate). Initially Assert keyholder(ness, chain_gate).
  Pursuit go_down for crew "going down after Garret" priority 20 when descended(crew) and asleep(garret) seeks at(crew, ring).
  Pursuit go_down for ness "going down with the crew" priority 20 when descended(crew) and not keeps(ness, jars) seeks at(ness, ring).
  Relation argued(group).
  Event crew_argue near crew when at(crew, ring) and at(ness, ring) and asleep(garret) and not argued(crew) "At the ninth vault's doorway Dagny's crew stand arguing in low voices. 'He'll keep,' Ness is saying. 'He's kept a year. Take the jars and come back for him with the sledge.' 'We came for him,' says the elder. 'And we go in for him when Dagny sends the long poles down, not before. I'll not have two of us stood in there.'" then { Assert argued(crew). Set arguedOn(crew) to day(clock). }
  Measure arguedOn(group).
  Pursuit free_him for crew "pulling the shutter cord on Garret" priority 25 when argued(crew) and day(clock) >= arguedOn(crew) + 3 and state(shutter, open) seeks state(shutter, shut).
  Action pack_jars(actor: group, site: place) "Pack the ninth vault's jars into a sack" {
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, ring) and at(jars, vault) and state(shutter, shut) and distinct(actor, party).
    Time 3.
    On success { Retract at(jars, vault). Assert keeps(actor, jars). }
    Seen "{actor} packs the jars from the ninth vault into a sack, wrapping each in straw.".
  }
  Pursuit take_jars for ness "packing the ninth vault's jars" priority 30 when at(ness, ring) and state(shutter, shut) and at(jars, vault) seeks keeps(ness, jars) using pack_jars.
  Pursuit go_back for ness "taking the jars up to sell" priority 20 when keeps(ness, jars) seeks at(ness, mutual_yard).
  Pursuit go_back for crew "going back up" priority 10 when descended(crew) and not asleep(garret) seeks at(crew, mutual_yard).
}

data/adventures/patient-star/undersun.ky:
Module season "The Patient Star" {
  // The Undersun (Tier II): an inverted citadel beneath the Late Sun, 300 metres across at its crown and 700 deep,
  // narrowing to a drilling tip. Every room is a moment cut from the plateau's past. Five rules: a room is a moment;
  // touch gives time; speech is laid; course-light doses; the name is the plan.
  Place undersun "the Undersun" is site within ghessil at 5, 1.
  Place crown "the Crown" is level within undersun.
  Place reach "the Seridane Reach" is level within undersun.
  Place silent_reach "the Silent Reach" is level within undersun.
  Place shaft_600 "the shaft at six hundred metres" is level within undersun.
  Place shaft_700 "the shaft at seven hundred metres" is level within undersun.
  Place shaft_foot "the foot of the shaft" is level within undersun.
  Place lreach "the Listeners' Reach" is level within undersun.
  Place tip "the Tip" is level within undersun.

  Place crown_entry "where the Courses broke through" is room within crown at 1, 0 underground.
  Place fall_chamber "the Fall" is room within crown at 0, 0 underground.
  Place fire_heart "the heart of the fire" is room within crown at 0, 1 underground.
  Place first_course "the First Course" is room within crown at 2, 0 underground.
  Place burning_wood "the Burning Wood" is room within crown at 1, 1 underground.
  Place crown_foot "the foot of the Crown" is room within crown at 1, 2 underground.

  Place reach_head "the head of the Seridane Reach" is room within reach at 1, 0 underground.
  Place granary_noon "the Granary at Noon" is room within reach at 0, 0 underground.
  Place schism "the Council of the Schism" is room within reach at 2, 0 underground.
  Place riot_hall "the Riot Hall" is room within reach at 1, 1 underground.
  Place bathhouse "the Bathhouse" is room within reach at 0, 1 underground.
  Place quarried "the Quarried Gallery" is room within reach at 2, 1 underground.
  Place reach_foot "the foot of the Seridane Reach" is room within reach at 1, 2 underground.

  Place shaft_top "the top of the shaft" is room within silent_reach at 0, 0 underground.
  Place plumb_mouth "the Plumb's mouth" is room within shaft_600 at 0, 1 underground.
  Place saro_stair "the top of Saro's stair" is room within shaft_700 at 0, 2 underground.
  Place shaft_bottom "the bottom of the shaft" is room within shaft_foot at 0, 3 underground.

  Place lreach_head "the head of the Listeners' Reach" is room within lreach at 1, 0 underground.
  Place breach_moment "the Breach, stopped" is room within lreach at 0, 0 underground.
  Place keystone_gallery "the Keystone Gallery" is room within lreach at 2, 0 underground.
  Place fair_moment "the Fair" is room within lreach at 1, 1 underground.
  Place tip_dome "the Tip" is room within tip at 0, 0 underground.

  // Course-light: every room of the Undersun is direct light for dose, and every room is laid.
  Initially Assert litGround(crown_entry). Initially Assert litGround(fall_chamber). Initially Assert litGround(fire_heart).
  Initially Assert litGround(first_course). Initially Assert litGround(burning_wood). Initially Assert litGround(crown_foot).
  Initially Assert litGround(reach_head). Initially Assert litGround(granary_noon). Initially Assert litGround(schism).
  Initially Assert litGround(riot_hall). Initially Assert litGround(bathhouse). Initially Assert litGround(quarried).
  Initially Assert litGround(reach_foot). Initially Assert litGround(shaft_top). Initially Assert litGround(plumb_mouth).
  Initially Assert litGround(saro_stair). Initially Assert litGround(shaft_bottom). Initially Assert litGround(lreach_head).
  Initially Assert litGround(breach_moment). Initially Assert litGround(keystone_gallery). Initially Assert litGround(fair_moment).
  Initially Assert litGround(tip_dome).
  Initially Assert laidRoom(granary_noon). Initially Assert laidRoom(riot_hall). Initially Assert laidRoom(schism).
  Initially Assert laidRoom(keystone_gallery). Initially Assert laidRoom(fair_moment). Initially Assert laidRoom(tip_dome).
  Initially Assert laidRoom(breach_moment). Initially Assert laidRoom(bathhouse).

  // The ways in: following Saro, or with a trowel, through the face of the Courses; or down the Plumb.
  Passage into_courses "into the Courses" is crawl between courses_face and crown_entry taking 20 minutes
    opening when travelsWith(saro, party) or holding(party, trowel_kind) "Course-glass cannot be cut, pierced or broken by anything you carry. A Mason's trowel lays and unlays it.".
  Passage plumb "the Plumb, by the rope" is shaft between coverers_works and plumb_mouth taking 1 hour needing rope.
  Initially Set wayDose(plumb) to 24. Initially Set wayDoseFelted(plumb) to 6.

  // The Crown's syllables were spoken before anyone listened: only the Keeping holds them, at the new moons; or
  // Lirem's astrolabe, held in the course-light, reads them off the courses.
  Discovery crown_map "The Crown's plan: its syllables, from the new moons of its first three centuries, laid out as rooms.".
  Passage fall_arch "a ribbed arch" is arch between crown_entry and fall_chamber.
  Passage dog_way "a round passage" is passage between crown_entry and first_course taking 3 minutes hidden until crown_map.
  Passage wood_edge "the edge of the Wood" is passage between crown_entry and burning_wood taking 5 minutes.
  Passage wood_line "the safe line through the smoke" is passage between burning_wood and crown_foot taking 20 minutes hidden until smoke_line.
  Passage fire_gaps "the gaps in the stopped fire" is passage between fall_chamber and fire_heart taking 5 minutes.
  Passage crown_down "the grammar stair" is stair between crown_foot and reach_head taking 10 minutes.

  Observe crown_entry_scene at crown_entry when true "Inside the Courses, light runs along every curve. The passage is coursed like masonry, banded dark and clear, without a seam, and it turns in ways stone would not.".
  Observe astrolabe_reads at crown_entry when carries(party, astrolabe) and not knows(party, crown_map) "Lirem's astrolabe swings in your hand until its pointer lies along the course-light. The rings turn of themselves, syllable by syllable, and you are reading a plan of rooms." teaches crown_map.

  // The Fall: the instant of impact, 2,290 BP. Stopped fire, a shock-front of compressed air, and the Splinter.
  Observe fall_scene at fall_chamber when true "A chamber sixty metres across, full of fire that does not move. Arcs of molten rock hang in the air like thrown ribbons. A curved sheet of something clear and rippled stands across the room, bending everything seen through it.".
  Thing shock_front "the shock-front" at fall_chamber {
    State standing "The clear rippled sheet stands across the chamber: air, compressed and stopped mid-blast.".
  }
  Initially Assert kept(shock_front).
  Hazard slap "the shock-front's slap" means "Deal (2d6) physical damage to ally unless dexterity save against (14).".
  Rule front_released when touched(shock_front) says "The air goes. It throws you ten metres back through the arch." {
    Retract touched(shock_front). Assert strikes(slap, party). Assert at(party, crown_entry). }
  Thing stopped_fire "the stopped fire" on fire_gaps {
    State unmapped dangerous "Between the ribbons of fire there are gaps, but you cannot tell from in among them which go through.".
    State mapped "You have the gaps in the fire mapped from the door: a crooked way in, a crooked way out.".
    Change map_gaps "Map the gaps in the fire from the doorway" from unmapped to mapped.
    Hurts with burn when unmapped then unmapped.
  }
  Hazard burn "the stopped fire" means "Deal (2d8) fire damage to ally.".
  Observe heart_scene at fire_heart when true "At the heart of the fire, in a hollow of stopped flame, lies a fist-sized lump of something that gives off light of its own.".
  Kind splinter_kind "the Splinter" is treasure worth 0 weighing 1
    described "A fist-sized piece of the seed, broken off when it fell. Warm to the hand; it gives off direct light, enough to hold a person at arm's length within a day.".
  Item splinter "the Splinter" is splinter_kind at fire_heart.
  // A very small Late Sun: whoever carries it stands in direct light, wherever they are.
  Relation carriesLight(group).
  Rule splinter_carried when carries(?c, splinter) and company(?c) and not carriesLight(?c) { Assert carriesLight(?c). }
  Rule splinter_dropped when carriesLight(?c) and not carries(?c, splinter) { Retract carriesLight(?c). }
  Rule splinter_doses when carriesLight(?c) and memberOf(?m, ?c) and not unslowed(?m) and not heldDeep(?m) { Increase dose(?m) by 2. }

  // The First Course: the shepherd's dog, the first moment the seed took. The Masons treat it as a shrine.
  Observe dog_scene at first_course when not state(dog_course, unlaid) "In a small round chamber of black-and-clear banding, a dog, mid-stride, its ears back.".
  Thing dog_course "the First Course" at first_course {
    State laid_dog "The dog is the cornerstone of everything below it.".
    State unlaid "The round chamber is empty. Something huge has settled above, and the way down is shut by fallen courses.".
    Change unlay_dog "Unlay the First Course with the trowel" from laid_dog to unlaid needing trowel_kind.
  }
  Initially Assert kept(dog_course).
  Observe dog_runs near dog_course when touched(dog_course) "Under your hand the dog finishes its stride, and the next, and you feel its heart going like a bird's; it is a long way from home and frightened. When you take your hand away it stops again, mid-stride.".
  Rule crown_falls when state(dog_course, unlaid) and not crownDropped(undersun) says "The whole Crown drops three metres onto the Reach below, with a sound that goes on for a long time." {
    Assert crownDropped(undersun). }
  Relation crownDropped(place).

  // The Burning Wood: smoke stopped in curtains; a flake of ash given time drifts along the safe line.
  Observe wood_scene at burning_wood when true "A pine forest on fire, stopped, with birds fixed in the air above it and smoke standing in solid grey curtains between the trunks.".
  Thing smoke "the curtains of smoke" at burning_wood {
    State rigid "The smoke stands in grey curtains, rigid as cloth on a frame.".
  }
  Initially Assert kept(smoke).
  Hazard choke "the smoke, given time" means "Deal (1d8) physical damage to ally unless constitution save against (12).".
  Rule smoke_flows when touched(smoke) says "The curtain goes soft under your hand and pours over you, choking and hot, until you pull your hand back." {
    Retract touched(smoke). Assert strikes(choke, party). }
  Thing ash "a flake of ash" at burning_wood {
    State hanging "A single flake of ash hangs in the air at the height of your eyes.".
  }
  Initially Assert kept(ash).
  Discovery smoke_line "The safe line through the Burning Wood: where a flake of ash, given time, drifts between the curtains.".
  Observe ash_drifts near ash when touched(ash) "Given time, the flake drifts, and does not fall: it goes sideways between two curtains, and turns, and turns again, along a line you could walk." teaches smoke_line.
  Observe crown_foot_scene at crown_foot when true "The Crown narrows to a stair that goes down by repeated forms: the same step laid again and again, as the same syllable was spoken again and again.".

  // The Seridane Reach: moments of Tamaun's life. Mapped by the Long Hour.
  Passage reach_noon "a granary arch" is arch between reach_head and granary_noon.
  Passage reach_schism "a council door" is doorway between reach_head and schism hidden until long_hour_read.
  Passage reach_riot "the way into the crowd" is passage between reach_head and riot_hall taking 3 minutes.
  Passage riot_exit "the Grammar door" is doorway between riot_hall and reach_foot.
  Passage bath_door "a bathhouse door" is doorway between riot_hall and bathhouse.
  Passage quarry_hollow "a smooth hollow" is passage between reach_head and quarried taking 5 minutes hidden until long_hour_read.
  Passage reach_drop "the stem, looped by rope" is shaft between reach_foot and shaft_top taking 30 minutes needing rope.

  Observe reach_head_scene at reach_head when true "The Reach opens under the Crown in galleries that are Tamaun's: plaster, bronze, a Seridane arch with its keystone carved; only no one living built any of it.".
  // The Granary at Noon: forty Laid, mid-task; Lirem with his astrolabe, his other hand toward the gong.
  Observe noon_scene at granary_noon when true "A vault full of Seridane workers, forty of them, mid-task: carrying jars, sweeping, one laughing with her head back. A scribe sits at a table with a stylus over a tablet. A thin man at the end of the room holds a bronze instrument of rings and pointers, his other hand raised toward a gong.".
  Observe noon_wakes at granary_noon when spokeAloud(party) "At the sound of your voice the whole granary moves: forty people take three steps, the laughing woman finishes her laugh, a jar is set down. Then they stop again where they are.".
  Discovery granary_plan "The scribe's tablet: a plan of Tamaun's Granary Ring with the channel settings for every vault.".
  Thing scribe_tablet "the scribe's tablet" at granary_noon {
    State on_table "A wax tablet under the scribe's stylus, ruled in a plan.".
    Tries looking.
  }
  Observe tablet_read near scribe_tablet when tried(scribe_tablet, looking) "It is a plan of the Granary Ring, with the angle of every channel marked beside its vault." teaches granary_plan.
  Thing lirem_hand "Lirem's hand" at granary_noon {
    Holds.
    State holding_it "Lirem's thin hand holds a bronze instrument of rings and pointers.".
    State empty_hand "Lirem's hand is empty, still raised a little toward the gong.".
  }
  Kind astrolabe_kind "Lirem's astrolabe" is treasure worth 0 weighing 1
    described "A bronze instrument of rings and pointers. Set to the Late Sun's depth it shows where any ray will fall; held in course-light, it reads the name-grammar.".
  Item astrolabe "Lirem's astrolabe" is astrolabe_kind in lirem_hand.
  Relation gonged(place).
  Rule hand_emptied when not inside(astrolabe, lirem_hand) and state(lirem_hand, holding_it) says "Lirem's hand, with nothing in it, finishes its movement: it strikes the gong." {
    Assert state(lirem_hand, empty_hand). Assert gonged(granary_noon). }
  Observe gong_alarm at granary_noon when gonged(granary_noon) and not gongPassed(party) "The gong's note goes out through the Reach, and everywhere, for a few seconds, the Laid take up their moments: you hear the riot in the next hall roar and stop.".
  Relation gongPassed(group).
  Rule riot_loosed when gonged(granary_noon) and not rioted(riot_hall) { Assert rioted(riot_hall). }
  Relation rioted(place).

  // The Council of the Schism: Selane arguing for the Covering, Amaru on the dais. A sentence at a touch.
  Observe schism_scene at schism when true "A council chamber. A young woman stands speaking, her hand raised. An old man sits on a dais. Every face in the room is turned to her.".
  Thing selane_words "the air in front of Selane's mouth" at schism {
    State unspoken "Selane's lips are parted on a word.".
  }
  Initially Assert kept(selane_words).
  Measure sentences(entity).
  Rule selane_speaks when touched(selane_words) and sentences(selane_words) < 4 {
    Increase sentences(selane_words) by 1. Retract touched(selane_words). }
  Observe selane_one near selane_words when sentences(selane_words) == 1 "'Lirem's chains are longer every year,' Selane says, in Old Seridan, and stops.".
  Observe selane_two near selane_words when sentences(selane_words) == 2 "'It is not resting on the rock. It is going through it, and the stone below answers each time it speaks.'".
  Observe selane_three near selane_words when sentences(selane_words) == 3 "'A thing that speaks is not always speaking to you. A mason calls out the courses as he lays them.'".
  Discovery seed_building "Selane's argument, in her own voice: the Late Sun is not speaking to anyone; it is building, and calling its courses as it lays them, and it is going down toward something.".
  Observe selane_four near selane_words when sentences(selane_words) == 4 "'Cover it, father. Not because it is a god. Because it is a builder, and we do not know what for.' Her hand comes down. Amaru, on the dais, has not moved." teaches seed_building.
  Topic amaru_selane with amaru "Tell the king his daughter's argument, word for word" when knows(actor, seed_building) once {
    Says "You say it as she said it. It takes Amaru a long time to understand that you are not inventing it. 'A builder,' he says. Then, after a very long time: 'Say it again.' You do. He asks you a third time.".
    On discuss { Assert grieves(amaru). }
  }

  // The Riot Hall: the grain riot of 1,575 BP, two hundred Laid. Every word spoken aloud gives them five seconds.
  Observe riot_scene at riot_hall when true "A broad hall packed with people in mid-struggle: sickles raised, poles swinging, a woman pulled backward by the hair, a man on the floor with his arm over his face. In the middle of the crowd stands a door. On the wall by the entrance someone has written, in chalk, a single sign in a script of overlapping circles.".
  Observe chalk_read at riot_hall when travelsWith(saro, party) "'Quiet,' says Saro, reading the chalk. She says it in a whisper.".
  // Said before the riot is told, because a three-minute act passes the rules once, in order (ledger, 9).
  Rule speaking_door when state(riot_door, open_g) and not doorSpoken(riot_door) { Assert spokeAloud(party). Assert doorSpoken(riot_door). Increase wordsLaid(party) by 10. }
  Hazard riot "five seconds of the riot" means "Deal (2d6) physical damage to ally unless dexterity save against (13).".
  Rule riot_given_time when at(party, riot_hall) and (spokeAloud(party) or rioted(riot_hall)) and not riotStruck(party) says "Two hundred people take up their riot for five seconds: sickles, poles, screaming. Then they stop where they are." {
    Assert strikes(riot, party). Assert riotStruck(party). }
  Relation riotStruck(group).
  Rule riot_still when riotStruck(party) and not spokeAloud(party) and not at(party, riot_hall) { Retract riotStruck(party). }
  Rule riot_spent when rioted(riot_hall) and riotStruck(party) { Retract rioted(riot_hall). }
  Discovery reach_syllables "The syllables of the Seridane Reach's Grammar doors, read from the Long Hour.".
  Observe syllables_from_hour near party when knows(party, long_hour_read) and not knows(party, reach_syllables) "The Long Hour gives you every door in the Reach by the syllable it was laid from." teaches reach_syllables.
  Thing riot_door "the Grammar door" on riot_exit {
    State shut_g blocking "A door of course-glass stands among the rioters. In its floor, if you look, the riot goes on, smaller, as if seen through water.".
    State open_g "The Grammar door stands open.".
    Change speak_syllable "Speak the door's syllable aloud" from shut_g to open_g after learning reach_syllables.
    Change lay_syllable "Lay the door's syllable into it with the trowel" from shut_g to open_g needing trowel_kind.
  }
  Relation doorSpoken(entity).
  Hazard floor_drop "the floor course unlaid" means "Deal (3d6) physical damage to ally unless dexterity save against (14).".
  Action guess_syllable(actor: group, site: place) "Speak a syllable at the Grammar door, guessing" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, riot_hall) and state(riot_door, shut_g)
      and not knows(actor, reach_syllables).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Assert strikes(floor_drop, actor). Assert spokeAloud(actor). Assert at(actor, reach_head). }
    Result "The floor course under you unlays, and you drop into its moment: the riot, all round you, very loud, for as long as you are falling. You come up out of it at the head of the Reach, bruised and shaking.".
  }
  // Speaking aloud in a laid room: talking to anyone, the company is heard, unless it whispers.
  Rule heard_aloud when addressed(?p, ?c) and company(?c) and at(?c, ?r) and laidRoom(?r) and not whispering(?c)
    and not spokeAloud(?c) { Assert spokeAloud(?c). Increase wordsLaid(?c) by 10. }
  Rule quiet_again when spokeAloud(?c) and company(?c) and not addressedAny(?c) { Retract spokeAloud(?c). }
  Query addressedAny(c: group) means addressed(?p, c).

  // The Bathhouse: steam so dense that light takes ten minutes to cross it. Gleaners nest here.
  Observe bath_scene at bathhouse when true "A Seridane bathhouse full of steam that stands like milk. When you hold up a light, its glow does not reach the far side for a long time; what you see across the room is ten minutes old.".
  Species gleaner "a gleaner" like great_centipede temperament defensive
    described "A thing the size of a hand, many-legged, of stopped iron: one of a swarm from another world, given work by the Masons. They gather what falls, and lay it.".
  Person gleaners "gleaners" at bathhouse {
    Role "a swarm of gleaners, nesting". Species gleaner. Numbers 4.
  }
  Observe gleaners_late at bathhouse when at(gleaners, bathhouse) "Across the steam, ten minutes ago, something many-legged was moving along the wall.".

  // The Quarried Gallery: the fourth Dane's reign, carried away; his keystone remains.
  Observe quarried_scene at quarried when true "A long hollow with smooth walls and tool-marks, as if a gallery had been carved out of the masonry and carried off. At its far end one block remains, carved with a name. Your eye will not stay on the name.".
  Thing dane_keystone "the fourth Dane's keystone" at quarried {
    State carved "A block of course-glass with a man laid in it, and a name cut over him that the eye slides off.".
  }
  Initially Assert kept(dane_keystone).
  Observe dane_speaks near dane_keystone when touched(dane_keystone) and not knows(party, dane_name) "Under your hand the man in the block draws breath, and says his own name, and you hear it, and keep it." teaches dane_name.

  // The Silent Reach: a bare stem in a thirty-metre shaft, grown during the burial. The Plumb breaks in at 600 metres;
  // Saro's stair climbs the stem from the bottom, a step a day.
  Passage shaft_down "the stem, by looped rope" is shaft between shaft_top and plumb_mouth taking 30 minutes needing rope.
  Passage shaft_down2 "down the stem to Saro's stair" is shaft between plumb_mouth and saro_stair taking 30 minutes needing rope.
  Passage saro_steps "Saro's stair" is stair between saro_stair and shaft_bottom taking 30 minutes.
  Passage tip_down "the stem's foot" is passage between shaft_bottom and lreach_head taking 10 minutes.
  Observe shaft_scene at shaft_top when true "A vertical shaft thirty metres across and three hundred deep, its walls cut smooth. Down its centre runs a column of dark metal and clear glass twelve metres thick, glowing along its curves. Warm air rises. From below comes a hammering, regular and patient.".
  Observe plumb_mouth_scene at plumb_mouth when true "The Coverers' borehole comes out of the shaft wall here, a glass-lined mouth half a metre across. There is nothing to stand on but a lip of rock and the stem.".
  Observe saro_stair_scene at saro_stair when true "A helical stair is being laid up the stem from the bottom, one step a day. Its top step is new and bright.".
  Observe shaft_bottom_scene at shaft_bottom when true "The foot of the shaft. Everything that has ever fallen down it lies here half-laid into the floor: a cutter's pack, a goat, a stone.".
  Person gleaners_low "gleaners at the foot of the shaft" at shaft_bottom {
    Role "a swarm of gleaners, laying what has fallen". Species gleaner. Numbers 6.
  }
  Hazard long_fall "the long fall" means "Deal (6d6) physical damage to ally.".

  // The Listeners' Reach: recent history, mapped by Teodar's count.
  Passage lr_breach "a stopped storm" is passage between lreach_head and breach_moment taking 3 minutes hidden until listeners_count.
  Passage lr_keystones "a vaulted gallery" is passage between lreach_head and keystone_gallery taking 3 minutes.
  Passage lr_fair "a fair's gate" is passage between lreach_head and fair_moment taking 3 minutes.
  Passage fair_exit "the drum door" is doorway between fair_moment and tip_dome.
  Observe lreach_scene at lreach_head when true "The newest courses: the plateau's own last three hundred years, laid one a month.".
  // The Breach: year 352, in storm. Four figures in wet felt, one with an iron pin.
  Observe breach_moment_scene at breach_moment when true "A night of storm, stopped. A stone culvert, a sluice frame, four figures in wet felt, one with an iron pin in his hand.".
  Thing breach_words "the air near the four in the storm" at breach_moment {
    State still_storm "Rain hangs between you and them.".
  }
  Initially Assert kept(breach_words).
  Observe breach_heard near breach_words when touched(breach_words) "A woman's voice in Tovashi, low, through the rain: 'Pull it, Bren. The fill will drink it.' A young man's: 'Ayzhe —' and the pin comes out of the frame in his hand." teaches breach_cut.
  // The Keystone Gallery: Ennick's held, Kell's dead and the Sixty, laid as ribs.
  Observe keystone_scene at keystone_gallery when true "A vaulted gallery whose ribs are people: men and women lying in clear glass, each with a small red brick carved with a knot above the chest, the way Ennick marks its held. At the far end, older ribs hold strangers in Tovash dress.".
  Observe doran_rib at keystone_gallery when not benighted(party) "One of the ribs is a thin man with his hands at his sides and his mouth a little open, and a fan of bright lines in the glass in front of his face where the sand was not quite clean. It is Doran, at the moment Ilis laid him." teaches held_feed.
  Thing keystones "the keystones" at keystone_gallery {
    State bearing "The keystones bear the courses above them.".
    State unlaid_k "The keystones are unlaid. Below this gallery the Undersun has dropped thirty metres and stopped.".
    Change unlay_keys "Unlay the keystones with the trowel" from bearing to unlaid_k needing trowel_kind.
  }
  Relation masonsComing(place).
  Rule lower_dropped when state(keystones, unlaid_k) and not masonsComing(ennick) says "Far below, the lower Undersun drops thirty metres and stops. Twenty years of growth, gone. The Masons at the Tip put down their work, and look up." {
    Assert masonsComing(ennick). }
  // The Fair: the Tovash fair of year 0. The way out is a Grammar door keyed to a beat.
  Observe fair_scene at fair_moment when true "The Tovash fair of year 0: horses, a cauldron, children with their arms out, and a drum held against a man's chest.".
  Thing drum_door "the drum door" on fair_exit {
    State shut_d blocking "A door of course-glass stands where the fair's gate was. Nothing is carved on it; in its floor a drum is being beaten, very small.".
    State open_d "The drum door stands open.".
    Change strike_drum "Strike the held drum in the moot song's count" from shut_d to open_d after learning moot_count.
    Change lay_drum "Lay the door's beat into it with the trowel" from shut_d to open_d needing trowel_kind.
  }
  Action guess_beat(actor: group, site: place) "Strike the held drum in a beat you guess" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, fair_moment) and state(drum_door, shut_d)
      and not knows(actor, moot_count).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Assert strikes(floor_drop, actor). }
    Result "The floor course unlays and drops you into the fair, a second of it: the drum, the horses, the children's voices, and the light coming up out of the ground. You climb out shaking.".
  }

  // U5, the Tip: Saro's workshop and the drill. Six Masons; under the floor, the Delver; a note once an hour.
  Observe tip_scene at tip_dome when true "At the bottom of the stem, a domed chamber where new courses glow bright along their edges. A low note sounds from below the floor, once an hour.".
  Person masons "six Masons" at tip_dome {
    Role "six figures very still around the walls, each holding a tool like a trowel". Ancestry human. Numbers 6. Peaceable.
  }
  Observe masons_seen near masons when at(masons, tip_dome) "Their hands have no temperature. Their faces are from six different worlds, and they all watch you the same way: with interest, and no fear at all.".
  Topic masons_were with masons "Ask the Masons who they were" when true once {
    Says "They answer one at a time, in the last languages they learned, and Tovashi after a moment, picked up from you. A smith. A ferryman. A woman who sang at funerals. None of them can say where; all of them can say what they made. 'This,' says the singer, and lays a hand on the course. 'This is better.'".
  }
  Discovery trowel_traded "The Masons will trade a trowel for a moment, and the price of a moment is one of your memories, cut out with a trowel.".
  Topic masons_trowel with masons "Ask the Masons for a trowel" when true once {
    Says "'A moment for a moment,' says the ferryman. 'One of yours. We cut it, you do not miss it. Nobody does.' He holds out his hand, palm up.".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, trowel_traded). }
  }
  // The spare trowel is declared in moments.kyr, beside its kind: an Item sees only its own file's kinds (ledger, 25).
  Discovery trowel_paid "A memory cut, and a trowel given for it.".
  Measure memories(group).
  Initially Set memories(party) to 12.
  Action pay_memory(actor: group, site: place) "Let the Masons cut one of your memories, for a trowel" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, tip_dome) and knows(actor, trowel_traded)
      and memories(actor) >= 1 and not paidMemory(actor).
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Decrease memories(actor) by 1. Assert paidMemory(actor). }
    Result "The ferryman lays his trowel against your temple, and something is gone. You do not know what. Nobody in the world will ever know what. He puts a trowel in your hand.".
  }
  Relation paidMemory(group).
  Observe trowel_given near party when paidMemory(party) and not knows(party, trowel_paid) "The trowel lies on the course at your feet where he set it." teaches trowel_paid.
  Species delver_kind "the Delver" like iron_golem temperament defensive
    described "The first Mason, which rode the seed down. Not human. It drills.".
  Person delver "the Delver" at tip_dome {
    Role "the first Mason, working in the drill-face under the floor". Species delver_kind. Level 12.
  }
  // Saro at the Tip: where she works, the courses grow ten times as fast.
  Topic saro_tip with saro travelling "Ask Saro what she will do here" when at(party, tip_dome) once {
    Says "Saro has her hand on the newest course already. 'Work,' she says. 'Here. It is going down to the stone that sings. I will help it go.' She looks at you with that great attention. 'You may stay. You may go. I am staying.'".
  }
}

data/adventures/the-long-man/company.kyr:
Module longman "The Long Man" {
  Company party "Your company" of 3 at road_end.
  Initially Set quantity(party, gold) to 12. Initially Set quantity(party, rations) to 2.
}

data/adventures/the-long-man/dale.kyr:
Module longman "The Long Man" {
  Description "Merrowdale: a dry dale under a long straight ridge the village calls the Long Man, a lake behind it, and three days before the autumn storm.".

  // The dale, north to south: Hollow Water, the Long Man across the dale's throat, the low fields, Merrow.
  Place dale "Merrowdale" is region.
  Place hollow "Hollow Water" is wilderness within dale at 1, 0.
  Place long_man "the Long Man" is site within dale at 1, 1.
  Place fields "the low fields" is wilderness within dale at 1, 2.
  Place merrow "Merrow" is settlement within dale at 0, 2.
  Place south "the south road" is wilderness within dale at 0, 3.

  Place inn "the Drowned Ox" is building within merrow.
  Place chapel "the Chapel of the Ford" is building within merrow.
  Place mill "Teller's mill" is building within merrow.
  Place cottage "Gammer Coller's cottage" is building within merrow.
  Place hall "the Hall" is building within merrow.

  Place road_end "the end of the south road" is room within south at 0, 0.
  Place green "Merrow green" is room within merrow at 1, 2.
  Place taproom "the Drowned Ox" is room within inn at 1, 3.
  Place nave "the chapel" is room within chapel at 0, 2.
  Place vestry "the vestry" is room within chapel at 0, 3.
  Place millhouse "the millhouse" is room within mill at 2, 2.
  Place reeve_room "Gammer Coller's kitchen" is room within cottage at 0, 1.
  Place hall_floor "the Hall" is level within hall.
  Place undercroft "the Hall's undercroft" is level within hall.
  Place yard "the Hall yard" is room within merrow at 1, 0.
  Place study "the steward's study" is room within hall_floor at 0, 0.
  Place chamber "the steward's bedchamber" is room within hall_floor at 1, 0.
  Place cellar "the Hall cellar" is room within undercroft at 2, 0.
  Place race "the mill race" is room within merrow at 2, 1.
  Place low_field "the low field" is room within fields at 0, 1.
  Place springs "the Weeping Springs" is room within fields at 0, 0.
  Place landing "the mill landing" is room within fields at 1, 1.
  Place hollow_door "the Hollow Door" is room within fields at 1, 0.
  // Where people go who have left the dale: downriver on the barge.
  Place downriver "downriver" is room within south at 1, 0.

  Passage south_road "the south road" is road between road_end and green taking 30 minutes.
  Passage ox_door "the Ox's door" is door between green and taproom.
  Passage chapel_porch "the chapel porch" is doorway between green and nave.
  Passage vestry_door "the vestry door" is door between nave and vestry.
  Passage mill_lane "the mill lane" is path between green and race taking 10 minutes.
  Passage mill_door "the mill door" is door between race and millhouse.
  Passage reeve_door "Gammer Coller's door" is door between green and reeve_room.
  Passage hall_lane "the Hall lane" is road between green and yard taking 30 minutes.
  Passage study_door "the study door" is door between yard and study.
  Passage chamber_door "the bedchamber door" is door between study and chamber.
  Passage cellar_stair "the cellar stair" is stair between yard and cellar.
  Passage dyke_path "the dyke path" is path between green and low_field taking 20 minutes.
  Passage spring_path "the spring path" is path between low_field and springs taking 20 minutes.
  Passage beck_path "the beck path" is path between low_field and landing taking 20 minutes.
  Passage mill_steps "the mill steps" is steps between millhouse and landing.
  Passage wall_foot "the foot of the wall" is path between springs and hollow_door taking 20 minutes.
  Passage door_path "the beck side" is path between landing and hollow_door taking 20 minutes.

  // Who comes up the south road: a company of its own (company.kyr) when the dale is a campaign, the world's company
  // when it is a country reached across a march (placed.kyr).

  Observe road_scene at road_end when true "The south road comes up out of the willows into a dale of black, wet-smelling earth. At its head a long green ridge lies across the valley, dead straight, like a sleeper under a blanket. A village of grey stone sits below it with its back to the hill.".
  Observe green_scene at green when not drowned(green) "A green with a well and a lime tree, and grey houses with their backs to the hill. The chapel stands at the low end by the beck; the Drowned Ox faces it across the grass. Up the lane, the Hall's roofs show at the north end of the Long Man.".
  Observe green_drowned at green when drowned(green) "Brown water stands over the green to the height of a man's waist, and moves. The lime tree is full of thatch.".
  Observe taproom_scene at taproom when true "A low taproom smelling of peat and wet wool. A sign over the hearth shows an ox up to its horns in water, which the landlord says is a joke.".
  Observe nave_scene at nave when true "A plain chapel with a floor of flagstones worn into hollows. By the door stands the font: a square grey pillar, smooth as soap, notched all the way up one edge. The highest notch is level with the roof-beam.".
  Observe vestry_scene at vestry when true "A cupboard of a room, with the parish register chained to a shelf and a basin of cold water.".
  Observe millhouse_scene at millhouse when not drowned(millhouse) "The millhouse shakes with the wheel. Flour hangs in the air like smoke.".
  Observe race_scene at race when true "The mill race runs full and loud along its stone channel to the wheel, fuller than a beck this size has any right to.".
  Observe reeve_scene at reeve_room when true "A kitchen with a peat fire, a cat, and on pegs by the door a row of tools for ditches: spades, a slasher, a long hook.".
  Observe yard_scene at yard when true "A cobbled yard under the north end of the Long Man, where the ridge rises behind the Hall like a wall behind a house.".
  Observe yard_smashed at yard when state(cart, smashed) "Something walked through the yard gate without opening it.".
  Observe study_scene at study when true "A steward's study: a fire, a desk heaped with bills, and the Hall's accounts in a row of ledgers.".
  Observe chamber_scene at chamber when true "A narrow bedchamber over the yard, with a cold grate, a washstand, and a bed with curtains of faded green.".
  Observe cellar_scene at cellar when true "The Hall cellar is old at the back, older than the Hall: walls of smooth grey stone, fitted without mortar. Barrels stand along them, and the air at the back is colder than a cellar's should be.".
  Item bar "an iron bar" is crowbar at cellar.
  Observe bar_seen at cellar when at(bar, cellar) "An iron bar leans against the barrels, one end bright with scraped bronze.".
  Observe field_scene at low_field when not drowned(low_field) "A low field of black earth under the Long Man. The furrows hold water, and the grass is the bright green of a meadow that is turning into a bog.".
  Observe field_drowned at low_field when drowned(low_field) "The low field is under a hand's depth of water. The furrows are gone; reeds are coming up through it.".
  Observe springs_scene at springs when true "At the foot of the Long Man a row of small springs comes out of the turf, clear and very cold. They run into a ditch that runs to the mill.".
  Observe landing_scene at landing when true "A stone landing where the beck widens below the mill, with rings for mooring.".
  Observe hollow_door_scene at hollow_door when true "At the south end of the Long Man the beck comes out of the hill through a great round arch of grey stone, smooth and pale, glazed blue-green where the water runs. An iron grate closes it, newer than the arch by a thousand years.".
  Observe downriver_scene at downriver when true "The beck goes on south toward the river and the towns.".

  // The people of Merrow, and what they want.
  Person venn "Aldous Venn" at study {
    Role "steward of the Hall". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner cheerful.
    Greets "Aldous Venn gets up from his bills with a smile that arrives a moment before the rest of him. 'A traveller, and armed,' he says. 'You will have seen my notice.'".
    Objects "Venn sees {?i} in your hands, and his face changes. 'That belongs to the Hall,' he says. 'Give it here.'".
  }
  Person dunnet "Dunnet" at yard {
    Role "foreman at the Hall". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner stoic.
    Greets "Dunnet, a big man with a slow face, straightens up from the cart and looks at you, and then past you at the hill, as if you might have brought something down off it.".
    Wants bandages. Wants tin_lantern.
    Objects "Dunnet looks at {?i}, and at you, and goes in to the steward without a word. The study door bangs.".
  }
  Initially Assert serves(dunnet, venn).
  Person ysolt "Mother Ysolt" at nave {
    Role "priest of the Chapel of the Ford". Ancestry human. Calling cleric. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner compassionate.
    Likeness "abbess".
    Greets "Mother Ysolt looks up from the parish register with the eyes of someone who has buried half the parish and christened the rest. 'You'll be after the steward's forty crowns,' she says. 'Sit down first.'".
    Wants keeper_mask.
  }
  Event mask_buried near ysolt when keeps(ysolt, ?face) and itemKind(?face, keeper_mask) "Mother Ysolt takes the grey face in both hands and looks at it a long time. That evening she buries it in the chapel yard with the words for the dead, and rings the bell once." then {
    Assert buried(?face).
  }
  Relation buried(item).
  Person hob "Hob Teller" at millhouse {
    Role "the miller". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner proud.
    Likeness "potter".
    Greets "Hob Teller looks up from the hopper, and his eyes go to your boots, wet from the beck, and back to your face. 'Mill's not grinding today,' he says, though it is.".
  }
  Person nell "Gammer Coller" at reeve_room {
    Role "the dyke-reeve". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner acerbic.
    Greets "Gammer Coller looks you over from her chair by the fire, slowly, the way she would look at a ditch. 'Well,' she says. 'Shut the door, or the cat will be out.'".
    Objects "'That is the reeve's rod,' says Gammer Coller, very quietly. 'It is not yours, and it is not mine to lose. Put it back.'".
  }
  Person martin "Martin Pask" at taproom {
    Role "landlord of the Drowned Ox". Profession innkeeper. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner jovial.
    Greets "'A traveller!' says Martin Pask, loud enough for half the place to hear. 'Sit, sit. Or stand. What'll it be?'".
    Sells rations for 2 coin from 6.
    Sells torch for 1 coin from 6.
  }
  Person folk "the people of Merrow" at green {
    Role "villagers". Ancestry human. Numbers 4. Peaceable.
  }
  Observe folk_here at green when at(folk, green) and not storming() and not dark() "A few people are at the well, and stop talking to watch you come.".
  Topic folk_long_man with folk "Ask the people at the well about the Long Man" when true once {
    Says "'The Long Man's barrow,' says a woman with a basket of eggs. 'There's a giant king under it, that the Long Folk buried with his gold. You don't go up there after dark.' She nods at the ridge. 'The Mower walks.'".
  }
  Topic folk_mower with folk "Ask the people at the well about the Mower" when true once {
    Says "'Grey,' says a boy, before anyone can stop him, 'and taller than the chapel door. It came down onto the green last week and stood looking at the springs half the night, and Hob Teller hid in his own millpond.' His mother cuffs him, not hard.".
  }
  Topic folk_venn with folk "Ask the people at the well about the steward" when true once {
    Says "They look at one another. 'Owes money downriver, they say,' says the woman with the eggs. 'The barge comes up for his old metal. He'll have put that notice up because the Mower knocked his cart about.'".
  }
  Topic martin_news with martin "Ask Martin Pask what is new in Merrow" when true once {
    Says "'Storm coming,' says Martin, wiping a pot. 'Three days, Gammer Coller says, and she's never been wrong in my life. And the Heron's due up the beck tomorrow noon for the steward's cart. Cass Rowell drinks here.' He sets the pot down. 'If you're going after the Mower, the steward's your man. I'd want paying first.'".
  }

  // The steward's notice, the steward's bronze, and the steward's key.
  Discovery bounty_known "The notice on the Ox's door, in a clerk's hand: WHOEVER LAYS THE MOWER THAT WALKS THE LONG MAN SHALL HAVE FORTY CROWNS OF THE STEWARD. A. VENN, FOR THE LORD." {
    Source notice "the steward's notice on the Ox's door" at green readable by party.
    Known by venn.
  }
  Thing cart "the cart under the tarpaulin" at yard {
    Holds.
    State covered closed "A cart stands under a tarpaulin with its shafts down, the tarpaulin roped tight.".
    State uncovered "The cart's tarpaulin is thrown back.".
    State smashed "The cart lies on its side with its wheels smashed and its tarpaulin torn.".
    Change uncover "Untie the tarpaulin on the cart" from covered to uncovered.
  }
  // The bronze is the steward's, he says, and his foreman says so first.
  Rule dunnet_sees_cart when state(cart, uncovered) and together(dunnet, party) and serves(dunnet, venn) and not noticedCart(dunnet) says "'That's the steward's,' says Dunnet, and comes over, not quickly. 'You'll want to ask him before you go in there.'" { Assert noticedCart(dunnet). }
  Relation noticedCart(group).
  Item teeth "a sack of bell-teeth" is bell_teeth in cart owned by venn.
  Thing cellar_chest "a barrel by the cellar's back wall" at cellar {
    Holds.
  }
  // The grate key is on the steward's belt by day, and on its hook by the study door while he sleeps; he lends it
  // to whoever takes his forty crowns. He sleeps after supper, in the room behind the study.
  Rule venn_retires when dark() and at(venn, study) and able(venn) { Assert at(venn, chamber). }
  Rule venn_rises when not dark() and at(venn, chamber) and able(venn) { Assert at(venn, study). }
  Thing key_hook "the hook by the study door" at study {
    Holds.
    State worn closed "The steward wears a big iron key on his belt.".
    State hung "A big iron key hangs on the hook by the study door.".
    State empty "Nothing hangs on the hook by the study door.".
  }
  Item key "the steward's iron key" is cell_key in key_hook owned by venn.
  // What a close look finds, of the things in the dale and the Hall (no try of them goes unanswered).
  Observe cart_looked near cart when tried(cart, looking) "The cart is built for more than wool: its axle would carry a millstone. Under the edge of the tarpaulin the bed is gouged pale, where something heavy and hard has been dragged in and out.".
  Observe chest_looked near cellar_chest when tried(cellar_chest, looking) "An old wine-barrel with its head set back loose. The top staves are bright where hands have been at them lately, and one is smeared with green, like the green on old bronze.".
  Observe hook_looked near key_hook when tried(key_hook, looking) "A plain iron hook by the study door, worn bright where a ring has hung from it for years.".
  Rule venn_sleeps when dark() and state(key_hook, worn) and not lends(venn, key, ?c) { Assert state(key_hook, hung). }
  Rule venn_wakes when not dark() and state(key_hook, hung) and not lends(venn, key, ?c) and inside(key, key_hook) { Assert state(key_hook, worn). }
  // The hook says what hangs on it: once the key is gone, nothing does.
  Rule hook_emptied when state(key_hook, hung) and not inside(key, key_hook) { Assert state(key_hook, empty). }
  Rule hook_filled when state(key_hook, empty) and inside(key, key_hook) { Assert state(key_hook, hung). }
  Discovery ledger_known "Venn's ledger: twelve bronze teeth sold to Cass Rowell of the barge Heron this year, at eight crowns the tooth, against a debt of sixty crowns, with more to come." {
    Source ledger "the steward's ledger" at study readable by party.
    Known by venn.
  }
  Discovery cellar_known "Behind a barrel in the Hall cellar, a door has been set into a hole broken through the old grey wall, into the inside of the Long Man." {
    Found by searching cellar "Behind the last barrel the old wall has been broken through, and a heavy new door set into the hole. Cold, dry air comes round its edges.".
    Found by searching gallery "Low in the gallery wall an old breach has been fitted with a heavy new door. It does not give: it is barred from the other side.".
    Known by venn, dunnet.
  }

  // Venn hides the bronze in the cellar at nightfall on the first day, and loads it onto the barge when it comes.
  Rule teeth_hidden when watch(clock) >= 60 and inside(teeth, cart) { Retract inside(teeth, cart). Assert inside(teeth, cellar_chest). }
  // Loaded, the teeth are Cass's: on her deck at the landing, hers to sell back, and gone downriver when she goes.
  Rule teeth_loaded when at(cass, landing) and inside(teeth, cellar_chest) { Retract inside(teeth, cellar_chest). Retract owns(venn, teeth). Assert at(teeth, landing). Assert aboard(teeth). }
  Relation aboard(item).
  Rule cass_wants when aboard(teeth) and at(teeth, landing) and not forSale(teeth) { Assert forSale(teeth). Assert soldBy(teeth, cass). Set price(teeth) to 12. }
  Rule teeth_sail when aboard(teeth) and at(teeth, landing) and at(cass, downriver) { Assert at(teeth, downriver). }
  // Told what the bronze held shut, Cass will not carry it: she leaves it on the landing and has the Hall's plate instead.
  Topic cass_weir with cass "Tell Cass Rowell what the bronze was holding shut" when knows(actor, wall_known) and knows(actor, teeth_taken) and aboard(teeth) {
    Says "Cass hears you out without a word, looking past you at the hill. 'My father was under a weir on the Lune when it went,' she says. 'I'll not carry one downriver in a sack.' She whistles, and one of her hands sets the sack down on the landing stones. 'The steward owes me sixty crowns. I'll have them in silver before dusk, or I'll have his plate.'".
    On discuss { Retract aboard(teeth). Retract forSale(teeth). Retract soldBy(teeth, cass). Assert dunned(venn). }
  }
  Relation dunned(group). Relation ruined(group).
  Rule venn_ruined when dunned(venn) and at(cass, downriver) and not ruined(venn) { Assert ruined(venn). }
  Observe study_stripped at study when ruined(venn) "The dresser by the fire is bare: the Hall's plate has gone downriver on the Heron.".
  // Cass drinks at the Ox for an hour while her hands load.
  Rule cass_drinks when watch(clock) >= 186 and watch(clock) < 192 and at(cass, landing) { Assert at(cass, taproom). }
  Rule cass_back when watch(clock) >= 192 and at(cass, taproom) { Assert at(cass, landing). }
  // The Ox's cellar is the lowest in Merrow but the mill's: when the low field goes under, Martin bails.
  Observe ox_bailing at taproom when drowned(low_field) and not drawn(hollow) and not broke(long_man) "Martin Pask is bailing his cellar by the bucket and swearing at the hill. 'Never in my life,' he says. 'Not once, not in a wet year.'".
  Observe cass_at_ox at taproom when at(cass, taproom) "Cass Rowell sits alone by the fire with her boots on the fender, reading a letter and moving her lips.".
  // Merrow's evenings are spent in the Ox, and its nights in its own beds.
  Rule folk_evening when dark() and untilLight(clock) > 42 and at(folk, green) and not storming() and not lostToWater(folk) { Assert at(folk, taproom). }
  Rule folk_bed when at(folk, taproom) and untilLight(clock) <= 42 { Assert at(folk, green). }
  Observe green_night at green when dark() and not drowned(green) "The green is dark. Somebody's dog barks once.".
  Observe ox_evening_first at taproom when at(folk, taproom) and watch(clock) < 144 "The taproom is full and loud. Everybody has an opinion about the steward's notice, and nobody means to go up the hill after dark to earn it.".
  Observe ox_evening_second at taproom when at(folk, taproom) and watch(clock) >= 144 and not state(leak_gate, mended) and not drawn(hollow) "The talk in the Ox is of the barge, and of the low field, where Ned Rook went in over his boots this afternoon by the springs, on ground that was dry at Lammas.".
  // Once the leak is shut or the lake is down, the low field is not the talk (the Bushweald play heard Ned Rook go in
  // over his boots the evening after the wall was mended).
  Observe ox_evening_eased at taproom when at(folk, taproom) and watch(clock) >= 144 and (state(leak_gate, mended) or drawn(hollow)) "The talk in the Ox is of the barge, and of the springs at the foot of the Long Man, which ran clear this morning for the first time since Lammas. Nobody says why.".
  // Hob walks up to the springs at dusk with his spade, and stands looking at the water.
  Rule hob_walks when dark() and untilLight(clock) > 48 and at(hob, millhouse) and not confessed(hob) { Assert at(hob, springs). }
  Rule hob_home when at(hob, springs) and untilLight(clock) <= 48 { Assert at(hob, millhouse). }
  Observe hob_watching at springs when at(hob, springs) "Hob Teller stands at the springs in the dusk with a spade over his shoulder, looking at the water as a man looks at a debt.".


  // Dunnet hurt: an arm bound properly buys what wages would.
  Observe dunnet_sling at yard when hurt(dunnet) and at(dunnet, yard) "Dunnet sits on the mounting-block with his arm in a sling of sacking and his jaw set.".
  Event dunnet_bound near dunnet when keeps(dunnet, ?b) and itemKind(?b, bandages) and hurt(dunnet) "Dunnet lets you set the arm and bind it, and only swears once. 'The bar comes off the cellar door at dark,' he says. 'For you. Not for him.'" then {
    Retract hurt(dunnet). Assert promisedDoor(dunnet). Retract serves(dunnet, venn).
  }
  // Pell's lantern brought back: Dunnet tells it all, and then tells Mother Ysolt.
  Event pell_told near dunnet when keeps(dunnet, lantern) "Dunnet turns the lantern over and over in his hands and wipes the glass with his thumb. 'Pell's,' he says. 'The steward told them Pell went down the river in the spring. He never. The clay stood up and took him while we had the teeth out, and I ran.' He gets up. 'I'm going to tell Mother Ysolt. Then they can all know.'" then {
    Assert confessedPell(dunnet). Retract serves(dunnet, venn).
  }
  Relation confessedPell(group). Relation pellKnown().
  // He goes down to the chapel at dusk, and by morning the whole parish has it.
  Rule dunnet_to_chapel when confessedPell(dunnet) and dark() and at(dunnet, yard) { Assert at(dunnet, nave). }
  Rule pell_known when confessedPell(dunnet) and at(dunnet, nave) and not pellKnown() { Assert pellKnown(). Assert exposed(venn). }
  Observe dunnet_at_chapel at nave when at(dunnet, nave) "Dunnet sits on the bench by the font with Pell's lantern on his knees.".
  Observe pell_mourned at green when pellKnown() and at(folk, green) and not dark() "At the well they are talking low about Pell, and nobody says the steward's name, and everyone means it.".
  // Dunnet is owed his wages, and is frightened of what is behind the cellar door.
  Relation promisedDoor(group).
  Topic dunnet_fear with dunnet "Ask Dunnet about the Mower" when true once {
    Says "Dunnet looks at the hill. 'It's not the Mower I mind,' he says. 'It's what's in the wet tunnel. It stood up out of the floor at Pell and me, all mud, and came after us. I'm not going back through that door, not for the steward, not for anyone.'".
  }
  Topic dunnet_door with dunnet "Ask Dunnet what is behind the cellar door" when knows(actor, cellar_known) or state(cellar_door, barred) {
    Says "'The inside of the Long Man,' says Dunnet. 'Tunnels, dry as a church, all that grey stone. And the wheels. We had the teeth out of the big wheel in the wet tunnel, twelve of them, before the mud stood up.' He looks at his boots. 'The steward keeps it barred now.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, cellar_known). }
  }
  Action pay_dunnet(actor: group, site: place) "Give Dunnet three coin toward the wages he is owed" {
    Description "He is owed three months, and the steward will not pay.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(dunnet, site) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 3
      and not promisedDoor(dunnet).
    On success {
      Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 3. Increase quantity(dunnet, gold) by 3. Assert promisedDoor(dunnet).
      Retract serves(dunnet, venn).
    }
    Result "Dunnet counts the coins twice. 'The steward sleeps after supper,' he says, low. 'The bar comes off the cellar door at dark, and goes back on at cockcrow. That's all. I never saw you.'".
  }
  // Dunnet takes the bar off at dark and puts it back at cockcrow; a bar the company lifted itself is its own affair.
  Rule door_unbarred when promisedDoor(dunnet) and dark() and state(cellar_door, barred) { Assert state(cellar_door, unbarred). Assert dunnetsBar(cellar_door). }
  Rule door_rebarred when dunnetsBar(cellar_door) and not dark() and state(cellar_door, unbarred) and not at(party, cellar) { Assert state(cellar_door, barred). Retract dunnetsBar(cellar_door). }
  Relation dunnetsBar(entity).

  // Venn: what he says, and what he pays.
  Topic venn_bounty with venn "Ask Aldous Venn about the Mower" when not exposed(venn) and not hostile(venn, actor) {
    Says "'The Mower,' says Venn, and smiles as if it were a joke between gentlemen. 'The Long Man's ghost. It walks the crest at night and frightens the parish, and now it has taken to coming down into my yard. Forty crowns, and you may keep the mask it wears to show for it; Mother Ysolt will want to bury it.' He unhooks a big iron key from his belt and hangs it by the door. 'It lies up inside the hill by day, the men say. That key opens the grate at the Hollow Door.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, bounty_known). Assert lends(venn, key, actor). Assert state(key_hook, hung). }
  }
  Topic venn_bronze with venn "Ask Aldous Venn what was in the cart" when knows(actor, ledger_known) and not exposed(venn) and not hostile(venn, actor) {
    Says "Venn's smile stays where it is, but his eyes go to the ledgers. 'Old metal,' he says. 'Lumber from the Long Folk's mill under the hill. The estate has debts, and the hill is the estate's.' He spreads his hands. 'Nobody in Merrow ever had a use for it.'".
  }
  // Shown his own ledger beside what the bronze held shut, he gives up the key, and then the dale.
  Topic venn_shown with venn "Show Aldous Venn his own ledger, and tell him what the bronze held shut" when knows(actor, ledger_known) and knows(actor, teeth_taken) and not exposed(venn) {
    Says "Venn reads his own hand as if a stranger had written it. 'A sluice,' he says. 'Old metal off a sluice.' He sits down. 'Sixty crowns, and a letter from the Lord every week asking where they are.' He unhooks the iron key from his belt and hangs it by the door, and does not look at it. 'Take it. Do what you like with the hill.' When you go out he is writing, fast, to Cass Rowell.".
    On discuss { Assert exposed(venn). Assert lends(venn, key, actor). Assert state(key_hook, hung). }
  }
  Relation exposed(group).
  Rule venn_flees when exposed(venn) and at(cass, landing) and able(venn) and not at(venn, landing) and not at(venn, downriver) { Assert at(venn, landing). }
  Rule venn_sails when exposed(venn) and at(venn, landing) and at(cass, downriver) { Assert at(venn, downriver). }
  Observe venn_waits at landing when exposed(venn) and at(venn, landing) "Aldous Venn sits on the Heron's hatch with a valise on his knees, and does not look up at the hill.".
  Action claim_bounty(actor: group, carrier: member, face: item, site: place) "Show Aldous Venn {face}" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(venn, site) and memberOf(carrier, actor)
      and ownedItem(face, carrier) and itemKind(face, keeper_mask) and not paidBounty(venn).
    On success { Decrease quantity(venn, gold) by 40. Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 40. Assert paidBounty(venn). }
    Result "Venn turns the grey face over in his hands, and for a moment he looks old. Then he counts out forty crowns, most of them in silver he has clearly borrowed. 'Merrow will sleep tonight,' he says.".
  }
  Relation paidBounty(group).
  Initially Set quantity(venn, gold) to 40.

  // Mother Ysolt and the font.
  Topic ysolt_mower with ysolt "Ask Mother Ysolt about the Mower" when not convinced(ysolt) {
    Says "'The Long Man is restless,' says Mother Ysolt. 'He was a king, and a cruel one; the font is his tally, a notch for every sin, and the parish has prayed him down for two hundred years. Now he walks again. Bring me his mask and I will put it in the ground with the proper words, and he will lie still.'".
  }
  Relation convinced(group).
  Topic ysolt_notches with ysolt "Tell Mother Ysolt what the notches on the font are" when knows(actor, notches_known) and not convinced(ysolt) {
    Says "Mother Ysolt stands a long time at the font with her hand flat on the stone, looking up at the highest notch and the roof-beam beside it. 'The chapel step,' she says at last. 'The register says the water came to the chapel step.' She turns. 'If it comes again, it will not stop at the step. I will ring the bell, and Merrow will go up the hill to the Hall, and the steward can say what he likes.'".
    On discuss { Assert convinced(ysolt). }
  }
  Discovery wept_known "The parish register, two hundred years back: 'In the year the Long Man wept, the water came over the low field to the chapel step. The Mower walked by day as well as night, and in seven days the water went back. The lord's men had dug into the Barrow for its gold.'" {
    Source register "the parish register" at vestry readable by party.
    Known by ysolt.
  }

  // Hob Teller and the springs.
  Topic hob_springs with hob "Ask Hob Teller about the springs" when not confessed(hob) {
    Says "'Blessed springs,' says Hob. 'My father's wheel stood still every dry summer. This one turns day and night.' He does not look toward the hill.".
  }
  Relation confessed(group).
  Topic hob_cuts with hob "Show Hob Teller the spade-cuts at the springs" when knows(actor, cuts_known) and not confessed(hob) {
    Says "Hob goes white, then red. 'It was the drought,' he says. 'A few spits with the spade, in the spring, to let them run. They've run harder every week since.' He looks at his mill, the lowest house in Merrow. 'I'll stake them and clay them over tomorrow, before light. God help me, I'll do it.'".
    On discuss { Assert confessed(hob). }
  }
  Rule hob_staunches when confessed(hob) and state(cuts, open) and untilLight(clock) == 1 { Assert state(cuts, staunched). }
  // What the springs are is not in their name: looking closely, or searching the place, finds the spade-cuts.
  Thing cuts "the spring-heads" at springs {
    State open "The springs pour out of the turf, cold and clear, more water than a few springs ought to give.".
    State staunched "The cuts at the springs have been staked and packed with clay. The water seeps instead of pouring.".
    Change staunch "Stake the spade-cuts and pack them with clay" from open to staunched needing digging or shovel after learning cuts_known.
  }
  Discovery cuts_known "Someone has cut the Weeping Springs wider with a spade, this year: the edges are still square." {
    Found by searching springs "Under the water the turf is cut in clean square bites, too regular for water to have made. A spade did this, not long ago.".
  }
  Observe cuts_looked near cuts when tried(cuts, looking) "Under the water the turf is cut in clean square bites, too regular for water to have made. A spade did this, not long ago." teaches cuts_known.

  // Gammer Coller and her rod.
  Topic nell_rhyme with nell "Ask Gammer Coller about the Mower" when true once {
    Says "'There's a rhyme,' says Gammer Coller. 'When the Mower walks the crown, keep the willow-roots cut down. When the Mower walks the green, the water's coming in between. When the Mower walks by day, Merrow, take your bed away.' She pokes the fire. 'It's been walking the green this month. Nobody asked me.'".
  }
  Topic nell_rod with nell "Ask Gammer Coller about the rod by her door" when true once {
    Says "'The dyke-reeve's rod,' she says, and takes it down: black wood, with notched bronze on both ends. 'Every reeve has had it since there were reeves. You measure a ditch with it.' She runs her thumb along the notches. 'Not that the notches match any measure I know.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, rod_seen). }
  }
  Topic nell_lend with nell "Ask Gammer Coller for the loan of her rod" when knows(actor, mower_keeps) and at(rod, reeve_room) {
    Says "She listens without a word while you tell her what the Mower does. Then she lays the rod on the table. 'I always thought it walked like a reeve,' she says. 'Bring it back.'".
    On discuss { Assert lends(nell, rod, actor). }
  }
  Item rod "the dyke-reeve's rod" is sluice_rod at reeve_room hidden until rod_seen owned by nell.
  Discovery rod_seen "Gammer Coller keeps an old rod shod in notched bronze, the dyke-reeve's rod, by her door.".

  // Cass Rowell's barge, the Heron: up the beck at noon on the second day, away at dusk.
  Person cass "Cass Rowell" at downriver {
    Role "master of the barge Heron". Ancestry human. Calling thief. Level 3. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner grim.
    Likeness "butcher".
    Greets "Cass Rowell looks at you, and at your hands, and at the bank behind you, in that order. 'If it's passage, I'm full,' she says. 'If it's business, say it.'".
    Buys bell_teeth for 8 coin.
  }
  Person hands "the Heron's hands" at downriver {
    Role "bargemen". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 2. Numbers 2.
  }
  Initially Assert serves(hands, cass). Initially Set quantity(cass, gold) to 60.
  Thing hold "the Heron's hold" at downriver {
    Holds.
  }
  Observe hold_looked near hold when tried(hold, looking) "The Heron's hold is open to the sky and wet underfoot. There is room in it for a good deal more than wool, and the boards are scored where something heavy was stowed and taken out again.".
  Rule cass_comes when watch(clock) >= 168 and watch(clock) < 204 and at(cass, downriver) { Assert at(cass, landing). Assert at(hands, landing). Assert at(hold, landing). }
  Rule cass_goes when watch(clock) >= 204 and at(cass, landing) and able(cass) { Assert at(cass, downriver). Assert at(hands, downriver). Assert at(hold, downriver). }
  Observe heron_scene at landing when at(cass, landing) "The barge Heron lies at the landing, low in the water, with a brown sail furled and two bargemen sitting on the hatch.".
  Topic cass_trade with cass "Ask Cass Rowell what she is carrying" when true once {
    Says "'Whatever pays,' says Cass. 'Wool down, iron up. Bronze, when the steward has it. He owes me sixty crowns and pays me in old teeth.' She looks you over. 'If you've teeth to sell, I buy at eight. If you want them back, they cost twelve. That's trade.'".
  }

  // The steward's grate, and the key that opens it.
  Thing grate "the iron grate" on culvert {
    State locked blocking "The iron grate is locked with a padlock the size of a loaf.".
    State open "The iron grate stands open on its hinges.".
    Change unlock "Unlock the grate with the steward's key" from locked to open needing key.
  }
  Observe grate_looked beside culvert as event when tried(grate, looking) "New iron in old stone, a thousand years apart. The hinges are greased, and the mud at the foot of the grate has been walked through, lately, in boots.".
  Initially Assert keyholder(venn, grate).
}

data/adventures/the-long-man/placed.kyr:
Module longman "The Long Man" {
  // The dale as a country beyond a march: the company that comes up the south road is the world's own.
  Entity party: group "Your company".
  // What the country below says of the dale (its innkeepers' rumour of the forty crowns): once Merrow is safe from its
  // wall, it is old news there, and they say so to whoever comes back down the north road.
  Entity word: fact "What is said of Merrowdale in the country below.".
  Rule word_old when (state(leak_gate, mended) or drawn(hollow) or (broke(long_man) and calm(long_man) and not lostToWater(folk))) and not stale(word) { Assert stale(word). }
}

data/adventures/the-long-man/wall.kyr:
Module longman "The Long Man" {
  Description "The Long Man: the crest a figure walks at night, and the grey galleries inside the hill.".

  Place inside "the galleries" is level within long_man.
  Place crest "the crest of the Long Man" is room within long_man at 1, 0.
  Place gauge_head "the gauge stone" is room within long_man at 2, 0.
  Place gallery "the grey gallery" is room within inside at 1, 1.
  Place sluice "the sluice chamber" is room within inside at 2, 2.
  Place rest "the keeper's niche" is room within inside at 0, 1.
  Place leak "the wet gallery" is room within inside at 1, 2.
  Place shaft_foot "the foot of the gauge shaft" is room within inside at 2, 1.
  // The clay core, where what the leak made of the clay goes when the leak is shut.
  Place core "the clay core" is room within inside at 0, 2.
  Initially Assert unlit(gallery). Initially Assert unlit(sluice). Initially Assert unlit(rest). Initially Assert unlit(leak).
  Initially Assert unlit(shaft_foot).

  Passage crest_steps "the steps up the Long Man" is steps between yard and crest taking 20 minutes.
  Passage valley_face "the valley face" is path between crest and springs taking 20 minutes.
  Passage crest_walk "the crest" is path between crest and gauge_head taking 10 minutes.
  Passage culvert "the culvert" is culvert between hollow_door and sluice taking 10 minutes.
  Passage broken_wall "the broken wall" is doorway between cellar and gallery hidden until cellar_known.
  Passage sluice_way "the sluice passage" is passage between gallery and sluice.
  Passage niche_way "the keeper's passage" is passage between gallery and rest.
  Passage wet_way "the wet passage" is passage between gallery and leak.
  Passage shaft_way "the shaft passage" is passage between gallery and shaft_foot.
  Passage gauge_shaft "the gauge shaft" is shaft between shaft_foot and gauge_head taking 30 minutes needing climbing or rope.
  Passage sinkhole "the sinkhole" is climb between crest and leak taking 20 minutes needing rope.

  // The bar is on the cellar side: only someone in the cellar can lift it.
  Thing cellar_door "the door in the broken wall" on broken_wall {
    State barred blocking "A heavy door closes the hole broken through the wall, barred on the cellar side.".
    State unbarred "The bar is off the door in the broken wall, and it stands a hand's width open on the dark.".
    Change lift "Lift the oak bar off the door in the broken wall" from barred to unbarred at cellar.
  }
  Observe door_looked beside broken_wall as event when tried(cellar_door, looking) "New planks, hung in a hole knocked through grey stone that was never meant to be broken: the stone is cracked for a yard round the hole, the way ice cracks.".
  Initially Assert keyholder(venn, cellar_door).
  // Shut in behind a barred door, a company can always make itself heard: at a price.
  Action hammer_door(actor: group, site: place) "Hammer on the door until someone in the cellar hears" {
    Description "Somebody will come in the end. Everybody at the Hall will know who it was.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, gallery) and state(cellar_door, barred)
      and knows(actor, cellar_known).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert state(cellar_door, unbarred). Assert hostile(venn, actor). }
    Result "You hammer on the oak until your hands ache. At last the bar scrapes off its brackets, and Dunnet's face looks in at you, white. 'The steward will hear of this,' he says, and he is right.".
  }

  Observe crest_scene at crest when not dark() "The crest of the Long Man is a dead-level walk of turf, wide as a lane. On one hand the dale falls away to Merrow's roofs; on the other, a long way down, lies Hollow Water, black and still, filling the valley to the hills. Nothing grows on the crest higher than a hand: every sapling has been cut off at the root, clean.".
  Observe crest_night at crest when dark() "By night the crest is a pale road between two darks: the dale's, with a few lights in it, and the lake's, with none.".
  Observe sinkhole_scene at crest when true "Halfway along, the turf has fallen into a raw hole a cart wide. Water drips somewhere far down in it.".
  Observe gauge_scene at gauge_head when true "At the north end of the crest a square grey stone stands over a square shaft going down into the hill. Notches are cut down every edge of the shaft, deeper than the light goes.".
  Observe gallery_scene at gallery when true "A tunnel lined with smooth grey stone, tall and narrow, as if cut for something taller than a man. The air is dry and still. Ways go off to either hand.".
  Observe sluice_scene at sluice when true "A chamber over the culvert, where the beck runs loud below an iron grating. Two great wheels of grey stone stand on their edges, set round with teeth of green bronze, and a third, smaller, works the shutter of the bottom sluice.".
  Observe rest_scene at rest when true "A niche in the gallery wall, taller than two men, with a ledge of grey stone at the back and tools laid on it in order: blades, hooks, a stone trowel, all of the same grey. Notches run in close rows up the walls.".
  Observe leak_scene at leak when not state(leak_gate, mended) "Water comes through a crack in the inner face of the gallery, a sheet of it, and runs away under the floor.".
  Observe leak_mended at leak when state(leak_gate, mended) "The wall of the gallery is wet, and no more.".
  Observe shaft_scene at shaft_foot when true "The bottom of a square shaft. Notches climb its four edges up into the dark, and the stone of the shaft-side toward the lake sweats.".

  // The Mower: it stands in its niche by day and walks the crest by night, and goes after its bronze.
  Person mower "the Mower" at rest {
    Role "the tall grey figure that walks the Long Man". Species automaton. Level 12.
    Wants bell_teeth.
  }
  Rule mower_rises when dark() and at(mower, rest) and able(mower) and not hunting(mower) { Assert at(mower, crest). }
  Rule mower_returns when not dark() and not at(mower, rest) and able(mower) { Assert at(mower, rest). Retract hunting(mower). }
  Relation hunting(group).
  // At midnight on the first night it comes down for the bronze that was in the cart, and finds the cart empty.
  Rule mower_hunts at yard when dark() and watch(clock) >= 96 and watch(clock) < 132 and state(cart, covered) and able(mower)
    says "Something tall comes over the yard wall without climbing it. The Mower goes to the cart, tears the tarpaulin away, finds nothing, and turns the cart over as if it were a barrow. A shaft flies. Dunnet, who came out with a lantern, goes down with a cry." {
    Assert state(cart, smashed). Assert hunting(mower). Assert at(mower, yard). Assert hurt(dunnet).
  }
  Relation hurt(group).
  Observe mower_crest at crest when dark() and at(mower, crest) "The Mower walks the crest, slowly, the length of it and back. Every few paces it stoops, and a long blade flicks, and something small falls." teaches mower_keeps.
  Observe count_matched at rest when knows(party, last_count) "The last row of notches on the niche wall is a count of days, and it stops at forty-one.".
  Observe mower_resting at rest when at(mower, rest) and able(mower) "The Mower stands in its niche: a figure taller than two men, grey and too smooth, with its long arms at its sides and a face like a blank mask. It does not move. On its breastplate, in the light, a row of notches." .
  Observe mower_yard at yard when at(mower, yard) "The Mower stands in the yard by the overturned cart, its blank face turned toward the cellar." .
  Discovery keeper_named "The notches on the Mower's breastplate, read: KEEPER OF THE WALL." {
    Found by searching rest with lore "The notches on the Mower's breastplate are writing, the same writing as on the walls. It says, as near as it can be read: KEEPER OF THE WALL.".
  }
  Discovery mower_keeps "The Mower keeps the Long Man: it cuts every sapling on the crest before its roots can crack the wall, and it goes after bronze taken from its wheels.".
  // Given back its bronze, it fits the teeth to the leak gate's wheel that night, and closes the gate. The company
  // that gave them sees it go into the hill (near the company, since it is the Mower that goes).
  Event mower_mends near party when keeps(mower, teeth) and not state(leak_gate, mended) "The Mower takes the sack of teeth in both hands, turns, and walks away into the hill. Some time later, deep inside the Long Man, something heavy closes with a sound like a bell." then {
    Assert state(leak_gate, mended). Assert at(mower, leak).
  }
  Item mask "the Mower's mask" is keeper_mask at core.
  Rule mower_falls when dead(mower) and at(mower, ?p) and at(mask, core) { Assert at(mask, ?p). }
  // By day it stands still in its niche, and its face is a mask that a bar can lever off. That lays it, as Venn wants
  // and Ysolt prays for; and then nobody keeps the wall.
  Hazard unmasking "The mask levered off" means "Kill ally.".
  Action unmask_mower(actor: group, site: place) "Get the bar under the Mower's face and lever it off" {
    Description "By day it does not move. Whatever it is, its face is a mask, and a mask comes off.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(mower, site) and at(mower, rest) and able(mower)
      and not dark() and holding(actor, crowbar) and not benighted(actor).
    On success { Assert strikes(unmasking, mower). Retract at(mask, core). Assert at(mask, rest). }
    Result "The bar goes in under the grey chin, and you lean on it. The mask comes away with a sound like a cracked bell, and the Mower folds down onto its ledge like a dropped coat, and is still.".
  }

  // The leak gate, and what the leak has made of the clay.
  Thing leak_gate "the bronze shutter" at leak {
    State jammed "A shutter of bronze teeth hangs half across the crack, on a wheel with twelve empty sockets.".
    State fitted "The bronze teeth are back in the shutter's wheel; it hangs open, ready to be turned.".
    State mended "The bronze shutter is closed across the crack, every socket of its wheel filled.".
    Change heave "Heave the shutter's wheel round and close it" from fitted to mended needing brawn.
  }
  Observe shutter_looked near leak_gate when tried(leak_gate, looking) and state(leak_gate, jammed) "Each of the twelve sockets is shaped for one of the bell-teeth, and each is bright at its edges where a bar went in and levered the tooth out. Water beads along the crack behind the shutter and runs down into the clay.".
  Observe shutter_seen near leak_gate when tried(leak_gate, looking) and not state(leak_gate, jammed) "Bronze, green with age, on a wheel of twelve sockets; behind it, the crack in the clay core, darker than the clay round it.".
  Action fit_teeth(actor: group, carrier: member, site: place) "Fit the bell-teeth back into the shutter's wheel" {
    Description "Twelve sockets, twelve teeth. They go in with a sound like a bell.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(leak_gate, site) and state(leak_gate, jammed)
      and memberOf(carrier, actor) and awake(carrier) and ownedItem(teeth, carrier).
    Time 6.
    Resolve drop(teeth, carrier).
    On success { Assert at(teeth, core). Assert state(leak_gate, fitted). }
    Result "One by one the teeth go into their sockets, and each one rings as it seats. When the twelfth is in, the wheel turns a finger's width under your hand.".
  }
  Person wet "the Wet" at leak {
    Role "a heaving mass of wet clay". Species slump. Level 5.
    Temperament territorial.
    Warns "At the far end of the wet gallery the floor heaves, and a shape stands up out of the clay, streaming, as tall as a door.".
    Comes "The Wet comes down the gallery at you, faster than mud should.".
  }
  // What the Wet took: the man who went in with Dunnet for the teeth.
  Item lantern "a miner's lantern" is tin_lantern at leak.
  Observe pell_seen at leak when at(lantern, leak) "At the far end of the gallery, half sunk in the clay, a man's lantern lies on its side, its glass packed with mud.".
  Rule wet_slumps at leak when state(leak_gate, mended) and at(wet, leak) says "The Wet sags, and sags, and is a heap of clay on the floor, and then is only floor." { Assert at(wet, core). }

  // The sluice: the bottom gate under the chamber. Opened, it fills the culvert and runs the beck high.
  Thing bottom_sluice "the bottom sluice" at sluice {
    State shut "The small wheel is turned home; the bottom sluice is shut.".
    State open dangerous "The small wheel is turned out, and below the grating the water roars.".
    Change open_it "Turn the small wheel and open the bottom sluice" from shut to open needing brawn.
    Change shut_it "Turn the small wheel home and shut the bottom sluice" from open to shut needing brawn.
  }
  Observe sluice_looked near bottom_sluice when tried(bottom_sluice, looking) "A shutter of grey stone in a groove, worked by the small wheel. The groove is worn as smooth as the font: it has gone up and down ten thousand times, and the last time not long ago.".
  Thing culvert_water "the water in the culvert" on culvert is scenery {
    State low "The beck runs ankle-deep along the culvert floor.".
    State high blocking dangerous "The culvert is full to the roof with fast brown water.".
  }
  Rule culvert_fills when state(bottom_sluice, open) and state(culvert_water, low) says "Somewhere below, the water changes its voice." { Assert state(culvert_water, high). }
  Rule culvert_drains when state(bottom_sluice, shut) and state(culvert_water, high) { Assert state(culvert_water, low). }
  Rule mower_guards_sluice when state(bottom_sluice, open) and together(mower, party) and able(mower) says "The Mower turns its blank face toward the open sluice, and then toward you." { Assert assails(mower, party). }

  // The gauge shaft and its notches.
  Discovery notches_known "The notches on the font are water heights, like the notches down the gauge shaft: the same cuts, the same spacing. The highest notch on the font is level with the chapel's roof-beam." {
    Source shaft_notches "the notches down the gauge shaft" at shaft_foot readable by party.
  }
  Discovery wall_known "The Long Man is a wall: it holds Hollow Water back from the dale, and the beck comes through it by a culvert.".
  Observe sluice_teaches at sluice when true "Above the grating the wheels and the culvert make plain what the Long Man is: not a barrow, a wall, with a lake behind it and a sluice through it." teaches wall_known.
  Observe teeth_missing at leak when not state(leak_gate, mended) "Fresh bright scars on the stone by the crack show where a bar has been used, and lately." teaches teeth_taken.
  Discovery teeth_taken "Twelve bronze teeth have been prised out of the wheel of the shutter that should close the leak in the Long Man.".

  // The storm comes on the third day; two hours after midnight the Long Man breaks, unless its leak is shut or the
  // lake is drawn down.
  Relation storming(). Relation broke(place). Relation drowned(place). Relation drawn(place).
  Rule storm_comes when watch(clock) >= 312 and not storming() and not calm(long_man) says "The wind goes round to the north, and the rain comes in over the fell in grey ropes." { Assert storming(). }
  Observe storm_scene at crest when storming() "Rain drives across the crest. Hollow Water has come up the lake face of the Long Man, grey and heaving, nearer than it was.".
  Rule field_wets when watch(clock) >= 240 and not state(leak_gate, mended) and not drowned(low_field) { Assert drowned(low_field). }
  Rule long_man_breaks when watch(clock) >= 396 and not state(leak_gate, mended) and not drawn(hollow) and not broke(long_man)
    says "In the dark, under the noise of the rain, there is another noise, very deep, like a wall falling a long way off. Then the sound of water." {
    Assert broke(long_man). Assert drowned(low_field). Assert drowned(green).
  }
  Hazard flood_waters "The flood" means "Deal (4d6) physical damage to ally unless dexterity save against (14).".
  Rule flood_takes when broke(long_man) and (at(party, green) or at(party, low_field) or at(party, landing) or at(party, millhouse) or at(party, nave) or at(party, taproom) or at(party, hollow_door) or at(party, springs))
    and not swept(party) { Assert strikes(flood_waters, party). Assert swept(party). }
  Relation swept(group).
  // Merrow on the hill, if Mother Ysolt rang the bell; otherwise Merrow in the low town when the water came.
  Rule bell_rung at green when storming() and convinced(ysolt) and at(folk, green)
    says "The chapel bell rings and rings, and doors open all over Merrow, and people go up the Hall lane in the rain with what they can carry." {
    Assert at(folk, yard). Assert at(ysolt, yard).
  }
  Relation lostToWater(group).
  Rule folk_lost when broke(long_man) and (at(folk, green) or at(folk, taproom)) { Assert lostToWater(folk). Assert at(folk, core). }
  Observe folk_saved at yard when at(folk, yard) and broke(long_man) "Merrow stands in the Hall yard in the rain, and looks down the lane at where it lived.".
  // The morning after the third night: the storm passes, and the dale is what the three days made it.
  Relation calm(place).
  Rule storm_passes when watch(clock) >= 432 and storming() says "The rain stops before dawn. The wind drops, and the dale lies under a washed, colourless sky." { Retract storming(). Assert calm(long_man). }
  Observe after_mended at green when calm(long_man) and not broke(long_man) and not drawn(hollow) "The beck runs brown but low between its banks, and nobody on the green is talking about the Long Man. The springs at its foot, people say, have nearly stopped.".
  Observe after_drawn at green when calm(long_man) and drawn(hollow) "Children stand on the dyke looking north, where the roofs of a grey town show above Hollow Water for the first time in a thousand years.".
  Observe after_broken at yard when calm(long_man) and broke(long_man) "Below the Hall the dale is one brown water from the ridge to the willows. The Long Man has a gap in it a hundred yards wide, and the lake is going out through it.".
  // Merrow safe from its wall: the leak shut, by the Mower or by the company; the lake drawn down; or the wall broken
  // with Merrow up the hill. Seen through, it is the company's experience (module.json, placed.json).
  Goal state(leak_gate, mended) or drawn(hollow) or (broke(long_man) and calm(long_man) and not lostToWater(folk)).
}

data/adventures/the-long-man/water.kyr:
Module longman "The Long Man" {
  Description "Hollow Water: the lake behind the Long Man, the Water-House on its island, and the town under it.".

  Place lakeshore "the lakeshore" is room within hollow at 0, 1.
  Place deep "the deep water" is room within hollow at 1, 1.
  Place water_house "the Water-House" is room within hollow at 2, 0.
  Place drowned_street "the drowned street" is room within hollow at 2, 1.
  Place face_house "the face-house" is room within hollow at 3, 1.
  Place last_house "the last house" is room within hollow at 2, 2.

  Passage lake_face "the lake face of the Long Man" is path between crest and lakeshore taking 20 minutes.
  Passage punt_way "out on Hollow Water" is ferry between lakeshore and deep taking 30 minutes.
  Passage island_way "the island landing" is ferry between deep and water_house taking 30 minutes.
  Passage house_steps "the steps below the Water-House" is steps between water_house and drowned_street.
  Passage face_door "a tall narrow door" is doorway between drowned_street and face_house.
  Passage last_door "a barred door" is door between drowned_street and last_house.

  Thing punt "an old punt" on punt_way {
    State beached blocking "An old punt lies drawn up in the reeds, grey with weather, its pole across the thwarts.".
    State afloat "The punt rides at the edge of the reeds.".
    Change launch "Push the punt off the reeds" from beached to afloat needing brawn.
  }
  Observe punt_looked beside punt_way as event when tried(punt, looking) "She is old and grey with weather, but somebody keeps her: her seams are fresh-tarred, and the pole across the thwarts is new ash.".
  Thing steps_water "the water over the steps" on house_steps is scenery {
    State under blocking "Below the Water-House door, steps go down into the lake, and the lake closes over them.".
    State drawn "The steps go down from the Water-House door into a street of grey houses, wet and shining.".
  }

  Observe shore_scene at lakeshore when not drawn(hollow) "Reeds, and black water going away to the hills, so still it holds the sky. The cold comes off it like a cellar's. Far out, a square tower stands up out of the lake on an island no bigger than a barn.".
  Observe shore_drawn at lakeshore when drawn(hollow) "The lake has drawn back from the reeds a long stone's throw, leaving mud, and the stumps of trees older than any in the dale.".
  Observe deep_scene at deep when true "Out on the water the punt pole finds no bottom. The water is cold enough to ache, and too clear: far down, something pale, like a roof.".
  Observe house_scene at water_house when true "One room, square and tall, of the same grey stone as the Long Man. In the middle of the floor stands a wheel of grey stone on an axle as thick as a man, and round the walls, in rows from floor to ceiling, notches.".
  Observe socket_seen at water_house when knows(party, rod_seen) "In the hub of the great wheel is a socket, square, its edges notched in a close pattern: the pattern on the shoe of Gammer Coller's rod." teaches rod_fits.
  Observe street_scene at drowned_street when true "A street of houses of grey stone with their roofs on, silted to the sills and shining with water. The doors are tall and narrow, and over each one a short row of notches, a little higher or lower from door to door, as if each house had measured the water for itself.".
  Observe face_house_scene at face_house when true "A long low room with a kiln at the far end, its mouth stopped with clay. Shelves run the length of both walls, and on them stand moulds of grey clay, each the hollow of a long, smooth face with no eyes.".
  Discovery moulds_read "The keepers' faces were fired here in moulds and set on last. A keeper wakes when it is given its face, and stops when it loses it." {
    Found by searching face_house "In the last mould on the last shelf lies a face already fired: grey, smooth, blind, never fitted to anything. Round the mould's rim runs a count of days in notches, the time it took to make.".
  }
  Item spare_face "a grey face, fired and never fitted" is keeper_mask at face_house hidden until moulds_read.
  Thing last_bar "the bar across the last house's door" on last_door {
    State barred blocking "A bar of black oak lies across the door in iron brackets, on the street side.".
    State lifted "The oak bar leans against the wall beside the open door.".
    Change lift "Lift the bar from the door" from barred to lifted at drowned_street.
  }
  Observe bar_looked beside last_door as event when tried(last_bar, looking) "The oak is black with the water, not with age, and the brackets are on the street side: whoever barred this door meant it to stay shut from outside.".
  Observe last_house_scene at last_house when true "One room. A table is laid for four, with bowls, a jug, and bread gone to grey stone. Nothing has been moved but by the water.".
  Observe tally_seen at last_house when true "Down the door-post runs a tally of days, cut neat and even. It stops at forty-one." teaches last_count.
  Discovery last_count "The last house of the drowned town was barred from outside, with its table laid for a meal. The tally of days on its door-post stops at forty-one, the same count as the last notches in the keeper's niche. The Hesk meant to come back.".
  Thing toy_bell "a child's bell of weirstone" at last_house {
    State still "On the sill sits a child's toy, a little bell of grey weirstone no bigger than a fist.".
    Tries pushing.
  }
  Observe bell_looked near toy_bell when tried(toy_bell, looking) "A little bell of grey weirstone, cut, not cast. Its clapper is a pebble of bronze on a thread of gut gone as hard as wire.".
  Event bell_answered near toy_bell when tried(toy_bell, pushing) "It rings, clear and long. Far off, under the hill, something rings back, once." then {
    Assert rung(toy_bell).
  }
  Relation rung(entity).

  Discovery rod_fits "The square socket in the hub of the Water-House wheel is notched to the pattern of the dyke-reeve's rod: the rod is a key to it.".
  Discovery hesk_known "The words cut round the Water-House wall, read: WE GAVE THE LOW HOUSES TO THE WATER, SO THAT THE FIELDS WOULD BE DRY. WE WILL KEEP THE WALL AS WE KEPT THE HOUSES." {
    Found by searching water_house with lore "The notches round the walls are writing, the writing of the Mower's breastplate. Round and round the room, as near as it can be read: WE GAVE THE LOW HOUSES TO THE WATER, SO THAT THE FIELDS WOULD BE DRY. WE WILL KEEP THE WALL AS WE KEPT THE HOUSES.".
  }
  Discovery town_known "Under Hollow Water stands a town of the people who built the Long Man, drowned by its own builders.".
  Observe street_teaches at drowned_street when true "Whoever lived here walked out of these doors uphill, and let the water in after them." teaches town_known.

  // The master wheel: worked with the rod, it draws the lake down by a man's height in two hours.
  Thing wheel "the great wheel" at water_house {
    State set "The great wheel stands with its square socket uppermost.".
    State turned "The great wheel has been turned its full round; somewhere below, water is going out with a long sigh.".
    Change turn "Set the rod in the socket and turn the great wheel" from set to turned needing sluice_rod.
  }
  Observe wheel_looked near wheel when tried(wheel, looking) "The great wheel is grey as the wall and taller than a man. In its hub is a square socket, its edges notched in a close pattern, made for something that is not here.".
  Measure drawsAt(place).
  Rule draw_begins when state(wheel, turned) and drawsAt(hollow) == 0 { Set drawsAt(hollow) to watch(clock). Increase drawsAt(hollow) by 12. }
  Rule lake_drawn when state(wheel, turned) and drawsAt(hollow) > 0 and watch(clock) >= drawsAt(hollow) and not drawn(hollow)
    says "Hollow Water goes down. It goes down the lake face of the Long Man a man's height, and the beck below the wall goes up the dale brown and roaring." {
    Assert drawn(hollow). Assert state(steps_water, drawn). Assert drowned(low_field). Assert drowned(millhouse).
  }
  Observe mill_drowned at millhouse when drowned(millhouse) "The beck has come in through the millhouse door. The wheel has stopped, jammed with branches, and Hob Teller is standing in his own millpond to the knees.".

  // The Old Jack keeps the deep water.
  Person jack "the Old Jack" at deep {
    Role "a pike as long as the punt". Species great_pike. Level 4.
    Temperament ambush.
    Warns "A shadow longer than the punt turns under the water, slowly, and comes up beneath you. It has seen you see it.".
    Comes "The water opens beside the punt, and the Old Jack comes up out of it with its mouth wide.".
  }

  // What the company is asked, and what it comes to see it must do.
  Objective lay_mower when knows(party, bounty_known) and not paidBounty(venn) and able(mower) and not knows(party, mower_keeps) "Aldous Venn will pay forty crowns for the Mower's mask.".
  Objective keep_wall when knows(party, teeth_taken) and knows(party, wall_known) and not state(leak_gate, mended) and not drawn(hollow) and not broke(long_man) "The Long Man is leaking where its bronze was taken, and the storm is coming.".
  Objective warn_merrow when knows(party, notches_known) and not convinced(ysolt) and not broke(long_man) "If the Long Man goes, the water will come over the chapel roof. Someone should tell Mother Ysolt.".
}

data/adventures/thrume/clocks.kyr:
Module thrume "Thrume" {
  Description "Thrume: a salt town where people pay to sleep, a giants' hold on the ridge, a mountain that is a body, a city that farms dreams, a tomb built to kill, a palace in a sky a thousand years gone, and what lies under every sleep.".

  // The country. The fells are the titan's body; everything but the dream and the Between is inside them or on them.
  Place fells "the Thrume country" is region.
  Place lowroad "the salt road" is wilderness within fells at 0, 3.
  Place saltgrave "Saltgrave" is settlement within fells at 1, 3.
  Place fellside "the fellside" is wilderness within fells at 1, 2.

  // Three clocks run under everything.
  // Thrume's stirring: two now; one more each morning the Margravine's overseer cuts; at six the ground shakes, at
  // ten he wakes.
  Measure stirring(place). Measure nextCut(place). Relation woken(place). Relation shaken(place).
  Initially Set stirring(fells) to 2. Initially Set nextCut(fells) to 144.
  Rule cut_stirs when cutting(brannoc) and watch(clock) >= nextCut(fells) and not woken(fells) {
    Increase stirring(fells) by 1. Set nextCut(fells) to nextCut(fells) + 144.
  }
  Rule ground_shakes when stirring(fells) >= 6 and not shaken(fells)
    says "The ground moves. Not a tremor: a slow, enormous shifting, like a sleeper turning over. Dust comes down from every roof-beam in the country, and then it is still." {
    Assert shaken(fells).
  }
  Rule thrume_wakes when stirring(fells) >= 10 and not woken(fells) and not sealed(fells) and not sungClean(fells)
    says "Thrume wakes. There is a sound under everything, deeper than sound, and then the fells stand up. Rivers run backwards off their shoulders. Somewhere to the south, where the Ebb is, the land is lifted and set down again in another place." {
    Assert woken(fells).
  }

  // Thrume's breath: an hour in, an hour out, for ever. The Lungs, the Room of Three Breaths and the cloud-stair keep
  // its time.
  Relation exhaling(place). Measure nextBreath(place).
  Initially Assert exhaling(fells). Initially Set nextBreath(fells) to 6.
  Rule breath_in when exhaling(fells) and watch(clock) >= nextBreath(fells) { Retract exhaling(fells). Set nextBreath(fells) to watch(clock) + 6. }
  Rule breath_out when not exhaling(fells) and watch(clock) >= nextBreath(fells) { Assert exhaling(fells). Set nextBreath(fells) to watch(clock) + 6. }

  // The host of Harle crosses the Ebb at the start of the tenth day. What stands on the Shoulder road that morning is
  // what the company left there.
  Relation crossed(place).
  Rule harle_crosses when watch(clock) >= 1296 and not crossed(fells) says "Word comes up the salt road at a gallop: the Duke of Harle's host is over the Ebb." { Assert crossed(fells). }

  // How it ends. These hold for ever once true; the epilogue observations below read them.
  Relation sealed(place). Relation sungClean(place). Relation cutOut(place).
  Observe end_woken at market when woken(fells) "Saltgrave is gone. Where the town was, a slope of new scree runs down into a valley that was not there yesterday, and the fells to the north are not where they were. Something vast is walking away into the west, taking its time.".
  Observe end_sung at market when sungClean(fells) and not woken(fells) "The fells are quiet, the right kind of quiet. The red salt in the Salt Office's cellar has gone grey and crumbles at a touch. People who never slept well in Saltgrave sleep now.".
  Observe end_sealed at market when sealed(fells) and not sungClean(fells) "The fells are still. Nobody in Saltgrave sleeps well, and nobody can say why, and the dream-houses stay shut.".
  Observe end_cut at market when cutOut(fells) "The Salt Office is loading wagons of red salt for the river, under guard, day and night. The springs above the town are running low, though it has rained.".
}

