data/goings-on/disputation/situation.kyr:
Module disputation "The disputation on the green" {
  Description "On market days two philosophers dispute on the green, and the town stands round to listen and take sides: one of the One, who teaches that all things are one thing and change is only seeming, and one of the Flow, who teaches that nothing stays. A sophist leans between them, and will argue either side for whoever pays. What the country's own history says would settle it, for whoever has found it.".
  Entity party: group "Your company".
  Place green "The green" is room.
  // The country's own history, for whoever has found it: who the first makers were, by their own marks, which still
  // read after them; how they ended; and the kingdom after them, and how it fell.
  Entity making: fact "Who the first makers were". Entity ending: fact "How the first makers ended".
  Entity successors: fact "The kingdom after them".
  Entity oneness: claim "that all things are one, and change is only seeming".
  Entity flux: claim "that nothing stays, and nothing made outlasts its making".
  Initially Assert refutes(making, flux). Initially Assert refutes(ending, oneness). Initially Assert refutes(successors, oneness).
  Entity dispute: fact "Two philosophers dispute at {green} on market days, one of the One and one of the Flow, and the town takes sides.".
  Initially Assert established(dispute).

  Person one "The philosopher of the One" at green { Role "a philosopher of the One". Peaceable. }
  Person flow "The philosopher of the Flow" at green { Role "a philosopher of the Flow". Peaceable. }
  Person sophist "The sophist" at green { Role "a sophist". Peaceable. }
  Initially Assert believes(one, oneness). Initially Set conviction(one, oneness) to 2. Initially Assert disputant(one).
  Initially Assert believes(flow, flux). Initially Set conviction(flow, flux) to 2. Initially Assert disputant(flow).
  Initially Set hire(one) to 0. Initially Set hire(flow) to 0.
  Relation heard(group). Relation answered(group, entity). Relation glanced(group).
  // A reason told badly is not lost: what the country's history says is still so, and it can be told again the next
  // day (a reason that failed its roll was gone for good: the play-structure investigation's PT-05).
  Relation faltered(group, entity).
  Rule told_again when faltered(?p, ?m) and untilLight(clock) == 1 { Retract faltered(?p, ?m). }
  Entity move_reason: fact "a reason". Entity move_after: fact "the kingdom after". Entity move_argue: fact "an argument".
  Entity move_sophist: fact "the sophist". Entity move_glance: fact "the old stones".

  Observe crowd at green when believes(one, oneness) and believes(flow, flux) "Two philosophers are disputing here, and a crowd stands round them: {one}, who holds that all things are one and change is only seeming, and {flow}, who holds that nothing stays. {sophist} leans between them with folded arms, and laughs at both.".
  Observe one_beaten at green when doubts(one, oneness) and not reasoned(one, oneness) "The crowd has gone over from {one} today, and laughs when {one} tries to speak.".
  Observe flow_beaten at green when doubts(flow, flux) and not reasoned(flow, flux) "The crowd has gone over from {flow} today, and laughs when {flow} tries to speak.".
  Observe one_recanted at green when reasoned(one, oneness) and doubts(one, oneness) "{one} no longer teaches the One: things end, {one} tells whoever will listen, and the end of them is not seeming.".
  Observe flow_recanted at green when reasoned(flow, flux) and doubts(flow, flux) "{flow} no longer teaches the Flow: some things stay, {flow} tells whoever will listen, longer than the hands that made them.".
  Observe one_cold near one when scorns(one, party) "{one} turns away from you.".
  Observe flow_cold near flow when scorns(flow, party) "{flow} turns away from you.".
  // Someone in the company who reads people sees it without being asked (a passive check: no roll): the philosopher
  // of the Flow keeps looking at the oldest stones in the town while saying that nothing stays.
  Entity glance: fact "The philosopher of the Flow looks at the oldest stones in the town every time the Flow is taught.".
  Initially Assert refutes(glance, flux).
  Observe flow_looks at green as sign when capable(party, insight) and believes(flow, flux) and not knows(party, glance) "Watching {flow} argue, you see where {flow}'s eyes go at each 'nothing stays': to the oldest stones in the town, which were old when the town was new." teaches glance.

  Topic one_doctrine with one "Ask {one} what the One is" when true once {
    Says "'There is one thing,' says {one}, 'and it does not change. The river, the hill, you and I and the dead: one thing, seen in pieces by eyes that see in pieces. What seems to end does not end. Nothing is lost, because nothing is apart.' The crowd murmurs; some of them nod.".
    On discuss { Assert heard(one). }
  }
  Topic flow_doctrine with flow "Ask {flow} what the Flow is" when true once {
    Says "'Nothing stays,' says {flow}. 'Not the river, not the hill, not the stones you stand on. What is made is unmade in the making; your house is already falling down. Hold on to nothing, and nothing will be taken from you.' The other half of the crowd laughs and claps.".
    On discuss { Assert heard(flow). }
  }
  Topic sophist_holds with sophist "Ask {sophist} what a sophist holds" when true once {
    Says "'Nothing at all,' says {sophist}, cheerfully. 'The truth is whatever is left standing when the arguing stops, and I can see to it that it is yours. Two coin, and I will argue either of them into the ground.'".
  }

  // A reason shakes a philosopher, and does not turn one: each has an answer to it, and lets the claim go only when
  // that answer is met in turn, or another reason is put. Whoever is shaken can no longer be argued down or bought
  // off: the dispute has become a real one. The follow-up independent review saw one example convert a philosopher
  // and finish the dispute.
  Relation gave(group, entity).
  Entity move_meaning: fact "whose words". Entity move_going: fact "which goes first".
  Entity move_lost: fact "what was lost". Entity move_names: fact "the names".

  // Against the Flow: the makers' own marks, which still read though the makers are long gone.
  Action answer_flow(actor: group, site: place) "Answer {flow} with the makers' own marks, which still read though they are gone" {
    Speaker flow. Time 5 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(flow, site) and heard(flow) and believes(flow, flux)
      and not scorns(flow, actor) and not answered(flow, move_reason) and not faltered(flow, move_reason) and knows(actor, making).
    Resolve check(actor, lore, dc_easy).
    On success { Assert answered(flow, move_reason). Assert gave(flow, move_reason). Decrease conviction(flow, flux) by 1. Assert reasoned(flow, flux). }
    On failure { Assert faltered(flow, move_reason). }
    Result "You tell {flow} what the first makers cut in their stones, and that it still reads, when no one alive has seen a maker. {flow} is quiet a long time, and the crowd with {flow}.".
    Otherwise "You tell {flow} of the makers' marks, but you tell it badly, and {flow} turns it into a joke about stones that the crowd likes better. The marks say what they say: another day, you might tell it better.".
  }
  Observe flow_grants_stones at green when believes(flow, flux) and gave(flow, move_reason) "{flow} has granted you the stones, and not what was meant by them. 'That went with the hands that cut them,' {flow} tells the crowd. 'What you read in old scratches is your own.'".
  Action answer_flow_meaning(actor: group, site: place) "Read {flow} the makers' marks as they stand, and ask whose words they are" {
    Speaker flow. Time 5 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(flow, site) and believes(flow, flux) and gave(flow, move_reason)
      and not scorns(flow, actor) and not answered(flow, move_meaning) and not faltered(flow, move_meaning) and knows(actor, making).
    Resolve check(actor, lore, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert answered(flow, move_meaning). Decrease conviction(flow, flux) by 1. }
    On failure { Assert faltered(flow, move_meaning). }
    Result "You give the crowd the marks as they stand, the makers' own name for themselves and the order they put things in, and nothing of yours in it. {flow} hears them through. 'Not yours,' {flow} says. 'Theirs. Then what they meant has stayed as well.'".
    Otherwise "What you remember of the marks comes out in your own words, and {flow} only nods: 'You see? Yours.' The crowd laughs. Another day, with the marks fresher in mind, you might read them better.".
  }
  Action answer_flow_glance(actor: group, site: place) "Ask {flow} why the old stones draw the eye of one who says that nothing stays" {
    Speaker flow. Time 5 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(flow, site) and heard(flow) and believes(flow, flux)
      and not scorns(flow, actor) and not answered(flow, move_glance) and not faltered(flow, move_glance) and knows(actor, glance).
    Resolve check(actor, insight, dc_easy).
    On success { Assert answered(flow, move_glance). Assert gave(flow, move_glance). Decrease conviction(flow, flux) by 1. Assert reasoned(flow, flux). }
    On failure { Assert faltered(flow, move_glance). }
    Result "{flow} looks at the shrine's stones, and then at you. 'Because they are still there,' {flow} says. 'I have looked at them every market day for twenty years, and said that nothing stays.'".
    Otherwise "{flow} only smiles. 'I look at them,' {flow} says, 'to see them going.' The crowd likes it. You saw what you saw: another day, you might put it better.".
  }
  Observe flow_holds_going at green when believes(flow, flux) and gave(flow, move_glance) "{flow} has owned to looking at the old stones, and says now that it is to watch them go: 'Look at the weather on them. Slowly is still going.'".
  Action answer_flow_going(actor: group, site: place) "Ask {flow} which will go first, the town or its old stones" {
    Speaker flow. Time 5 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(flow, site) and believes(flow, flux) and gave(flow, move_glance)
      and not scorns(flow, actor) and not answered(flow, move_going).
    Resolve check(actor, insight, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert answered(flow, move_going). Decrease conviction(flow, flux) by 1. }
    On failure { Assert answered(flow, move_going). }
    Result "'The town,' says {flow}, too quickly. 'The town, and me, and everyone here. They will still be standing.' {flow} looks at the stones a long while.".
    Otherwise "'Both,' says {flow} easily, 'each in its time,' and the crowd is satisfied.".
  }
  Event flow_comes_round near flow when doubts(flow, flux) and reasoned(flow, flux) "{flow} is quiet a long while, and then says it to the crowd, loud enough for all of them to hear: 'I have taught wrong.' Afterwards {flow} comes to you: 'If you are going where the old words are, I would read them with you.'" then {
    Assert willing(flow, party).
  }
  // Against the One: how the first makers ended, and the kingdom after them, which also ended.
  Action answer_one(actor: group, site: place) "Tell {one} how the first makers ended" {
    Speaker one. Time 5 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(one, site) and heard(one) and believes(one, oneness)
      and not scorns(one, actor) and not answered(one, move_reason) and not faltered(one, move_reason) and knows(actor, ending).
    Resolve check(actor, lore, dc_easy).
    On success { Assert answered(one, move_reason). Assert gave(one, move_reason). Decrease conviction(one, oneness) by 1. Assert reasoned(one, oneness). }
    On failure { Assert faltered(one, move_reason). }
    Result "You tell {one} how the first makers ended, as their own stones tell it. {one} listens to the end, and the crowd with {one}. 'A people,' {one} says, 'and then not.'".
    Otherwise "You tell {one} how the makers ended, but {one} hears it out and smiles: 'They are here still, in the One, as you are.' The crowd nods along. It is still how they ended: another day, you might tell it better.".
  }
  Observe one_holds_wave at green when believes(one, oneness) and gave(one, move_reason) "{one} has granted that the makers ended, and not that anything ended with them. 'A wave goes back into the sea,' {one} tells the crowd. 'You have told me that they ended. You have not told me that anything was lost.'".
  Action answer_one_lost(actor: group, site: place) "Ask {one} why the makers cut their own end in stone, if nothing was lost" {
    Speaker one. Time 5 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(one, site) and believes(one, oneness) and gave(one, move_reason)
      and not scorns(one, actor) and not answered(one, move_lost) and not faltered(one, move_lost) and knows(actor, ending).
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert answered(one, move_lost). Decrease conviction(one, oneness) by 1. }
    On failure { Assert faltered(one, move_lost). }
    Result "'Because they were there,' you say, 'and did not think it seeming.' {one} starts to answer, and stops. 'They grieved,' {one} says at last. 'Nobody grieves a wave.'".
    Otherwise "'To show us what seeming looks like,' says {one}, gently, and the crowd nods. Another day, you might find the words.".
  }
  Action answer_one_after(actor: group, site: place) "Tell {one} of the kingdom that came after the makers, and how it fell" {
    Speaker one. Time 5 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(one, site) and heard(one) and believes(one, oneness)
      and not scorns(one, actor) and not answered(one, move_after) and not faltered(one, move_after) and knows(actor, successors).
    Resolve check(actor, lore, dc_easy).
    On success { Assert answered(one, move_after). Assert gave(one, move_after). Decrease conviction(one, oneness) by 1. Assert reasoned(one, oneness). }
    On failure { Assert faltered(one, move_after). }
    Result "You tell {one} of the kingdom that came after the makers, what it was and how it fell, with the names in it. 'Twice, then,' {one} says. 'Twice in this one country, a whole people ended.'".
    Otherwise "{one} lets you finish. 'Kingdoms are seeming,' {one} says, 'like the clouds,' and the crowd is with {one} again. The kingdom fell all the same: another day, you might tell it better.".
  }
  Observe one_holds_breath at green when believes(one, oneness) and gave(one, move_after) "{one} has heard the kingdom out, and says now that it was once, seen twice: 'Peoples come and go as the breath goes in and out. The breathing is one.'".
  Action answer_one_names(actor: group, site: place) "Ask {one} to say the fallen kingdom's names to the crowd, and tell it they are here still" {
    Speaker one. Time 5 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(one, site) and believes(one, oneness) and gave(one, move_after)
      and not scorns(one, actor) and not answered(one, move_names).
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert answered(one, move_names). Decrease conviction(one, oneness) by 1. }
    On failure { Assert answered(one, move_names). }
    Result "{one} begins, and stops at the second name. Nobody in the crowd knows it. 'They are not here,' {one} says quietly. 'Nobody here has ever heard of them.'".
    Otherwise "{one} says the names, calm as a prayer, and the crowd hears them as a prayer.".
  }
  Event one_comes_round near one when doubts(one, oneness) and reasoned(one, oneness) "{one} sits down heavily. 'I will have to think again from the beginning,' {one} says. Then, to you: 'You know where the old things are. Let me come with you, and see them end for myself.'" then {
    Assert willing(one, party).
  }
  // Argument without a reason: it wins the day and is gone by morning, and is not forgiven.
  Action argue_flow(actor: group, site: place) "Argue {flow} down: some things stay" {
    Speaker flow. Time 5 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(flow, site) and heard(flow) and believes(flow, flux)
      and not scorns(flow, actor) and not answered(flow, move_argue)
      and not reasoned(flow, flux).
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert answered(flow, move_argue). Decrease conviction(flow, flux) by 2. Assert swayedBy(flow, flux, actor). }
    On failure { Assert answered(flow, move_argue). }
    Result "You turn {flow}'s own words on {flow}, faster than {flow} can answer, until the crowd is laughing and {flow} has nothing to say. It is a victory. It is not a reason.".
    Otherwise "{flow} lets you talk yourself out, and then says one thing, and the crowd laughs at you instead.".
  }
  Action argue_one(actor: group, site: place) "Argue {one} down: things change" {
    Speaker one. Time 5 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(one, site) and heard(one) and believes(one, oneness)
      and not scorns(one, actor) and not answered(one, move_argue)
      and not reasoned(one, oneness).
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert answered(one, move_argue). Decrease conviction(one, oneness) by 2. Assert swayedBy(one, oneness, actor). }
    On failure { Assert answered(one, move_argue). }
    Result "You tie {one} in {one}'s own knots, one after another, until the crowd is jeering and {one} stops trying to answer. It is a victory. It is not a reason.".
    Otherwise "{one} answers every point with the same calm, and the crowd tires of you first.".
  }
  // The sophist argues for whoever pays: the day is won, and nothing else.
  Action hire_sophist_flow(actor: group, site: place) "Pay {sophist} two coin to argue {flow} into the ground" {
    Speaker sophist. Time 10 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(sophist, site) and at(flow, site) and heard(flow)
      and believes(flow, flux) and not scorns(flow, actor) and not answered(flow, move_sophist) and not reasoned(flow, flux)
      and quantity(actor, gold) >= 2.
    On success { Assert answered(flow, move_sophist). Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 2. Increase quantity(sophist, gold) by 2.
      Decrease conviction(flow, flux) by 2. Assert swayedBy(flow, flux, actor). }
    Result "{sophist} pockets the coin, steps up beside {flow}, and takes {flow} apart in a quarter of an hour, cheerfully, to the delight of the green. Then {sophist} winks at you. 'By tomorrow,' {sophist} says, 'it will all be believed again. It always is.'".
  }
  Action hire_sophist_one(actor: group, site: place) "Pay {sophist} two coin to argue {one} into the ground" {
    Speaker sophist. Time 10 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(sophist, site) and at(one, site) and heard(one)
      and believes(one, oneness) and not scorns(one, actor) and not answered(one, move_sophist) and not reasoned(one, oneness)
      and quantity(actor, gold) >= 2.
    On success { Assert answered(one, move_sophist). Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 2. Increase quantity(sophist, gold) by 2.
      Decrease conviction(one, oneness) by 2. Assert swayedBy(one, oneness, actor). }
    Result "{sophist} pockets the coin, steps up beside {one}, and takes {one} apart in a quarter of an hour, cheerfully, to the delight of the green. Then {sophist} winks at you. 'By tomorrow,' {sophist} says, 'it will all be believed again. It always is.'".
  }

  // Unfinished until it is settled (arguing one down for the day had taken it out of the company's notes: the
  // play-structure investigation's PT-25); and said so when neither will hear the company.
  Query disputeSettled() means (reasoned(one, oneness) and doubts(one, oneness)) or (reasoned(flow, flux) and doubts(flow, flux)).
  Query shunned() means scorns(one, party) and scorns(flow, party).
  Objective disputed when knows(party, dispute) and not disputeSettled() and not shunned() "Two philosophers dispute at {green}: the One against the Flow. What the country's own history says could settle it.".
  Objective disputed_shut when knows(party, dispute) and not disputeSettled() and shunned() "Neither philosopher at {green} will hear you now: you had them argued down without a reason, and it is not forgiven.".
  Goal (reasoned(one, oneness) and doubts(one, oneness)) or (reasoned(flow, flux) and doubts(flow, flux)).
}

data/goings-on/drover/oxen/situation.kyr:
Module oxen "The thing that took the oxen" {
  Description "Whatever had the drover's oxen dragged them off from the ditch to a den in the wild. The trail is there to be read from the road, the son wants to see the end of it, and the yoke was his grandfather's.".
  Entity party: group "Your company".
  Place road "The road" is room.
  Place lair "The den" is room. Entity track: passage "The track to the den".
  Entity wife: group "The drover's wife". Entity son: group "The drover's son". Entity beasts: group "the beasts".
  Entity found_cart: fact "The drover's cart went off the road in the night.".
  // The trail from the ditch to the den nearest the drover's town (see the drover's scenario), told by the son, who
  // read it, once the cart is found; and a way there for whoever has heard it.
  Entity trail: fact "From the ditch below {road}, two furrows and a line of great prints go up the bank and away toward {lair}.".
  Initially Assert leadsTo(trail, lair). Initially Assert leadsVia(trail, track).
  Initially Assert revealedBy(track, trail).
  // Dealt with as the den is: dead, or driven off or laid to rest.
  Query dealt() means dead(beasts) or peaceable(beasts).
  Topic son_after with son "Ask {son} what he means to do now" when knows(actor, found_cart) and not dealt() once {
    Says "'Whatever took them is up at {lair},' says {son}. 'I saw the marks from the ditch: two furrows, and prints too big for any dog.' He turns the spear in his hands. 'I want to see it. And I want the yoke back. It was Grandfather's.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, trail). }
  }
  Objective oxen when knows(party, trail) and not dealt() "Whatever took the drover's oxen dens at {lair}.".
  // The yoke, among the bones once the den is dealt with; carried home, it hangs over the hearth where it always hung.
  Kind ox_yoke "an ox-yoke" is treasure worth 2 weighing 8 described "An old ox-yoke of ash, carved along the bow with oak leaves, and worn smooth where the necks went.".
  Entity yoke_seen: fact "The drover's ox-yoke lies among the bones at {lair}.".
  Item yoke "the drover's ox-yoke" is ox_yoke at lair hidden until yoke_seen.
  Observe yoke_glimpse at lair when dealt() and not knows(party, yoke_seen) "Among the bones at the back an ox-yoke lies where it was dragged, carved along the bow with oak leaves." teaches yoke_seen.
  Relation hung(group).
  Event yoke_seen_home near wife when carries(party, yoke) and not hung(party) "{wife} sees it before you say anything, and puts down what is in her hands. 'You brought it back,' she says. 'Hang it where it was.'".
  Action hang_yoke(actor: group, carrier: member, site: place) "Hang the yoke over the hearth, where it always hung" {
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(wife, site) and memberOf(carrier, actor) and ownedItem(yoke, carrier)
      and not hung(actor).
    Time 2 minutes.
    Resolve drop(yoke, carrier).
    On success { Assert at(yoke, site). Assert hung(actor). }
    Result "It goes up on its two pegs over the hearth as if it had never been down. {wife} looks at it a long time, and does not say anything else, and does not need to.".
  }
  Goal hung(party).
}

data/goings-on/drover/situation.kyr:
Module drover "The drover who did not come home" {
  Description "A drover went out on the road three days ago with a cart and two oxen and did not come home. His dog did, alone, in the night. His wife cooks at the inn and will not talk about it; his son talks of nothing else.".
  Entity party: group "Your company".
  Place green "The green" is room.
  Place taproom "The taproom" is room.
  Place road "The road" is room.
  Relation told(group). Relation gone(group).
  Entity missing: fact "A drover went out on the road from {green} three days ago and did not come home. His dog did.".
  Initially Assert established(missing). Initially Assert staged(road, missing).

  Person wife "The drover's wife" at taproom { Role "the drover's wife, who cooks at the inn". Pronouns she. Peaceable. }
  Person son "The drover's son" at green { Role "the drover's son, who wants to go after his father". Pronouns he. Peaceable. }
  // The dog that came home: a real dog, lame in the off forefoot, who lets anyone who is kind to her look at her; and
  // whoever does sees where she has been.
  Person dog "the grey dog" at green { Role "the drover's dog". Species dog. Pronouns she. Peaceable. }
  Observe dog_waits near dog of dog when not told(wife) and at(dog, green) "A grey dog lies by the door of {taproom} with her head on her paws, watching the road. She holds one forefoot off the ground.".
  Observe dog_in near dog of dog when told(wife) and at(dog, taproom) "The grey dog lies by the kitchen fire with her chin on her paws.".
  Rule dog_goes_in when told(wife) and at(dog, green) { Assert at(dog, taproom). }
  Entity dog_mud: fact "The grey dog came home caked in black ditch-mud, the off forefoot cut as if on iron.".
  Observe dog_tells near dog as sign when petted(dog, party) and not knows(party, dog_mud) "Under your hand her coat is stiff with dried black mud to the belly: ditch-mud, not road dust, as if she had lain a long time somewhere low and wet. The pad of the off forefoot is cut clean across, the way iron cuts." teaches dog_mud.
  Observe dog_muddy near dog of dog as sign when knows(party, dog_mud) and not knows(party, found_cart) "Her coat is stiff with black ditch-mud to the belly.".
  // The ruts the road speaks of are a thing to follow, not only to search for: the cart was found only by the
  // generic "Search here" (the play-structure investigation's PT-08).
  Thing ruts "the fresh ruts" at road {
    State fresh "Fresh ruts run off the edge of the road here, where the bank drops away.".
    State followed "The ruts go over the edge of the road and down the bank, to the ditch.".
    Change follow "Follow the ruts over the edge" from fresh to followed.
  }
  Rule ruts_followed when state(ruts, followed) and not knows(party, found_cart) says "Below the road, where the bank drops away, a cart lies on its side in the ditch with a man under it, a day or more dead. The oxen are gone; something had them, and dragged them off toward the hills." teaches found_cart { }
  Rule ruts_read when knows(party, found_cart) and state(ruts, fresh) { Assert state(ruts, followed). }

  Discovery found_cart "The drover's cart went off the road in the night. He is under it, a day or more dead, and whatever had the oxen dragged them off toward the hills." {
    Found by searching road "Below the road, where the bank drops away, a cart lies on its side in the ditch with a man under it, a day or more dead. The oxen are gone; something had them, and dragged them off toward the hills.".
  }
  // To the drover's own child the man under the cart is their father, known before the face is (the M16 free play
  // found him "a man" to his child, in the words a stranger would find him in). Seen once: what it teaches is a mark
  // with no words, never told as something known.
  Entity father_known: fact "".
  Observe father_seen at road as event when kin(party, wife) and knows(party, found_cart) and not knows(party, father_known) "It is your father. You know the coat first, and the hands, before you will let yourself know the face." teaches father_known.
  Item knife "a drover's knife with a horn handle" is dagger at road hidden until found_cart.
  // Said while it is so: taken, the knife is no longer in his belt (the follow-up review took it and it stayed).
  Observe knife_belt at road when knows(party, found_cart) and at(knife, road) and not buried(party) and not fetched(party) "His knife is still in his belt.".

  // What becomes of him is the company's to choose, and the family's to hear: covered where he lies, for the village
  // to fetch home in the morning, or buried by the road with the words said; and either way somewhere to stand a
  // while, later (the follow-up review found nothing to do for him but read that he was there).
  Relation covered(group). Relation buried(group). Relation fetched(group). Relation stood(group).
  Action cover_drover(actor: group, site: place) "Cover him with the cart's sheet, and stand his whip up to mark the place" {
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, road) and knows(actor, found_cart) and not covered(actor)
      and not buried(actor).
    Time 10 minutes.
    On success { Assert covered(actor). }
    Result "You get the sheet off the load and over him, and weigh its corners down with stones, and stand his whip up in the bank where anyone coming along the road will see it.".
  }
  Action bury_drover(actor: group, site: place) "Bury him by the road, and say the words over him" {
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, road) and knows(actor, found_cart) and not buried(actor)
      and not fetched(actor).
    Time 120 minutes.
    On success { Assert buried(actor). Retract covered(actor). }
    Result "It takes the best part of two hours, with what you have to dig with. You lay him in the bank above the ditch, facing the road, and heap the ditch-stones over him, and say what words you have.".
  }
  Observe drover_covered at road when covered(party) and not fetched(party) "The cart's sheet lies over him, weighted with stones, and his whip stands up in the bank.".
  Observe drover_cairn at road when buried(party) "Above the ditch a cairn of ditch-stones stands new by the road, facing it.".
  Observe knife_cairn at road when buried(party) and at(knife, road) "His knife lies on the cairn: nobody could bring themselves to bury it, or to take it.".
  // Told, the wife says what will be done: fetched home in the morning, or let lie where he is.
  Event wife_will_fetch near wife when told(wife) and covered(party) "'You covered him,' she says. 'Then we will go for him in the morning, with the reed-cutters' cart, and bring him home.'".
  Event wife_hears_cairn near wife when told(wife) and buried(party) "'You buried him,' she says. 'By the road?' She is quiet a while. 'He would like that. He could never stand to be under a roof.'".
  Rule drover_fetched when told(wife) and covered(party) and not buried(party) and untilLight(clock) == 1 {
    Assert fetched(party).
  }
  Observe drover_grave at green when fetched(party) "At the edge of {green} there is a new grave, with a drover's whip laid along it.".
  Action stand_at_grave(actor: group, site: place) "Stand a while at the grave" {
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and told(wife) and not stood(actor)
      and ((buried(actor) and at(actor, road)) or (fetched(actor) and at(actor, green))).
    Time 10 minutes.
    On success { Assert stood(actor). }
    Result "You stand a while. Nobody says anything, and nothing needs saying.".
  }
  Event son_at_grave near party when stood(party) and travelsWith(son, party) and awake(member_son_person) "'Somebody should sing him something terrible,' says {son}. Nobody does; but you all think of it, and it helps.".

  // To one of the family the drover is a father, his wife a mother, his son a brother: they say other things.
  Observe wife_kin near wife when kin(party, wife) and not told(wife) "Your mother is at the hearth with her back to the room.".
  Observe son_kin near son when kin(party, son) and not told(son) and at(son, green) "Your brother is sitting on a rail with your father's old spear across his knees, watching the road. He is taller by a head than when you went away.".
  Observe son_kin_in near son when kin(party, son) and not told(son) and at(son, taproom) "Your brother sits by the kitchen fire with your father's old spear across his knees, not drinking. He is taller by a head than when you went away.".
  // Until he has somewhere to go, the son keeps the green by day and comes in to his mother after dark.
  Rule son_goes_in when dark() and at(son, green) and not willing(son, party) { Assert at(son, taproom). }
  Rule son_comes_out when not dark() and at(son, taproom) and not willing(son, party) { Assert at(son, green). }
  Observe son_kin_ready near son when kin(party, son) and told(son) and not knows(party, found_cart) "Your brother is waiting by the rail with the spear, ready when you are.".
  Observe wife_kin_told near wife when kin(party, wife) and told(wife) "Your mother is at the hearth, at her work, and looks up now and then at the door.".
  Topic wife_where with wife "Ask your mother where he was going" when kin(actor, wife) and not told(wife) once {
    Says "'Out on {road}, with the salt for the reed-cutters,' says your mother, and keeps her eyes on the pot. 'Three days there and back, the way he goes. The dog came home on the fourth, lame in the off foot.' She wipes her hands, though they are dry. 'Nobody will go and look. I am glad you came.'".
  }
  Topic wife_told_kin with wife "Tell your mother what you found on the road" when knows(actor, found_cart) and kin(actor, wife) and not told(wife) once {
    Says "Your mother does not sit down. She takes your face in her hands and looks at it for a long time. 'I knew,' she says. 'The dog knew.' Then she goes back to the pot, because there are people to feed.".
    On discuss { Assert told(wife). }
  }
  Topic son_plan with son "Ask {son} what he means to do" when kin(actor, son) and not knows(actor, found_cart) and not told(son) once {
    Says "'Go after him,' says {son}. 'Mother says wait. I have waited three days.' He looks at you, and at the road. 'If you are going, I am coming with you. If you are not, I am going anyway.'".
    On discuss { Assert willing(son, actor). Assert told(son). }
  }
  // Not to one who knelt by the cart himself: he was there.
  Topic son_found_kin with son "Tell {son} what you found" when knows(actor, found_cart) and kin(actor, son)
    and not knows(actor, son_knelt) once {
    Says "{son} hears it out, and is quiet for a long time. 'Then whatever had the oxen is still out there,' he says. 'I want to see it.'".
    On discuss { Assert willing(son, actor). Assert told(son). }
  }
  Topic wife_husband with wife "Ask {wife} about her husband" when not told(wife) and not kin(actor, wife) once {
    Says "'He went out with the cart three days back,' says {wife}, and keeps her eyes on the pot. 'The dog came home. He didn't.'".
  }
  Topic wife_told with wife "Tell {wife} what you found on the road" when knows(actor, found_cart) and not told(wife) and not kin(actor, wife) once {
    Says "{wife} puts down the ladle and sits. After a while she says, 'I knew. The dog knew.' She takes coin from her apron and puts it in your hand without counting it. 'For going.'".
    On discuss { Assert told(wife). Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 6. }
  }
  Topic wife_knife with wife "Show {wife} her husband's knife" when carries(actor, knife) and told(wife) once {
    Says "She turns the knife over in her hands, and gives it back. 'Keep it. He would want it used, not hung on a wall.'".
  }
  Topic son_father with son "Ask {son} about his father" when not knows(actor, found_cart) and not kin(actor, son) once {
    Says "'Three days,' says {son}. 'Mother says wait. I have waited.' He looks at the road. 'If you are going that way, I will come.'".
  }
  Topic son_found with son "Tell {son} what you found" when knows(actor, found_cart) and not kin(actor, son)
    and not knows(actor, son_knelt) once {
    Says "{son} hears it out. 'Then whatever had the oxen is still out there,' he says. 'I am coming with you. No hire. I want to see it.'".
    On discuss { Assert willing(son, actor). Assert told(son). }
  }
  // Once he has come with you, the son talks on the way: he knows the road his father took, and the cart.
  Topic son_road with son travelling "Ask {son} about the road your father took" when kin(actor, son) and awake(member_son_person) and not knows(actor, found_cart) once {
    Says "'{road}, to market. He knew every rut of it.' {son} kicks at a stone. 'He had the left wheel out of true all spring and would not see to it. If the cart went off the road, look for where a wheel like that would take it.'".
  }
  Topic son_road_stranger with son travelling "Ask {son} about the road his father took" when not kin(actor, son) and awake(member_son_person) and not knows(actor, found_cart) once {
    Says "'{road}, to market,' says {son}. 'He knew it in the dark. The left wheel of the cart was out of true. If it went off the road, that is why.'".
  }
  Topic son_night with son travelling "Sit up late with {son}" when awake(member_son_person) and dark() once {
    Says "'He used to sing to the oxen,' says {son}. 'Terrible songs. He made them up as he went, and they liked them better than anything.' He is quiet a while. 'Mother would not have him sing in the house.'".
  }
  Event son_wheel at road when travelsWith(son, party) and awake(member_son_person) and at(party, road) and not knows(party, found_cart) "{son} stops where the ruts go off the road and stands looking at them. 'That is the left wheel,' he says. 'That is his.'".
  // He kneels there once, before the company's eyes: something seen, not something learned, so what it teaches has no
  // words (the M16 free play found his kneeling filed among what it knew).
  Entity son_knelt: fact "".
  Observe son_kneels at road as event when travelsWith(son, party) and awake(member_son_person) and knows(party, found_cart) and not knows(party, son_knelt) "{son} goes down the bank to the cart before anyone can stop him, and kneels there a long time. When he comes back up he has nothing to say, and nobody asks him to." teaches son_knelt.
  // On the road with you he is himself, after the cart as before it: what he makes of where you take him, what he
  // remembers, and who he sits with (M16's deepening asked for one companion with a perspective, a memory and people
  // of his own). Said where the company is: one who has joined it stands nowhere of his own (his words at the grave,
  // said where he stood, were never heard while he went with you).
  Event son_under near party when travelsWith(son, party) and awake(member_son_person) and at(party, ?p) and unlit(?p) and not benighted(party) "{son} keeps to the middle of the light and does not look behind him. 'Father would never go under a roof he could not see the end of,' he says. 'I used to think it was because he was a coward. I think now it was because he had sense.'".
  Event son_binds near party when travelsWith(son, party) and awake(member_son_person) and memberOf(?m, party) and needsCare(?m) and not joinedAs(?m, son) "{son} binds the hurt fast and badly, the way Father bound the oxen when they went lame. 'Hold still,' he says, in Father's voice, and then stops, surprised at himself.".
  Event son_purse near party when travelsWith(son, party) and awake(member_son_person) and quantity(party, gold) >= 60 "{son} weighs the purse in his hand. 'More than Father had in a year of droves,' he says. 'Mother is not to know how we came by it.' He thinks. 'Or she is, and we will not tell her.'".
  Event son_with_mother near party when travelsWith(son, party) and awake(member_son_person) and told(wife) and at(party, taproom) and at(wife, taproom) and kin(party, son) "{son} sits down by your mother without a word, and she puts a hand on his arm without looking at him. That is all either of them will say about it, tonight.".
  Event son_and_fellow near party when travelsWith(son, party) and awake(member_son_person) and travelsWith(?f, party) and distinct(?f, son) "{son} watches {?f} a while, when {?f} is not looking. 'Father would have liked {?f},' he says. 'He would have said so twice, and then given {?f} the worst ox.'".
  Topic son_after with son travelling "Ask {son} what he will do now" when kin(actor, son) and awake(member_son_person) and knows(actor, found_cart) once {
    Says "'Take Father's road to market, I suppose,' says {son}, 'if anything comes back of the oxen. Somebody has to.' He looks along the road a while. 'You will go back over the hills.' He does not ask you to stay, which is how you know he wants you to.".
  }
  Topic son_after_stranger with son travelling "Ask {son} what he will do now" when not kin(actor, son) and awake(member_son_person) and knows(actor, found_cart) once {
    Says "'See Mother right,' says {son}. 'Then I don't know. Father would have known.' He shoulders the spear. 'Till then I'm with you, if you'll have me.'".
  }
  Topic son_home with son travelling "Ask {son} about home" when kin(actor, son) and awake(member_son_person) once {
    Says "'You remember the flood year?' says {son}. 'You carried me over the ford on your back and told me there were eels in it the size of oxen. I did not go near water again until I was ten.' He grins for the first time. 'There were not, were there.'".
  }
  // Left alone too long, the son goes out after his father himself.
  Rule son_goes at green when watch(clock) >= 204 and not told(son) and at(son, green) says "{son} has taken his father's old spear and gone out on the road alone. Nobody stopped him." { Retract at(son, green). Assert gone(son). }

  Objective road when knows(party, missing) and not knows(party, found_cart) and not kin(party, wife) "A drover from {green} went out on the road and did not come home.".
  Objective tell when knows(party, found_cart) and not told(wife) and not kin(party, wife) "The drover's wife, at the inn, does not know what you found.".
  Objective road_kin when kin(party, wife) and not knows(party, found_cart) "Your father went out on {road} with the cart, and did not come home.".
  Objective tell_kin when kin(party, wife) and knows(party, found_cart) and not told(wife) "Your mother, at the inn, does not know what you found.".
  Goal told(wife).
}

