data/goings-on/players/situation.kyr:
Module players "The players on the green" {
  Description "A company of travelling players, on their way west over the march to the Trial of the Wheel at Pentrice, is stuck in a town on the west road: their chain-man has gone off with the takings, and whoever keeps travellers here has chained their wagon to a post until the reckoning is paid.".
  Entity party: group "Your company".
  Place town "The town" is settlement.
  Place green "The green" is room.
  Entity keeper: group "Whoever keeps travellers".
  Entity priest: group "Whoever keeps the god".
  Entity trader: group "Whoever sells".

  // ── What can be known, and what the country over the march will read ────────────────────────────────────────────
  Entity on_green: fact "A company of players, Gosse's Company, is stuck at {town} on its way west to the Trial of the Wheel at Pentrice: their chain-man went off with the hat, and {keeper} has chained their wagon until the reckoning is paid.".
  Initially Assert established(on_green).
  Entity joined: fact "You have taken service with Gosse's Company for the season: a share of the house, and the honour of the profession. They go on ahead of you to Pentrice, over the march west, to the Painted Moon by the Westgate.".
  Entity seen_show: fact "You have seen Gosse's Company play The Shepherd's Revenge in {town}.".
  Entity freed: fact "You got the players' wagon off the chain in {town}, on their way west to Pentrice.".
  Entity lem_kept: fact "Lem Coyle, the players' chain-man, was paid what he was owed, and has gone west to see the Trial.".
  Initially Assert established(joined). Initially Assert established(seen_show). Initially Assert established(lem_kept). Initially Assert established(freed).

  Relation stuck(group). Relation reckoned(group). Relation gone(group). Relation hatHome(group). Relation lemPaid(group).
  Relation lemSent(group). Relation hatRound(group). Relation showPlayed(group).
  Initially Assert stuck(gosse).

  // ── The players ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person gosse "Absalom Gosse" at green {
    Role "the actor-manager of Gosse's Company". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner jovial.
    Greets "A big old man in a coat that was crimson once rises from the wagon's tail-board with his hand on his heart, as if you were the Margrave. 'A face from the world,' he says, in a voice that would carry to the back of a field. 'Absalom Gosse, of Gosse's Company, at your service and very much at your mercy.'".
    Wants players_hat.
  }
  Person hepzibah "Hepzibah Dimmock" at green {
    Role "the players' prompter". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner stoic.
    Greets "A small grey woman sits on the tail-board with a book on her knee and a pencil in her hair, sewing a gold braid back onto a king's cloak. She looks at you over her spectacles and goes on sewing.".
  }
  Person pudding "Jem Pudding" at green {
    Role "the players' clown". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner cheerful.
    Greets "A thin man with a face like a folded napkin is lying on his back on the ground with a bear's head on his stomach. He raises one hand without moving anything else. 'Mind her,' he says. 'She is asleep, and she is a duchess when she wakes.'".
  }
  Species dancing_bear "an old dancing bear" like bear tame described "A big brown bear, grey about the muzzle, with a leather collar and no teeth to speak of. She smells of honey and wet straw.".
  Person the_bear "Patience" at green {
    Role "the players' bear". Species dancing_bear. Peaceable. Pronouns she.
    Greets "Patience ambles to the end of her rope to see who you are, and goes through your hands for honey.".
  }
  Thing wagon "the players' wagon" at green {
    State chained "A tall wagon, painted with a sun and a moon and the words GOSSE'S COMPANY in red letters gone pink, stands on {green} with its shafts down. A chain runs from its back wheel to a post, and the chain has a padlock on it.".
    State free "The players' wagon stands on {green} with its shafts up, loaded to the roof, a painted cloth rolled on top.".
  }
  Observe green_players at green when stuck(gosse) and not gone(gosse) "A bear is asleep on the ground by the players' wagon, with a thin man for a pillow, and a big old man in a faded crimson coat sits on the wagon's tail-board looking at the sky as if it owed him money.".
  Observe green_players_free at green when reckoned(gosse) and not gone(gosse) "Gosse is walking slowly round the wagon with his hands behind his back, inspecting its wheels as if he had just bought it.".
  Observe green_players_gone at green when gone(gosse) "There are wheel-ruts in the dust of {green}, and a ring of flattened ground where a bear lay.".

  // The town's own people on the players.
  Topic keeper_players with keeper "Ask {keeper} about the players stuck here" when stuck(gosse) and not gone(gosse) once {
    Says "'Four nights' bed and board for seven and a bear,' says {keeper}, 'and the bear eats for three. Eight coin. They had it, too, in the hat, Tuesday night: the whole town went to see them. And then their man who leads the bear went off with the hat.' {keeper} folds the cloth. 'I don't doubt the old man means to pay. He means a great many things. The wagon stays chained till someone does.'".
  }
  Topic priest_players with priest "Ask {priest} about the players" when not gone(gosse) once {
    Says "{priest} smiles, and then tries not to. 'They played the Shepherd's Revenge here on Tuesday, and the clown sat in my place at the front and gave a sermon, and I am still not sure whether I should have minded.' Then, more soberly: 'The man who went off with the hat was Lem Coyle, who leads their bear. He was not a bad man at the shrine. I saw him go out along the common toward the old lime-kiln, with the hat under his coat like a hen.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, lem_where). }
  }
  Topic trader_players with trader "Ask {trader} about the players" when not gone(gosse) once {
    Says "'They owe me for candles and a pot of honey,' says {trader}, 'and I would give them the candles again for the bear's dance alone. Lem Coyle bought a bottle off me Tuesday with a coin out of the hat. Said it was his wages.' {trader} shrugs. 'Maybe it was.'".
  }

  Topic gosse_trouble with gosse "Ask Gosse what has happened" when stuck(gosse) and not gone(gosse) once {
    Says "'A small reverse,' says Gosse. 'A tragedy in the classical sense: brought about by a flaw in the hero, who failed to pay his chain-man for four months.' He spreads his hands. 'Lem has gone off with the hat, and the hat had the reckoning in it, and our host has chained the wagon, and this week the Trial of the Wheel opens at Pentrice over the march and we must be there or die in a ditch.' He looks at you sidelong. 'I do not ask for money. I never ask for money. I mention that it exists.'".
  }
  Topic hepzibah_lem with hepzibah "Ask Hepzibah about Lem" when stuck(gosse) and not gone(gosse) once {
    Says "'He's owed four months,' says Hepzibah, biting off a thread. 'Four coin, since he will ask for it. I have it written down.' She turns a page of the book on her knee, a fat book of cues and accounts. 'Absalom pays his players in compliments, and most of us have learned to eat them. Lem has a mother.' She looks at you over her spectacles. 'If you find him, don't hurt him. He's a good hand with the bear.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, lem_owed). }
  }
  Topic pudding_patience with pudding "Ask Pudding about the bear" when not gone(gosse) once {
    Says "'Patience,' says Pudding, without lifting his head. 'Thirty-one, which is old for a bear and young for a duchess. She dances if you hum, and eats honey if you have it, and she has never in her life hurt anyone but a goose, and that was a misunderstanding.' He scratches her ear. 'Lem led her round the crowd with the hat on her head. Twice what any of us take. Nobody refuses a bear.'".
  }
  Discovery lem_where "Lem Coyle, who led the players' bear, went out along the common toward the old lime-kiln with the hat under his coat." { Known by priest. }
  Discovery lem_owed "Lem Coyle is owed four months' wages, four coin, and Hepzibah Dimmock has it written down." { Known by hepzibah. }

  // ── Lem, at the lime-kiln ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Place kiln "the old lime-kiln on the common" is room within town at 2, 2.
  Passage common_path "the path across the common" is path between green and kiln taking 20 minutes hidden until lem_where.
  Observe kiln_scene at kiln when true "A squat old kiln of blackened stone at the end of the common, with a hawthorn growing out of its top. The fire-hole is big enough to sit in out of the wind.".
  Person lem "Lem Coyle" at kiln {
    Role "the players' chain-man, sitting in the kiln's fire-hole". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner grim.
    Greets "A young man with a broken nose is sitting in the kiln's fire-hole with a bottle and a battered tall hat in his lap. He puts his arm round the hat when he sees you.".
  }
  Kind players_hat "the players' hat" is gear worth 0 weighing 1
    described "A tall black hat with a ribbon round it gone green, heavy with coins at the bottom. Somebody has written GOSSE inside the band.".
  Item hat "the players' hat" is players_hat at kiln hidden until hat_loose.
  Discovery hat_loose "Lem Coyle has let go of the players' hat.".
  Topic lem_why with lem "Ask Lem why he took the hat" when not lemSent(lem) and not hatHome(gosse) once {
    Says "'Wages,' says Lem. 'Four months of them. Four coin. He says next town, next town, and at the next town there's a new cloak for the king.' He drinks. 'I took what was mine and then I sat here, because the rest isn't mine and I'm not a thief, I'm just a fool who can't walk back into town.' He looks at the hat. 'There's twelve in it. Take the eight that's theirs if you want. I'm keeping my four.'".
  }
  Action pay_lem(actor: group, site: place) "Pay Lem his four months' wages from your own purse, and take the hat back to the players" {
    Speaker lem. Time 2 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(lem, site) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 4
      and not lemSent(lem) and not hatHome(gosse) and not knows(actor, hat_loose).
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 4. Increase quantity(lem, gold) by 4. Assert lemPaid(lem). Assert lemSent(lem).
      Assert knows(actor, hat_loose). Assert knows(actor, lem_kept). Retract at(lem, kiln). }
    Result "Lem looks at the four coins in your hand a long time before he takes them. Then he gets up, and dusts off the hat, and holds it out to you with both hands like a deacon with the plate. 'Tell him I'll see the Trial,' he says. 'From the yard, with the fishwives. Tell Patience I said goodbye.' He goes off along the common, west, not looking back.".
  }
  Action talk_lem_back(actor: group, site: place) "Talk Lem into taking his four coin from the hat and giving the rest back" {
    Speaker lem. Time 5 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(lem, site) and not lemSent(lem) and not hatHome(gosse)
      and not knows(actor, hat_loose).
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert lemSent(lem). Assert knows(actor, hat_loose). Assert knows(actor, lem_kept). Retract at(lem, kiln). }
    Result "You tell him what Hepzibah said: that it is written down, that he is owed it, that nobody thinks him a thief who matters. He counts four coins out of the hat into his own pocket, slowly, so you can see it is four. Then he gives you the hat. 'Tell Patience I said goodbye,' he says, and goes off west along the common, toward the march.".
    Otherwise "He holds the hat tighter. 'You're his,' he says. 'You talk like him.'".
  }
  Action take_hat(actor: group, site: place) "Take the hat off Lem" {
    Speaker lem. Time 2 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(lem, site) and not lemSent(lem) and not hatHome(gosse)
      and not knows(actor, hat_loose).
    Resolve check(actor, intimidation, dc_easy).
    On success { Assert lemSent(lem). Assert knows(actor, hat_loose). Retract at(lem, kiln). }
    Result "He does not fight you for it. He lets you take it out of his arms, and gets up, and goes off across the common the other way with his bottle, toward nowhere in particular.".
    Otherwise "He gets his back against the kiln wall and the hat behind him, and you see he would rather be hit than give it up.".
  }

  Event hat_home near gosse when keeps(gosse, hat) "Gosse weighs the hat in his hand, and tips it, and counts what falls out with his lips moving. Then he goes and puts it into the hands of {keeper}, with a bow that is very nearly sincere, and the chain comes off the wheel." teaches freed then {
    Assert hatHome(gosse). Assert reckoned(gosse). Retract stuck(gosse). Assert state(wagon, free). }

  // ── Paying, or making the money ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Action pay_reckoning(actor: group, site: place) "Pay {keeper} the players' reckoning, eight coin" {
    Speaker keeper. Time 2 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(keeper, site) and stuck(gosse) and not gone(gosse)
      and quantity(actor, gold) >= 8.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 8. Increase quantity(keeper, gold) by 8. Assert knows(actor, freed). Assert reckoned(gosse). Retract stuck(gosse).
      Assert state(wagon, free). }
    Result "{keeper} counts the coins twice, as if they might be a trick of the players', and goes out to unlock the chain. Out on {green}, Gosse stands up very slowly from the tail-board and takes off his hat to you.".
  }
  // In the evening, if the players have a crowd and someone to go round with the hat, the green pays.
  Query evening() means hour(clock) >= 17 and hour(clock) < 21.
  Action hat_round(actor: group, site: place) "Get the players to play in the open this evening, and take the hat round yourself" {
    Time 6.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, green) and at(gosse, green) and stuck(gosse)
      and not gone(gosse) and evening() and not hatRound(actor).
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert hatRound(actor). Assert knows(actor, freed). Assert reckoned(gosse). Retract stuck(gosse). Assert state(wagon, free). Assert knows(actor, seen_show).
      Assert showPlayed(gosse). }
    On failure { Assert hatRound(actor). Assert knows(actor, seen_show). Assert showPlayed(gosse). }
    Result "Gosse plays the prologue to six people and a dog and finishes it to forty; Pudding plays the shepherd and his own sheep; and when the hat goes round, you take it, and you look each of them in the eye, and you name the ones who have not paid in a voice the whole of {green} can hear. The hat comes back heavy. It is enough for {keeper}, and a coin over for the bear.".
    Otherwise "They play well. The crowd laughs in the right places. But when you take the hat round, people find they have left their purses at home, and the hat comes back with three coins in it and a button.".
  }
  Action bear_round(actor: group, site: place) "Lead Patience round the crowd on her chain, with the hat on her head" {
    Time 6.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, green) and at(gosse, green) and stuck(gosse)
      and not gone(gosse) and evening() and not hatRound(actor).
    Resolve check(actor, woodcraft, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert hatRound(actor). Assert knows(actor, freed). Assert reckoned(gosse). Retract stuck(gosse). Assert state(wagon, free). Assert knows(actor, seen_show).
      Assert showPlayed(gosse). }
    On failure { Assert hatRound(actor). Assert knows(actor, seen_show). Assert showPlayed(gosse). }
    Result "Pudding hums, and Patience gets up on her hind legs with a sigh like a bellows and dances, slow, turning, with the hat on her head. You lead her round. Nobody refuses a bear. Children put coins in with both hands; {priest} puts one in and pretends not to have. When Patience sits down again the hat is so heavy it falls off her head.".
    Otherwise "Patience will not go round. She sits down where she is and looks at you with great patience and declines to dance for anyone but Pudding, and the crowd laughs at you, kindly, and pays very little.".
  }
  Action tumble_round(actor: group, site: place) "Go on yourself between the scenes, and do what you do" {
    Time 6.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, green) and at(gosse, green) and stuck(gosse)
      and not gone(gosse) and evening() and not hatRound(actor) and craft(actor, craft_stage).
    On success { Assert hatRound(actor). Assert knows(actor, freed). Assert reckoned(gosse). Retract stuck(gosse). Assert state(wagon, free). Assert knows(actor, seen_show).
      Assert showPlayed(gosse). }
    Result "Gosse looks at you once, as one of the profession looks at another, and gives you the space between the second scene and the third. You do what you do. The crowd, which has seen the players twice already this week, has not seen you; and when Gosse comes on again he has to wait for them to stop. The hat comes back heavy, and Hepzibah writes something in her book.".
  }

  // ── Gosse's offer ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Topic gosse_thanks with gosse "Ask Gosse what he will do now" when reckoned(gosse) and not gone(gosse) and not knows(actor, joined) once {
    Says "'Go west,' says Gosse, 'at first light, over the march to Pentrice, where three companies will play three nights before the city in the Trial of the Wheel, and the Bench of four will give one of them the Patent: a house of its own, for ever. A roof, my friend. Forty-one years I have played under the sky.' He considers you. 'I have lost a chain-man and found a better one. A season's work, a share of the house, and the honour of the profession, which is worth precisely nothing and which I would not sell for a crown. We lodge at the Painted Moon by the Westgate. Think about it.'".
  }
  Topic gosse_join with gosse "Tell Gosse you will take service with his company for the season" when reckoned(gosse) and not gone(gosse) and not knows(actor, joined) once {
    Says "Gosse takes your hand in both of his. 'Done,' he says. 'Before witnesses: Hepzibah, write it down.' Hepzibah writes it down. 'You will walk faster than Patience,' Gosse says. 'Go by your own road; but be at the Painted Moon by the Westgate before the Trial, and ask for the loft. We shall want you for everything.' Pudding, from the ground, says: 'He means we shall want you to carry everything.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, joined). }
  }
  Topic gosse_profession with gosse "Tell Gosse you are of the profession yourself" when craft(actor, craft_stage) and not gone(gosse) once {
    Says "Gosse looks at you again, properly, the way one player looks at another across a crowd: the hands, the feet, the voice. 'So you are,' he says softly. 'So you are. Then you know what it is to be stuck in a strange town with a bear and no hat.' He laughs, enormously. 'Hepzibah, here is somebody who knows.'".
  }

  // The players go on to Pentrice the morning after they are free; if nobody frees them, they sell the king's cloak to
  // pay and go on in the end, a week late and poorer.
  Rule players_go when reckoned(gosse) and hour(clock) == 6 and not gone(gosse) { Assert gone(gosse). }
  Rule players_give_up when watch(clock) >= 1008 and stuck(gosse) and not gone(gosse) { Retract stuck(gosse). Assert reckoned(gosse). Assert gone(gosse). }
  Rule players_leave when gone(gosse) and at(gosse, green) and not at(party, green) {
    Retract at(gosse, green). Retract at(hepzibah, green). Retract at(pudding, green). Retract at(the_bear, green). Retract at(wagon, green).
    Assert stale(on_green). }
  Rule lem_leaves when lemSent(lem) and at(lem, kiln) { Retract at(lem, kiln). }

  Objective players when knows(party, on_green) and stuck(gosse) and not gone(gosse) "Gosse's Company, players, are stuck at {town} until someone pays their reckoning.".
  Objective players_west when knows(party, joined) "Be at the Painted Moon by the Westgate of Pentrice, over the march west, before the Trial of the Wheel.".
  Goal reckoned(gosse).
}

data/goings-on/quarrel/situation.kyr:
Module quarrel "The boundary stones" {
  Description "The innkeeper and the merchant have not spoken since the spring, when the stones between the inn's garden and the merchant's yard moved a stride in the night. The priest knows where they stood, and will not say so to the merchant's face: the merchant gives the most at the shrine.".
  Entity party: group "Your company".
  Place town "The town" is settlement.
  Place taproom "The taproom" is room.
  Place shop "The shop" is room.
  Place shrine "The shrine" is room.
  Entity keeper: group "The innkeeper".
  Entity trader: group "The merchant".
  Entity priest: group "The priest".
  Relation restored(group). Relation bought(group). Relation offered(group).
  Entity feud: fact "The innkeeper and the merchant have not spoken since the boundary stones moved.".
  Initially Assert established(feud).

  Place garden "the inn's back garden" is room within town at 1, 2.
  Passage back_door "the back door of the inn" is door between taproom and garden.
  Observe garden_scene at garden when not restored(trader) "Cabbages, a hen-house, a washing line. A row of white stones runs across the bottom of the garden, freshly set, a stride inside the hedge.".
  Observe garden_settled at garden when restored(trader) "The white stones are back in their old holes along the hedge.".
  Discovery holes "The boundary stones were dug up and set a stride into the inn's garden: their old holes are still there, under the grass by the hedge." {
    Found by searching garden "Under the grass along the hedge, your heel finds the old holes: square, stone-sided, a stride outside the new row. The stones were moved.".
  }

  Topic keeper_stones with keeper "Ask {keeper} about the stones" when not restored(trader) once {
    Says "'Moved in the night,' says {keeper}, wiping the same cup. 'A stride of my garden, and the well with it. Ask the priest. Ask anyone. Nobody will say it to {trader}.'".
  }
  Topic trader_stones with trader "Ask {trader} about the stones" when not restored(trader) and not bought(actor) once {
    Says "'{keeper} drinks and dreams,' says {trader}. 'Those stones are where my father set them.' Then, lower: 'If anyone asks, you saw nothing. Five coin for your trouble.'".
    On discuss { Assert offered(actor). }
  }
  // The coin is taken only once it has been offered.
  Topic trader_bribe with trader "Take {trader}'s five coin and say nothing" when offered(actor) and not restored(trader) and not bought(actor) {
    Says "{trader} counts the coins into your hand. By evening the whole town knows you took them.".
    On discuss { Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 5. Assert bought(actor). Assert refusesService(keeper, actor). }
  }
  Topic trader_holes with trader "Tell {trader} about the old holes under the grass" when knows(actor, holes) and not restored(trader) and not bought(actor) once {
    Says "{trader} goes red, then white. 'All right,' {trader} says. 'All right. I will set them back, and pay for the cabbages.'".
    On discuss { Assert restored(trader). }
  }
  Topic priest_stones with priest "Ask {priest} about the stones" when not restored(trader) once {
    Says "'They were moved in the spring,' says {priest}. 'I married {keeper}'s parents in that garden; I know where the stones stood. But {trader} gives the most at the shrine, and I have a roof to mend.'".
  }
  Topic keeper_thanks with keeper "Tell {keeper} the stones are going back" when restored(trader) and not bought(actor) once {
    Says "{keeper} puts down the cup, and pushes six coin back across the counter. 'For your trouble. Nobody else in this town would have said it to {trader}.'".
    On discuss { Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 6. }
  }

  Objective stones when knows(party, feud) and not restored(trader) and not bought(party) "The innkeeper and the merchant are at odds over the boundary stones behind the inn.".
  Goal restored(trader).
}

data/kits/bounty/elders/patron.kyr:
Module elders_patron "The elders' price" {
  Description "The settlement's elders pool what they have to see the raiders' band broken, and will feed and house whoever breaks it for as long as they live.".
  Entity party: group "Your company".
  Place town "The settlement the raiders prey on" is room.
  // Where the raiders hold out: their word puts it on the company's map, somewhere to set out for.
  Place lair "Where the raiders hold out" is room.
  Entity chief: group "The raiders' chief".
  Entity band: group "The raiders".
  Person elders "the elders" at town {
    Role "the settlement's elders". Ancestry human. Calling commoner. Level 2. Numbers 3. Peaceable.
    State conferring "Three old people stand together by the well with their heads close, and stop talking when you come near.".
    Offers lodging "a bed and a hot supper in one of their houses" for 0 coin.
  }
  // Their tables are for whoever breaks the band; until then, strangers pay at the inn like anyone.
  Initially Assert refusesService(elders, party).
  Entity price: fact "The elders will pay twenty-five crowns, pooled, to see the raiders' band broken, and feed whoever does it.".
  Initially Assert established(price).
  Initially Assert leadsTo(price, lair).
  Topic offer with elders "Ask the elders what they are whispering about" when true once {
    Says "'Them up at {lair},' says the oldest, and doesn't need to point. 'We've put together what we can. Twenty-five crowns, to see that band broken: not the chief, the band, every last one run off or under. And whoever does it eats at our tables till they die.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, price). }
  }
  Relation met(entity).
  Objective band_price when knows(party, price) and not thanked(elders) "The elders will pay twenty-five crowns to see the raiders' band broken.".
  Rule band_broken when (not able(band) or routed(band)) and not met(price) { Assert met(price). }
  Topic claim with elders "Tell the elders the band is broken" when met(price) and knows(actor, price) once {
    Says "The elders count out the coins on the well's lid, slowly, arguing about one of them. Then the oldest shakes your hand and says you will not pay for a meal here again.".
    On discuss { Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 25. Assert thanked(elders). Retract refusesService(elders, actor). }
  }
  Relation thanked(group).
  Goal thanked(elders).
}

data/kits/bounty/kit.json:
{
  "version": 1,
  "id": "bounty",
  "name": "A price on a power",
  "about": "A settlement that a power preys on puts a price on the power's chief. It needs a power some earlier placement established, the settlement that power raids, the people the power acts through, and where it holds out (which the offer puts on the company's map); who offers the money, and what they want for it, is Deem's to propose.",
  "slots": {
    "victim": { "is": "raids(?raider, ?victim)", "requires": ["not bountyOn(?victim, ?raider)"] },
    "power": { "is": "raids(?power, ?victim) and power(?power)" },
    "chief": { "is": "chief(?power, ?chief)" },
    "band": { "is": "band(?power, ?band)" },
    "lair": { "is": "holds(?power, ?lair)" }
  },
  "proposals": {
    "patron": { "table": "bounty_patron", "by": "terrain" }
  },
  "provides": ["bountyOn(?victim, ?power)"],
  "tables": "tables.json",
  "modules": [
    { "id": "patron", "when": { "patron": "widow" }, "bundle": "widow/module.json",
      "imports": { "party": "@party", "town": "?victim", "chief": "?chief", "band": "?band", "lair": "?lair" } },
    { "id": "patron", "when": { "patron": "elders" }, "bundle": "elders/module.json",
      "imports": { "party": "@party", "town": "?victim", "chief": "?chief", "band": "?band", "lair": "?lair" } }
  ]
}

data/kits/bounty/tables.json:
{
  "bounty_patron": {
    "discriminator": "terrain",
    "groups": {
      "default": [
        { "_key": "widow", "__weight": 2, "_why": "a widow whose son went after the raiders, who will pay her savings for their chief, gone" },
        { "_key": "elders", "_why": "the settlement's elders, who pool what they have for the band broken, and feed whoever does it" }
      ]
    }
  }
}

data/kits/bounty/widow/patron.kyr:
Module widow_patron "A widow's price" {
  Description "A woman whose son went after the raiders and did not come back puts her savings on their chief: dead or run, she does not care which.".
  Entity party: group "Your company".
  Place town "The settlement the raiders prey on" is room.
  // Where the raiders hold out: her word puts it on the company's map, somewhere to set out for.
  Place lair "Where the raiders hold out" is room.
  Entity chief: group "The raiders' chief".
  Entity band: group "The raiders".
  // Known by how she is seen: nobody tells a stranger her name.
  Person widow "the woman in black" at town {
    Role "a widow whose son went after the raiders". Ancestry human. Calling commoner. Level 1. Peaceable.
    State waiting "A woman in black sits on the step of a cold house with her hands in her lap, watching the road.".
  }
  Entity price: fact "A widow will pay her savings and her son's ring for the raiders' chief, dead or run off.".
  Initially Assert established(price).
  Initially Assert leadsTo(price, lair).
  Topic offer with widow "Ask the woman in black what she is waiting for" when true once {
    Says "'For somebody to go up there,' she says, looking toward {lair}, 'and do what my boy went to do.' She opens her hand: coins, and a ring. 'All I have, for {chief}. Dead or run, I don't care which. Just gone.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, price). }
  }
  Relation met(entity).
  Objective chief_price when knows(party, price) and not knows(party, paid_out) "A widow will pay her savings to see the raiders' chief dead or run off.".
  Rule chief_gone when (not able(chief) or routed(chief)) and not met(price) { Assert met(price). }
  Item ring "her son's ring" is grave_rings at town hidden until paid_out.
  Entity paid_out: fact "The widow has paid the company her savings and her son's ring.".
  Initially Assert established(paid_out).
  Topic claim with widow "Tell the woman in black it is done" when met(price) and knows(actor, price) once {
    Says "She doesn't cry. She counts the coins into your hand one at a time, and then puts the ring on top, and goes inside and shuts the door.".
    On discuss { Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 15. Assert knows(actor, paid_out). }
  }
  Goal met(price) and knows(party, paid_out).
}

data/kits/raider-hold/hobs/folk.kyr:
Module hob_folk "Hobs" {
  Description "Hobs: small, quick, spiteful people who live by robbing the roads at night and the farms when they are hungry. They laugh while they rob, ransom what they cannot eat, and cannot abide the sound of a bell.".
  Entity party: group "Your company".
  Place outside "The approach" is room.
  Place road "The road they watch" is room.
  Place town "The settlement they rob" is room.
  Place yard "Inside the gate" is room.
  Place hall "The hall" is room.
  Place den "The chief's place" is room.
  Place pens "The pens" is room.
  Place store "The store" is room.
  Place lookout "The lookout" is room.
  Place bolt "Where the back way comes out" is room.
  Place chapel "Where they stole the bell" is room.
  Entity gate: passage "The way in".
  Entity chest: thing "The chief's chest".
  Entity heap: thing "The plunder".
  Entity backway_known: fact "The back way out of the hold".

  Person watchers "the hobs on the gate" at yard {
    Role "two hobs keeping the way in". Ancestry goblin. Calling thief. Level 1. Numbers 2.
    Called "Snig", "Tatterlip".
    Guards gate.
    State watching blocking "Two hobs squat just inside the way in, dicing with knucklebones and watching who comes.".
    State roving "The hobs who kept the gate have gone out raiding themselves; the way in is unwatched.".
  }
  Person raiders "the raiding party" at hall {
    Role "hobs who go out on the roads at night". Ancestry goblin. Calling thief. Level 1. Numbers 3.
    Called "Nettle", "Gristle", "Old Burdock".
    Uses go, assail. Plans 6 steps.
    State idle "Three hobs sharpen cudgels by the fire and argue about whose turn it is to carry the sack.".
  }
  Person gaffer "the Gaffer" at den {
    Role "chief of the hobs". Ancestry goblin. Calling thief. Level 3.
    Wants grave_rings. Wants chapel_plate. Wants jade_idol. Wants toll_silver. Wants bronze_bearing.
    State presiding "The Gaffer sits on a heap of stolen fleeces in a bishop's mitre and somebody's spectacles, and watches you with very bright eyes.".
  }
  Initially Assert serves(watchers, gaffer). Initially Assert serves(raiders, gaffer).
  Person captive "the shepherd's boy" at pens {
    Role "a boy taken off the farms". Ancestry human. Calling commoner. Level 1. Peaceable.
    State penned "A boy sits among the stolen sheep with his hands tied, trying not to cry.".
    State loose "The shepherd's boy rubs his wrists and looks at the way out.".
    Change untie "Untie the shepherd's boy" from penned to loose.
    Uses go. Plans 12 steps.
  }
  Pursuit stay_close for captive "keeping close to you" priority 30 when following(captive, party) seeks together(captive, party).
  Item handbell "a chapel handbell, wrapped in sacking" is bell in heap.
  Item chalice "a stolen chalice" is chapel_plate in chest.
  Item rings "a string of rings off the dead" is grave_rings in heap.

  Observe empty_frame at chapel when not freed(captive) "The bell is gone from its frame over the well. 'Hobs,' people say, and spit, and nobody has gone after it.".
  Observe clappers at outside when true "Up on the hold, things hang where anyone coming can see them: among them bells, every one with its clapper torn out.".
  // What the boy knows: the back way out, and what the hobs are afraid of.
  Entity bell_dread: fact "Hobs cannot abide the sound of a bell: ring one where they are and they run.".
  Initially Assert established(bell_dread).
  Topic boy_bells with captive "Ask the shepherd's boy about the hobs" when true once {
    Says "'They stole the bell off our chapel,' the boy whispers, 'and then they wouldn't touch it. Burdock wrapped it in a sack with his eyes shut. They can't stand bells. Our priest used to ring them off the farms, before.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, bell_dread). }
  }
  Topic boy_way with captive "Ask the shepherd's boy how the hobs come and go" when true once {
    Says "'There's a back way,' he says. 'I've seen them go out of it with sacks and come in without. I don't know where it comes out.'".
  }
  Rule boy_follows when state(captive, loose) and not acceptsEscort(captive, party)
    says "The boy grabs your sleeve. 'Take me home?'" { Assert acceptsEscort(captive, party). }
  Initially Assert home(captive, town). Initially Set thanks(captive) to 8.
  Rule boy_home when cameHome(captive) and not freed(captive)
    says "The boy's mother sees him from a doorway and comes running with her apron over her mouth." {
    Assert freed(captive).
  }
  Relation freed(group).

  // At night on the road: the raiding party waits beside it and falls on whoever passes.
  Relation quiet(group). Relation paid(group). Relation rung(place).
  Measure shame(group).
  // The raiding party is the band the Gaffer sends to hold anything the hobs take.
  Initially Assert posts(raiders, gaffer).
  Rule waylay when at(party, road) and dark() and dice(clock) <= 4 and at(raiders, hall) and able(raiders)
    and not quiet(raiders) and not tolerates(raiders, party)
    says "Shapes rise out of the dark beside the road: hobs, grinning, with cudgels and a sack for whatever you are carrying." {
    Assert at(raiders, road). Assert assails(raiders, party).
  }
  Rule waylay_watch when at(party, road) and dark() and dice(clock) <= 4 and state(watchers, roving) and able(watchers)
    and at(watchers, yard) and not tolerates(watchers, party)
    says "Two hobs drop out of a tree onto the road in front of you, and two more behind." {
    Assert at(watchers, road). Assert assails(watchers, party).
  }
  Rule raiders_home when able(raiders) and at(raiders, road) and not together(raiders, party) { Assert at(raiders, hall). }
  Rule watchers_home when able(watchers) and at(watchers, road) and not together(watchers, party) { Assert at(watchers, yard). }
  // The farms: on a dark night the raiders go out to the settlement and take what they can carry.
  Rule raid when untilLight(clock) == 4 and dice(clock) <= 25 and able(raiders) and at(raiders, hall) and not quiet(raiders)
    and not at(party, town) { Increase losses(town) by 1. }
  Rule spite when alarmed(gaffer) and untilLight(clock) == 4 and able(raiders) and not quiet(raiders) and not at(party, town) {
    Increase losses(town) by 1.
  }
  Observe raided at town when losses(town) >= 1 and losses(town) <= 2 "Hobs were at the farms again in the night: a ewe gone, a hen-house kicked in, and little muddy footprints on a windowsill.".
  Observe raided_hard at town when losses(town) >= 3 "The farms round about have been robbed night after night. People are sleeping in their byres with pitchforks, and talking about leaving.".
  // A raiding party that was beaten stays home three nights; if it is gone, the gate-hobs take to the road instead.
  Rule lie_low when routed(raiders) and able(raiders) and not quiet(raiders) {
    Assert quiet(raiders). Set shame(raiders) to 3. Assert at(raiders, hall).
  }
  Rule lick_wounds when quiet(raiders) and not paid(gaffer) and untilLight(clock) == 1 and shame(raiders) >= 1 {
    Decrease shame(raiders) by 1.
  }
  Rule recovered when quiet(raiders) and not paid(gaffer) and shame(raiders) <= 0 {
    Retract quiet(raiders). Retract routed(raiders).
  }
  Rule new_raiders when not able(raiders) and able(watchers) and state(watchers, watching) and untilLight(clock) == 1
    and not paid(gaffer) { Assert state(watchers, roving). }
  // Trouble at the hold rouses it: the raiding party comes for whoever is inside.
  Rule alarm when (routed(watchers) or not able(watchers) or not able(gaffer)) and not alarmed(gaffer) { Assert alarmed(gaffer). }
  Pursuit defend for raiders "turning out to defend the hold" priority 30 when alarmed(gaffer) and not quiet(raiders)
    and (at(party, yard) or at(party, hall) or at(party, den) or at(party, pens) or at(party, lookout))
    seeks assails(raiders, party).
  Rule gaffer_fights when together(gaffer, party) and able(gaffer) and alarmed(gaffer) and not tolerates(gaffer, party)
    says "The Gaffer comes off his fleeces with a knife in each hand, cackling." { Assert assails(gaffer, party). }

  // A bell rung where hobs are, or within earshot of them, sends them running out of the back way.
  Action ring_bell(actor: group, site: place) "Ring the bell" {
    Description "Swing it hard. Whatever is within earshot will hear it.".
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and holding(actor, bell) and not rung(site).
    On success { Assert rung(site). }
    Result "The bell's voice goes out over everything.".
  }
  Rule bell_watchers when rung(?p) and able(watchers) and not routed(watchers) and (at(watchers, ?p) or (connects(?w, ?p, ?q) and at(watchers, ?q)))
    says "The hobs clap their hands over their ears and run, howling, the way hobs run from a bell." {
    Assert routed(watchers). Retract state(watchers, watching). Assert at(watchers, bolt).
  }
  Rule bell_raiders when rung(?p) and able(raiders) and not routed(raiders) and (at(raiders, ?p) or (connects(?w, ?p, ?q) and at(raiders, ?q)))
    says "Somewhere close a hob shrieks, and feet go scrabbling away." { Assert routed(raiders). Assert at(raiders, bolt). }
  Rule bell_gaffer when rung(?p) and able(gaffer) and (at(gaffer, ?p) or (connects(?w, ?p, ?q) and at(gaffer, ?q)))
    and not routed(gaffer) says "The Gaffer screams like a kettle and goes out of the back way with his mitre over his ears." {
    Assert routed(gaffer). Assert at(gaffer, bolt).
  }
  Rule bell_fades when rung(?p) { Retract rung(?p). }

  // A parley at the way in; and treasure for the Gaffer buys the farms a month's peace.
  Action parley(actor: group, site: place) "Call to the hobs for a parley" {
    Description "Stand where they can see you, empty-handed, and ask to talk to whoever is in charge.".
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and connects(gate, site, ?in) and at(watchers, ?in) and able(watchers)
      and state(watchers, watching) and not alarmed(gaffer) and not tolerates(watchers, actor).
    Time 3.
    On success { Assert tolerates(watchers, actor). Assert tolerates(raiders, actor). Assert tolerates(gaffer, actor). }
    Result "There is a lot of giggling. Then Snig sticks his head out. 'Gaffer says come in and wipe your feet. Don't touch nothing.'".
  }
  Rule caught_thieving when tolerates(gaffer, party) and not alarmed(gaffer) and (at(party, store) or at(party, pens))
    and ((capable(party, stealth) and dice(clock) <= 15) or (not capable(party, stealth) and dice(clock) <= 50))
    says "'OI!' A hob in the doorway points at you with his whole arm. 'THIEVES!'" { Assert alarmed(gaffer). }
  Rule truce_broken when alarmed(gaffer) and tolerates(watchers, party) {
    Retract tolerates(watchers, party). Retract tolerates(raiders, party). Retract tolerates(gaffer, party).
  }
  Topic gaffer_terms with gaffer "Ask the Gaffer what it would take to leave the farms alone" when tolerates(gaffer, party) once {
    Says "The Gaffer takes off his spectacles and polishes them on his beard. 'Shiny things,' he says. 'A ring, a cup, a pretty. Give the Gaffer something he likes and the farms can sleep. For a month, say. A month is a long time for a hob.'".
  }
  Rule tribute when keeps(gaffer, ?gift) and not paid(gaffer)
    says "The Gaffer bites it, holds it to the light and bites it again. 'The farms can sleep,' he says. 'A month.'" {
    Assert paid(gaffer). Assert quiet(raiders). Set shame(raiders) to 30.
  }
  Rule peace_wears when paid(gaffer) and untilLight(clock) == 1 and shame(raiders) >= 1 { Decrease shame(raiders) by 1. }
  Rule peace_ends when paid(gaffer) and shame(raiders) <= 0 { Retract paid(gaffer). }
  Goal not able(gaffer) or routed(gaffer) or paid(gaffer) or freed(captive).
}

